text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T02:06:46-07:00","id":1461523,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'm assuming justin was more economical than anarchs which wasted page after page but it sounds like it needed more time to breathe. How much of the book is fluff and crunch vs ic puff pieces and art?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T02:12:22-07:00","id":1461524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461418#post1461418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, phrasings like <i>&quot;Ultimately, Sabbat vampires don\u2019t have a choice in many of the actions they take. In giving themselves to the Beast, they\u2019ve set aside that central riddle of the Kindred condition.&quot;</i> don't give the impression that the authors think a deprogramming is possible.<br /> <br /> Second, if they did, then being able to play Sabbat members, especially one's with still some shreds of Humanity, would be a far better representation of how those things work and a recognition that people in such a state are still people.<br /> <br /> Like how people sometimes leave Scientology, QAnon and ISIS, after a long time of suffering while their twisted beliefs conflict with their actual best interests, and would also respect the feelings of their loved ones that desperately want to get them back.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat isn't a RL terrorist group, but fiction is a means for us to understand and explore reality. By making the Sabbat unplayable and the existence of conflicted members impossible they're barring an important avenue for exploration and a tacit statement about their world view. Given the context and proportions, the former is far more problematic than the later, since it is just a game, but the later is still problematic nonetheless and something that really ticks me off.<br /> <br /> It is too easy to write-off extremists as non-human and don't think further about it. And that's exactly what they did.<br /> <br /> <br /> I agree and that's implicit on that post, but it doesn't change that for a lot of old Sabbat groups it'll rub the wrong way nevertheless. They'll <b>indeed</b> be told that to play by the lore they will have to dump the Sabbat, staying is not an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t have access to the pdf and I\u2019m not sure how to ask without offence so I apologise in advance for asking about what is probably a misunderstanding.<br /> Reading this it seems like V5 is presenting the Sabbat as inhuman religious terrorists to be used as old time orcs,<br /> while simultaneously having intelligence agencies as representative of humanity drone bombing them\u2026in the middle east.<br /> This isn\u2019t actually true right?<br /> I admit I find the SI sometimes comes to close to glorifying state agencies,the military etc. for my comfort so I might be too sensitive and I find it difficult to express myself freely in English.<br /> Again,this is probably a misunderstanding but I would be grateful if anyone could explain a bit more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25477-perisa","name":"Perisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T02:20:09-07:00","id":1461525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Perisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461524#post1461524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t have access to the pdf and I\u2019m not sure how to ask without offence so I apologise in advance for asking about what is probably a misunderstanding.<br /> Reading this it seems like V5 is presenting the Sabbat as inhuman religious terrorists to be used as old time orcs,<br /> while simultaneously having intelligence agencies as representative of humanity drone bombing them\u2026in the middle east.<br /> This isn\u2019t actually true right?<br /> I admit I find the SI sometimes comes to close to glorifying state agencies,the military etc. for my comfort so I might be too sensitive and I find it difficult to express myself freely in English.<br /> Again,this is probably a misunderstanding but I would be grateful if anyone could explain a bit more.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I think that's not remotely true.<br /> <br /> I think I mentioned multiple times how that's completely not the case.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are, however, 100% portrayed as monstrous and evil with an absolute revelry in every atrocitity and depravity possible. They have also suffered the absolute worst from the Second Inquisition. That's because the Sabbat disdain the Masquerade, though, and hate the idea of backing down from Kine. Hence, they have suffered more casualties from it than the Anarchs and Camarilla combined.<br /> <br /> But they are well-written erudite and philosophical monsters. With well-justified and well-written philosophy.<br /> <br /> You aren't just an orc if you're shown as terrible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T02:33:02-07:00","id":1461528,"title":"","content":"Any reference to the Nosferatu inter sect communications still being a thing or is that gone now?<br /> I could see it going either way; either the sabbat fracture meaning that anybody who would previously communicate over sect lines has left, or that even the hardcore sabbat are willing to trade some information albeit it's more limited and not a pleasant experience for either side","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25078-brickman","name":"Brickman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T02:42:51-07:00","id":1461531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brickman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461528#post1461528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any reference to the Nosferatu inter sect communications still being a thing or is that gone now?<br /> I could see it going either way; either the sabbat fracture meaning that anybody who would previously communicate over sect lines has left, or that even the hardcore sabbat are willing to trade some information albeit it's more limited and not a pleasant experience for either side</div> </div> </div> </div>There's almost no discussion of individual Clans in the book, only the Paths. As stated, it feels like a massive chunk of this book was excised. I hope they'll make a Sabbat Companion PDF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T03:00:00-07:00","id":1461533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Perisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461524#post1461524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t have access to the pdf and I\u2019m not sure how to ask without offence so I apologise in advance for asking about what is probably a misunderstanding.<br /> Reading this it seems like V5 is presenting the Sabbat as inhuman religious terrorists to be used as old time orcs,<br /> while simultaneously having intelligence agencies as representative of humanity drone bombing them\u2026in the middle east.<br /> This isn\u2019t actually true right?<br /> I admit I find the SI sometimes comes to close to glorifying state agencies,the military etc. for my comfort so I might be too sensitive and I find it difficult to express myself freely in English.<br /> Again,this is probably a misunderstanding but I would be grateful if anyone could explain a bit more.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book presents the Sabbat as antagonists and has A LOT of useful information and suggestions for using them as such in a game. Are there rules? Discipline powers are there as are stat lines for Sabbat types. As a Storyteller's tool this book is excellent. For players it MIGHT be useful if you can convince your ST to give you access to some of the Sabbat specific powers (which are nasty, I wouldn't do it for example) or if the ST wants to make the effort, Path descriptions may be adapted in V5 &quot;morality&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T03:12:41-07:00","id":1461536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461456#post1461456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean it says that Ur-Shulgi is battling a Three-Eyed Witch (Salubri ancient?) and a massive storm of the dead. Oh and all of the houses where the mortals live have claw marks on them. Which is important because vampires need blood to live. I think whatever the situation in Alamut is that it is no longer operating on gritty urban fantasy rules but Mage 2nd Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see that. The in character vampire who wrote that article states that none of the Banu Haqim can access Alamut, that the laws of physics do not apply up there (1 night spans 40 nights?) that. And keep in mind Alamut has the heartsblood well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T03:29:57-07:00","id":1461538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461536#post1461536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see that. The in character vampire who wrote that article states that none of the Banu Haqim can access Alamut, that the laws of physics do not apply up there (1 night spans 40 nights?) that. And keep in mind Alamut has the heartsblood well.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true:<br /> <br /> <i>It is in the clutches of an Ancient who was Ancient<br /> when the children of Caine were young, a killer<br /> of killers.<br /> <br /> It is in the clutches of a witch with three eyes<br /> whose vitae enthralls those who partake of it in but<br /> a single draught.<br /> <br /> It is in the clutches of a cult that reveres yet<br /> dreads the rising of those who have been judged.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T03:47:27-07:00","id":1461541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461538#post1461538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While true:<br /> <br /> <i>It is in the clutches of an Ancient who was Ancient<br /> when the children of Caine were young, a killer<br /> of killers.<br /> <br /> It is in the clutches of a witch with three eyes<br /> whose vitae enthralls those who partake of it in but<br /> a single draught.<br /> <br /> It is in the clutches of a cult that reveres yet<br /> dreads the rising of those who have been judged.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Ur-Shulgi, the Salubri coming after his Baali friends, and the True Black Hand!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T04:28:14-07:00","id":1461543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Perisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461524#post1461524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading this it seems like V5 is presenting the Sabbat as inhuman religious terrorists to be used as old time orcs,<br /> while simultaneously having intelligence agencies as representative of humanity drone bombing them\u2026in the middle east.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on what you call old time orcs. I'd say they're more like Drow.<br /> <br /> And we can't say much about the Second Inquisition yet. The first book gave that vibe to a lot of players, but others pointed out that many other interpretations are possible where this is not the case. Without their own book yet we can't say for sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461525#post1461525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I think that's not remotely true.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what either of you understand as orcs, but in D&amp;D they have well-written and well-justified philosophies. In Tolkien they're fairly intelligent, despite disorganized, with many complex creations of their own.<br /> <br /> So... I'd say old-time orcs is a pretty accurate description. Modern orcs are far more nuanced, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461536#post1461536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see that. The in character vampire who wrote that article states that none of the Banu Haqim can access Alamut, that the laws of physics do not apply up there (1 night spans 40 nights?) that. And keep in mind Alamut has the heartsblood well.</div> </div> </div> </div>My opinion on the matter is from a purely Doylist perspective. The Assamites as religious extremist assassins aren't just a simplistic stereotype that I found boring as hell before I could comprehend how racist it was, they're also, well, racist. An abhorrent misrepresentation of a culture and the cultural appropriation of the history of the Nizari State. So Alamut blowing up with the last vestiges of that version of the clan can only be a good thing.<br /> <br /> On top of that, Ur-Shulgi is like 5 times Samuel Haight in character absurdity. It should have never been and the setting will be better if he's excised from existence by whatever Paradox Realm is engulfing the castle. Killing [Ravnos] only cost so much effort because Ur-Shulgi wasn't there to fart it out of reality, he's just too lazy to outright win the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T04:30:27-07:00","id":1461544,"title":"","content":"Sounds like one more advance in the attempt to launch more profitable media from Masquerade, while limiting bad PR and controversy. Sales of the game was probably a distant third priority if it was in there at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461525#post1461525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hence, they have suffered more casualties from it than the Anarchs and Camarilla combined.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one thing I found reasonable and an organic development in this edition. The exponential increase in mobile recording devices among the kine, and the vast disparity between the Sabbat and Camarilla in the amount of resources thrown at the maintaining of the masquerade. The differences in sect emphasis on the masquerade. Sabbat was always going to get burned bad by the inquisition<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461538#post1461538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While true:<br /> <br /> <i>It is in the clutches of an Ancient who was Ancient<br /> when the children of Caine were young, a killer<br /> of killers.<br /> <br /> It is in the clutches of a witch with three eyes<br /> whose vitae enthralls those who partake of it in but<br /> a single draught.<br /> <br /> It is in the clutches of a cult that reveres yet<br /> dreads the rising of those who have been judged.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like Rayzeel, a female Salubri as old or probably older than Ur-Shulgi, and another candidate for third Baali. Or First Baali, depending on the origin story picked. Although the first bit could imply that the original builder has come for Alamut and found it infested with Cainites.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T06:41:35-07:00","id":1461550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461538#post1461538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While true:<br /> <br /> <i>It is in the clutches of an Ancient who was Ancient<br /> when the children of Caine were young, a killer<br /> of killers.<br /> <br /> It is in the clutches of a witch with three eyes<br /> whose vitae enthralls those who partake of it in but<br /> a single draught.<br /> <br /> It is in the clutches of a cult that reveres yet<br /> dreads the rising of those who have been judged.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and how does he know these things? Basically heresay because he could not visit Alamut. The only thing he knows is that &quot;something&quot; happened one night but doesn't know exactly what besides the fact the village near Alamut was depopulated via some sort of evil ritual. None of these things mean Ur-Shulgi is dead (quite the contrary actually) nor that the Assamite loyalists are gone (and keep in mind they are supposed to represent the majority of their clan).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My opinion on the matter is from a purely Doylist perspective. The Assamites as religious extremist assassins aren't just a simplistic stereotype that I found boring as hell before I could comprehend how racist it was, they're also, well, racist. An abhorrent misrepresentation of a culture and the cultural appropriation of the history of the Nizari State. So Alamut blowing up with the last vestiges of that version of the clan can only be a good thing.<br /> <br /> On top of that, Ur-Shulgi is like 5 times Samuel Haight in character absurdity. It should have never been and the setting will be better if he's excised from existence by whatever Paradox Realm is engulfing the castle. Killing [Ravnos] only cost so much effort because Ur-Shulgi wasn't there to fart it out of reality, he's just too lazy to outright win the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the original clans were simplistic stereotypes and often offensive ones. Just think of the way the Giovanni were (actually are, to this day) presented, a family of italian american necromancers who &quot;love&quot; their family in incestuous ways and are basically meant to represent italian/americans as mafia stereotypes (in the clumsiest of ways). Or think of the Ravnos/Gypsys issue. In this regard the original Assamites were NOT as bad as many of the others. Yes, they were meant to represent the Nizari Isma'ili sect and the State founded by Hassan-i Sabbah and it was done in the usual clumsy way (&quot;these are Vampire assassins!&quot;) but they at least had redeeming qualities, for example their original version stressed their respect for mortals and them acting as defenders of humans as opposed to the depredations of the get of Caine (this was later toned down, because as a setting V:tM assumes that &quot;good vampires&quot; do not really exist).<br /> <br /> As for Ur-Shulgi, you are clearly exaggerating. In Revised he was introduced as an extremely powerful 4th gen vampire but he does nothing even remotely comparable to what a just awakened and starved Ravnos does in the Week of Nightmares. V20 expands Ur-Shulgi story hinting that he might be the original Shaitan a <i>widderslainte</i> turned vampire by Haqim to lure all the Baali together so they could be dealt with, it's also implied that Al-Asharad could have broken the Tremere curse himself if he so wanted but decided against it, finding the price to do so too onerous as the ritual to break the curse required the killing of several Assamite elders. When awakened Ur-Shulgi simply had no such qualms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 09-26-2021, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T08:08:00-07:00","id":1461554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461550#post1461550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the original clans were simplistic stereotypes and often offensive ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the original <i>independent clans</i>, yes. So what? I have to like one instance of racism because it wasn't the worst one?<br /> <br /> I want better depictions for Giovanni, Setites and Ravnos, too. And the Banu Haqim already got a better treatment, the ones in Alamut are the simplistic AND boring ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461550#post1461550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Ur-Shulgi, you are clearly exaggerating. In Revised he was introduced as an extremely powerful 4th gen vampire but he does nothing even remotely comparable to what a just awakened and starved Ravnos does in the Week of Nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that the Week of Nightmares is itself full of absurd feats and the Masquerade won't ever fall because Plot Armor doesn't change that Ur-Shulgi is both poorly devised as character and powerful beyond good storytelling.<br /> <br /> Currently WoD's Alamut contains the main force of a bad stereotype and a lame Dark Sue. And I want both to go to editorial Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T08:51:46-07:00","id":1461558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461418#post1461418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, phrasings like <i>&quot;Ultimately, Sabbat vampires don\u2019t have a choice in many of the actions they take. In giving themselves to the Beast, they\u2019ve set aside that central riddle of the Kindred condition.&quot;</i> don't give the impression that the authors think a deprogramming is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the question is not &quot;Can they be rehabilitated?&quot; but &quot;Why bother?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Anarchs are Camarilla are often sociopaths, and they are facing the psychopaths of the Sabbat. Why should they bother with trying to help the dangerously cruel and violent members of an enemy sect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T09:35:01-07:00","id":1461563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461558#post1461558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe the question is not &quot;Can they be rehabilitated?&quot; but &quot;Why bother?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Anarchs are Camarilla are often sociopaths, and they are facing the psychopaths of the Sabbat. Why should they bother with trying to help the dangerously cruel and violent members of an enemy sect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they fear their own beasts. If we can redeem <b>them</b>, then there is hope for <b>me</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T10:41:07-07:00","id":1461571,"title":"","content":"Frankly I'd be more worried about the Sabbat 'redeeming' others since they were 'right' about everything, have a coherent ideology, are unified in a way other sects armt and he paths don't have any of the drawbacks humanity has in v5.<br /> <br /> &quot;Shed all that hypocritical angst and live the best you, its not like you're actually helping or protecting any kine with it anyway.&quot; <br /> <br /> Lol I just realised the v5 soft reboot has already hit the issue the game had in 93. The Sabbat is still way better designed as a vampiric group than the anarchs and are genrally more interesting. I look forward to 2031 Sabbat Revised revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-26-2021, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T11:08:42-07:00","id":1461577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461571#post1461571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly I'd be more worried about the Sabbat 'redeeming' others since they were 'right' about everything, have a coherent ideology, are unified in a way other sects armt and he paths don't have any of the drawbacks humanity has in v5.<br /> <br /> Shed all that hypocritical angst and live the best you<br /> <br /> Lol I just realised the v5 soft reboot has already hit the issue the game had in 93. The Sabbat is still way better designed as a vampiric group than the anarchs and are genrally more interesting. I look forward to 2031 Sabbat Revised revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see:<br /> <br /> 1. Live as part of the decadent Illuminati.<br /> <br /> 2. Live wild and free as party animals and gang members.<br /> <br /> 3. Be a suicidal death cultist worshiping the First Murderer.<br /> <br /> Decisions, decisions.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think the biggest benefit, though, is finally the Anarchs and the Sabbat feel completely distinct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T11:30:56-07:00","id":1461581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461571#post1461571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly I'd be more worried about the Sabbat 'redeeming' others since they were 'right' about everything, have a coherent ideology, are unified in a way other sects armt and he paths don't have any of the drawbacks humanity has in v5.<br /> <br /> &quot;Shed all that hypocritical angst and live the best you, its not like you're actually helping or protecting any kine with it anyway.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Trying to cling to the mindset of a different species is a doomed effort that leads to becoming a wight. All humanity following vampires are baffling imbeciles who need to be put down for the good of the vampire species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 09-26-2021, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T11:38:01-07:00","id":1461582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461577#post1461577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2. Live wild and free as party animals and gang members.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>2) slowly fall to the Beast as you crumble under the weight of your own hypocrisy and your hyper violent lifestyle or bend the knee to the ivory tower because you have no long term plan and your now old enough to abuse rather than be abused....because after all that's what you did with the kine anyway as you realize you were never free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-26-2021, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T11:54:34-07:00","id":1461585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461558#post1461558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Anarchs are Camarilla are often sociopaths, and they are facing the psychopaths of the Sabbat. Why should they bother with trying to help the dangerously cruel and violent members of an enemy sect?</div> </div> </div> </div>That wasn't the point, it wasn't an analysis of what the other sociopaths should do, it was an analysis of what the design decisions meant as such. Out of character, not in it (or, now that I learned and enjoy the terms, Doylist, not Watsonian).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461571#post1461571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly I'd be more worried about the Sabbat 'redeeming' others since they were 'right' about everything, have a coherent ideology, are unified in a way other sects armt and he paths don't have any of the drawbacks humanity has in v5.<br /> <br /> &quot;Shed all that hypocritical angst and live the best you, its not like you're actually helping or protecting any kine with it anyway.&quot;<br /> <br /> Lol I just realised the v5 soft reboot has already hit the issue the game had in 93. The Sabbat is still way better designed as a vampiric group than the anarchs and are genrally more interesting. I look forward to 2031 Sabbat Revised revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wait, you'll see. We'll have a decent Anarch write-up in the 50th Anniversary Edition.<br /> <br /> <i>PS.: I just realized that this is really a possibility and it scares and amuses me in equal amounts.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T13:38:25-07:00","id":1461605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461582#post1461582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2) slowly fall to the Beast as you crumble under the weight of your own hypocrisy and your hyper violent lifestyle or bend the knee to the ivory tower because you have no long term plan and your now old enough to abuse rather than be abused....because after all that's what you did with the kine anyway as you realize you were never free.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you're going eat a baby either way, at least be the guy who doesn't think it's a virtue.<br /> <br /> The problem with Paths is you aren't really AVOIDING falling to the beast. You're just sticking yourself halfway to wassail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T13:54:57-07:00","id":1461608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461605#post1461605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, if you're going eat a baby either way, at least be the guy who doesn't think it's a virtue.<br /> <br /> The problem with Paths is you aren't really AVOIDING falling to the beast. You're just sticking yourself halfway to wassail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your shame achieves nothing if anything you drag further people down with your tethers to kine, furthermore you just make the other vampires miserable as well<br /> <br /> That's all any vampire does unless you achieve you opt out the great jihad. The average humanity follower degenerates into a mass murdering scumbag in the long run. A path member still struggles with the Beast, they just establish meaningful boundaries relevant to an eternity of blood and horror. The correct move if you want to maintain humanity is to opt out of the great game, something which will NEVER happen in the anarchs.<br /> <br /> Edit-on reflection anarchs should bring back path of etelechy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-26-2021, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T14:11:29-07:00","id":1461610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461605#post1461605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if you're going eat a baby either way, at least be the guy who doesn't think it's a virtue.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, and this is a serious question because it does really relate to how practical Humanity is vs. Paths in V5, why?<br /> <br /> How is it better to kill a child when you fully believe that you're committing an evil act that has no justification, compared to killing a child that you know other people will view as a horrible act but you believe you're on firm ethical grounds to do?<br /> <br /> If you take this out of the fiction of vampires, doing evil you know is evil is, in most philosophic system, is worse than doing something other people consider evil but you believe is not evil. For all the comparisons to fanatical terrorists regarding the Sabbat, you're effectively comparing the Anarchs to serial killers.<br /> <br /> How is it better for fending off the Beast to be Jeffrey Dahmer instead of a Daesh militant? Because that's effectively the claim you're making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T14:26:13-07:00","id":1461614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461610#post1461610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it better for fending off the Beast to be Jeffrey Dahmer instead of a Daesh militant? Because that's effectively the claim you're making.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume at the very basic that vampires who fight their evil but fail are objectively better than those who revel in it.<br /> <br /> The book does a good job of differentiating the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T17:06:25-07:00","id":1461626,"title":"","content":"But you're saying the Anarchs are the Sect of those that revel as they live wild, party, and do crime. The Sabbat don't revel in being evil, they revel in being inhuman; because factually they aren't human anymore. <br /> <br /> That's part of the problem that has been brought up already around how people treat fanatics. Fanatics don't think they're the evil ones, they think they're the ones that are right even if it means doing things that wouldn't be acceptable in less &quot;dire&quot; circumstances. The Sabbat can't be a death cult and vampires that only exist to revel in evil. That's not how cults work. A death cult is there to program you into thinking dying for the cause is morally good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T17:32:43-07:00","id":1461629,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is the sheer nastiness of the other sects and kindred in general in v5 is so severe that its hard to really come down that hard on the Sabbat. You can argue their outlook and attitudes are worse in intent but is their really that much difference with the relentlessly violent anarchs or the pointlessly cruel carmarilla? I mean your victims are still just as dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T17:35:46-07:00","id":1461630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461626#post1461626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat can't be a death cult and vampires that only exist to revel in evil. That's not how cults work. A death cult is there to program you into thinking dying for the cause is morally good.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's a big part of what the Paths always were. On a <i>mechanical</i> level they're there to anchor your Humanity by calling it another name and giving other sins. But on a <i>storytelling</i> level they do a lot of other things. They relay the notion that fanatics have a system, aren't just evil for the sake of evil. They are strict codes of conduct. They show what final goal the believer seeks that justifies their actions. They make the mindset of those monsters relatable. And they don't weaken the role of Humanity in the game, but reinforce it by contrast, showing at the same time what it means to abandon Humanity and that anyone staving off the Beast is still humane in some fundamental way.<br /> <br /> Giving deep cultural descriptions to the Paths is nice, but removing the rules weakens all those storytelling roles, a lot. It is outright saying that they're evil for evil's sake, something the Sabbat never was and isn't that interesting for an entire sect. Heck, it wasn't enough even for the Baali, even they got deeper than that because it is boring. By this move the Sabbat, <i>the game's representation of religious and political extremism</i>, lost nuance and turned into simplistic evil, not more, but simpler evil, their belief systems set aside as mere color for their actions, their lives meaningless, and by not being meant to ever be played, unrelatable. Non-persons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T17:52:44-07:00","id":1461632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461629#post1461629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem is the sheer nastiness of the other sects and kindred in general in v5 is so severe that its hard to really come down that hard on the Sabbat. You can argue their outlook and attitudes are worse in intent but is their really that much difference with the relentlessly violent anarchs or the pointlessly cruel carmarilla? I mean your victims are still just as dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? My take on the subject is while there's bad seeds and usually in charge, most of the vampires even among Elders refrain from killing for killings sake when they can. The Sabbat...does not.<br /> <br /> That by itself is a big difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461630#post1461630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's a big part of what the Paths always were. On a <i>mechanical</i> level they're there to anchor your Humanity by calling it another name and giving other sins. But on a <i>storytelling</i> level they do a lot of other things. They relay the notion that fanatics have a system, aren't just evil for the sake of evil. They are strict codes of conduct. They show what final goal the believer seeks that justifies their actions. They make the mindset of those monsters relatable. And they don't weaken the role of Humanity in the game, but reinforce it by contrast, showing at the same time what it means to abandon Humanity and that anyone staving off the Beast is still humane in some fundamental way.<br /> <br /> Giving deep cultural descriptions to the Paths is nice, but removing the rules weakens all those storytelling roles, a lot. It is outright saying that they're evil for evil's sake, something the Sabbat never was and isn't that interesting for an entire sect. Heck, it wasn't enough even for the Baali, even they got deeper than that because it is boring. By this move the Sabbat, <i>the game's representation of religious and political extremism</i>, lost nuance and turned into simplistic evil, not more, but simpler evil, their belief systems set aside as mere color for their actions, their lives meaningless, and by not being meant to ever be played, unrelatable. Non-persons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its emphasized in V5 but it was always there that the degeneration of Humanity is actually part of a larger cult breakdown process. It's meant to remove the independence of the Sabbat members and their ability to dwell among regular humanity so that they are isolated and more subceptible to the indoctrination of the Sword of Caine. Basically, if you're a vampire and they make you kill your family or other horrible atrocities then you have nowhere to turn to but the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> One thing the book does well is describing how the Sabbat break down its members' morality, personality, and identity. The Paths are things that are easier to believe that all Sabbat are following because this new version makes it clear they destroy the person they used to be. So much so that it comments under Lucita's write-up that the fact she goes by her original moral name is found to be WEIRD.<br /> <br /> Before I felt the Followers of Set were MUCH more believable in creating Path Followers than the Sabbat but now I totally believe it.<br /> <br /> The &quot;reveling in evil&quot; seems like it doesn't serve a purpose but it absolutely does in making you dependent on the Sabbat, isolated, and willing to do whatever you're told. The Paths are really a post-facto justification to force you into one of the sect's necessary roles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-26-2021, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T18:15:47-07:00","id":1461634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461632#post1461632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? My take on the subject is while there's bad seeds and usually in charge, most of the vampires even among Elders refrain from killing for killings sake when they can. The Sabbat...does not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you get the idea that the Sabbat kill for the sake of it? The Sabbat don't kill for the sake of killing. They kill for strongly defined philosophic reasons. They kill to prove their ideology is correct. The existence of Paths, even with V5's approach, is proof enough of that.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs, in V5, kill when they feel like it because they have no rules to say when killing a human is right or wrong; just their personal moral compass and the Beast.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat kill, or don't kill, based on the dictates of their Paths. The need to kill according to the dictates of their Path or lose to the Beast instead of just abandoning Humanity. They have <i>rules</i> they need to follow.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are the most purposeful in their kills because their ideology demands it, even as it also demands they be the most willing to kill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Before I felt the Followers of Set were MUCH more believabel in creating Path Followers than the Sabbat but now I totally believe it. </div> </div> </div>You don't seem to be appreciating how cult indoctrination works.<br /> <br /> The Revised Sabbat had it correct: most Sabbat were on Humanity because most Sabbat were still new to the Sect and still going through the indoctrination process. Paths represented a source of elevated status in the cult hierarchy. Managing to adopt a Path made you more elite in the cult than those still struggling with Humanity. Achieving a high bearing in your Path made you more elite. That is how the whole psychology of these things works. It's a multistage process where members progress into smaller and smaller circles of more social standing via more sacrifice of the self to the cult. You don't jump from normal person thinking the cult leader has some intriguing ideas, to an induction ceremony that teaches you all the secrets and expects you to act with complete dedication to the cause. You get drawn in via cycle of escalation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T18:22:02-07:00","id":1461635,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461632#post1461632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;reveling in evil&quot; seems like it doesn't serve a purpose but it absolutely does in making you dependent on the Sabbat, isolated, and willing to do whatever you're told. The Paths are really a post-facto justification to force you into one of the sect's necessary roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are talking about fundamentally different things. You're focused on how the book makes sense from the Watsonian perspective, how the descriptions fit the results they have in the characters' lives.<br /> <br /> But the problem I'm talking about is the Doylist perspective, what the book tells to the reader about those themes. What meaning the book as a book derives from the story it tells. Which experiences it proposes to the players, what themes it wants to explore. And how it connects to the outside world, because every story connects to real life in many ways, and Vampire was always meant to go far on this path (as arguable as its success and sensibility was)<br /> <br /> I can totally comprehend how the indoctrination presented in the book can create this horde of terrorists, there is no need to tell me. But what does it says to the reader about extremism as a phenomenon and the real people affected by it? It is in this point that I can't condone those decisions in the context of Vampire and the more I think about it or you demonstrate how thoroughly they are convinced that extremists aren't worth to think off as people anymore. the more I find it an abject treatment of a sensitive subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T18:22:04-07:00","id":1461636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461634#post1461634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where do you get the idea that the Sabbat kill for the sake of it? The Sabbat don't kill for the sake of killing. They kill for strongly defined philosophic reasons. They kill to prove their ideology is correct. The existence of Paths, even with V5's approach, is proof enough of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of those philosophical reasons is to show their absolute contempt for human beings and how their lives are valueless. The Sabbat have a philosophical belief that human life is worthless.<br /> <br /> Another reason is to play soccer with their heads.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Anarchs, in V5, kill when they feel like it because they have no rules to say when killing a human is right or wrong; just their personal moral compass and the Beast. </div> </div> </div>And some Anarchs absolutely believe in egalitarianism to the point of viewing keeping a ghoul as a form of slavery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Sabbat kill, or don't kill, based on the dictates of their Paths. The need to kill according to the dictates of their Path or lose to the Beast instead of just abandoning Humanity. They have <i>rules</i> they need to follow. </div> </div> </div>Yes, including a Path that demands you never hesitate to kill and you kill any vampire that shows an ounce of humanity (Death and Soul, Path of Caine).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Sabbat are the most purposeful in their kills because their ideology demands it, even as it also demands they be the most willing to kill. </div> </div> </div>Yes but their purpose is to show it every possible chace they can get. Sabbat ritae include killing for fun and in sadistic ways like hunting down humans for sport and killing them for food.<br /> <br /> The distinction is meaningless as they kill dozens of times more than other vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't seem to be appreciating how cult indoctrination works. </div> </div> </div>It's very similar how terrorists and cults both work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Revised Sabbat had it correct: most Sabbat were on Humanity because most Sabbat were still new to the Sect and still going through the indoctrination process. Paths represented a source of elevated status in the cult hierarchy. Managing to adopt a Path made you more elite in the cult than those still struggling with Humanity. Achieving a high bearing in your Path made you more elite. That is how the whole psychology of these things works. It's a multistage process where members progress into smaller and smaller circles of more social standing via more sacrifice of the self to the cult. You don't jump from normal person thinking the cult leader has some intriguing ideas, to an induction ceremony that teaches you all the secrets and expects you to act with complete dedication to the cause. You get drawn in via cycle of escalation. </div> </div> </div>Frankly, given the Beast and Blood Bond, I'm willing to believe it's much-much faster for vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T18:29:28-07:00","id":1461638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461635#post1461635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> We are talking about fundamentally different things. You're focused on how the book makes sense from the Watsonian perspective, how the descriptions fit the results they have in the characters' lives.<br /> <br /> But the problem I'm talking about is the Doylist perspective, what the book tells to the reader about those themes. What meaning the book as a book derives from the story it tells. Which experiences it proposes to the players, what themes it wants to explore. And how it connects to the outside world, because every story connects to real life in many ways, and Vampire was always meant to go far on this path (as arguable as its success and sensibility was)<br /> <br /> I can totally comprehend how the indoctrination presented in the book can create this horde of terrorists, there is no need to tell me. But what does it says to the reader about extremism as a phenomenon and the real people affected by it? It is in this point that I can't condone those decisions in the context of Vampire and the more I think about it or you demonstrate how thoroughly they are convinced that extremists aren't worth to think off as people anymore. the more I find it an abject treatment of a sensitive subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well, I feel like you the book is much-much needed and absolutely important from a Doylist perspective to snap down on a unfortunate tendency to paper over the dark side of subject matter. In Star Wars, there's still a huge chunk of the fandom who have the belief &quot;The Empire is right&quot; and a fandom for them. They demanded the material try to gloss over the xenophobia, bruality, and corruption of the Empire. In short, the attempt to &quot;nuance&quot; to the Empire unwittingly ended up endorsing fascism.<br /> <br /> I feel like the depiction of the Sabbat here is a nice wake up call that the actions the Sabbat take are repulsive, are terrible, and that there's not nearly as much &quot;cool&quot; or &quot;justified&quot; about them as perhaps some gamers think. People who think the Sabbat are somehow enlightened or transcending morality versus people who take advantage of the newly Embraced and destroy both them as well as converts.<br /> <br /> In that term, it is an objective good.<br /> <br /> Like Revised, I'm glad the book doesn't engage in apologia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T20:26:11-07:00","id":1461640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461636#post1461636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very similar how terrorists and cults both work.</div> </div> </div> </div>That the Sabbat is, arguably, more controlling than the Camarilla is interesting given the supposedly freedom fighters opposing the Cam. But the Sabbat exercise more thought controll through the paths than the Camarilla does. The Cam wants obedience. The Sabbat want your soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T22:31:07-07:00","id":1461642,"title":"","content":"Are we really arguing over the fact that Anarchs kill without meaning and are without ideology, whereas poor Sabbat has strict Paths that make for purposeful killings? <br /> <br /> To get on a Path you have to be on Humanity 3 -or lesser- in Revised. That meant you already were a barely functioning serial killer, that Humans found instinctively frightening. Paths gave you the strenght - literally - to stop worrying about doing things that would have made a serial killer degenerate! <br /> <br /> A life of street violence might bring you down to Humanity 5: to reach 4 , you have to be someone like the SS or Pol Pot soldiers. <br /> <br /> Discussing with a cultured Sabbat on a Path doesn't mean discussing with someone &quot;who is relatable&quot;, it basically means having a chat with Heinrich Himmler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T22:55:06-07:00","id":1461643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461629#post1461629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem is the sheer nastiness of the other sects and kindred in general in v5 is so severe that its hard to really come down that hard on the Sabbat. You can argue their outlook and attitudes are worse in intent but is their really that much difference with the relentlessly violent anarchs or the pointlessly cruel carmarilla? I mean your victims are still just as dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Camarilla institutional nastiness ranges from corrupt Western politicians to military dictators<br /> <br /> Anarch institutional nastiness ranges from gang violence to Cuba<br /> <br /> Sabbat institutional nastiness ranges from North Korea to Ted Bundy. <br /> <br /> They are not really the same levels of nastiness, and in no way cruel Camarilla or nasty Anarchs create similar levels of misery than those generated by a Sabbat bishopric. <br /> <br /> And this was already well established in VtM lore, since at least 1992. Nowhere Sabbat was ever presented as a moral equivalent to the Camarilla and the Anarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T23:12:33-07:00","id":1461644,"title":"","content":"There's actually a bit of fiction in this book that directly addresses it.<br /> <br /> Basically:<br /> <br /> &quot;How bad can the Sabbat be.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You don't get it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What do you mean? All vampires are vicious evil killers.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You really don't get it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What do you mean?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Dude, I've seen them feed. When they feed, they don't just leave a guy with a hangover and some missing time. They ripped apart the guy like a pack of animals. They did it for fun. They aren't like other vampires. As bad as they are, they are worse.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-27-2021, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T01:06:02-07:00","id":1461646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461638#post1461638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Revised, I'm glad the book doesn't engage in apologia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you want to mean that the books engage in apologia for abuse, sexual assault, gaslighting, murder, deceit, money laundering, corruption, conspiracy, etc, etc, since they give you rules for playing Camarilla and Anarchs, I find it dishonest to conflate the request of a sensible and playable approach to the subject with a demand to gloss over and apologia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461642#post1461642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Discussing with a cultured Sabbat on a Path doesn't mean discussing with someone &quot;who is relatable&quot;, it basically means having a chat with Heinrich Himmler.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis is not about saying that the Sabbat is less destructive or just as destructive. This is not about saying they're morally justifiable.<br /> <br /> It is about recognizing that, <u>as a game that explores the human psyche under pressure to do evil</u>, it isn't helping its cause by portraying some monsters as relatable and others not.<br /> <br /> Did you ever had a loved one in the clutches of a cult? Or know someone who had? Can you tell in those peoples' faces that their loved ones aren't relatable as people anymore, they're just evil minions to you now?<br /> <br /> Because my problem is to treat murderers and rapists as relatable people and terrorists as mere mindless minions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T01:27:05-07:00","id":1461648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461638#post1461638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very well, I feel like you the book is much-much needed and absolutely important from a Doylist perspective to snap down on a unfortunate tendency to paper over the dark side of subject matter. In Star Wars, there's still a huge chunk of the fandom who have the belief &quot;The Empire is right&quot; and a fandom for them. They demanded the material try to gloss over the xenophobia, bruality, and corruption of the Empire. In short, the attempt to &quot;nuance&quot; to the Empire unwittingly ended up endorsing fascism.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to be more an argument against the current depiction of the Camarilla than for the depiction of the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T01:38:40-07:00","id":1461649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461636#post1461636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1)One of those philosophical reasons is to show their absolute contempt for human beings and how their lives are valueless. The Sabbat have a philosophical belief that human life is worthless.<br /> <br /> Another reason is to play soccer with their heads.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2)And some Anarchs absolutely believe in egalitarianism to the point of viewing keeping a ghoul as a form of slavery.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 3)Yes, including a Path that demands you never hesitate to kill and you kill any vampire that shows an ounce of humanity (Death and Soul, Path of Caine).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 4)Yes but their purpose is to show it every possible chace they can get. Sabbat ritae include killing for fun and in sadistic ways like hunting down humans for sport and killing them for food.<br /> <br /> The distinction is meaningless as they kill dozens of times more than other vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 5)It's very similar how terrorists and cults both work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Frankly, given the Beast and Blood Bond, I'm willing to believe it's much-much faster for vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Mostly yes, some Paths have (or used to have) no regard for humans either way.<br /> <br /> 2) True.<br /> <br /> 3) Death and the Soul didn't used to require that, is that new?<br /> <br /> 4) Sabbat games differ in degree from Anarch games, not intent, it is competition, it is 'team building' it is a show of strength....<br /> <br /> 5) Which would be the point of the Sect and what they represent in the setting, Secular power is the Camarilla, Spiritual Power is the Sabbat, and Rebellion is the Anarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T01:59:37-07:00","id":1461652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461643#post1461643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Camarilla institutional nastiness ranges from corrupt Western politicians to military dictators<br /> <br /> Anarch institutional nastiness ranges from gang violence to Cuba<br /> <br /> Sabbat institutional nastiness ranges from North Korea to Ted Bundy.<br /> <br /> They are not really the same levels of nastiness, and in no way cruel Camarilla or nasty Anarchs create similar levels of misery than those generated by a Sabbat bishopric.<br /> <br /> And this was already well established in VtM lore, since at least 1992. Nowhere Sabbat was ever presented as a moral equivalent to the Camarilla and the Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prior to v5 this w<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">as </span></span></span>l<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"fon