:"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T01:59:56-07:00","id":1461653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461644#post1461644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's actually a bit of fiction in this book that directly addresses it.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, that's just in-character propaganda. That is literally how othering works to paper over the speaker's side's flaws by saying their enemy's flaws are so bad that there's no comparison.<br /> <br /> Why does any non-Sabbat vampire have a reason to be honest about the Sabbat? How do they even really know what's in the Sabbat's members heads instead of just relating a story colored by emotional shock? That's not a scholarly study of the Sabbat distilled into something easy to understand, it's just anti-Sabbat talking points to scare young vampires from giving a Sabbat recruiter the time of night.<br /> <br /> Again, this isn't about any sort of objective assessment of &quot;who's more evil.&quot; But from the subjective standpoint on the ground, compare how the average US rural citizen views the US government, and views the Taliban, to how the average rural Afghani views the US government, and views the Taliban. Because which facts matter change drastically based on where you live.<br /> <br /> The reason the US lost the war in Afghanistan can easily be boiled down to exactly what monteparnas is saying: losing track of the fact that the enemy is still made of up human beings with all the emotional complexities that goes with that.<br /> <br /> Having a chat with Himmler is actually important to do. Not because you need to both sides anything, but because if you ever want to stop the next Himmler, you have to understand what makes a guy like that tick. Brushing off your enemies - military, ideological, whatever - as monsters that you can't talk to and learn to see their perspective, is one of the most dangerous things to do if you actually want to beat your enemies. The ability to sit down and listen, to unravel what creates such horrible people, is one of the most valuable tools in such a conflict. History is replete with examples of large cultures with huge infrastructure and resources getting overconfident that power lets them get their way, and then losing to enemies that on paper shouldn't have stood a chance because those small weak cultures understood their enemies better.<br /> <br /> Both for our characters,and our own emotional edification when exploring ourselves through the role-play of monsters, putting ourselves in someone else's head is vital.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T02:13:14-07:00","id":1461654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461649#post1461649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Death and the Soul didn't used to require that, is that new?</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit complicated.<br /> <br /> V20 basically compressed Path of Bones and Path of Death and the Soul into the same thing.<br /> <br /> Bones does have &quot;Refusing to kill when the opportunity sets itself,&quot; as a sin. Where in the Revised Death and the Soul the sin is, &quot;Not killing when useful or necessary.&quot; However, Bones has, &quot;Making a decision based on emotion rather than logic,&quot; as a worse sin than refusing to kill, where Death and the Soul has acting on emotion as a significantly higher up sin on its chart.<br /> <br /> So V20 Death and the Soul as just Bones with a different name does include what CT said, but removes important context on the need for it to be a considered and logical action that furthers the character's study of death. In either case followers of the Path don't just kill every mortal they come across, they kill as part of their experimentation and observations whenever they can.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T02:23:25-07:00","id":1461655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461654#post1461654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A bit complicated.<br /> <br /> V20 basically compressed Path of Bones and Path of Death and the Soul into the same thing.<br /> <br /> Bones does have &quot;Refusing to kill when the opportunity sets itself,&quot; as a sin. Where in the Revised Death and the Soul the sin is, &quot;Not killing when useful or necessary.&quot; However, Bones has, &quot;Making a decision based on emotion rather than logic,&quot; as a worse sin than refusing to kill, where Death and the Soul has acting on emotion as a significantly higher up sin on its chart.<br /> <br /> So V20 Death and the Soul as just Bones with a different name does include what CT said, but removes important context on the need for it to be a considered and logical action that furthers the character's study of death. In either case followers of the Path don't just kill every mortal they come across, they kill as part of their experimentation and observations whenever they can.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Caine has/had a duty to Diablerise Humane vampires, Death and the Soul doesn't seem to regard them any more or less than anyone, or anything else...so not a specific kill command, which was my impression of CT was saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T02:27:04-07:00","id":1461656,"title":"","content":"The more I read the more I'm puzzled you gave it a 4.5. Don't you claim to like Sabbat?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T03:27:44-07:00","id":1461658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461655#post1461655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Caine has/had a duty to Diablerise Humane vampires, Death and the Soul doesn't seem to regard them any more or less than anyone, or anything else...so not a specific kill command, which was my impression of CT was saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah.<br /> <br /> I parsed CT as this, &quot;Yes, including a Path that demands you never hesitate to kill and you kill any vampire that shows an ounce of humanity (Death and Soul, Path of Caine).&quot; meant:<br /> <br /> &quot;Including the Path of Death and the Soul that demands you never hesitate to kill, and the Path of Caine that demands you kill any vampire that shows an ounce of humanity.&quot; rather than both Paths demanding both actions.<br /> <br /> Edit: though the Path of Caine bit is also hyperbolic. They have to take out vampires that embrace Humanity. They're supposed to guide vampires on Humanity to a Path if they can (obviously Path of Caine is their preference, but they're rather see you join a different Path than kill you for clinging to something you aren't anymore).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 09-27-2021, 06:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T04:45:28-07:00","id":1461662,"title":"","content":"I've skim-read the book now. It's basically what everyone who liked the Sabbat was worried it would be. If you liked Revised Guide to the Sabbat, stick to that. If you want the Sabbat as bogeymen, pick up this book instead. <br /> <br /> It feels very much like a GM-focussed guide on how to make VTM orcs, to borrow someone else's analogy upthread. If you want to kill shady NPCs without remorse (ironically), this is the book that shows you how. This Sabbat has no redeeming qualities and behaves with a high level of stupidity.<br /> <br /> Besides the Discipline powers, which are quite cool, I don't think there's much of value to those who want to actually play Sabbat characters. The Path descriptions lose a tonne of nuance, making them barely recognisable, and all the Clans and Bloodlines have basically been relegated to one catch-all 'antitribu' because the Sabbat fully reject their heritage now.<br /> <br /> So if you want to play Sabbat characters, you can probably save yourself $40 (and all the aggro with international shipping if you're outside the US). The layout is better than the core, though, and there's marginally more useful info than the Anarchs book (the content is more valuable on average but there's less of it).<br /> <br /> All in all, I'd give it a 2/5, which is generous. It would be 1.5/5 if I were being uncharitable, and that's solely for the layout and Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 09-27-2021, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T05:00:32-07:00","id":1461664,"title":"","content":"^ Now that's a review I can trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T06:29:33-07:00","id":1461672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461662#post1461662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've skim-read the book now. It's basically what everyone who liked the Sabbat was worried it would be. If you liked Revised Guide to the Sabbat, stick to that. If you want the Sabbat as bogeymen, pick up this book instead. <br /> <br /> It feels very much like a GM-focussed guide on how to make VTM orcs, to borrow someone else's analogy upthread. If you want to kill shady NPCs without remorse (ironically), this is the book that shows you how. This Sabbat has no redeeming qualities and behaves with a high level of stupidity.<br /> <br /> Besides the Discipline powers, which are quite cool, I don't think there's much of value to those who want to actually play Sabbat characters. The Path descriptions lose a tonne of nuance, making them barely recognisable, and all the Clans and Bloodlines have basically been relegated to one catch-all 'antitribu' because the Sabbat fully reject their heritage now.<br /> <br /> So if you want to play Sabbat characters, you can probably save yourself $40 (and all the aggro with international shipping if you're outside the US). The layout is better than the core, though, and there's marginally more useful info than the Anarchs book. <br /> <br /> All in all, I'd give it a 2/5, which is generous. It would be 1.5/5 if I were being uncharitable, and that's solely for the layout and Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>My toughts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T06:59:15-07:00","id":1461674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461656#post1461656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I read the more I'm puzzled you gave it a 4.5. Don't you claim to like Sabbat?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes,<br /> <br /> I absolutely loved that this book got into the focus on what I love most about the Sabbat in their culture. It talked extensively about how the Paths influence sect life and how the day-to-day Sabbat acted. One of the things I HATED about the previous books was the fact that the Sabbat were constantly soft-pedaled and made into &quot;Camarilla-Lite&quot; at the top and &quot;Anarch-Lite&quot; at the bottom when the Sabbat were people who needed to have their own unique culture.<br /> <br /> The best part of the book for me is the fact that we get into the nightly life of Sabbat on the Path of Cathari, what their havens look like, how they indoctrinate other Kindred, and discussion of what it means to be trapped inside the cult life. It's one of those things that make me just roll my eyes at the description of treating the Sabbat as &quot;orcs&quot; because the book finally starts addressing what has been seriously lacking in previous books.<br /> <br /> 1. How do Sabbat DIFFER from the other sects?<br /> 2. How does it FEEL to be a Sabbat.<br /> 3. What do Sabbat do on their nights?<br /> <br /> I have my complaints about the book but it is far less than the Camarilla and Anarch books that just seem to be edgy for the sake of edgy versus purposeful horror. Two books that lacked any real in-universe content and just meandered all over the place in weird directions (Why does the Camarilla book have Ashirra and Second Inquisition sections? What do Anarchs actually BELIEVE?). This is a massive-massive improvement.<br /> <br /> Justin Achilli did a fantastic job of managing to make sense of what had been an extremely weird and bizarre decision to put the Sabbat off to one side. He justified it in the Watsonian sense but also made the Sabbat decision make sense out of universe. The change form the Doyleist perspective was, &quot;How do we make the Sabbat significantly different from the Anarchs and Camairlla?&quot; That has always been a struggle and now they have a far more distinct identity with the role of Anti-Clans and Paths replacing the previous Camarilla lite qualities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T07:11:44-07:00","id":1461675,"title":"","content":"I now heared that the Camarilla and Anarch books are edgy quite often. I found them incoherent, but edgy wasn't on my mind when reading them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T07:11:45-07:00","id":1461676,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a><br /> <br /> <b>My own Sabbat campaign</b><br /> <br /> I should note that part of my feelings toward this book are going to be influenced by my own Sabbat campaign where the question of &quot;What is the nature of the Sabbat?&quot; has been a question for roughly 20 years of gaming with my Sabbat PCs. My two favorite Sabbat player characters were a Tzimisce Elder who was one of the original Anarchs (Transylvania Chronicles) and a Serpent of Light Elder. I also enjoyed playing a Salubri Antitribu Templar.<br /> <br /> One of the constant undercurrents of the Sabbat in my games was the struggle between the Sabbat who were genuinely of the Paths of Enlightenment's &quot;higher&quot; levels (those who understand it was to become posthuman alternatively amoral ubermensch) vs. those who only had a cursory Beast-driven understanding of the tenets. In simpler terms, <b>2nd Edition Sabbat vs. Revised</b> with the former being admirable noble demons in their own way and the Revised Sabbat representing the nasty mindless monsters. It was an idea the Sabbat were failing as a sect and had become obsessed with killing and territory over their original goals.<br /> <br /> I also really emphasized the role of <b>Infernalism</b> in the Sabbat as I've always enjoyed the idea that the Sabbat philosophically set themselves against God (even if many are atheists) and have a strong contingent of those who make pacts with demons or are corrupted by the Baali's teachings. In part because the Inquisition can't coherently make a statement as to why they shoudn't do this beyond, &quot;demons bad.&quot; I've had many demon hunter Sabbat in my ganes and they're the best time to have Camarilla/Anarch and Sabbat team up.<br /> <br /> This book definitely feels like it could be an updated metaplot to my own games. It provides a coherent path of Point A to Point B that the &quot;Bestial&quot; Sabbat have won the war against the former. The Sabbat have failed as a sect and now there's a bunch of Kindred, alien and otherwise, being forced to flee the sinking ship. <u>Failure is not a bad thing when roleplaying vampire, though</u><b>.</b> The Transylvania Chronicles makes the fact you are unable to &quot;win&quot; the Anarch Revolt a major part of the storyline.<br /> <br /> <b>My current Sabbat campaign inspired by this game</b><br /> <br /> The roleplaying opportunities of this are tremendous and I've already started a new MIAMI BY NIGHT campaign this week with already a few sessions underway. The premise is that a pair of Lasombra women have been trapped in the Underworld for the past two decades and they emerge in Miami, Florida only to find that the Second Inquisition have purged the city and the Sabbat that have survived are a bunch of suicidal nutjobs. Furthermore, that the time in the Abyss has caused them to lose hold of their Paths somehow. It will become a question of what a Sabbat means and how they will adapt to this new world.<br /> <br /> This book is very helpful to that.<br /> <br /> I think their goal I will &quot;nudge&quot; them to will be to join the Church of Caine and Anarchs to form a New Sabbat out of the ashes of the old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-27-2021, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T07:13:52-07:00","id":1461677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461675#post1461675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I now heared that the Camarilla and Anarch books are edgy quite often. I found them incoherent, but edgy wasn't on my mind when reading them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anarch was more needlessly edgelord. Camarilla was more, &quot;Let's talk about everything but the actual Camarilla.&quot;<br /> <br /> I liked sections of the latter.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member