its enemies.<br /> <br /> 4. That is, those &quot;guiding&quot; the Sabbat (as it were) know EXACTLY what they're doing with it. (Although, for Storytellers, there doesn't necessarily need to be an elder mastermind in every chronicle. Some and perhaps most domains just end up in the path of destruction.)<br /> <br /> 5. The big change between editions is that Sabbat sect structure no longer exists in mockery of the Camarilla, as it did in certain legacy editions (VRev/ V20). That's why the book opens with Vykos admonishing the assembled leaders &quot;the way we did things doesn't hold up anymore.&quot;<br /> <br /> 6. Straight up, the Sabbat has been WRECKED, crushed between Second Inquisition and Gehenna War. It's eviscerated sect ranks, putting them on the succeed-or-die-trying trajectory. They exist to provoke, and to show the costs of taking the blood-and-fire approach to problem solving.<br /> <br /> 7. The Sabbat book in particular takes this &quot;what's happening NOW?&quot; approach to using them. You can use the legacy-edition materials to help give context, but if you're running a V5 chronicle, you don't need to use that info, and you can plug-and-play introduce them to a chronicle.<br /> <br /> 8. Insofar as &quot;the entire sect&quot; equals actually any one thing, probably. &quot;The entire sect&quot; includes everything from holdout domains still observing the rites of the past to the 12-strong pack of Vaulderie-bound blood-maniacs not knowing there's anyone other than them doing it.<br /> <br /> 9. There's absolutely nothing wrong with playing an edition you prefer. Dance with the one who brung ya, if that's what gives you the most enjoyment!<br /> <br /> 10. Did you get the Companion? It's free and covers the Tzimisce. I'm sure there are individuals of &quot;Pander lineage&quot; out there, but the Sabbat doesn't afford clan much significance as of V5... and there were probably a lot of Panders-descended Cainites thrown into the breach already.<br /> <br /> 11. Indeed. And the (non-fledgling) Tzimisce have returned to not giving a shit about larger vampire politics as the usefulness of the Sabbat has eroded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the information, that helps to contextualize.<br /> <br /> But unfortunately it seems by those answers, and especially by #6 that all my assumptions weren't just right, but it was indeed by design.<br /> <br /> It is a dumber Sabbat, made dumber for the purpose of showing that acting dumb gets you killed.<br /> <br /> Orcs never were that imbecile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T23:08:46-07:00","id":1461920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461896#post1461896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>No one said that.</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's interesting that no one said that. Apart from praise towards the Art and layout of the book, you seem to be the only person saying positive things about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T23:53:56-07:00","id":1461921,"title":"","content":"Please don't comment on red text.<br /> <br /> And the book has a lot of positive feedback on Reddit and other sites. Just generally, the primary complaint seems to be, &quot;No, it is absolutely 100% not for Sabbat play.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is something I agree is stupid.<br /> <br /> The secondary complaint is one that I keep bringing up, &quot;The book is way too short.&quot;<br /> <br /> The third complaint is it's way too expensive for its size.<br /> <br /> Which I also agree with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T23:56:04-07:00","id":1461922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461921#post1461921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please don't comment on red text.<br /> <br /> And the book has a lot of positive feedback on Reddit and other sites. Just generally, the primary complaint seems to be, &quot;No, it is absolutely 100% not for Sabbat play.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is something I agree is stupid.<br /> <br /> The secondary complaint is one that I keep bringing up, &quot;The book is way too short.&quot;<br /> <br /> The third complaint is it's way too expensive for its size.<br /> <br /> Which I also agree with.</div> </div> </div> </div>but at the same time most of the praise for the book is &quot;i didn't like the sabbath and i'm glad they're gone&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T00:02:40-07:00","id":1461923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461922#post1461922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but at the same time most of the praise for the book is &quot;i didn't like the sabbath and i'm glad they're gone&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is ridiculous because they've been gone for most of the game line [sent off to the Middle East like that wasn't part of Earth] and they're finally back.<br /> <br /> And thank Caine for that.<br /> <br /> I suppose my love of the Sabbat is why I'm so positive about this book. The lack of a Sabbat book at the start of the game line was the worst thing about V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywo