3d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T04:29:22-07:00","id":1461938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">do we really need to make comparisons of liking V5 to liking warcrimes? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>you're right, war crimes aren't nearly as bad as V5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T05:32:03-07:00","id":1461943,"title":"","content":"Lol calm down everyone. Its just a book and we don't have to buy it. V20/revised is still a really good game.<br /> <br /> By an amusing coincidence in gearing up to a one of 40k roleplay orcs game on Saturday. All this description of sabbat as orcs has reminded me playing complete bastards is really fun. I'm looking forward to firing my crappy gun from the truck while yelling and bullying goblins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T07:52:35-07:00","id":1461955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, How can I trust that when most people still interested in picking up a V5 book... like V5. It's like hearing some nationalist military enthusiasts have possitive spins on war crimes. Or maybe, Vampire fans have been so tortured by bad books that the Sabbat book seems great (The Mandolorian effect?)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461938#post1461938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> you're right, war crimes aren't nearly as bad as V5</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You recall we don't allow edition warring, right?<br /> <br /> Dislike it all you want. V20 and V5 are both lines produced by OPP and random bashing is not tolerated for either.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-29-2021, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T08:31:36-07:00","id":1461957,"title":"","content":"I will say that what this book does positively can be summarized as bullet points:<br /> <br /> 1. The fact is that the Sabbat have been absent from the gameline for the better part of a few years and this has been a massive loss to the setting. They're an integral part of the setting like the Camarilla and Anarchs. Their return is an automatic win and I'm glad we've finally got them back to be used.<br /> <br /> 2. The fact that Paths are once more canonized is something that manages to at least fill the hole that certain players had a serious issue with. While Humanity in V5 is far more flexible, some players flat out have no ability to deal with it and the Touchstone rules preclude certain archetypes. Diablerists and mass Embraces for example.<br /> <br /> 3. I do like the write-ups for the Paths that we've gotten and the larger focus on them that the Sabbat has given them before. One of the failures of previous Editions is that it doesn't give nearly as much insight into how Paths interact as it does here.<br /> <br /> 4. The Sabbat now have a far more distinctive identity from the Anachs and the Camarilla with the &quot;Dark Reflections&quot; thing having always made it a bit questionable what the real difference was. It always was somewhere in the Middle just meaner and that made it seem like the sect wasn't as unique as it could be.<br /> <br /> 5. I really am intrigued by the &quot;Clan is meaningless&quot; matter that is a rejection of the Camarilla's super-focus on lineage and their Clan cultures. This was always a tendency and seeing that the Tzimisce and Lasombra did NOT destroy their Antediluvians, it's understandable why it would no longer be as important. Certainly Antitribu no longer is a joke for cannon fodder of the Tzimisce and Lasombra.<br /> <br /> 6. A lot of light retcons that fix what had been problems of the Edition so far like the Gehenna War going off to the Middle East and other matters. The Sabbat now look like they weren't all jumping down the gullets of the Ancients but inflicting serious damage.<br /> <br /> 7. I like the depiction of the Sabbat as simultaneously far more savage but far more united. This is not a Sabbat on the verge of Civil War but united under one cause and Blood Bound to one another properly.<br /> <br /> 8. All the implied defections to the Anarchs and Camarilla making the two sects more Sabbat-like now makes more sense with the mainstream's Sabbat's change. It means that there's a larger Sabbat story with the Church of Caine, Harbingers of Skulls, and other groups.<br /> <br /> 9. Nicely gross and evil occultism with the Disciplines and &quot;mass Embrace of zombie Thin Bloods&quot; stuff.<br /> <br /> 10. Vykos and Lucita are still there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T08:42:42-07:00","id":1461959,"title":"","content":"Its great Justin gave some insight to why he wrote what he did. Here's my issue for it. It sounds like a story that someone could explore and run as their tabelcanon, not something you should probably do for the product you are looking to sell and make money off of as a business. TTRPG already don't make a lot of money. They just don't. And top tier is Wizards of the Coast. White Wolf used to be number 2 in the industry. Now...no idea. But my point is you have kind of a niche product. Why would you want to alienate an already small customer base and say &quot;hey you can keep using your favorite edition!&quot; Like ya...I know that. I am here as a consumer saying I want to give you money, but your telling me money isn't welcome here. Because its not the way we want you to play the game anymore and doesn't fit in with our vision. <br /> <br /> That's silly to me. Alienating old consumers saying, buy our old stuff the new isn't for you! Is saying we don't want your money. Your product should be inclusive to your established consumer base, not exclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T08:53:58-07:00","id":1461963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461959#post1461959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its great Justin gave some insight to why he wrote what he did. Here's my issue for it. It sounds like a story that someone could explore and run as their tabelcanon, not something you should probably do for the product you are looking to sell and make money off of as a business. TTRPG already don't make a lot of money. They just don't. And top tier is Wizards of the Coast. White Wolf used to be number 2 in the industry. Now...no idea. But my point is you have kind of a niche product. Why would you want to alienate an already small customer base and say &quot;hey you can keep using your favorite edition!&quot; Like ya...I know that. I am here as a consumer saying I want to give you money, but your telling me money isn't welcome here. Because its not the way we want you to play the game anymore and doesn't fit in with our vision.<br /> <br /> That's silly to me. Alienating old consumers saying, buy our old stuff the new isn't for you! Is saying we don't want your money. Your product should be inclusive to your established consumer base, not exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that Justin probably would have written whatever they wanted him to and wrote the product they wanted. Which is to establish the Sabbat Bible for spinoffs like the upcoming TV shows and video games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divide