--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461920#post1461920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's interesting that no one said that. Apart from praise towards the Art and layout of the book, you seem to be the only person saying positive things about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have seen the preview and the reviews of the book, and the discussions. And I find myself agreeing with CTPhipps. I am only slow the buy the book because it is expensive and I don't see myself running a VtM for a year or more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T13:39:09-07:00","id":1462002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461988#post1461988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I think the point is wouldn't it be nice in a world where both could exist and be enjoyed? Cast a wide net, not a small net.</div> </div> </div> </div>In an very meaningful sense, they do coexist. You can go buy any V20 product from DTRPG right now, in digital or print.<br /> <br /> V20 is also a fairly complete edition. There's very little that feels &quot;missing,&quot; and a lot of that is just unexplored plot hooks rather than not having updates to specific groups or the like (esp. not in the V20 model of being an omnibus focused edition).<br /> <br /> There's a reason Onyx Path was pitching a new edition of VtM of their own after all.<br /> <br /> I just really hope that the Paradox folks don't let anyone try the &quot;just use X20!&quot; for the other game lines though, because there's a huge amount of books that aren't getting made for them to bring them on par with how much V20 covered. W20 is going to end without something as basic as a Litany of the Tribes 20th to compliment Lore of the Clans as an update to Tribebook stuff that didn't make it into W20 core. M20 is going to continue getting &quot;stuff Brucato wants to do,&quot; instead of a bunch of bread and butter stuff (like a Guide to the Traditions 20th to compliment Technocracy Reloaded, and a book to expand on the Disparate Alliance as a brand new faction that doesn't have old material to fill in the gaps on to help expand them to be equals to the Traditions and Technocracy). Etc. And of course all the games that don't even have 20th core books at all.<br /> <br /> Paradox isn't inherently wrong to make choices that alienate some fans. That always happens with new editions; even if a lot of us can point to dozens of things that would have made us happier with V5 and wouldn't subtract from V5's new direction. But I'm very worried that they don't appreciate the vitriol they're risking with these attitudes once they get away from VtM.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T15:49:36-07:00","id":1462030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462002#post1462002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brucato wants to do,&amp;quot; instead of a bunch of bread and butter stuff (like a Guide to the Traditions 20th to compliment Technocracy Reloaded, and a book to expand on the Disparate Alliance as a brand new faction that doesn't have old material to fill in the gaps on to help expand them to be equals to the Traditions and Technocracy). Etc. And of course all the games that don't even have 20th core books at all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> Oddly one of my primary fears about the next mage edition is that the disparate alliance will be pushed at the expense of the union and the Traditions. Which I'll conceed is stupid but speaks to my sense of....distrust from recent decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar"