text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T16:00:01-07:00","id":1462034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461999#post1461999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I think m</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">arvel </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">and dc </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">are h</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">aving simular issue from wh</span></span></span>at you're suggesting might occur <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">with the comics were no ones buying them. I'm unsure how that will be </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">an issue with tho</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">se excessive numbers of movies but It seems </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">an problem somehow.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Running a business is tricky, even if you have a good revenue elsewhere you can't just throw money at things without justification. The success of an arm of the company can't be used to justify others not bringing numbers. There are several reasons, but many can be boiled down to a simple statement: an organization never have enough money. The more you grow, the more you have projects that have costs, and you're all the time making choices about how to allocate resources. And to the general public the company is just a rich monolith, but inside each project and arm is a complex network of interests and stakeholders, going from big investors to workers that need to justify their jobs.<br /> <br /> Of course, you can do that in several ways. Currently WotC's main strategy is the crossing over of D&amp;D and MtG, so they're willing to suffer a lesser revenue in D&amp;D as long as it drives up Magic's sales (that make a helluva lot of money). That way D&amp;D does bring revenue anyway, it just isn't direct. But as I see the current Marvel's strategy do not have a transfer point where comics sales help movie sales, and the comics are declining. I seriously think the webcomic format is the future, to be honest, but changing format on your core business is another big challenge.<br /> <br /> Paradox is a games company first AFAIK. The WoD IP is a business asset, but the TTRPG isn't their core business anyway. To anyone that thinks it to be unfair I point first to the fact that without them there would not be a 5th edition in any way or form, and I do think it is a good development in itself. But it doesn't mean that their decisions for the setting are all the best for their purposes. To be sincere I think it have more to do with a specific vision for the setting than with it being more or less welcoming for games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T16:08:26-07:00","id":1462035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462034#post1462034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox is a games company first AFAIK. The WoD IP is a business asset, but the TTRPG isn't their core business anyway. To anyone that thinks it to be unfair I point first to the fact that without them there would not be a 5th edition in any way or form, and I do think it is a good development in itself. But it doesn't mean that their decisions for the setting are all the best for their purposes. To be sincere I think it have more to do with a specific vision for the setting than with it being more or less welcoming for games.</div> </div> </div> </div>A reminder again that they've also got their show and movie IP deal done. They've got what they want and will have the same with their video games too...eventually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://variety.com/2021/film/news/world-of-darkness-eric-heisserer-christine-boyland-vampire-werewolf-1234961512/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://variety.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/World-of-Darkness.jpg?w=1000&amp;h=562&amp;crop=1\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://variety.com/2021/film/news/world-of-darkness-eric-heisserer-christine-boyland-vampire-werewolf-1234961512/\" target=\"_blank\"> &lsquo;World of Darkness&rsquo; Universe Coming to TV, Film With Eric Heisserer, Christine Boylan, &lsquo;The Witcher&rsquo;s&rsquo; Hivemind </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://variety.com/2021/film/news/world-of-darkness-eric-heisserer-christine-boyland-vampire-werewolf-1234961512/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://variety.com/2021/film/news/world-of-darkness-eric-heisserer-christine-boyland-vampire-werewolf-1234961512/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Eric Heisserer (\"Shadow and Bone\"), Christine Boylan (\"The Punisher\") and Hivemind are developing World of Darkness' universe for film, TV. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So V5 has achieved its goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T16:22:20-07:00","id":1462038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462035#post1462035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So V5 has achieved its goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too soon to say for sure. This is certainly a victory for them (not necessarily for V5, but it IS a victory for them regardless), but we don't have proof of consistency yet. Let's have the first shows and games roll up and see how it unfolds. And how much V5 affects it positively or negatively, which is another question entirely. This is a business model, not a single project, so we have to wait and see the markets' response and the strategy's replicability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T16:27:22-07:00","id":1462039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462038#post1462038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too soon to say for sure. This is certainly a victory for them (not necessarily for V5, but it IS a victory for them regardless), but we don't have proof of consistency yet. Let's have the first shows and games roll up and see how it unfolds. And how much V5 affects it positively or negatively, which is another question entirely. This is a business model, not a single project, so we have to wait and see the markets' response and the strategy's replicability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps but they also won Origins awards and did a campaign of international sales that has done well. In simple terms, the casual fan likes it and they're the only people who matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T16:30:12-07:00","id":1462040,"title":"","content":"I asked Justin Achilli these questions:<br /> <br /> <b>Couple of questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Will we ever find out if Lucita is truly dead or alive?<br /> <br /> 2. Is the Salubri Antitribu still a thing or was their &quot;avenging their Clan&quot; always a failure in the making?</b><br /> <br /> <i>Answers:<br /> <br /> 1) Sounds like a story perhaps worth telling.<br /> <br /> 2) I honestly don't think they were well-equipped to pursue the vengeance they wanted.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T17:30:35-07:00","id":1462048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462039#post1462039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps but they also won Origins awards and did a campaign of international sales that has done well.</div> </div> </div> </div>How much does winning an industry award actually matter? Have you ever actually seen someone say, &quot;I wasn't really considering playing X, but it one an Origin Award so now I've got to see what the hype is.&quot; or any other sort of statement that the people that actually spend money on these things look to the Origin Awards (or any similar awards) as what guides their decision making?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In simple terms, the casual fan likes it and they're the only people who matter. </div> </div> </div>In what business model?<br /> <br /> That's not how pretty much any niche market works. &quot;Casual fans like it,&quot; is great for selling the core book, but it's not how you build repeat customers that keep buying supplements, and that will follow you to other media. That's what hardcore fans do. If the job of V5 is to kick off a brand that people invest in, they need to either keep existing hardcore fans, or generate new one. Casual fans will move on (at least as customers, they might keep playing V5 but they'll stop buying WoD brand products) to the next thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T18:00:37-07:00","id":1462050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462048#post1462048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what business model?<br /> <br /> That's not how pretty much any niche market works. &quot;Casual fans like it,&quot; is great for selling the core book, but it's not how you build repeat customers that keep buying supplements, and that will follow you to other media. That's what hardcore fans do. If the job of V5 is to kick off a brand that people invest in, they need to either keep existing hardcore fans, or generate new one. Casual fans will move on (at least as customers, they might keep playing V5 but they'll stop buying WoD brand products) to the next thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the market that there's a lot more sales internationally than from the hardcore gamers and selling a far vaster amount than before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T18:32:11-07:00","id":1462052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462050#post1462050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the market that there's a lot more sales internationally than from the hardcore gamers and selling a far vaster amount than before.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should know by the make-up of this forum (that is quite niche by itself) that international sales aren't by any stretch the same as selling to casual fans. I'm a hardcore fan, like many here in Brazil. There are hardcore fans all around the world.<br /> <br /> But as I said, we have to wait and see. In simpler terms the books are dong well, that is unavoidable truth. Casual and hardcore here aren't really helpful definitions as each one will have distinct concepts of what they are. But <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> is right on one thing, even if the RPG isn't the main profit source, for a sustainable market it needs consistent new sales, which for books means mostly the same people buying new books.<br /> <br /> There are other aspects of it, too. They had a far more aggressive and invested marketing strategy, which is a plus, and are dealing in a far distinct environment, with, and this is true, a far more professional approach, something the RPG market in general lacked until the turn of the millennium. It is hard to pinpoint the effects of any particular variable in the current success because they're too many.<br /> <br /> Regardless, it is a success for now. But regardless again, we need time to say more on the matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462040#post1462040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Is the Salubri Antitribu still a thing or was their &quot;avenging their Clan&quot; always a failure in the making?[/B]<br /> <br /> 2) I honestly don't think they were well-equipped to pursue the vengeance they wanted.[/I]</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I never thought the Salubri Antitribu fitted the Sabbat. They were pretty much its opposite, trying to avenge their elders instead of slaying them. I've been waiting for the clan reunion for a long time and I personally don't care about Salubri-haters' opinions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T18:33:37-07:00","id":1462053,"title":"","content":"I didn't ask about how expanding an international sales and physical store presence push can boost sales if you have the resources to invest in it properly.<br /> <br /> Where's your sales data that shows that the success of V5 core is carrying over to continual large scale success for V5 supplements? Where's the evidence that it's translating to more revenue for other media projects?<br /> <br /> Increasing the scale doesn't change the basic economic principles at play. Gambling as an entertainment industry is orders of magnitude larger than RPGs. That doesn't mean only &quot;casual&quot; gamblers matter. Ever successful casino and so on needs a balance of casual players and big spenders. If you lose the casuals the big spenders go somewhere else because they still want the people as part of the experience. If you lose the big spenders, the casuals aren't spending enough to actually support the atmosphere that keeps the casual around and things go downhill financially.<br /> <br /> RPGs have a lot of similarities here. Most RPG players don't even buy anything (their GMs do), or maybe buy 1-2 books. More invested fans (esp. the GMs) spend a lot more which makes sure gaming groups have all the books they want to play with. You need both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T18:41:59-07:00","id":1462056,"title":"","content":"Fair point. It's also a pointless exercise as we don't know how Paradox measures success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-29-2021, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T19:08:42-07:00","id":1462060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462052#post1462052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I never thought the Salubri Antitribu fitted the Sabbat. They were pretty much its opposite, trying to avenge their elders instead of slaying them. I've been waiting for the clan reunion for a long time and I personally don't care about Salubri-haters' opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I quite liked them in an anti villain context. As a group in the Sabbat who are a little aloof from the sect since it privately sickens them but as proffesional soldiers an asset. It made an interesting contrast with the tremere being the villest clan in the carmarilla. As I've mentioned before on of favourite other players was a salubri who's distaste of the sect soured into outright hatred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T19:12:33-07:00","id":1462061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462060#post1462060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I quite liked them in an anti villain context. As a group in the Sabbat who are a little aloof from the sect since it privately sickens them but as proffesional soldiers an asset. It made an interesting contrast with the tremere being the villest clan in the carmarilla. As I've mentioned before on of favourite other players was a salubri who's distaste of the sect soured into outright hatred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm picturing the Path of Honorable Accord getting discredited because of a massive uprising of the Salubri Antritribu that did a huge amount of damage to the sect, perhaps destroying the old Black Hand.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T19:56:05-07:00","id":1462068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462040#post1462040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked Justin Achilli these questions:<br /> <br /> <b>Couple of questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Will we ever find out if Lucita is truly dead or alive?<br /> <br /> 2. Is the Salubri Antitribu still a thing or was their &quot;avenging their Clan&quot; always a failure in the making?</b><br /> <br /> <i>Answers:<br /> <br /> 1) Sounds like a story perhaps worth telling.<br /> <br /> 2) I honestly don't think they were well-equipped to pursue the vengeance they wanted.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Have you read Khaldoun Khelil's tweet thread on the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T20:13:37-07:00","id":1462070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462068#post1462068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Have you read Khaldoun Khelil's tweet thread on the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't say I have!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T21:47:47-07:00","id":1462073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462035#post1462035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A reminder again that they've also got their show and movie IP deal done. They've got what they want and will have the same with their video games too...eventually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://variety.com/2021/film/news/world-of-darkness-eric-heisserer-christine-boyland-vampire-werewolf-1234961512/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://variety.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/World-of-Darkness.jpg?w=1000&amp;h=562&amp;crop=1\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://variety.com/2021/film/news/world-of-darkness-eric-heisserer-christine-boyland-vampire-werewolf-1234961512/\" target=\"_blank\"> &lsquo;World of Darkness&rsquo; Universe Coming to TV, Film With Eric Heisserer, Christine Boylan, &lsquo;The Witcher&rsquo;s&rsquo; Hivemind </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://variety.com/2021/film/news/world-of-darkness-eric-heisserer-christine-boyland-vampire-werewolf-1234961512/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://variety.com/2021/film/news/world-of-darkness-eric-heisserer-christine-boyland-vampire-werewolf-1234961512/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Eric Heisserer (\"Shadow and Bone\"), Christine Boylan (\"The Punisher\") and Hivemind are developing World of Darkness' universe for film, TV. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So V5 has achieved its goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>In development means next to nothing; a Crow remake has been in development Hell since 2008, a live action Akira has been on Warner\u2019s development schedule since 2002, It took 12 years for National Treasure 3 to get a script approved to get development moving\u2026 then 2020 happened. Channing Tatum waited so long for the Gambit movie Fox promised him that the entire movie studio got eaten by Disney and that deal now is dead.<br /> <br /> Hell, back in 2008, Disney even had an option for Rifts from Palladium Books\u2026 until it finally decided it wasn\u2019t worth keeping the option alive\u2026 but a Rifts movie was actually \u201cin development.\u201d<br /> <br /> Unless and until there\u2019s a script, actors and release date (and sometimes not even then), \u201cin development\u201d isn\u2019t worth more than the option money the studio offered for potential use of the IP.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I don\u2019t think they needed to streamline or simplify a damned thing for the RPG. Fans are intelligent enough to recognize that different media an IP appears in have differences and that books often have significantly more nuance and depth than visual media (ex. the ASoIaF novels vs. the GoT tv show).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T21:57:36-07:00","id":1462076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462073#post1462073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, I don\u2019t think they needed to streamline or simplify a damned thing for the RPG. Fans are intelligent enough to recognize that different media an IP appears in have differences and that books often have significantly more nuance and depth than visual media (ex. the ASoIaF novels vs. the GoT tv show).</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't an argument I would care about anyway. I am a 25+ year vampire fan and genuinely just prefer the way the sects are presented in V5.<br /> <br /> Obviously YMMV.<br /> <br /> And yes, I 100% agree that the Sabbat should be playable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T22:56:11-07:00","id":1462079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462073#post1462073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I don\u2019t think they needed to streamline or simplify a damned thing for the RPG. Fans are intelligent enough to recognize that different media an IP appears in have differences and that books often have significantly more nuance and depth than visual media (ex. the ASoIaF novels vs. the GoT tv show).</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't need but appear to be doing. If it is true, then it is an unwise decision. Yet, a single unwise decision doesn't mean the end for the line.<br /> <br /> But I am leaning to believe it is actually a mix of streamlining and simply a specific vision. That happens to be against the tastes of many players.<br /> <br /> Again, we actually have a lot of maybes here and I'm almost curious enough to research the matter myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":"09-30-2021, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T22:58:04-07:00","id":1462080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462061#post1462061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now I'm picturing the Path of Honorable Accord getting discredited because of a massive uprising of the Salubri Antritribu that did a huge amount of damage to the sect, perhaps destroying the old Black Hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall the largest group of adherents to the Path of Honorable Accord were the Ventrue antitribu. They're obviously all dead or left the Sect. I'm guessing the Path got tossed out because the Path wasn't &quot;monstrous&quot; enough for NPC antagonists. <br /> <br /> I guess it gives me hope though that the Path of Honorable Accord and perhaps other less monstrous Paths could get rules for PCs someday. A lot of vampires on that and other Paths seem to have left the Sabbat, so maybe we could get rules for playing non-Sabbat Paths. I won't hold my breath though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T22:58:48-07:00","id":1462081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462048#post1462048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How much does winning an industry award actually matter? Have you ever actually seen someone say, &quot;I wasn't really considering playing X, but it one an Origin Award so now I've got to see what the hype is.&quot; or any other sort of statement that the people that actually spend money on these things look to the Origin Awards (or any similar awards) as what guides their decision making?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In what business model?<br /> <br /> That's not how pretty much any niche market works. &quot;Casual fans like it,&quot; is great for selling the core book, but it's not how you build repeat customers that keep buying supplements, and that will follow you to other media. That's what hardcore fans do. If the job of V5 is to kick off a brand that people invest in, they need to either keep existing hardcore fans, or generate new one. Casual fans will move on (at least as customers, they might keep playing V5 but they'll stop buying WoD brand products) to the next thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> V5 has been released in the same year, or with a year's delay all over the world, with a continous stream of manuals, and comes in print. You can find it on Amazon and traditional retail stores.<br /> <br /> V20 was released mostly as a Kickstarter and POD line of books, with only the Corebook widely distributed in retail (and then, with translations coming at very different times, if I'm not mistaken a Spanish translation arrived that V5 was already on the market).<br /> <br /> <b>Again, can I point out that we italian fans, in 10 years, got only the V20 corebook and companion, and we are getting Lore of the Clans on October?</b><br /> <br /> Except for Cult of the Blood Gods which is blocked by licensing issues, <b>a different company has instead published all of the V5 books: they are also ready to bring Sabbat to the market. I highly doubt they would have done so if it wasn't commercially viable.</b><br /> <br /> The RPG market may be overwhelmingly american in nature, and you americans may be able to get a V20 book published in 2008 or 2010 from Noble Knight, or get it from Drivethru easily: but the world is still bigger than America, and V5 pattern of distribution is evidently stronger than V20.<br /> <br /> At least this should be recognized, even by full-time V5 bashers.<br /> <br /> BTW recognizing this doesn't mean saying tha V20 is bad or OPP cannot do his job. V20 had amazing manuals and OPP is a hugely successful company: nonetheless, it haa a different, smaller business presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T23:02:00-07:00","id":1462083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1461980#post1461980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me this would a really good time to do a limited reprint of revised. Sweeten the pill a little while, make a few quid and get a feel for how popular Sabbat actually is with the fanbase</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why on Earth should a company re-publish products from two editions ago when you are launching a new one? I mean, I get what the meaning of this would be (&quot;<i>mwahaha, you silly V5 lovers and publishers, even Revised books 25 years old are better than yours, and they are gonna sell like crazy crushing your game</i>&quot;), but surely you recognize there's quite an excessive amount of wishful thinking in this proposal !<br /> <br /> BTW, one can buy every Revised manual from Drivethrurpg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T23:04:38-07:00","id":1462085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462080#post1462080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I recall the largest group of adherents to the Path of Honorable Accord were the Ventrue antitribu. They're obviously all dead or left the Sect. I'm guessing the Path got tossed out because the Path wasn't &quot;monstrous&quot; enough for NPC antagonists.<br /> <br /> I guess it gives me hope though that the Path of Honorable Accord and perhaps other less monstrous Paths could get rules for PCs someday. A lot of vampires on that and other Paths seem to have left the Sabbat, so maybe we could get rules for playing non-Sabbat Paths. I won't hold my breath though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest, I have an entirely different theory that's much-much more depressing.<br /> <br /> Why was the Path of Honorable Accord and Path of Beast tossed?<br /> <br /> Because they didn't have the page space for it.<br /> <br /> I 100% believe they would have been included in a 200 page version of the book. This book feels like it had SERIOUS trimming to get it out for the end of 2021. Possibly for Blood Hunt's release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T23:08:01-07:00","id":1462086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462081#post1462081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> V5 has been released in the same year, or with a year's delay all over the world, with a continous stream of manuals, and comes in print. You can find it on Amazon and traditional retail stores.<br /> <br /> V20 was released mostly as a Kickstarter and POD line of books, with only the Corebook widely distributed in retail (and then, with translations coming at very different times, if I'm not mistaken a Spanish translation arrived that V5 was already on the market).<br /> <br /> <b>Again, can I point out that we italian fans, in 10 years, got only the V20 corebook and companion, and we are getting Lore of the Clans on October?</b><br /> <br /> Except for Cult of the Blood Gods which is blocked by licensing issues, <b>a different company has instead published all of the V5 books: they are also ready to bring Sabbat to the market. I highly doubt they would have done so if it wasn't commercially viable.</b><br /> <br /> The RPG market may be overwhelmingly american in nature, and you americans may be able to get a V20 book published in 2008 or 2010 from Noble Knight, or get it from Drivethru easily: but the world is still bigger than America, and V5 pattern of distribution is evidently stronger than V20.<br /> <br /> At least this should be recognized, even by full-time V5 bashers.<br /> <br /> BTW recognizing this doesn't mean saying tha V20 is bad or OPP cannot do his job. V20 had amazing manuals and OPP is a hugely successful company: nonetheless, it haa a different, smaller business presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for that international perspective.<br /> <br /> I was also told by my associates in Brazil that vampire never went out of style there and I get the impression that European markets are the same. It was only in America they decided to abandon the World of Darkness and call it suddenly corny.<br /> <br /> Getting to non-American markets was a big-big deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T23:09:31-07:00","id":1462087,"title":"","content":"I still can't get my head around the notion that V5 was &quot;made for TV&quot; or &quot;made for games&quot;<br /> <br /> Unless you've got a really specific game in mind and you're willing to smash the rest of the world for it, it really isn't better for TV or games. Pre-V5 you had a bunch or tools you could use on a blank canvas, The only real thing you had to use of some complexity are the vampires themselves and some of the clans. outside of a very misguided revised scenarios there were few big events and few things to get in the way of the story you wanted to tell. <br /> V5 makes all the factions super central to the conflict. Your stories will always be overshadowed by sectarian divides and upsets or the SI or Gehenna or the beckoning. How could that possibly be a better environment for a writer, director, game designer or whatever? It's like being given Superman as an IP to play with but Lex luthor, Jimmy Olsen and Lois Lane are dead and he's only allowed to fight Doomsday. Yeah, that might make a really good movie, but you aren't getting the most out of the character. As soon as you've done one story, anyone who's a fan of superman, or going to want to profit from superman, is going to want to return to the time of actually having all the options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T23:12:03-07:00","id":1462088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462087#post1462087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still can't get my head around the notion that V5 was &quot;made for TV&quot; or &quot;made for games&quot;<br /> <br /> Unless you've got a really specific game in mind and you're willing to smash the rest of the world for it, it really isn't better for TV or games. Pre-V5 you had a bunch or tools you could use on a blank canvas, The only real thing you had to use of some complexity are the vampires themselves and some of the clans. outside of a very misguided revised scenarios there were few big events and few things to get in the way of the story you wanted to tell.<br /> <br /> V5 makes all the factions super central to the conflict. Your stories will always be overshadowed by sectarian divides and upsets or the SI or Gehenna or the beckoning. How could that possibly be a better environment for a writer, director, game designer or whatever? It's like being given Superman as an IP to play with but Lex luthor, Jimmy Olsen and Lois Lane are dead and he's only allowed to fight Doomsday. Yeah, that might make a really good movie, but you aren't getting the most out of the character. As soon as you've done one story, anyone who's a fan of superman, or going to want to profit from superman, is going to want to return to the time of actually having all the options.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's remotely true. Chicago by Night shows V5 as it should be played. So do the comics and LA by Night.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I do think there's a substantial number of V5 detractors who will never pick up CBN or see these products because it should be in the main book. V5 has sect books but very few other supplements outside of OPP's works.<br /> <br /> I think V5 should have had its own version of DAMNATION CITY really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T23:45:45-07:00","id":1462091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462081#post1462081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">americans may be able to get a V20 book published in 2008 or 2010</div> </div> </div> </div>No one can get V20 published in 2008 or 2010. It didn't existed back then.<br /> <br /> And yes, they have a far more efficient international distribution. We don't have a V20 translation in Brazil at all, but the V5 books aren't a problem to find.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462085#post1462085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why was the Path of Honorable Accord and Path of Beast tossed?<br /> <br /> Because they didn't have the page space for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said that Honorable Accord was explicitly said to not be present anymore in the Sabbat, right?<br /> <br /> If this is the case, then I find it unlikely that this specific Path was left out due to page count. Its easier to use the same space to say that other Paths exist, but with less followers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462086#post1462086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was also told by my associates in Brazil that vampire never went out of style there and I get the impression that European markets are the same. It was only in America they decided to abandon the World of Darkness and call it suddenly corny.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what you mean by this, exactly, but yes, it never ceased to be a thing around here. But AFAIK no one decided to abandon the WoD and call it corny. WoD had a full decade of compounding rules and lore bugs and that was true everywhere. It was still fun and had a lot of fans. They rolled out the Time of Judgement and the nWoD, then in 2 years got bought by CCP. CCP was a hellhole for WW, the same-ish goal of Paradox but horrible inner organization.<br /> <br /> WoD was never abandoned, it was a victim of bad business management. V20 only happened at all due to Kickstart and is hardly a proper edition since at first it couldn't make major changes no matter what. The reason I don't like to call it a proper edition is because it works under the constraints of a kind of License Limbo. CCP didn't create nothing with the IP because they fucked-up royally with their projects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T23:47:18-07:00","id":1462092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462091#post1462091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one can get V20 published in 2008 or 2010. It didn't existed back then.<br /> <br /> And yes, they have a far more efficient international distribution. We don't have a V20 translation in Brazil at all, but the V5 books aren't a problem to find.<br /> <br /> <br /> You said that Honorable Accord was explicitly said to not be present anymore in the Sabbat, right?<br /> <br /> If this is the case, then I find it unlikely that this specific Path was left out due to page count. Its easier to use the same space to say that other Paths exist, but with less followers.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know what you mean by this, exactly, but yes, it never ceased to be a thing around here. But AFAIK no one decided to abandon the WoD and call it corny. WoD had a full decade of compounding rules and lore bugs and that was true everywhere. It was still fun and had a lot of fans. They rolled out the Time of Judgement and the nWoD, then in 2 years got bought by CCP. CCP was a hellhole for WW, the same-ish goal of Paradox but horrible inner organization.<br /> <br /> WoD was never abandoned, it was a victim of bad business management. V20 only happened at all due to Kickstart and is hardly a proper edition since at first it couldn't make major changes no matter what. The reason I don't like to call it a proper edition is because it works under the constraints of a kind of License Limbo. CCP didn't create nothing with the IP because they fucked-up royally with their projects.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it said that there were a few Honorable Accord left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-30-2021, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T23:50:17-07:00","id":1462093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462092#post1462092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it said that there were few Honorable Accord left.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then yes, it may have been lack of space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T01:01:05-07:00","id":1462100,"title":"","content":"One issue I have is that Paths aren't a Sabbat-thing. Paths were a -everybody but the Camarilla- thing. With Anarchs being big-boys and the Camarilla regressing faster than the axis during 1945, surely paths should be in the limelight? But no, they're writeoffs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T01:09:08-07:00","id":1462101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462100#post1462100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One issue I have is that Paths aren't a Sabbat-thing. Paths were a -everybody but the Camarilla- thing. With Anarchs being big-boys and the Camarilla regressing faster than the axis during 1945, surely paths should be in the limelight? But no, they're writeoffs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of that is the problem of Paths. If you make them conveinant then why stay on humanity and, well, that ruins the game.<br /> <br /> Hence why Justin made them impossible to do in Revised.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T01:18:35-07:00","id":1462102,"title":"","content":"Does being on a Path really ruin the game? I don't think it does. It just leads to a different kind of game. Otherwise, VTDA/DAV/V20DA would fail at the first hurdle, since just about everyone is on a Road or Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T01:26:54-07:00","id":1462103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462102#post1462102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does being on a Path really ruin the game? I don't think it does. It just leads to a different kind of game. Otherwise, VTDA/DAV/V20DA would fail at the first hurdle, since just about everyone is on a Road or Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your game is about personal horror, I suspect so yes. It's a storytelling choice and changing the rules changes the tone of the game. Imagine removing SAN from Call of Cthulhu.<br /> <br /> It could be spectacularly fun (and is) but it is not the same game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T01:40:23-07:00","id":1462105,"title":"","content":"Most Vampire games aren't about personal horror, or at least, if you want personal horror, you can see abandoning humanity as a failure and not have to ruin the game by everyone else by demanding that the paths need to suck.<br /> <br /> Part of what makes humanity compelling is that there's viable alternatives. You can choose to be a good person, you can choose to be an honourable villain, or you can choose to torture people as a religion. Humanity should be it's own reward, not the best path so you best stick to it.<br /> <br /> Superman isn't all about punching supervillains and catching planes from the sky. If he was just that, it'd be boring and he'd never be such a lasting character. You can't just zero in on personal horror to the absolute detriment of absolutely everything else. Especially as I don't really find V5's idea of personal horror to be mature...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-30-2021, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T02:42:20-07:00","id":1462106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462103#post1462103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If your game is about personal horror, I suspect so yes. It's a storytelling choice and changing the rules changes the tone of the game. Imagine removing SAN from Call of Cthulhu.<br /> <br /> It could be spectacularly fun (and is) but it is not the same game.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Vtm's humanity and CoC's sanity are not comparable, humanity is not in any way as central to vampire as sanity is in cthulhu.<br /> <br /> Sanity is literally a second lifepoint pool fundamentally ingrained in every mechanics of the game.<br /> <br /> Humanity is something you can pretty much forget in a game of vampire until someone enter frenzy and kill a jogger.<br /> <br /> It is more akin to the alignement of D&amp;D, a part of your character, but not fundamental to most parts of the game.<br /> <br /> Vtm is a game that pretend to be about personal horror, but whose entire setting and mechanics leads to games of conspiracies, supernatural conflicts and &quot;vampires in trencoats&quot;.<br /> <br /> And I can onoy agree with Mywifeisscary, v5 vision of personal horror is not very mature. It sound like a teenager's desire to be adult than actual maturity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T04:25:47-07:00","id":1462113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462081#post1462081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 has been released in the same year, or with a year's delay all over the world, with a continous stream of manuals, and comes in print. You can find it on Amazon and traditional retail stores.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a huge investment on Paradox's part that they don't negotiate into their deal with Onyx Path, so the X20 books, CofD, and Exalted continue to struggle in the trenches. This is an active choice by Paradox for how things are handled. If Paradox wanted, as the owners of the IP, they could have the same push for the Onyx Path made books as their in-house books and other licensed products.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...with only the Corebook widely distributed in retail... </div> </div> </div>V20 core was never like this. It was a promotional product for the Grand Masquerade Convention that was in such demand they tossed together an online store that basically just existed for V20 core orders, and then the CCP merger happened and V20 core was moved to DTRPG.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, can I point out that we italian fans, in 10 years, got only the V20 corebook and companion, and we are getting Lore of the Clans on October? </div> </div> </div>Sure, but I'm not sure why you're saying this to me. I was pushing back against the assertion that &quot;only casual fans matter.&quot;<br /> <br /> The V5 big international and physical store push is something we don't know how profitable it is, and how much Paradox actually cares about being profitable compared to using it as a brand builder. If making it happen was cheap or easy, every gaming company would be doing it, but they don't because it's a huge investment before they know how profitable it will end up being.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T04:38:06-07:00","id":1462116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462101#post1462101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of that is the problem of Paths. If you make them conveinant then why stay on humanity and, well, that ruins the game.<br /> <br /> Hence why Justin made them impossible to do in Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where maturity comes in. If you want to play a game with angsty characters that are pretty much waiting to either get killed or degenerate into a villan, then the humanity path is perfect to experience that. If people are abandoning that given other choices, then it speaks volume how bad V5 is designed.<br /> <br /> In my playgroup humanity was often to the detriment of schemeing, combat, political horror, institutional horror etc. So having rules to cater to that playstyles would have been much appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27028,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","user":"Ignithas","date":". 09-30-2021, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T05:09:41-07:00","id":1462120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462103#post1462103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If your game is about personal horror, I suspect so yes. It's a storytelling choice and changing the rules changes the tone of the game. Imagine removing SAN from Call of Cthulhu.<br /> <br /> It could be spectacularly fun (and is) but it is not the same game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bizarrely evil hat built a Call of Cthulhu game with no sanity mechanic because its 'problematic'.....which ironically has a lot of problematic implications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-30-2021, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T06:04:15-07:00","id":1462122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462120#post1462120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bizarrely evil hat built a Call of Cthulhu game with no sanity mechanic because its 'problematic'.....which ironically has a lot of problematic implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate of Cthulhu was quite something...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T07:08:45-07:00","id":1462127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462070#post1462070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't say I have!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It lays out their thought process on why they made the book the way they did. Pretty interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T07:28:24-07:00","id":1462129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462127#post1462127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It lays out their thought process on why they made the book the way they did. Pretty interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>For reference: <a href=\"https://mobile.twitter.com/kkhelil/status/1442922965155278849\" target=\"_blank\">https://mobile.twitter.com/kkhelil/s...22965155278849</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T08:03:12-07:00","id":1462133,"title":"","content":"It is funny how he writes that deprogramming shovel heads makes good use of their cultural tension, but the actual book disentivising said action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T11:48:31-07:00","id":1462145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462122#post1462122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate of Cthulhu was quite something...</div> </div> </div> </div>They should have just made the Terminator....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T12:49:07-07:00","id":1462147,"title":"","content":"Paths make the horror, and serve as a great analogy of how shit goes to fuckery<br /> Humanity keeps vampires nice. It restrains them, it keeps them from doing really bad things... that greatly gets in the way of horror. Imagine a slasher flick where the killer wants to kill his victims as painlessly and as humanely as possible, or better yet, spends half the run time angsting about the one or two murders he plans to commit... that's not anywhere near so scary as a psycho sexual torture enthusiast. As the later can be just as introspective as the former, the former doesn't have advantages. But most vampires aren't slashers, they're worse, they're politicians. A greedy politician with a moral bottom line is bad, but it's not horror. It becomes horror when his morality is entirely alien to the common people and he's willing or even delighted to screw everyone else in his ambition. Horror comes from the unknown. It comes from extremes, it comes from separation. An Emo is more a threat to himself than to the rest of humanity, how does he scare other people? &quot;Personal horror&quot; is personal and it's not going to work if you thrust your own stupid issues onto someone else, but a horror that targets everyone? That's worthwhile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T13:22:52-07:00","id":1462148,"title":"","content":"When I think of what the most personal horror VtM could be it's always the idea of playing a shovel head thats just clawed their way out of the wet earth and now just has to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T14:09:15-07:00","id":1462155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462101#post1462101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of that is the problem of Paths. If you make them conveinant then why stay on humanity and, well, that ruins the game.<br /> <br /> Hence why Justin made them impossible to do in Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>.<br /> Funny, humanity ruins most games tbh,.at least for me, it.isn't interesting, isn't fun, and If I wanted alignments D20 systems and Rifts (of all things) does them better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T14:14:43-07:00","id":1462156,"title":"","content":"In my games the horror is visiting Camarilla cities and seeing how close to wights all the vampires have become because they try to cling to &quot;humanity&quot;, a way of thinking native to a very different species, and therefore a doomed, insane mindset for a vampire. I emphasize how Cammies all look like late stage cancer victims/drug-addicts/Palpatine types. They convert Cammy neonates desperate to avoid becoming wights themselves, seeking any way out of the insanity the Cammy elders have forced on them. The Camarilla is a tremendous source of horror in my Sabbat games. My players get to save Cammy neonates from the curse of Camarilla dictates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 09-30-2021, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T14:15:38-07:00","id":1462157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462155#post1462155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny, humanity ruins most games tbh,.at least for me, it.isn't interesting, isn't fun, and If I wanted alignments D20 systems and Rifts (of all things) does them better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you are entitled to your opinion. For me the guilt and horror of the condition is the best part<br /> <br /> I love Paths and think they're essential to the games but I also believe they should never be EASY.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-30-2021, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T14:24:20-07:00","id":1462160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462157#post1462157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well you are entitled to your opinion. For me the guilt and horror of the condition is the best part<br /> <br /> I love Paths and think they're essential to the games but I also believe they should never be EASY.</div> </div> </div> </div>They shouldn't be, but Revised tried to make them impossible, because they are badwrongfun, an dthen we have V5...which is shallower that a gothnet poetry board from the mid 90s... Oh I forgot to mention the game and setting that does humanity, sanity and the lack of both best, at least for me : Eclipse Phase, cosmic horror vs transhumanism, easiest summary I can give: Altered Carbon in The Expanse after Skynet read the Necronomicon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T14:28:06-07:00","id":1462161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462101#post1462101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of that is the problem of Paths. If you make them conveinant then why stay on humanity and, well, that ruins the game.<br /> <br /> Hence why Justin made them impossible to do in Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that Paths aren't convenient, with the exception of badly written ones (1st version Paradox). They're not only full of their own challenges to stay on Path, they are mechanically disadvantageous when you need to switch Virtues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462103#post1462103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your game is about personal horror, I suspect so yes. It's a storytelling choice and changing the rules changes the tone of the game. Imagine removing SAN from Call of Cthulhu.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's just the &quot;One Right Way&quot; BS many are complaining. Paths don't remove the personal horror. They do change the game, but that isn't necessarily bad either as no one is saying that Paths should exist AND STs should feel an obligation to allow them in each and every chronicle.<br /> <br /> But exploring the struggle to change and stay in such a different morality compass is definitely an avenue for exploring personal horror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462105#post1462105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of what makes humanity compelling is that there's viable alternatives. You can choose to be a good person, you can choose to be an honourable villain, or you can choose to torture people as a religion. Humanity should be it's own reward, not the best path so you best stick to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it isn't even that Humanity isn't the best Path, as it is the only one with as many direct mechanical benefits for a high rating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462157#post1462157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Paths and think they're essential to the games but I also believe they should never be EASY.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one said they should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T14:33:36-07:00","id":1462162,"title":"","content":"The problem is... the mechanics of Humanity (in any edition of VtM) are so disconnected from the players that the guilt and horror isn't immersive enough to add to the game. Vampires feel guilty because the dice tell them to feel guilty instead of how their actions and those consequences actually impact the character on any truly relatable level.<br /> <br /> Consider how many editions of the game are written such that (at least how the mechanics play out) you can do any level of monstrosity as long as you feel bad about it afterwards. In V20 when you succeed in your Conscience check and don't lose Humanity, it's because you feel guilty. In V5 when you roll to see to the Stains you've accumulated through various bad acts... same thing.<br /> <br /> It is a horrific setup in its own way, but very much not the personal horror and character study the game is aiming for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T16:07:39-07:00","id":1462168,"title":"","content":"i'm somewhat bemused by the suggestion of the paths as 'easy' or for powergamers. They're just as restrictive and complex as humanity, killing is genrally a Tabboo on most and the ones which it isnt are very restrictive in their own ways I mean saying sorry or doing as your told is the equivelant of throwing a baby in the blender on the path of night and you still have rules against murder.<br /> <br /> Has anyone else read Khaldoun Khelil's account of V5 Sabbat, his internal logic on how they've been treated is......interesting.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/kkhelil/status/1442922965155278849\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2040737120151625728/WYHy5p-L_400x400.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/kkhelil/status/1442922965155278849\" target=\"_blank\"> Khaldoun Khelil \ud83c\uddf5\ud83c\uddf8\ud83c\udf49\ud83c\udde9\ud83c\uddff (@kkhelil) on X </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/kkhelil/status/1442922965155278849\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/kkhelil/status/1442922965155278849 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> V5 Sabbat : First let me say this was the book I'd been hoping to write for 20 years, so being part of the creative team was a dream come true. My posts are my own, I don't believe in canon but perhaps it'll give insight into where my part of the work was coming from 1/x #vamily </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-30-2021, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T16:21:20-07:00","id":1462169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462168#post1462168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i'm somewhat bemused by the suggestion of the paths as 'easy' or for powergamers. They're just as restrictive and complex as humanity, killing is genrally a Tabboo on most and the ones which it isnt are very restrictive in their own ways I mean saying sorry or doing as your told is the equivelant of throwing a baby in the blender on the path of night and you still have rules against murder.<br /> <br /> Has anyone else read Khaldoun Khelil's account of V5 Sabbat, his internal logic on how they've been treated is......interesting.<br /> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/kkhelil/status/1442922965155278849\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/kkhelil/status/1442922965155278849</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the link!<br /> <br /> Here's what he had to say, everyone:<br /> <br /> 1. V5 Sabbat : First let me say this was the book I'd been hoping to write for 20 years, so being part of the creative team was a dream come true. My posts are my own, I don't believe in canon but perhaps it'll give insight into where my part of the work was coming from 1/x #vamily<br /> <br /> 2. Antagonists: When I write for V5 I try to make sure that as many options are possible for players and STs regardless of the game type. Spirituality, transhumanism, and esoterica were all basically locked in the Sabbat in older editions and that's no longer the case. 2/x<br /> <br /> 3. Now you can play a Cam Tzimsice worshiping Caine or a Hecata rebel obsessed with the book of Nod and so on. Those stories are no longer locked behind Sect walls. This also meant the role of the V5 Sabbat could be reimagined in ways that bolstered V5's core themes 3/x<br /> <br /> 4. The V5 Sects would be clarified and sharpened, but your options within them broadened and deepened. This also meant that the elements that portrayed the Sabbat as a dark/edgy reflection of the Camarilla were redundant to story needs. Now the Sword was unsheathed. 4/x<br /> <br /> 5. Playability: So why make them Antagonists? Simply put that's where the story took us. No one can control your table and there's certainly ample material to create Sabbat PCs in V5, but that's not the core story V5 is telling. Does that makes Sabbat for advanced players only? 5/x<br /> <br /> 6. No. The Sabbat is for everyone and Vampire the Masquerade would be hollow without them. The Gehenna War is everywhere and in turn so is the Sabbat. Pieces of their ideals and story are now embedded in the game's DNA. You cannot escape them. 6/x<br /> <br /> 7. By making the story elements that were once &quot;reserved&quot; for the Sabbat player in older editions part of V5's core story we at once freed these incredible narratives from behind a veil, but in turn the Sabbat couldn't survive as it was and be true to its namesake. 7/x<br /> <br /> 8. Internal Tension: While the Sabbat could be called hypocritical, I prefer to think of them as having powerful internal tensions. They want personal freedom, but the powers they fight against are too powerful to face unless they're unified, devoted and immune to subjugation 8/x<br /> <br /> 9. Individuals, Clan, and personal ambition still exist in the Sabbat, but those have to be tempered against their culture. A coterie deprogramming a fresh shovelhead or navigating the spirituality of an Lasombra who just joined the Ivory Tower would make use of that tension 9/x<br /> <br /> 10. Themes: The V5 Sabbat book also explores themes that are now central to the whole game. Never before has so much of the Sabbat's philosophy, lore and concerns been such an integral part of the game from corebook on. 10/x<br /> <br /> 11. The Beckoning, Gehenna and the nature of the Antediluvians are explored as story elements because the Sabbat has opened these wounds. Vampires can no longer hide from whats coming. In many ways the 2nd inquisition is only a symptom. A stop gap implemented by clueless mortals 11/x<br /> <br /> 12. In the Sabbat book it tackles the question of what it means to win the Gehenna War. What is an Antediluvian and how can they be defeated? What secrets are the Sabbat searching for in the blood of elders that will arm them against monsters clad in the armor of aeons? 12/x<br /> <br /> 13. The Sabbat Victorious: I think of V5 as the Black Hand triumphant. Vampire as a game has never been more Sabbat than it is now. The veil has been drawn and the elders exposed. We were right all along and it's a Diablerie that I'm proud to have been a part of. Praise Caine 13/x","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T16:51:45-07:00","id":1462174,"title":"","content":"I think he makes a valid point that if you're opening up a lot of Sabbat options within the Camarilla, there is less &quot;need&quot; to play a Sabbat character in V5's setting. You can now play a Noddist Tzimisce in the V5 Camarilla if you want to.<br /> <br /> Whether someone would rather just play a Noddist Tzimisce in the pre-V5 Sabbat is a separate question, though. Pre-V5 Sabbat is still a <i>very</i> different beast from the V5 Camarilla, just like V5 is a very different beast from previous editions of the game.<br /> <br /> There are clearly lots of posters on this forum happy to stick with earlier editions. I'd be hard-pressed to name any posters here who want to keep playing the Sabbat in V5's setting. They seem mostly happy to stick with earlier editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T17:03:17-07:00","id":1462178,"title":"","content":"Personally i found the statement paradoxical considering player options have been severly curtained with an entire sect missing for play and one severely limited in fluff and several clans have been severely diluted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-30-2021, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T17:06:08-07:00","id":1462179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462178#post1462178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally i found the statement paradoxical considering player options have been severly curtained and several clans have been severely diluted and theirs a chronic lack of supplementary fluff I this brave new world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect part of this may well be the different ways STs have been playing the game at their home tables. If a Lasombra Antitribu is not something that would be the target of hundreds of attacks by Sabbat all the time (and Marcus Vitel was sentenced to die once his Clan was revealed) but just another Clan, you will find them joining the Camarilla to be a wet fart.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, and?&quot;<br /> <br /> If the idea of a Tzimisce in the Camarilla was UNTHINKABLE, then it might be a big change.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T17:10:44-07:00","id":1462180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462179#post1462179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect part of this may well be the different ways STs have been playing the game at their home tables. If a Lasombra Antitribu is not something that would be the target of hundreds of attacks by Sabbat all the time (and Marcus Vitel was sentenced to die once his Clan was revealed) but just another Clan, you will find them joining the Camarilla to be a wet fart.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, and?&quot;<br /> <br /> If the idea of a Tzimisce in the Camarilla was UNTHINKABLE, then it might be a big change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that just throwing the baby out with the bathwater? I suspect that the number of people who play sabbat games outnumber people who play lasombra antritrbu by a considerable amount. It'd be the equivalent of have the ventrue defect to the anarchs if their was an interest in anarch ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-30-2021, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T17:40:10-07:00","id":1462185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462180#post1462180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that just throwing the baby out with the bathwater? I suspect that the number of people who play sabbat games outnumber people who play lasombra antritrbu by a considerable amount. It'd be the equivalent of have the ventrue defect to the anarchs if their was an interest in anarch ventrue.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand, I feel it may be the reference pools of the people involved not intersecting. Lasombra Antitribu are like the 3rd or so most played Clan in LARP.<br /> <br /> Sabbat, the Night in Question aside, are almost NONEXISTENT by comparison in LARP.<br /> <br /> Which means that players who LOVE the Sabbat are likely to be tabletop gamers and confused why Lasombra Antis are so important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-30-2021, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T17:52:56-07:00","id":1462189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462185#post1462185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I understand, I feel it may be the reference pools of the people involved not intersecting. From what I understand, Lasombra Antitribu are like the 3rd or so most played Clan in LARP.<br /> <br /> Sabbat, the Night in Question aside, are almost NONEXISTENT by comparison in LARP.<br /> <br /> Which means that players who LOVE the Sabbat are likely to be tabletop gamers and confused why Lasombra Antis are so important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that would explain some of the angry grumbles about letting larpers run the show I've heard from other tabletop players. It does seem a very unproductive to restructure the tabletop corebook with mind to what larpers do at the expense of tabletop trends. Denying tabletop players a core option to smooth things over for larpers I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-30-2021, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T18:00:12-07:00","id":1462190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462189#post1462189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that would explain some of the angry grumbles about letting larpers run the show I've heard from other tabletop players. It does seem a very unproductive to restructure the tabletop corebook with mind to what larpers do at the expense of tabletop trends. Denying tabletop players a core option to smooth things over for larpers I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps but it is also recognizing the popularity of a Clan with a devoted part of the fandom that is a major reason why V:TM is still a thing in 2021.<br /> <br /> Certainly, those LARPer Lasombra shouldn't have to deal with the TT game's saying, &quot;Oh the Lasombra will eventually kill you all because that's what the book says.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or maybe they should. Either way, it wasn't a decision made as arbitrarily as might initially appear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T18:01:42-07:00","id":1462191,"title":"","content":"In my experience, Lasombra <i>antitribu</i> are also very popular among tabletop gamers. So I think V5 further opening them up as an option in the Camarilla was a good idea.<br /> <br /> Though like a lot of things V5, the implementation was problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T18:07:41-07:00","id":1462193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462190#post1462190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps but it is also recognizing the popularity of a Clan with a devoted part of the fandom that is a major reason why V:TM is still a thing in 2021.<br /> <br /> Certainly, those LARPer Lasombra shouldn't have to deal with the TT game's saying, &quot;Oh the Lasombra will eventually kill you all because that's what the book says.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or maybe they should. Either way, it wasn't a decision made as arbitrarily as might initially appear.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty binary way of looking at it and dismissive of sabbat players. It would be pretty easy to just say something like &quot;lasombra antitribu have had a surge in numbers that the main clans headhunting them individually is no longer viable.&quot; As opposed to &quot;were going to throw up roadblocks to you playing sabbat while claiming were diversifying gamestyles.&quot; It's not like playing antitribu in the Sabbat means the entire main Clan bears down you in v20<br /> <br /> I really really hope so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-01-2021, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T18:14:40-07:00","id":1462196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462193#post1462193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a pretty binary way of looking at it and dismissive of sabbat players. It would be pretty easy to just say something like &quot;lasombra antitribu have had a surge in number that the main clans headhunting them individually is no longer viable.&quot; As opposed to &quot;were going to throw up roadblocks to you playing sabbat while claiming were diversifying gamestyles.&quot; It's not like playing antitribu in the Sabbat means the entire main Clan bears down you in v20<br /> <br /> I really really hope so.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not me being dismissive because of two factoids:<br /> <br /> 1. The Sabbat should absolutely be playable.<br /> <br /> 2. The Sabbat should have rules for playing in this book.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, that doesn't mean the defection shouldn't have happen. In Chicago by Night, it says that half the Clan stayed with the Sabbat so the defection does nothing to HURT Sabbat play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T18:53:01-07:00","id":1462198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462191#post1462191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience, Lasombra <i>antitribu</i> are also very popular among tabletop gamers. So I think V5 further opening them up as an option in the Camarilla was a good idea.<br /> <br /> Though like a lot of things V5, the implementation was problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The very fact that the Lasombra <i>Antitribu</i> were a thing pretty much means that they were already an option in the Camarilla, so the defection had no purpose in this sense.<br /> <br /> And the headhunting? Seriously, how feasible this headhunt really is? Once you're already safe in a Camarilla city what will they do? And now that the Sabbat is in the full &quot;clans don't matter&quot; mode it is even more nonsense.<br /> <br /> But the defection had nothing to do with the current state of the Sabbat. It didn't existed yet when the defection was written. It was, indeed, just a play to favor LARP players in a time when the Sabbat was still removed from the setting for all practical purposes (since they seem to think that the Middle East is in another world).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T19:56:55-07:00","id":1462203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462198#post1462198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The very fact that the Lasombra <i>Antitribu</i> were a thing pretty much means that they were already an option in the Camarilla, so the defection had no purpose in this sense.<br /> <br /> And the headhunting? Seriously, how feasible this headhunt really is? Once you're already safe in a Camarilla city what will they do? And now that the Sabbat is in the full &quot;clans don't matter&quot; mode it is even more nonsense.<br /> <br /> But the defection had nothing to do with the current state of the Sabbat. It didn't existed yet when the defection was written. It was, indeed, just a play to favor LARP players in a time when the Sabbat was still removed from the setting for all practical purposes (since they seem to think that the Middle East is in another world).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the purpose of the defection is itself a justification: a big setting-shaking up event that causes a change to the status quo.<br /> <br /> I've mentioned how much contempt I have for static settings. They just don't hold any interest for me and it's ultimately what killed my love for Eberron. It's not that I can't make my own setting events but metaplot has an important role in my games that it gives a shared experience that players and Storytellers can write their campaigns around. I love &quot;living&quot; campaigns and shake ups have a factor to them that forces player characters to react to them as the kind of events that are unpredictable and change their world. When WW2 happens in a Pulp campaign, it's something that your player characters have to adapt to and react to despite it not being centered on them.<br /> <br /> It makes the world feel &quot;bigger&quot; and more authentic because the events are not entirely centered around the player characters. How do they feel about the Lasombra defection? What's their opinion on the Sabbat seemingly collapsing? Do they have an opinion on the Second Inquisition? Lots of things to discuss in-character and many a chronicle I have made have started this way: &quot;You wake up from torpor and find out everything is different!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T20:22:25-07:00","id":1462207,"title":"","content":"There's a rather big difference between, &quot;I don't like how they changed the setting's world,&quot; and, &quot;I don't like changing the setting period.&quot;<br /> <br /> You continue to treat anyone that doesn't like <b>how</b> the setting changes were implemented as if they wouldn't be happy with any change.<br /> <br /> It's why your 4.5/5 rating feels so... unhelpful. You acknowledge so many things V5 Sabbat didn't do right, but apparently, &quot;its different enough from Revised Sabbat to piss off fans of Revised Sabbat that don't like the changes,&quot; is worth at least 3 of those stars.<br /> <br /> It might be helpful to remember that the vast majority of VtM fans are fans of a game where a changing world was always part of the game by the time 2e started. We're not complaining that V5 changes things, but treating us like we are when we complain about how V5 changed things doesn't serve and purpose I can fathom.<br /> <br /> And most games figure out a very simple compromise here: adventure modules. If you want a book that deals with, &quot;you go into a long torpor and everything is different when you wake up,&quot; you can do that without radically changing the game's setting for everyone that doesn't want that much change.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T20:34:43-07:00","id":1462210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462196#post1462196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not me being dismissive because of two factoids:<br /> <br /> 1. The Sabbat should absolutely be playable.<br /> <br /> 2. The Sabbat should have rules for playing in this book.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, that doesn't mean the defection shouldn't have happen. In Chicago by Night, it says that half the Clan stayed with the Sabbat so the defection does nothing to HURT Sabbat play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apart from requiring the Sabbat to have swallowed the idiot Stella mass blackhole to set the defection in motion, then destroying all the factions and politics of the Sabbat, and then lying to us by claiming, as the devs have, that the TS system allows you to mimic paths anyway ...and them hand an unearned victory to the Anarchs on a global scale...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 09-30-2021, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T20:44:03-07:00","id":1462213,"title":"","content":"The problem isn't the defection <i>per se</i> at all. If it had a good story behind and a sensible justification many of us would be agreeing to it. But the way it happened just makes the Lasombra look stupid, and when a change happens in a badly written way that seems to have been poorly thought off instead of the result of a good plot idea, then we can guess the motives of the change.<br /> <br /> Motives that only serve to contextualize, as the change can be well done or not independently from them. They could have thought of a better way for the defection to happen. Maybe some Lasombra struck a deal with the Cam so they could defect in large enough numbers to make a headhunt impossible even as a joke. Maybe the Amici and/or some other Lasombra elders struck the deal to defect while sabotaging some key Lasombra institutions, which is WAY more sensible than accepting full civil war and could actually be indeed a good plan for the clan anyway instead of trying to call a loss into a win because they like to lose to show power.<br /> <br /> Lucita, who have been Sabbat for a short time, could have made any number of policy changes that resulted in the interest and opportunity for the large defection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T21:04:03-07:00","id":1462217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462207#post1462207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a rather big difference between, &quot;I don't like how they changed the setting's world,&quot; and, &quot;I don't like changing the setting period.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't hold any dislike of the changes to the Sabbat against anyone. I think it's a perfectly valid opinion. I was just sharing why I like metaplot in general. I think it's entirely possible to hold completely contradictory opinions about something and just wanted to share what I enjoyed about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462213#post1462213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lucita, who have been Sabbat for a short time, could have made any number of policy changes that resulted in the interest and opportunity for the large defection.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I hate is Lucita looked like she was going to regain some of her old character but they seem to have doubled down on her as a stereotypical Chaotic Evil Keeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-01-2021, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T21:30:20-07:00","id":1462220,"title":"","content":"An explanation for why I like Sabbat: The Black Hand for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> .<br /> <br /> 1. To be frank, the majority of the **** 1/2star rating comes immediately from the fact that it was absolutely absurd to have to wait as long as we did for a Sabbat supplement. Not only did we have to have the Tzimisce and Lasombra waited on in supplements away from the main book but we also had the Sabbat exiled to nowhere (the Middle East being a place I could reach in a day) as if it wasn't a third pillar sect. The Sabbat main book should have always been one of the original three supplements for V:TM 5th Edition.<br /> <br /> 2. I'm a huge fan of Justin Achilli and want to state that the quality of the writing for this book is just flat out superior to the Camarilla and Anarch books. It's also third person and not in-universe, which means that it is clearer, more concise and more USEFUL than the previous two books. It gives a description of what the Sabbat is, what the Sabbat's culture is, Disciplines, and storytelling advice.<br /> <br /> 3. I don't feel comfortable downgrading a book's rating for what it is NOT. Speaking as a guy who reviews books as part of his profession (I review at Booknest.EU and have over 200 reviews there), I feel like you cannot be upset with a book for not being the way you want it. It doesn't matter if the V5 Sabbat SHOULD have had a playable faction, it's something they chose not to do and I'm not the writer. I can only judge the material on what it sets out to do.<br /> <br /> Did I *WANT* the following?:<br /> <br /> * Path rules<br /> * Loresheets<br /> * The (False) Black Hand having at least a paragraph?<br /> * Rules for playing Sabbat defectors<br /> * More History about how this happened<br /> * The Sabbat Inquisition<br /> * Infernalism<br /> <br /> Absolutely, but I feel like I can't be mad it DIDN'T have these things.<br /> <br /> 4. I removed the half star that I did because the book is ridiculously short and overpriced. It should be 200 pages at the very least and it really should be 300+ pages for the fact it's so goddamn expensive. The book quality is tremendous but it's deeply underdeveloped. I feel like they should have combined this book and the V5 Companion (Ravnos, Tzimisce, and Salubri as Clans in the Sabbat isn't a bad combination either). It would have resolved a lot of issues I had and bumped it up to 5 stars. I was tempted to go 4 stars for the book but I admit I decided to ere on the side of positive because the Sabbat were finally back and no longer being un-personed like someone in 1984.<br /> <br /> 5. I felt the book was consistent in its vision and while I may prefer a Sabbat that is more intellectual, erudite, and distinct (as well as mostly on Humanity), I can't say that it was an unbelievable development for the Sword of Caine. I admit that I took the book was presently what the Sabbat had degenerated INTO rather than always were meant to be. The savages had taken over and the original Anarchs had either defected or were pulling the strings. The new Sabbat seems to be a metaphor for terrorism and religious fascism, which is something that certainly exists and was a version of the Sword of Caine I recognized. Its a tragedy that the Sabbat has become THIS but that doesn't mean it's a bad story.<br /> <br /> 6. Ratings are always a summary of my overall positivity to a subject and not going to cover all the actual ups and downs of something. What I liked, I liked very much. What I didn't like, I pointed out in the main part of the review.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-01-2021, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T22:10:34-07:00","id":1462227,"title":"","content":"Back on the LARP topic...as someone who was literally in charge of sabbat for one of the major LARP organizations (100+ chronicles) for 6 and half years....the assement on the popularity of sabbat and lasombra in LARPs is widely inaccurate. In the orgnization I am still a part of...lasombra are probably the most common sabbat pc there and there atleast 30+ individual sabbat games.<br /> <br /> Every single sabbat player in this larp org I have spoken too...including the lasombra players (which I still help oversee) all of them...and I mean all of them...thought the lasombra defection to the cam in V5 was ridiculous and made no sense. And that's not a small number of people.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry the assement about sabbat, lasombra, and larps is just incorrect. Lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T22:13:32-07:00","id":1462229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462227#post1462227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on the LARP topic...as someone who was literally in charge of sabbat for one of the major LARP organizations (100+ chronicles) for 6 and half years....the assement on the popularity of sabbat and lasombra in LARPs is widely inaccurate. In the orgnization I am still a part of...lasombra are probably the most common sabbat pc there and there atleast 30+ individual sabbat games.<br /> <br /> Every single sabbat player in this larp org I have spoken too...including the lasombra players (which I still help oversee) all of them...and I mean all of them...thought the lasombra defection to the cam in V5 was ridiculous and made no sense. And that's not a small number of people.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry the assement about sabbat, lasombra, and larps is just incorrect. Lol</div> </div> </div> </div>I could well be 100% wrong in what I've heard and the scuttlebutt is completely inaccurate. I will say, though, maybe the guy in charge of LARP Sabbat might have a biased view.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I stand corrected on Sabbat not being as popular in LARP, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T22:19:54-07:00","id":1462230,"title":"","content":"I mean...I can give actual numbers for the larp org I'm in. But I'm still a guy on the internet and like all things...you can choose to believe what you like on a forum lol.<br /> <br /> Now if you will excuse me I have to get back to planing my palla grande event on our discord lol. I just wanted to pipe up that for me and my experience, not on a forum, that wasn't the case :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T22:24:07-07:00","id":1462231,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Cam has all the Sabbat options now so you don't really need the Cam&quot;<br /> <br /> Except that ruins the Cam. <br /> And we still don't have paths in the Cam<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","ti