i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T03:49:47-07:00","id":1462417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462415#post1462415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you didn't have a strong will, you wouldn't be Sabbat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> but their is no reason to risk it in the first place, far better just kill the elder and be done with it than risk possession for no real gain, and large potential losses, it's Russian Roulette crossed with heroin that may kill all your allies as well...If you're weak enough to be a junkie, you're to weak to be useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 10-02-2021, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T04:21:44-07:00","id":1462419,"title":"","content":"I must admit I'm genuinely curious about the in house decision decision to downplay honorable accord. The path meshes very well with their vision of modern sabbat as a unified coherent sect especially compared to the cathari. The lasombra defection link is a retcon/plothole since most path members were noted to be tzmisce or ventrue and betraying the Sabbat is a level one sin on the path so its definitely an deliberate choice.<br /> The question is-why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T04:26:12-07:00","id":1462420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462419#post1462419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must admit I'm genuinely curious about the in house decision decision to downplay honorable accord. The path meshes very well with their vision of modern sabbat as a unified coherent sect especially compared to the cathari. The lasombra defection link is a retcon/plothole since most path members were noted to be tzmisce or ventrue and betraying the Sabbat is a level one sin on the path so its definitely an deliberate choice.<br /> The question is-why?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the book flat out acts like the Path of Honorable Accord = The Path of Chivalry, which is absolutely not the case. This is a weird retcon and Justin knows better so I assume it's deliberate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T08:56:21-07:00","id":1462430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462386#post1462386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well they're 900 years old so Methusaleh is pretty close.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books say methuselahs are one thousand or more years old, but I think a better definition is more like two thousand. Vampires like Lucita and Vykos just don't operate on the same level that Mithras, Helena, or Menele do. Pretty much all of the archetypal hidden puppet-masters we see in the By Nights are two thousand or more years old (and only four or five steps removed from Caine). One thousand is square in the middle of the Middle Ages. That doesn't invoke the same sense of historic grandeur for me as a creature that predates the rise of Christianity.<br /> <br /> Side tangent, but the core rulebook's definition of &quot;methuselah&quot; has never made sense to me. It just doesn't bear it out with the game's published NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T08:57:00-07:00","id":1462431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462419#post1462419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must admit I'm genuinely curious about the in house decision decision to downplay honorable accord. The path meshes very well with their vision of modern sabbat as a unified coherent sect especially compared to the cathari. The lasombra defection link is a retcon/plothole since most path members were noted to be tzmisce or ventrue and betraying the Sabbat is a level one sin on the path so its definitely an deliberate choice.<br /> The question is-why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not evil-seeming enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T09:14:54-07:00","id":1462433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462430#post1462430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The books say methuselahs are one thousand or more years old, but I think a better definition is more like two thousand. Vampires like Lucita and Vykos just don't operate on the same level that Mithras, Helena, or Menele do. Pretty much all of the archetypal hidden puppet-masters we see in the By Nights are two thousand or more years old (and only four or five steps removed from Caine). One thousand is square in the middle of the Middle Ages. That doesn't invoke the same sense of historic grandeur for me as a creature that predates the rise of Christianity.<br /> <br /> Side tangent, but the core rulebook's definition of &quot;methuselah&quot; has never made sense to me. It just doesn't bear it out with the game's published NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the word methuselah is another example of the unreliable narrator at work. The true ancients are so subtle that most vampires have never heard of them. Methuselah is the word vampires use for the oldest vampires who nonetheless get their hands dirty often enough to be in the public eye. Those vamps tend to be about a 1,000.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T09:30:54-07:00","id":1462435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462430#post1462430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The books say methuselahs are one thousand or more years old, but I think a better definition is more like two thousand. Vampires like Lucita and Vykos just don't operate on the same level that Mithras, Helena, or Menele do. Pretty much all of the archetypal hidden puppet-masters we see in the By Nights are two thousand or more years old (and only four or five steps removed from Caine). One thousand is square in the middle of the Middle Ages. That doesn't invoke the same sense of historic grandeur for me as a creature that predates the rise of Christianity.<br /> <br /> Side tangent, but the core rulebook's definition of &quot;methuselah&quot; has never made sense to me. It just doesn't bear it out with the game's published NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought it is at least 1000 years old (probably not literally, more like 1100-1500 minimum) <i>and</i> 4th or 5th Generation. The experience of age, the insights derived from the use of the higher-level vampiric powers, and the sheer potency of the Vitae (shown best in increased maximum traits) all combine to create a person wholly on another level of supernatural and mundane (thinking capabilities, strength of character, aspirations etc.) prowess.<br /> The Revised Corebook states &quot;<i>At a point between a vampire's thousandth and two thousandth year, a grave change change overtakes the Kindred.</i>&quot;<br /> Though I'd agree that the archetypal Methuselahs are those who are over 2000 years old (let's say at least 1800 years).<br /> Aren't newly Embraced 4th and 5th Generation Kindred specifically called Young Methuselahs? This indicates that such Vampires are on a kind fast-track, both in regard to status, and personal development and prowess.<br /> <br /> An interesting question is whether the Inner Councilors of the Clan Tremere could be considered to be Methuselahs. I think that Meerlinda and Etrius certainly could be called Methuselahs, when their experience and insights from being former Mages are taken into account, and also the fact that they have been in the leadership of Clan Tremere since its creation.<br /> The rest of the Council of Seven, not so much. Though they do have Thaumaturgy 8-9 (as well as the immensely useful Auspex and Dominate as the other Clan Disciplines) and the unity of the Tremere Pyramid behind them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T10:37:32-07:00","id":1462443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462435#post1462435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought it is at least 1000 years old (probably not literally, more like 1100-1500 minimum) <i>and</i> 4th or 5th Generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels like a fair standard in the Modern Nights. Mithras was Embraced in ~1200 BCE and would have thus &quot;become&quot; a methuselah at ~200 BCE.<br /> <br /> In the Dark Medieval and earlier eras, standards are different. In <i>Constantinople by Night</i>, Caius is fifth generation and around ~900 years old, but his traits aren't significantly more impressive than the city's other elders. Back then I think it was still possible for many fifth-generation vampires to be considered &quot;mere&quot; elders.<br /> <br /> The Followers of Set specifically define a methuselah as a vampire who's survived a Sothic turn--that is, any vampire who is 1,461 or more years old. I always thought an even better definition was a vampire who's survived one Sothic turn per generation removed from Set. So a 4th-generation Setite &quot;officially&quot; becomes a methuselah at 1,461, a 5th-generation one becomes a methuselah at 2,922, a 6th-generation one becomes a methuselah at 4,383, and so on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though I'd agree that the archetypal Methuselahs are those who are over 2000 years old (let's say at least 1800 years). </div> </div> </div>This is also a good point on archetypes vs. strict definitions.<br /> <br /> Helena, Menele, and Mithras are some of the game's most archetypal methuselahs. They're ancient creatures who effortlessly manipulate lesser vampires and dominate their respective corners of the game setting.<br /> <br /> Hedeon Yaroslavich is ~1500 and fifth generation. He doesn't hide his existence to the extent that Helena and Menele do, but I never got the impression he was particularly well-known outside of Eastern Europe. He's also poised to potentially take over the Oradea League. Is he a methuselah? The term seems apt for him. What about Critias, who's fifth generation and ~2500 years old, but leads an existence largely identical to the other Chicago primogen? His only 6+ Discipline is an Auspex power that lets him looks (even) smarter than he is. He's more like an elder who just happens to be particularly old, rather than a true methuselah, despite the fact that &quot;by the numbers&quot; he's more of a methuselah than Hedeon is. Granted, Hedeon's Disciplines are also more powerful, so there you go.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, I think methuselah is more of a social distinction than a hard set of criteria.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An interesting question is whether the Inner Councilors of the Clan Tremere could be considered to be Methuselahs. I think that Meerlinda and Etrius certainly could be called Methuselahs, when their experience and insights from being former Mages are taken into account, and also the fact that they have been in the leadership of Clan Tremere since its creation.<br /> <br /> The rest of the Council of Seven, not so much. Though they do have Thaumaturgy 8-9 (as well as the immensely useful Auspex and Dominate as the other Clan Disciplines) and the unity of the Tremere Pyramid behind them. </div> </div> </div>Etrius is described (out-of-character) as a methuselah in <i>Transylvania Chronicles IV</i>. Which I'd agree with. He's powerful enough to compete on the same level as vampires like Mithras.<br /> <br /> Goratrix is definitely a methuselah too for the same reasons.<br /> <br /> I agree the other councilors probably aren't methuselahs. I also tend to think no other councilors in the Modern Nights are fourth generation. Some might not even be fifth. Some councilors have had a lot of turnover (like Africa's) and it strains credulity to me that there would happen to be another fourth-generation Tremere waiting in the wings for a spot to open. There are probably Tremere like Karl Schrekt and Ulugh Begh who are more potent than councilors like Elaine de Calinot and simply don't want her job. Not all councilorships or councilors are created equal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T11:00:38-07:00","id":1462447,"title":"","content":"I suppose it depends on where you're looking for. A 1000 year old vampire to a 13th generation Neonate is going to be someone who wields vast power, influence, and personally near unkillable. Lucita is able to possibly become Regent of the Sabbat and dominate the region absolutely. Obviously, they're not going to be as powerful as a 2000 year old vampire but 1000 is always at the bare minimum of methuselah sttus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T11:25:21-07:00","id":1462450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462412#post1462412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 60 revised core.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't says a Methuselah must be 4th or 5th gen, it says they are <i>rumored</i> to be 4th and 5th gen, but defines them directly as, and I quote:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A vampires who has existed for a millennium or more; an elder who no longer exists among the greater whole of Kindred society. </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462413#post1462413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if sex completely obliterated your mind and overwrote it with whoever you did it with....aka Ego death.</div> </div> </div> </div>You talk as if being possessed by the elder was a rule and not a rumor that only canonically happened twice and both times in extremely exceptional circumstances. As popular as the idea of possession by the eaten vampire is, this is no regular danger of Diablerie.<br /> <br /> To be very clear, Tremere was barely an Ancilla, with 111 years, when he diablerized a frigging Ante with mastery of Auspex and Obeah. Coven was a fledgling that diablerized one of the most ancient and powerful Ventrue Methuselah, and even then they battled for years and descriptions of the result aren't consistent on when and if Mithras &quot;won&quot; in a sense that can be called Coven losing his own identity. V5 does set this a likely, but only due to ritual interference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462431#post1462431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not evil-seeming enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is indeed the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462433#post1462433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the word methuselah is another example of the unreliable narrator at work. The true ancients are so subtle that most vampires have never heard of them. Methuselah is the word vampires use for the oldest vampires who nonetheless get their hands dirty often enough to be in the public eye. Those vamps tend to be about a 1,000.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mine is another interpretation. The books state that at about one thousand kindred go through some behavioral changes and stop interacting so much. Vykos in this sense is an outlier, but still barely there, I'd give him at least a few more centuries.<br /> <br /> I think the known Methuselah, apart from just being the historical/mythical characters the authors thought would be fun to put, can be considered the ones who lived through this process and got back to participate enough for some of their shenanigans to become known. So younger Methuselah are either too uninvolved or didn't did enough yet to become known.<br /> <br /> Another interesting fact is that this leaves enough space for the ST to put their own Methuselah in the game at a more comfortable scale, being free to create the character from scratch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462435#post1462435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting question is whether the Inner Councilors of the Clan Tremere could be considered to be Methuselahs. I think that Meerlinda and Etrius certainly could be called Methuselahs, when their experience and insights from being former Mages are taken into account, and also the fact that they have been in the leadership of Clan Tremere since its creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I prefer to let the term be linked solely to age. I like the idea that generation may bring power, but age is what truly transforms a vampire for worse or better.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the original members of the Inner Council are a special case. They were already centuries old as Mages, making them very unique psyches to begin with. They may already be considered as Methuselah, or maybe as something even stranger.<br /> <br /> I do agree that, in the end, 1000 isn't a hard rule, just the bare minimum, but I don't think that power should be the definition, either. Being a Methuselah is about behaving as a Methuselah. Taking the game to another level. But I also think that all Methuselah shouldn't be thought as on the <i>same</i> level exactly. This isn't helpful. What is important is that they're somehow set apart from Kindred society, they're &quot;above&quot; it in a way a &quot;common&quot; Autarkis or Inconnu isn't. But this can still cover a broad spectrum of characters.<br /> <br /> Either way I'd say Lucita may be ready to go through it soon simply because she already started to have a personality change (a very lame one), while Vykos may take quite some time. Or not, even in mortals those changes in outlook and behavior are sometimes sudden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T12:04:34-07:00","id":1462452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462431#post1462431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not evil-seeming enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol if anyone at the development team thought that I'd strongly recommend they re-read tenants, note the wording of some of rules and some of things not covered all....torture for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T12:08:14-07:00","id":1462453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462447#post1462447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it depends on where you're looking for. A 1000 year old vampire to a 13th generation Neonate is going to be someone who wields vast power, influence, and personally near unkillable. Lucita is able to possibly become Regent of the Sabbat and dominate the region absolutely. Obviously, they're not going to be as powerful as a 2000 year old vampire but 1000 is always at the bare minimum of methuselah sttus.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also changed by edition, with Methuselahs being unnatural disasters of epic scale ( Menele causing Pompeii for instance) to demigods (The Archangel, The Dracon) and Warlords Hardestadt the Elder, to something beyond vampirism like Demdemeh,. V5 doesn't have the mechanics to even approach them, hell previous editions gave up for some of them Elimelech the Twice Damned, Ur Shulgi. <br /> <br /> To be a Methuselah is to be a blood god in the literal sense, one of the most powerful beings in the WoD, capable of devastation of a biblical scale, but involved in the deepest conflicts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 10-02-2021, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T12:32:10-07:00","id":1462458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462453#post1462453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also changed by edition, with Methuselahs being unnatural disasters of epic scale ( Menele causing Pompeii for instance) to demigods (The Archangel, The Dracon) and Warlords Hardestadt the Elder, to something beyond vampirism like Demdemeh,. V5 doesn't have the mechanics to even approach them, hell previous editions gave up for some of them Elimelech the Twice Damned, Ur Shulgi.<br /> <br /> To be a Methuselah is to be a blood god in the literal sense, one of the most powerful beings in the WoD, capable of devastation of a biblical scale, but involved in the deepest conflicts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but not all Methusalehs are made equal. I remind you that the first Methusaleh we meet is the 2000 year old Lucian in Forged in Steel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T13:31:01-07:00","id":1462472,"title":"","content":"Lucian definitely isn't a &quot;real&quot; methuselah. Like Critias, he's just an elder who happens to have been around for a very long time.<br /> <br /> But as <i>Lair of the Hidden</i> notes, &quot;there are methuselahs and then there are methuselahs.&quot; Ones like Alexander or Julia Antasia just aren't in the same league as ur-Shulgi.<br /> <br /> There are also significant power ranges and disparities among neonates, ancillae, and elders. Methuselahs are the same in that regard; some are just weaker than others. See Critias' relatively modest stats next to Hedeon Yaroslavich's.<br /> <br /> While it's less likely there are weak Antediluvians, <i>Gehenna</i> (the sourcebook) even posited the existence of Mekhet as a &quot;wandering Jew&quot; Antediluvian significantly weaker than his peers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T15:34:57-07:00","id":1462482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462472#post1462472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lucian definitely isn't a &quot;real&quot; methuselah. Like Critias, he's just an elder who happens to have been around for a very long time.<br /> <br /> But as <i>Lair of the Hidden</i> notes, &quot;there are methuselahs and then there are methuselahs.&quot; Ones like Alexander or Julia Antasia just aren't in the same league as ur-Shulgi.<br /> <br /> There are also significant power ranges and disparities among neonates, ancillae, and elders. Methuselahs are the same in that regard; some are just weaker than others. See Critias' relatively modest stats next to Hedeon Yaroslavich's.<br /> <br /> While it's less likely there are weak Antediluvians, <i>Gehenna</i> (the sourcebook) even posited the existence of Mekhet as a &quot;wandering Jew&quot; Antediluvian significantly weaker than his peers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure not every methuselah is equal but i get the sense Ur-shulgi is more the outlier then the norm. He is closer to ante level than other methuselahs. I dont think its fair to compare him to the likes of mithras or alexander, His dots in blood sorcery alone would probably make him more powerful then even some antes. I dont see someone like absimiliard having any defence against him even if he is an ante.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 10-02-2021, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T15:38:52-07:00","id":1462483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462472#post1462472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lucian definitely isn't a &quot;real&quot; methuselah. Like Critias, he's just an elder who happens to have been around for a very long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Critias is probably one of the most powerful active vampires in the world. Its just he's so brainwashed he doesn't seem to realize it.<br /> <br /> He's just been a (to quote Supernatural) condom for Menele for millennia.<br /> <br /> I assume probably outright possessed for many of those years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T15:42:57-07:00","id":1462485,"title":"","content":"My personal theory is ul shulgi is an archduke, neverborn or some other mega demon infesting a methusulah because the host is potent enough to hold the essence. Alternatively ul shugi is just something....else pretending to be a methusulah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-02-2021, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"t