rewolf and mage white wolf seem allergic to the idea of the good guys scoring wins.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the Technocracy winning against Ravnos made them look too justified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T03:30:18-07:00","id":1462637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462632#post1462632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like the Technocracy winning against Ravnos made them look too justified.</div> </div> </div> </div> The technocracy was always one of the more complex bad guy factions. To me, It didn't really justify them since it simply re enforced what was already known about them. <br /> <br /> Considering v5 I'm genuinely anxious if they'll deny you the ability to play them with next edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-04-2021, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T06:03:19-07:00","id":1462644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462637#post1462637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The technocracy was always one of the more complex bad guy factions. To me, It didn't really justify them since it simply re enforced what was already known about them.<br /> <br /> Considering v5 I'm genuinely anxious if they'll deny you the ability to play them with next edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the books went to pretty elaborate lengths trying to make the Technocracy a complex villain for a group that wanted to commit genocide and end democracy.<br /> <br /> One-dimensional bad guys? No. Playing a Man in Black and conspiracies is just as much fun as playing a vampire.<br /> <br /> But I liked GTTT that remembered they had skills like Terrorism and Torture as well as opening fiction that they were kidnapping kids to experiment on.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T06:15:38-07:00","id":1462645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462644#post1462644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like the books went to pretty elaborate lengths trying to make the Technocracy a complex villain for a group that wanted to commit genocide and end democracy.<br /> <br /> One-dimensional bad guys? No. Playing a Man in Black and conspiracies is just as much fun as playing a vampire.<br /> <br /> But I liked GTTT that remembered they had skills like Terrorism and Torture as well as opening fiction that they were kidnapping kids to experiment on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but killing ravnos isn't really contradicted by those things. If anything they all feed into the fact the technocracy will do anything to win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T10:14:51-07:00","id":1462666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462645#post1462645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but killing ravnos isn't really contradicted by those things. If anything they all feed into the fact the technocracy will do anything to win.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but if you have the Sabbat, Pentex, or Technocracy literally save the world then they look more effective than, say, the Traditions or Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T10:47:54-07:00","id":1462672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462632#post1462632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Technocracy winning against Ravnos made them look too justified.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462666#post1462666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True but if you have the Sabbat, Pentex, or Technocracy literally save the world then they look more effective than, say, the Traditions or Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is less that they are justified and more that they do have the right goals. They have nothng in common with the Sabbat or the Pentex.<br /> <br /> <i>As villains</i>, the theme of the Technocracy is the idea that the ends justify the means. And what set them apart immediately as villains is that their ends are for the greater good. They want the safety and betterment of humanity at large, and that is something many players perceived and embraced. They are grey villains, maybe not your cup of tea, and that means they are also good guys with some frequency depending on context.<br /> <br /> They aren't completely good even there, though. WoN problem's aside, assuming it as written they still sacrificed more than 60 thousand innocent lives without really having any right to do so. And they absolutely would sacrifice more if needed, the entire country if that was the case (about 180 million people IIRC). Their main inner conflict is shown in the fact that the operation's leader clearly don't want to make those sacrifices, <u>but he will</u>, he's relatively happy at the end that their nukes are responsible for <i>only</i> around 60k deaths.<br /> <br /> Would the Traditions do the same? Another thing in Mage is that the players are expected to be good guys at least at some extent, and the core laws of the Traditions are fairly Humanist, being more ethical as the Union as a whole. But the Traditions have much more inner groups that hold far lower moral standards.<br /> <br /> Mage 1st edition had, from all the 1st edition splats, the main conflict that aged worse. It was excessive Luddite and anarchic and it didn't made sense for that many players for long. Remember that the Technocracy isn't just a group wanting to end democracy and commit genocide, they're the representation of order and science in a setting that is all about personal belief. Making them the one-dimensional villains of their first convention books is to make proper science and technology into that same one-dimensional villainy, something many, many players didn't buy into, so they argued that it should be, to some extent, the Traditions' propaganda instead of truth.<br /> <br /> Guide to the Technocracy already shows a far more nuanced in the group. Yeah, they have a lot of unsavory people and practices. But they also have a lot of inside people avoiding or even preaching for the end of those practices. There are a lot of bad people, but there are a lot of good people that stay in, because their focus is in the goal of making the world safe and prosperous for the common people.<br /> <br /> On this aspect, I don't think the Technocracy as a bad choice of final executioner of Ravnos. I think it should have been written differently and the operation should have been conducted by a local branch instead of an american officer, among other changes. But they are exactly the supernatural group that dedicated themselves for centuries to deal with such a situation for the sake of the world even if it cost them everything they had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T11:05:33-07:00","id":1462675,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the trick with the Technocracy is that they're only &quot;evil&quot; relative to the main protagonists of Mage; easily the most generally heroic/humane of the core three settings... they didn't even get an &quot;End of Days&quot; to match Gehenna or the Apocalypse until Revised shoehorned it in. The Technocracy is faceless authoritarian evil if you're some newly Awakened human learning that you can actually rewrite your destiny... but compared to vampires or the Wyrm or the Nephandi they're maybe a two on the Villainy scale.<br /> <br /> Basically, the Technocracy is Magneto vs. the Traditions' X-Men. Sometimes he's your enemy on philosophical grounds... other times, like when you've got a Brood/Phalanx/Future Sentinels invasion on your hand, he's fighting on your side against the bigger bad because everyone recognizes that without survival the philosophical argument is pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T11:21:18-07:00","id":1462677,"title":"","content":"If you say so, I suppose I think recent years has me less comfortable with Far Right, &quot;Hard Men Making Hard Choices&quot;, Surveillance State protagonists.<br /> <br /> To each their own.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T11:34:22-07:00","id":1462681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462677#post1462677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you say so, I suppose I think recent years has me less comfortable with Far Right, &quot;Hard Men Making Hard Choices&quot;, Surveillance State protagonists.<br /> <br /> To each their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irl politics doesn't really mesh well with wod politics but The technocratic are hard hard left. Unified collectivist ascension at the expense of individual ascension. No hard men made the decision to nuke ravnos or torture a 14 year old hollow one because it was made by a comitee who double checked an approved by the regulatory department ...which for me personally as a hard line winger is far more terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-04-2021, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T11:46:02-07:00","id":1462684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462677#post1462677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you say so, I suppose I think recent years has me less comfortable with Far Right, &quot;Hard Men Making Hard Choices&quot;, Surveillance State protagonists.<br /> <br /> To each their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its funny... I've never once thought of the Technocracy as Far Right. Quite the opposite.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy has always been the Atheist Globalist Authoritarian faction who believes in quashing individual liberties in the name of a collective good as determined by panels of unelected &quot;experts.&quot;<br /> <br /> ETA: The Traditions aren't Far Right either... they're the Hard Libertarians (pro-legalize everything + defund government) and Religious Fanatics like the Westborough Baptists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 10-04-2021, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T12:01:00-07:00","id":1462687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462684#post1462684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its funny... I've never once thought of the Technocracy as Far Right. Quite the opposite.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy has always been the Atheist Globalist Authoritarian faction who believes in quashing individual liberties in the name of a collective good as determined by panels of unelected &quot;experts.&quot;<br /> <br /> ETA: The Traditions aren't Far Right either... they're the Hard Libertarians (pro-legalize everything + defund government) and Religious Fanatics like the Westborough Baptists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh,<br /> <br /> I think of them as Far Right due to the fact they're a global militaristic ultra-nationalist state (the Union itself vs. Sleeper polities ) that exists primarily as defined by their eternal (600 year) war on &quot;The Other&quot; as their chief defining force. The fetishization of technology that they do is notably distinct from pursuit of science itself as the Union exists to define scientific parameters for the public even in the wake of not being true. Which is to say they are the masters of proganda and fake news. Very Umberto Eco's points of fascism.<br /> <br /> But then again, it's a fictional organization and does not correspond to RL at all because I've had plenty of fans give good arguments that it fits a lot of Right Wing conspiracy theories as well.<br /> <br /> It's obviously something up to the Storytellers and I concede the argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T12:01:08-07:00","id":1462688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462677#post1462677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you say so, I suppose I think recent years has me less comfortable with Far Right, &quot;Hard Men Making Hard Choices&quot;, Surveillance State protagonists.<br /> <br /> To each their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's comparing Apples and Oranges. I'll try to give you an example.<br /> <br /> In the MtA setting, the Traditions are the people that welcome anti-vaccine, flat-earth and anti-mask beliefs. They're the ones where Nationalistic ideas have a place to go. Those aren't ideas welcomed by the whole Council, but by their decree they have a safe place within. While in the Union such nonsense is outright banned as it is against the well being and education of the masses.<br /> <br /> Both groups shun racism, although white-supremacists can be found on both. And you're wrong in thinking they are genocides, both groups find genocide abhorrent. I don't know where you even found this bit. They had a tendency for some ethnocentrism, but that was much more author prejudice as in first edition other ethnicities were shown as &quot;good-savages&quot; &quot;primitives&quot; and &quot;exotic&quot; racial stereotypes that the Traditions wanted to protect their right of being like that, while the bad Technocracy wanted to make them use telephones, computers and cotton clothes.<br /> <br /> Don't try to divide them as left and right, because this is not really how it works. They were born from a skewed vision of both the authors had in 1st edition and don't really stand up to this under greater scrutiny, and that was recognized as soon as the middle to end of 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> Oh, and in modern american (and really, most of the world) politics, both are actually pretty left-winged as a whole. The Union isn't against modern democracy, either, as they want to nudge things from afar, even the Ivory Tower, not to overthrow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T12:03:48-07:00","id":1462689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462687#post1462687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's obviously something up to the Storytellers and I concede the argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't wanted to make a bigger deal of it, you just ninja'd me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T17:04:56-07:00","id":1462737,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve never cared much for the Week of Nightmares. Not because it made the Technocracy look good, but because the Technology and the themes of Mage undermined Vampire themes. V:tM is a game about gothic horror, politics, and vampiric scheming and plotting. The Antediluvians and their awakening is a Biblical prophesy, and it will bring about the end times. Killing Ravnos with spirit nukes and space mirrors is something we should see in Rifts or 40K, not Vampire: the Masquerade. Dealing with the Antediluvians shouldn\u2019t just be a matter of sufficient dakka, where Ravnos has x amount of MDC and each nuclear bomb does y amount. That is what I didn\u2019t like about the Week of Nightmares. As far as I\u2019m concerned, there should be no Technocracy at all in V:tM.<br /> <br /> Now, in the Mage setting, the Technocracy is cool and it is fitting that they would use whatever force they have at their disposal to stop a super powerful reality deviant. The Technocracy can be great villains, they can also be great heroes as well. The Technocracy is an institution with many shades of gray that can seem to be villains or heroes from different perspectives. Much like real world powerful institutions/governments can.<br /> <br /> I would agree that the Technocracy are left wing if real world political affiliations were to be applied to them. They are, in a sense, Alex Jones\u2019 conspiracy theories made manifest in a role playing setting. They even have a faction called The New World Order. That doesn\u2019t make the Traditions right wing, they are just a loose affiliation of ideologies that don\u2019t fit into the Technocracy\u2019s world view, which could include the far right among numerous other world views, though they are called the \u201cTraditions\u201d after all - they represent old beliefs and traditions that won\u2019t surrender to modernity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T17:17:36-07:00","id":1462740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462737#post1462737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would agree that the Technocracy are left wing if real world political affiliations were to be applied to them. They are, in a sense, Alex Jones\u2019 conspiracy theories made manifest in a role playing setting. They even have a faction called The New World Order. That doesn\u2019t make the Traditions right wing, they are just a loose affiliation of ideologies that don\u2019t fit into the Technocracy\u2019s world view, which could include the far right among numerous other world views, though they are called the \u201cTraditions\u201d after all - they represent old beliefs and traditions that won\u2019t surrender to modernity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it would be a very weird Right Wing group compromised of indigenous peoples and brown folk. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T17:27:06-07:00","id":1462742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462740#post1462740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean it would be a very weird Right Wing group compromised of indigenous peoples and brown folk. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of right wing groups that have non-white people. In fact, it might surprise you to learn that there are entire countries out there that are almost entirely non-white that have their own right wing political parties and movements made up of non-white people who are opposed by left wing parties or movements also made up of non-white people. <br /> <br /> Though, the traditions aren\u2019t explicitly right wing, they are anything that doesn\u2019t fit into the Technocracy\u2019s agenda, which includes a bunch of wildly divergent belief systems which would be at odds if the Technocracy weren\u2019t so dominant. Though if there is some indigenous group that wants to preserve their culture, their religion, their language, their way of life before contact with the modern Western world - what else could you call such a group but conservative? The exact culture, religion, and lifestyle they seek to preserve is different from that of a fundamentalist Christian living in Appalachia, but yet they both seek to preserve their traditions and against the same monolithic forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T18:07:32-07:00","id":1462743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462742#post1462742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are plenty of right wing groups that have non-white people.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more the indigenous part that makes the joke work, I think.<br /> <br /> Part of the weirdness of M:TA's Technocracy is they were supposed to have started out as a bunch of decent people then became the EVIL Technocracy....around the 19th century.<br /> <br /> Which is a weird time to say colonialism among mages became really bad.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, can't wait for Victorian Age Mage. I look forward to flying around my airship like Robur, fighting the Queen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T18:31:17-07:00","id":1462746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462740#post1462740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean it would be a very weird Right Wing group compromised of indigenous peoples and brown folk. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>But you have no idea of how much Right-Wing do that irl, especially the far-right.<br /> <br /> People with ultra-nationalistic agendas are extremely racist and xenophobic <i>in their own area</i>, but they tend to form some kinship with equally ultra-nationalists from other places. Watch how world leaders play when dealing with each other. The same also happens at smaller scales if indigenous far-righters think they can get away with it. It is uncommon because they generally can't, but it isn't unheard of.<br /> <br /> Little Brother was frequently depicted as pretty nationalistic in their own way. What would those depictions do if some European Garou offered then a right-wing style alliance in exchange of help to finally expel non-indigenous presence from a big chunk of North America with prejudice? I'm talking secession and Shadowrun-style Native States.<br /> <br /> Not that those are exactly common, as I said both institutions would be fairly left-wing in RL politics. But the Traditions accept extremists of both ends in their midst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T19:02:10-07:00","id":1462752,"title":"","content":"Their human counterparts basically did much such offers.... and then tossed the treaties in the trash after they stopped needing proxy fighters to settle things between each other. I think the WtA general portrays Garou history as a mirror in that regard: the first wave of European Garou made deals to stick to the east coast (esp. the lands without caretakers because of Middle Brother's sacrifice) and keep things that way, and then as colonialism spread west, the European Garou used the changing reality to claim old deals weren't valid any more and demand new ones, rinse, repeat.<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> <br /> Though to repeat myself from far too many other threads: Mage isn't about right vs. left. It's about statism vs. anti-statism (and it's many forms). The Union is an extreme take on statism: they are constantly pushing for the state to control more and more of personal life (even purging elements that supported non-statist cultural expressions like religion). The Union's enemies, from the organized Traditions to the various independent Crafts, have a whole spectrum of disagreements over why they don't like statism, but they all agree they need to fight it. By necessity and time, the Traditions represent as classically liberal anti-statist position where the state is only valid to protect individual liberties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T02:04:48-07:00","id":1462782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462746#post1462746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you have no idea of how much Right-Wing do that irl, especially the far-right.<br /> <br /> People with ultra-nationalistic agendas are extremely racist and xenophobic <i>in their own area</i>, but they tend to form some kinship with equally ultra-nationalists from other places. Watch how world leaders play when dealing with each other. The same also happens at smaller scales if indigenous far-righters think they can get away with it. It is uncommon because they generally can't, but it isn't unheard of.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which explains some off the more racist members of the disparate alliance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-05-2021, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T11:25:59-07:00","id":1462906,"title":"","content":"I thought the Disparate Alliance was one of the worst features of M20.<br /> <br /> There's <i>already</i> a faction for anti-statist traditionalist mages who want to preserve the old ways and keep their brand of magic alive in modern times. It's called the Traditions.<br /> <br /> The Disparates basically seem like inserts to give minority cultures their own faction. Even leaving aside the incongruity in the Dreamspeakers still belonging to the Traditions and the Knights Templar belonging to the Disparates (???), the four factions are meant to cover some really big ideas. The Traditions are the classic wizards keeping myth and wonder alive in a secular age. The Technocracy is the cold and sterile science relentlessly driving that secular age. The Nephandi are existence-hating nihilists who've given up on building a better world. The Marauders are mad wizards who've been shattered by hubris, trauma, and tragedy. Again, these factions cover big ideas that can encompass a wide range of belief systems and sociopolitical ideologies. The Traditions and the Technocracy can be left wing or right wing. They are bigger than that. They represent timeless ideas that were just as relevant in 1992 as they are in 2021.<br /> <br /> And then we have the Disparates. They don't encompass a timeless idea that feels like it could've existed in 1992. They feel pulled from 2010s+ Twitter woke culture that insists on greater representation for groups that were represented just fine in the existing four factions. And, on top, there are some author lines that say they're the best at fighting the Nephandi and better/more hardcore than the Traditions in various ways. They feel like an obvious author favorite and clumsy insert to make the game more culturally sensitive.<br /> <br /> I say this as someone who's pretty politically left-leaning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T11:43:56-07:00","id":1462910,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it feels like they were a big neon sign flashing &quot;Western Culture BAD, outsiders &amp; minorities GOOD&quot; while completely ignoring that at least four of the Traditions aren't primarily composed of Westerners and white people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T12:16:43-07:00","id":1462913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462910#post1462910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it feels like they were a big neon sign flashing &quot;Western Culture BAD, outsiders &amp; minorities GOOD&quot; while completely ignoring that at least four of the Traditions aren't primarily composed of Westerners and white people.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the Hollow Ones were always annoyed everyone assumed they were Traditions. Mostly because the Technocracy didn't care.<br /> <br /> There were Crafts before they banded together but it seems redundant when there were, as stated, already a band of Crafts gathered together for survival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T12:29:14-07:00","id":1462918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462910#post1462910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it feels like they were a big neon sign flashing &quot;Western Culture BAD, outsiders &amp; minorities GOOD&quot; while completely ignoring that at least four of the Traditions aren't primarily composed of Westerners and white people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Akashics - Tibetan mysticism, Cult of Ecstasy - Ecstatics/Dervishes, Celestial Chorus - Middle Eastern Religion (including Jewish, Christian, Muslim, Mithras and Zorostrian), Dreamspeakers - Indigenous Shamanism, Euthanatos - Indo-European Chthonic Mystery Religions, Order of Hermes - Egyptian/Roman/European Hermeticism, Sons of Ether - Mad Science, Verbena - Pre-Christian European Paganism, Virtual Adepts - Reality is a Program.<br /> <br /> The Verbena and the Hermetics are the only ones you could explicitly label European and only the Hermetics if you ignore the Egyptian roots of Hermetic practices or that it includes Houses that embrace African and Asian High Ritual Magic as part of their Order.<br /> <br /> The only way you could accuse the Traditions of being Eurocentric or claim them to not be radically Multicultural is if you're using some toxic definition that counts only absolute exclusion of European culture/populations as acceptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T13:23:05-07:00","id":1462924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462906#post1462906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Disparate Alliance was one of the worst features of M20.</div> </div> </div> </div>I partially disagree.<br /> <br /> The thing with the DA that makes complete sense is their place in the in-setting politics. The Council of Nine Traditions can potentially include each and every rl mystic practice, but in-game it is still a very specific political body, with specific structures and magical traditions that newcomers are required to observe. It isn't a happy union of cultures, it is an institution with its own history and chain of command. And with its own power structure that simply isn't that open. Even among the Traditions not everyone is happy with the Council, and inside each Tradition there is also a lot of conflicts and unhappy marriages among their constituent traditions.<br /> <br /> So I don't think that the Disparate Alliance is a bad idea. Maybe the Knights Templar being there, because of their own history, is. But for many Crafts the Council isn't their champion against the Technocracy, but just another bunch of tyrants wanting to impose their own ways all the same. And in that situation, the DA makes a lot of sense as communications develop among those previously dispersed Crafts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T13:53:50-07:00","id":1462930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462918#post1462918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Akashics - Tibetan mysticism, Cult of Ecstasy - Ecstatics/Dervishes, Celestial Chorus - Middle Eastern Religion (including Jewish, Christian, Muslim, Mithras and Zorostrian), Dreamspeakers - Indigenous Shamanism, Euthanatos - Indo-European Chthonic Mystery Religions, Order of Hermes - Egyptian/Roman/European Hermeticism, Sons of Ether - Mad Science, Verbena - Pre-Christian European Paganism, Virtual Adepts - Reality is a Program.<br /> <br /> The Verbena and the Hermetics are the only ones you could explicitly label European and only the Hermetics if you ignore the Egyptian roots of Hermetic practices or that it includes Houses that embrace African and Asian High Ritual Magic as part of their Order.<br /> <br /> The only way you could accuse the Traditions of being Eurocentric or claim them to not be radically Multicultural is if you're using some toxic definition that counts only absolute exclusion of European culture/populations as acceptable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They aren't Eurocentric, they are however centralised with a command structure, strictures, rules etc, and one that treated the Hollow Ones like crap...I can see why people would leave, or never join in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T14:23:15-07:00","id":1462931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462930#post1462930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't Eurocentric, they are however centralised with a command structure, strictures, rules etc, and one that treated the Hollow Ones like crap...I can see why people would leave, or never join in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the way, most of this command structure <b><u>is</u></b> Eurocentric.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T15:28:46-07:00","id":1462939,"title":"","content":"Besides the Templars are the monster hunting Christians, not the global conspiracy from Assassins Creed. That's the NWO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T20:06:05-07:00","id":1462957,"title":"","content":"I don't mind the DA, but it really only makes sense as a product of the metaplot; hence it feeling out of place with the others.<br /> <br /> As far as anti-statist bickering, if the Traditions are classical liberals, the DA is more the libertarian side of the coin, where the state is only valid as an ad-hoc negotiating body between individuals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462939#post1462939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides the Templars are the monster hunting Christians, not the global conspiracy from Assassins Creed. That's the NWO.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Templars were part of the global conspiracy until the NWO kicked them out, which is part of the oddity of their presence in the DA considering how many other members of the DA the Templars had persecuted while part of the Order of Reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T21:28:32-07:00","id":1462962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462939#post1462939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides the Templars are the monster hunting Christians, not the global conspiracy from Assassins Creed. That's the NWO.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Templars ARE the global conspiracy. They only went their separate ways from the Union because they refused secularism. hey wanted the Technocracy to be all about scienc <b><u>and Christianity as the only acceptable faith</u></b>. Their presence in the DA is quite nonsensical for their lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T21:52:04-07:00","id":1462965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462918#post1462918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Verbena and the Hermetics are the only ones you could explicitly label European and only the Hermetics if you ignore the Egyptian roots of Hermetic practices or that it includes Houses that embrace African and Asian High Ritual Magic as part of their Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought the Wu Lung and Ngoma worked just fine in the Order of Hermes. Some of the Crafts work fine as outsiders, but I thought Revised had a good idea moving more of them into the Traditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only way you could accuse the Traditions of being Eurocentric or claim them to not be radically Multicultural is if you're using some toxic definition that counts only absolute exclusion of European culture/populations as acceptable. </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that was the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T22:16:25-07:00","id":1462972,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, another reason I don't like the Disparates? They don't gel as neatly with the game's metaphysics.<br /> <br /> The Marauders are Dynamism. The Technocracy is Stasis. The Nephandi are Entropy. The Traditions are Balance. The factions represent each branch of the Metaphysic Trinity* (or the union of those branches) and the four types of Avatars. There's good symmetry there. It feels right from a game design and an in-universe perspective.<br /> <br /> The Disparates align with... what branch of the Trinity? I guess Balance too, but that makes them redundant. We already have a faction that covers Balance. It's just another way the new faction feels awkwardly tacked on.<br /> <br /> * It also raises interesting questions--the Marauders and Nephandi are obviously screwed up and can't be allowed to win the Ascension War, so does that mean the Technocracy is too, because any mage society aligning too closely with one Trinity branch is a bad idea? Or, is Stasis actually the only &quot;good&quot; branch? That'd mean Traditions are tainted for their association with Dynamism and Entropy, but less so than the Marauders and Nephandi because they still have some Stasis as a stabilizing influence. This is a fun debate mages can have and the Disparates just muddy the waters, because the Trinity is no longer clearly linked to the main factions in the Ascension War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T22:27:03-07:00","id":1462973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462962#post1462962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Templars ARE the global conspiracy. They only went their separate ways from the Union because they refused secularism. hey wanted the Technocracy to be all about scienc <b><u>and Christianity as the only acceptable faith</u></b>. Their presence in the DA is quite nonsensical for their lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe the Disparate Alliance ones do any world domination anymore.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T00:14:57-07:00","id":1462980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462973#post1462973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe the Disparate Alliance ones do any world domination anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, but then that's being inconsistent. What happened to explain such a radical change in their mindset when their very reason to leave the Union was that non-Christianity was inconceivable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T01:02:11-07:00","id":1462983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462965#post1462965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that was the case.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">There's a lot of assumptions of bad faith in the criticism of the Traditions here that I think is against the arguers rather than the content. Please stop. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T01:04:06-07:00","id":1462984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462980#post1462980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not, but then that's being inconsistent. What happened to explain such a radical change in their mindset when their very reason to leave the Union was that non-Christianity was inconceivable?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the impression I got from their write-up was they were Order of Reasoners who wanted to fight reality deviants not conquer the Earth. The &quot;Christianity is the one true religion&quot; became problematic for them because they believed in it while it was an opiate of the masses for the rest of the Cabal of Pure Thought.<br /> <br /> Sort of like how I've always ran the Followers of Set versus the Lasombra. There's believers in the latter but the latter mostly note how much religion can be used to control people while its more a side effect of the Followers of Set who genuinely believe all of Set's tenets.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T02:02:11-07:00","id":1462986,"title":"","content":"See, to me, the Disparates all seem like they're highly traditional, natural xenophobes with an unwillingness to share or be subject to outside power and thus they want outsiders to fuck off. <br /> <br /> Why the fuck would such people make an alliance when the whole point was they don't want a fucking alliance? Strikes me as yuppie, virtue signalling bullshit of the highest order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T03:11:48-07:00","id":1462988,"title":"","content":"For the same reason most political alliances end up forming: you get wiped out without numbers. The Disparate Alliance is 100% built on the groups hating the Technocrats and Traditions (and the Ascension War just feeding into Nephandi goals) so hard that they'll stomach working together until the two big groups trying to force them all to join a side go away.<br /> <br /> There's no away the Alliance holds if the Union breaks up and the Traditions disband as a unified entity. It exists solely because they're all tired of getting shat on by the bigger factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T04:48:40-07:00","id":1462992,"title":"","content":"Do mages really work so well together globally that locals can't fend them off? They're not vampires who can send wave after wave of neonates at the problem till it goes away. Mages are hard to replace and nodes need to be defended. The Wu Lung, for example; Canonically sexist, very probably racist. But the fact that they're threatened by outsiders gives them very good reason to work together well, <i>with other Wu Lung</i>. How many other disparates have a presence in China? What use is a knights templar in shanghai? And why would a KT come to China to help with matters when he has more pressing issues back home? The two big-dogs are also less inclined to bother the Wu Lung when they're dancing with eachother. <br /> <br /> Anyhow we're wildly off topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T06:58:07-07:00","id":1462996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462965#post1462965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought the Wu Lung and Ngoma worked just fine in the Order of Hermes. Some of the Crafts work fine as outsiders, but I thought Revised had a good idea moving more of them into the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was also the perfect antidote to the various bad racial stereotypes by saying \u201cthere\u2019s more styles of magical practice in Asia than just mystic martial arts; not every magician on the continent of Africa is some tribal Shaman.\u201d It\u2019s acknowledging the practitioners as individuals and not just racial stereotypes.<br /> <br /> Frankly, instead of the Disparate Alliance (the crafts of which had mostly joined the Traditions in Rev), I think a far better approach would have been, sorta like Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom, a look at how the principles of each Tradition can be found around the world (ex. just about every culture has some variation of the cycle of life and death the Euthanatos/Chakravati harness in their practices).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T08:13:39-07:00","id":1463001,"title":"","content":"Probably a good idea to take this to the Mage forum.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T11:26:21-07:00","id":1463011,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element\">Boom</a>, Disparate thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T05:04:05-07:00","id":1463215,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">fmo<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462443#post1462443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Followers of Set specifically define a methuselah as a vampire who's survived a Sothic turn--that is, any vampire who is 1,461 or more years old. I always thought an even better definition was a vampire who's survived one Sothic turn per generation removed from Set. So a 4th-generation Setite &quot;officially&quot; becomes a methuselah at 1,461, a 5th-generation one becomes a methuselah at 2,922, a 6th-generation one becomes a methuselah at 4,383, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Now this is interesting to see strict mythological and religious belief be taken into consideration in this. This gives a strong impression about the Setites' organization, knowledge and seriousness as a Clan.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462443#post1462443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Most probably it is. Though I very much like the idea that there is some mystical or supernatural component to it. A kind higher state of Vampirism that is achieved through a combination of factor, maybe with some additional powers or opportunities unlocked by it. </span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">The leadership of the Tal'Mahe'Ra outlined in their V20 book gives interesting examples to consider in regard to a Kindred being recognized as a Methuselah</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Antoinette Sauveterre is a 6</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><sup>th</sup></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Generation Toreador Embraced in 983. She is a Seraphim in her Sect, noted as being widely respected and sought after, not aligned with the Camarilla or the Sabbat, and is probably one of the foremost authorities among the Bahari. Her description has this cool part: \u201c</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><i>You're a powerful create with an extensive network of allies and those who owe you favors. You rarely get ignored or denied your wishes, and you are impatient with those who do not follow your commands. You can be polite and civil when necessary, but your worship of Lilith has made your cruel and contemptuos to any but your closest allies.</i></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u201d Though she probably is not considered a Methuselah...still, maybe some Kindred would make the consideration, if it is a social or political distinction. Anotoinette is kind of awesome. An over 1000 year old Vampire who is a Seraphim </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><i>and </i>a</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Toreador </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><i>and </i>a</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Bahari leader? A Toreador Bahari is already interesting enough, but with her also being a Seraphim it is all the more intriguing. What a nice combination. And she is noted to prefer to dress in street casual or business casual (not for her are fancy dresses or official suits) Hers picture is also very nice \u2013 so insidious, mysterious, and judgemental.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Pietro is a 5</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><sup>th</sup></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Generation Lasombra Embraced in 250, and is also a Seraphim. Seems like he clearly is a Methuselah. His picture is amazing as well.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Anadja is a 5</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><sup>th</sup></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Generation Ventrue Embraced in 1000, and she is the Del'Roh of the Tal'Mahe'Ra. She kind of misses on the age criterion, but considering her position (held for around 250 years so far) she just might be considered a Methuselah.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462443#post1462443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Etrius is described (out-of-character) as a methuselah in <i>Transylvania Chronicles IV</i>. Which I'd agree with. He's powerful enough to compete on the same level as vampires like Mithras.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">That just reminded me of an in-universe part in some V5 book which has a line for each Camarilla Clan going \u201c<i>Hail [Methuselah's name], [Methuselah's name], [Methuselah's name] spawn of [Antediluvian's name].</i>\u201d The Tremere line has \u201c<i>Hail Tremere, Meerlinda, Etrius, spawn of Tremere.</i>\u201d I kind of dislike it, because it is factually incorrect, and also why is Tremere mentioned twice? Should have been Grimgroth or another of the old guard Tremere. Though it might be a reference to the fact of the ritual self-Embrace. At the same time, I very much like it as an admission of Clan Tremere's status among the Kindred society. Nice to see Tremere Kindred mentioned along with ancient Methuselahs.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462443#post1462443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goratrix is definitely a methuselah too for the same reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Forgot about him. And a Sabbat-aligned Methuselah he is, at that! His defection came late enough that he probably lowered his Generation back when Tremere leaders were doing it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462443#post1462443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree the other councilors probably aren't methuselahs.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Abetorius and Grimgroth could also be considered. Abetorius' Embrace is given as 1103 and Grimgroth's as 1210. Grimgroth was a Mage so this helps in recognizing him at a Methuselah. I don't know about Abetorius, most likely he was one as well considering he got assigned to Middle East straight away back in the early medieval already. Such a responsibility this early implies prior experience in Nightfolk matters.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462443#post1462443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">I also tend to think no other councilors in the Modern Nights are fourth generation.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Some might not even be fifth. Some councilors have had a lot of turnover (like Africa's) and it strains credulity to me that there would happen to be another fourth-generation Tremere waiting in the wings for a spot to open. </span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Abetorius was around for the period of Diablerizing Salubri, so he is 4th Generation in all likelihood. Grimgroth is a Childe of Tremere, after Tremere lowered his Generation to 3rd. I couldn't find information about Xavier de Cincao. Elaine is written to be &quot;15th century French noblewoman&quot;, and while there isn't such confirmation in regard to Wyncham I assume he</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"> is relatively young based on the fact that he replaced his predecessor as Councillor around a hundred years ago.</span></span><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> This leaves Elaine de Calinot and Thomas Wyncham as the the minority in the Council of Seven who were not around to lower their Generation by tracking down a Salubri.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">However, why do you assume that a Salubri Vampire is needed? They could very well track down a Methuselah of another Clan - most likely one not heavily involved with the Camarilla. And certainly there would be some Methuselahs that would be enemies of Clan Tremere. Considering what members of Clan Tremere did in the medieval times to the Salubri, I think they are very skilled and experienced in hunting down even the most ancient Kindred. So newly initiated Inner Councillors would get some help and backup in lowering their Generation. It just makes sense that an Inner Councillor is to be of 4</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><sup>th</sup></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Generation \u2013 consider the mystical connotations, and being able to carry the responsibility and achieve results. And also being able to Embrace 5th Generation Childer might be an important factor too.<br /> <br /> Maybe there is some high level Ritual for lowering Generation that some Tremere Vampires have hidden away? Makes sense as one of the ultimate secrets and rewards within the Tremere Pyramid.</span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462443#post1462443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">There are probably Tremere like Karl Schrekt and Ulugh Begh who are more potent than councilors like Elaine de Calinot and simply don't want her job. Not all councilorships or councilors are created equal. </span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">I have to note that he couldn't just have her position, because he lacks the knowledge, experience, and predispositions that made Elaine de Calinot the choice to be the leader of Tremere efforts in Africa. And consider that maybe Elaine has just the qualities and character that despite her being younger (and probably less skilled in some areas) than these particular old guard Tremere Vampires, she just might be more worthy and suited to be on the Inner Council of Seven. Age is not a strict limit on potential and achievement - Monica Chang created the Path of Technomancy and she is a 12</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><sup>th</sup></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Generation Kindred, Embraced around 1880. Also I think that the 'wild' or 'unknown' continents (Africa, Asia, South America) are not some lost cause assignments. Meerlinda managed to establish herself excellently in North America back then when it was also an unknown, uncertain, and wild area.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">I apologize if I seem too vehement, it is just I am a big Tremere fan (and by extension fan of the entire Council of Seven concept) and I think Elaine the Calinot has one of the best pictures in the World of Darkness (and remember that a picture can tell more than a thousand words). So striking (the throne, the staff), with a symbol in the background, and a very nice pose. I wish there would be more written about her, and the other of the newer Inner Councillors. From what little is written about her, there is one particularly noteworthy detail - back when she was a Pontifex she hunted semi-openly in Africa, going down to a village at night and taking her due. Pretty unusual and bold for a Tremere Vampire, isn't it?<br /> So all in all I disagree with the idea that she is somehow held back by the fact that she is the Councillor with Africa as her assigned area.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-09-2021, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T06:27:22-07:00","id":1463218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463215#post1463215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That just reminded me of an in-universe part in some V5 book which has a line for each Camarilla Clan going \u201c<i>Hail [Methuselah's name], [Methuselah's name], [Methuselah's name] spawn of [Antediluvian's name].</i>\u201d The Tremere line has \u201c<i>Hail Tremere, Meerlinda, Etrius, spawn of Tremere.</i>\u201d I kind of dislike it, because it is factually incorrect, and also why is Tremere mentioned twice? Should have been Grimgroth or another of the old guard Tremere. Though it might be a reference to the fact of the ritual self-Embrace. At the same time, I very much like it as an admission of Clan Tremere's status among the Kindred society. Nice to see Tremere Kindred mentioned along with ancient Methuselahs.<br /> <br /> Forgot about him. And a Sabbat-aligned Methuselah he is, at that! His defection came late enough that he probably lowered his Generation back when Tremere leaders were doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be a difference between edits, but I found &quot;Hail Tremere, Goratrix, and Meerlinda, spawn of Tremere!&quot;. It's odd that Etrius is absent from that and we still have &quot;Tremere&quot;, &quot;spawn of Tremere&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T07:08:56-07:00","id":1463221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463218#post1463218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This might be a difference between edits, but I found &quot;Hail Tremere, Goratrix, and Meerlinda, spawn of Tremere!&quot;. It's odd that Etrius is absent from that and we still have &quot;Tremere&quot;, &quot;spawn of Tremere&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think I simply misremembered it. I think it should have been &quot;Hail Meerlinda, Etrius, and Goratrix, spawn of Tremere!&quot;. Or maybe Abetorius or Grimgroth instead of Goratrix. Still incorrect though (the original Tremere Council of Seven self-embraced, after all), but I suppose it gets a point across. The inclusion of Goratrix is interesting, considering this is from V5 Camarilla book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-09-2021, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T09:08:17-07:00","id":1463230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463221#post1463221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I simply misremembered it. I think it should have been &quot;Hail Meerlinda, Etrius, and Goratrix, spawn of Tremere!&quot;. Or maybe Abetorius or Grimgroth instead of Goratrix. Still incorrect though (the original Tremere Council of Seven self-embraced, after all), but I suppose it gets a point across. The inclusion of Goratrix is interesting, considering this is from V5 Camarilla book.</div> </div> </div> </div>The chant does also hail Ur-Shulgi. Although the whole ceremony sounds like a black mass for the sake of transgression than a serious cult with its own theology, so they might not be too concerned about details like what the methuselahs actually want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T12:19:49-07:00","id":1463247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462443#post1462443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Followers of Set specifically define a methuselah as a vampire who's survived a Sothic turn--that is, any vampire who is 1,461 or more years old.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463215#post1463215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now this is interesting to see strict mythological and religious belief be taken into consideration in this. This gives a strong impression about the Setites' organization, knowledge and seriousness as a Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I forgot to comment earlier: a Sothic turn is actually 1,460 years on our counting, and the Setites would know that. The Sothic Cycle was the Egyptian way to correct that extra \u00bc of a day in the end of the year that we correct through leap years. A Sothic Cycle of 1,461 Egyptian years (365 days) is exactly the same as a current cycle of 1,460 years (365 day plus leap years of 366 days). The first year of a Sothic Cycle is marked by the rising of the star Sirius in 19 July.<br /> <br /> For the Setites the current calendar would mostly be considered an improvement anyway, as it corrects most astronomical imprecision within the Civil Calendar, and it is easy enough to keep track of the Egyptian Civil Calendar in tandem with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463215#post1463215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anadja is a 5th Generation Ventrue Embraced in 1000, and she is the Del'Roh of the Tal'Mahe'Ra. She kind of misses on the age criterion,</div> </div> </div> </div>We're in the 21st century, since you're talking a V20 book she doesn't miss it anymore. Although it is quite early, going strictly by the 1 thousand criteria she's there already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463215#post1463215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201c<i>Hail Tremere, Meerlinda, Etrius, spawn of Tremere.</i>\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if the line does have Tremere two times it may stand correct. He is Tremere (the person), spawn of Tremere (the House). They were already called Tremere as an organization before they were a clan, as this was the name of their Hermetic House.<br /> <br /> The founders, specifically, can also be considered Methuselahs because they already had centuries of life before their embrace, as House Tremere was foremost in magic for life extension and immortality among the Order of Hermes. Meerlinda, as an example, had about 300 years when they &quot;self-embraced&quot;.<br /> <br /> And the House reference is more likely because if it was considered by the creator of the ritual they wouldn't be 'spawn of Tremere', either, but 'spawn of Goratrix', who was the creator of the concoction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463215#post1463215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">assigned to Middle East straight away back in the early medieval already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitions, definitions. Early times of the DA setting, not early Middle Ages. Early Middle Ages is a well defined period that ends around the beginning of the 11th century, they weren't even vampires by them. From a historical POV the DA setting is almost at the end of the Middle Ages.<br /> <br /> And gaining responsibilities at this point isn't that impressive in a vampiric sense. At this time Clan Tremere is still very new, the conversion of House Tremere into vampires just begun. Despite Goratrix giving the idea earlier, the decision for a slow conversion into vampires was only really taken by Tremere in 1055, and it was subtle enough to only be discovered in 1199, even then &quot;light&quot; enough for judgement be passed by the Order of Hermes only in 1202 and still with House Tytalus being against condemnation.<br /> <br /> So the whole debacle was really new and the Tremere couldn't really rely on experienced vampires because this was not a thing among them yet. Only talent as mortal Magi counted, and many were Embraced already with big duties in mind, as was with Grimgroth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463215#post1463215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abetorius was around for the period of Diablerizing Salubri, so he is 4th Generation in all likelihood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, those two specifically are indeed 4th gen. Abetorius was Embraced by an already 4th gen Meerlinda and later lowered through diablerie. Grimgroth was Embraced by an already 3th gen Tremere, being maybe the first &quot;legit&quot; 4th gen in the clan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463215#post1463215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, why do you assume that a Salubri Vampire is needed? They could very well track down a Methuselah of another Clan</div> </div> </div> </div>The founders aren't legit 4th gen. The ritual made them something between 6th and 10th equivalent. They got to 4th exclusively through diablerie. That way it is very unlikely that they had any qualms about diablerizing outside the Salubri. Especially since they were already in a war with the Tzimisce and the creation of the Gargoyles attracted the Nosferatu and Gangrel to this war. This war was already older than their self-Embrace, it started with Tremere occupation of Transilvanya in the early 800's, a century before the foundation of Ceoris.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463215#post1463215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe there is some high level Ritual for lowering Generation that some Tremere Vampires have hidden away?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlikely, first because they have a strong association with diablerie, second because this is specifically an Assamite thing, so it would step on some thematic toes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463215#post1463215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I think that the 'wild' or 'unknown' continents (Africa, Asia, South America) are not some lost cause assignments.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't a notion House Tremere had in the early 11th century. It is a notion US citizens have due to poor education on world history. By the time the big center of culture for most European scholars was the Mediterranean Sea, including North Africa and the Middle East. Despite little contact China and India are known due to the Silk Road. The Islamic occupation of the Iberian Peninsula brought academic contact that was fundamental in the rediscovery of Greek philosophy in Europe. The Tremere are a Hermetic House, they literally put a lot of faith in Egyptian mysticism. And after discovery South America was far more relevant for Europe than North America up to the beginning of the 20th century, economically and politically.<br /> <br /> Up until the First World War North America is among the most backwaters place in the world by European standards, especially the US.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T23:57:46-07:00","id":1463291,"title":"","content":"How does Vaulderie work? Sorry if this has already been answered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;bas