> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's incredibly lazy. What rules does it actually have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T12:57:05-07:00","id":1463343,"title":"","content":"Outside of some new powers, I don't believe the book has any major rules in it, as it's a ST guide book, not a character (even as antagonists) creation book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T13:09:58-07:00","id":1463344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463343#post1463343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of some new powers, I don't believe the book has any major rules in it, as it's a ST guide book, not a character (even as antagonists) creation book.</div> </div> </div> </div> So from the perspective on an experienced gm and thr \u00a340 price tag does it actually offer anything at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T14:02:23-07:00","id":1463347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463344#post1463344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So from the perspective on an experienced gm and thr \u00a340 price tag does it actually offer anything at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the better reviews I've seen. It's long, but pretty in-depth. I would say this does not amount to a $45 Sect Book, but rather a $20 &quot;<i>Clanbook: Sabbat</i>,&quot; if you will. Some updates, definitely well-written, and a nice break from in-character essays, at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kFi2K_KYe1M&amp;t=320\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kFi2K_KYe1M&amp;t=320\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kFi2K_KYe1M&amp;t=320\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kFi2K_KYe1M&amp;t=320 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T14:30:02-07:00","id":1463349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463344#post1463344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So from the perspective on an experienced gm and thr \u00a340 price tag does it actually offer anything at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't own it, and I haven't read through it, but I feel that's going to be very subjective. Well, actually, I don't know anyone that agrees it's worth the sticker price regardless of quality (well, besides people that think RPG books are, in general, vastly under priced and thus make it very hard for games to be profitable but that's whole different issue).<br /> <br /> From what I gather unless you're planning to run the Sabbat in the V5 setting and thus want the updates on what's happened to them and how to implement the new take on them... there's not really a lot to get out of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T15:03:44-07:00","id":1463351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463344#post1463344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So from the perspective on an experienced gm and thr \u00a340 price tag does it actually offer anything at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it's fantastic setting building and lore but it's overpriced to the extreme.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T09:53:33-07:00","id":1463432,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.strangeassembly.com/2021/review-sabbat-the-black-hand-vampire-the-masquerade\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.strangeassembly.com/2021...the-masquerade</a><br /> <br /> Strange Assembly, like me and 25 Years, gives the book very high praise.<br /> <br /> EXAMPLE: <i>The Sabbat of V5 is in some ways a purer Sabbat, more reminiscent of the original conception of the sect. Gone are the byzantine political structures, the multiple ancient subsects, the pseudo-Masquerade, and the Camarilla-like politics that were added to make the Sabbat more functional for use as protagonists. The Sabbat has been ravaged by the Second Inquisition and flinging itself headlong into the Gehenna War. Mexico City has been abandoned. The title of Regent ostensibly exists, but is empty. Cardinals are just those Sabbat with a large enough war party and visions of grandeur. Instead, the Sabbat are stripped down to their antagonistic roots \u2013 a fanatical enemy hellbent on destruction and heedless of the Masquerade. It is not a coincidence that shifting the Sabbat away from the notion of being potential protagonists has also stripped them of many aspects that made that just another Camarilla \u2013 just another a worldwide political organization of vampires, albeit with a different sort of rhetoric and Blood Bonds.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T10:42:19-07:00","id":1463438,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat is back to just being a way of saying that cities in Latin America are so cartoonishily violent that even vampires fear, but it's no harm to the Masquerade because here in the south we're just dumb mongrels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T10:57:31-07:00","id":1463440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463438#post1463438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat is back to just being a way of saying that cities in Latin America are so cartoonishily violent that even vampires fear, but it's no harm to the Masquerade because here in the south we're just dumb mongrels.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the opposite of that. Part of the reason I feel the Sabbat is no longer holding territory is that White Wolf is sick of telling non-American players, &quot;Oh, by the way, the Sabbat rules your territory and made it a murderous hellhole.&quot; This is hearsay but this is literally why Mexico City is Camarilla now because, shock of shocks, there's a bunch of Mexican City V:TM players who don't like their city being portrayed as Mordor.<br /> <br /> It's also 100% confirmed why Montreal is Camarilla because the CHAPTERS creative team were V:TM fans...in Montreal. They just didn't like the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> What you're describing is the Sabbat up until V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-11-2021, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T11:18:04-07:00","id":1463443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463440#post1463440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's the opposite of that. Part of the reason I feel the Sabbat is no longer holding territory is that White Wolf is sick of telling non-American players, &quot;Oh, by the way, the Sabbat rules your territory and made it a murderous hellhole.&quot; This is hearsay but this is literally why Mexico City is Camarilla now because, shock of shocks, there's a bunch of Mexican City V:TM players who don't like their city being portrayed as Mordor.<br /> <br /> It's also 100% confirmed why Montreal is Camarilla because the CHAPTERS creative team were V:TM fans...in Montreal. They just didn't like the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> What you're describing is the Sabbat up until V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Cam players get fanservice and Sabbat players get hammered back into our badwrongfun box. Nice. I wish they could just be honest and the us to go f ourselves, and be done with the drip feeding hints of maybe this books is kinda Sabbat when that is always a lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 10-11-2021, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T11:37:53-07:00","id":1463444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463443#post1463443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Cam players get fanservice and Sabbat players get hammered back into our badwrongfun box. Nice. I wish they could just be honest and the us to go f ourselves, and be done with the drip feeding hints of maybe this books is kinda Sabbat when that is always a lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we can both acknowledge Mexico was overdone as Central American Mordor. The Nosferatu there used to have pool parties with Nephandi and Black Spiral Dancers and I'm not even exaggerating.<br /> <br /> But yes, a lot of changes seem to be Paradox asking, &quot;Okay, who is still a fan of White Wolf in 2018? Oh, lots of people in Central and South America? Europe? LARPers? Let's cater to them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T14:51:15-07:00","id":1463472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463432#post1463432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strange Assembly, like me and 25 Years, gives the book very high praise.</div> </div> </div> </div>That feels a bit... cherry picked? The review is positive, but acknowledges that significant portion of fans aren't going to like it because of how much it tossed previous stuff. Many of the same flaws are noted that make the book a lot less than it could have been (though the price isn't mentioned in that one...).<br /> <br /> It also seems to continue the trend of forgetting that the first Players Guide to the Sabbat was published in 1992, and the idea the game supprting playing Sabbat didn't magically spring up in Revised; mostly to justify the claim that this represents some sort of &quot;return to original form,&quot; narrative that doesn't hold up to scrutiny for those of us that remember what VtM 1e and early 2e actually looked like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463440#post1463440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the opposite of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure the residents of Tijuana appreciate their city continuing to be the &quot;acceptable hellhole&quot; for non-Mexican creatives to use when they want to make somewhere in Mexico actively horrible. Since the Sabbat still hold it.<br /> <br /> And the Sabbat losing territory so heavily told as them losing Central and South American cities isn't the opposite. It's just a different problem where the &quot;White&quot; North American and European focused Camarilla is storming into Latin America to &quot;liberate&quot; them from the Sabbat. That's not a good narrative for anyone that understand the history of the places involved.<br /> <br /> Lets also remember that pre-V5 many major cities in Latin America were Independent with no affiliation to the Camarilla, Sabbat, or Anarchs. Ignoring that just makes the &quot;Cam take over Sabbat territory,&quot; narrative even worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Part of the reason I feel the Sabbat is no longer holding territory is that White Wolf is sick of telling non-American players, &quot;Oh, by the way, the Sabbat rules your territory and made it a murderous hellhole.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Then... maybe listening to someone from Brazil that isn't getting that message from all of this is a sign that Paradox's attempts - however well intentioned - aren't necessarily doing what they think they're doing.<br /> <br /> She obviously can't speak for everyone living in Latin America, but she's someone that's supposed to be getting this message, not you or I. And if she's not feeling it...maybe look at the text for something that actually backs it up with a good narrative instead of a different bad narrative to change her mind instead of talking about Paradox's intentions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is hearsay but this is literally why Mexico City is Camarilla now because, shock of shocks, there's a bunch of Mexican City V:TM players who don't like their city being portrayed as Mordor. </div> </div> </div>That doesn't justify everything in the book by itself. I never met or talked to anyone from Miami that had a problem with the official material on it being controlled by the Sabbat (probably because that's mostly Revised, and thus didn't have the 2e height of gonzo stuff that Mexico City got hit with). Lots of described Sabbat cities weren't WoD: Mordor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463444#post1463444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yes, a lot of changes seem to be Paradox asking, &quot;Okay, who is still a fan of White Wolf in 2018? Oh, lots of people in Central and South America? Europe? LARPers? Let's cater to them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. But are they actually doing a good job of that?<br /> <br /> What cities have shown up with detailed descriptions? Which cities have books or games set in it? Seems pretty US biased to me.<br /> <br /> Are people from Central and South America being given a setting where vampires from their part of the world have agency and thus they have agency, or are they still just geopolitical pawns for foreign vampires to push around because they don't actually get to be important on their own?<br /> <br /> Austrians are told that as a citizenry they don't give a shit about the most massive counter-terrorist operation in a major metropolitan area that destroyed a number of historical buildings happened in their capital with no accountability to the foreign governments that did it or the government of Austria for letting it happen. Germany and the UK are similarly completely oblivious or OK with similar hyper-aggressive police state actions against unknown and covered up &quot;bad guys&quot; with no accountability from their governments despite the turmoil in their largest cities. Spanish and Portuguese citizens are still dealing with being the acceptable place to put most European Sabbat,and the excuse of it being a former power base for the Lasombra doesn't work with the Lasombra defecting to the Cam. Oh,and I'm sure the Balkan countries continuing to have a bad international reputation makes them feel catered to as Belgrade is Sabbat territory.<br /> <br /> Intentions are great, but reality matters more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T15:03:29-07:00","id":1463474,"title":"","content":"I'm not attempting to lecture <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> , just pointing out Paradox's plans. I also think ANY Sabbat cities left are going to have the problem listed above. Which means the argument is they haven't gone FAR ENOUGH to remove the Sabbat as the one dimensional baddies ruling over Latin America. I also note that the opinion on the Sabbat ruling over cities being offensive I have heard from Mexican and Canadian fans both. So it's not my opinion (which I don't feel comfortable judging).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That doesn't justify everything in the book by itself. I never met or talked to anyone from Miami that had a problem with the official material on it being controlled by the Sabbat (probably because that's mostly Revised, and thus didn't have the 2e height of gonzo stuff that Mexico City got hit with). Lots of described Sabbat cities weren't WoD: Mordor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amusingly in contrast to my Mexican associates, one of my online gaming groups is entirely composed of Floridians and their opinion is, &quot;The Sabbat controls Miami? Sounds legit.&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> OK. But are they actually doing a good job of that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not qualified to judge that and I certainly don't begrudge others for thinking they aren't. However, the point is that Paradox DOES recognize it as a problem and wanted to try to reverse it. I'm not suggesting they're doing it well, only that the problem is not one created by V5 but one that is trying to address it.<br /> <br /> Notably, I wanted to also bring up OPP created the Drowned to address the Sabbat issue. The whole &quot;Native vampires taking back Latin America from the Sabbat.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Austrians are told that as a citizenry they don't give a shit about the most massive counter-terrorist operation in a major metropolitan area that destroyed a number of historical buildings happened in their capital with no accountability to the foreign governments that did it or the government of Austria for letting it happen. Germany and the UK are similarly completely oblivious or OK with similar hyper-aggressive police state actions against unknown and covered up &quot;bad guys&quot; with no accountability from their governments despite the turmoil in their largest cities. Spanish and Portuguese citizens are still dealing with being the acceptable place to put most European Sabbat,and the excuse of it being a former power base for the Lasombra doesn't work with the Lasombra defecting to the Cam. Oh,and I'm sure the Balkan countries continuing to have a bad international reputation makes them feel catered to as Belgrade is Sabbat territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which kind of dovetails back to my point: the Sabbat having territory is something V5 is trying to stop because of the inherent racism and nationalism. The problem is that it seems to be half-measures. But it definitely is taking steps to address it unlike previous editions that were all in on it.<br /> <br /> Also, the Austrians don't believe that the buildings were blown up by the Austrian government (presumably as part of allied but member NATO relations) but they believe Al-Qaeda blew them up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-11-2021, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T15:26:24-07:00","id":1463479,"title":"","content":"I would actually be very interested in what WOULD be a very good way to address the issue and would love to hear pitches as its something I've struggled with myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T16:23:02-07:00","id":1463486,"title":"","content":"I can't judge Paradox's plans, I can judge their results.<br /> <br /> When I read 1st ed core for the first time, the Sabbat was described as basically Sauron's Army. But also as a rumor, something no one really knows about and many suspected to be just BS invented to keep Neonates from trying their luck in those cities. I loved it. I liked to imagine what the truth could be, as the basic description was too obviously bullshit. I didn't wanted to play a game where the villains were a bunch of psychos eternally on cocaine implying that Latin Americans, or anyone for that matter, live in Mordor and are too dumb for this to be a Masquerade breach.<br /> <br /> The moment I started to hear that WW made the Sabbat be exactly what the rumors said, I got furious. It would be about a decade and a half before I gave them the right of the doubt and start to read things about the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> And lo and behold, I found out that the Sabbat was more complex than that. It wasn't exactly fine, but it got to be far better than their initial depiction and than other Camarilla or fucked-up players made it appear to be. What's more, there was material that I could really focus on and, instead of just dump the whole concept of the sect, I could work with it to have a good adversary for my play style. One that didn't meant I'm a dumb mongrel living in Mordor.<br /> <br /> Rio de Janeiro being Sabbat isn't the problem. What the Sabbat meant is the problem. Making the Sabbat more complex changed what it meant. Now we just aren't Mordor anymore because the White Knights of the North saved us, how grateful I should be... it isn't as if in the last time we've got a military coup followed by about 20 years of US-sanctioned dictatorship that we still feel the deep marks in our society and find secret mass graves from time to time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463479#post1463479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would actually be very interested in what WOULD be a very good way to address the issue and would love to hear pitches as its something I've struggled with myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Sabbat? Reinforce nuance instead of ditching it. The problem with a setting like WoD is that you're always talking about a representation of real people. This is not an utterly fictional world, it is a mirror to ours, so making associations is unavoidable. Every assumption of the setting will inevitably be an assumption about real places, real things, real people. And it is such on design, as the setting was created to be a social criticism.<br /> <br /> You must understand the irl side of an issue to make decisions ad be prepared to own your decisions. Preferably consult with people related to that or let then be the authors. All over the place it is the same core problem: this is about real people. Real people live in slums, real people live in every country and continent, real people are brainwashed by cults, real people become extremists, real people see their loved ones becoming extremists, real people are in both sides of every conflict, no side is more real than the other.<br /> <br /> So the solution can't be to ask which people won't care about their hometowns becoming Mordor, or which group is ok to treat as Sauron's Army. It is to accept that every conflict is nuanced and offer players the tools to explore and adapt such nuances, and do it walking with the people you want to represent instead of showing off your good will to them. And unfortunately, yes, that means the WoD won't have a lot of places for pure evil irredeemable villains. The real world don't offer easy paths for goodness, its dark mirror shouldn't, either.<br /> <br /> OBS.: I live far from Rio de Janeiro, but my father's family is from there, so I know the city a little and went there several times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T16:24:44-07:00","id":1463487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463432#post1463432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.strangeassembly.com/2021/review-sabbat-the-black-hand-vampire-the-masquerade\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.strangeassembly.com/2021...the-masquerade</a><br /> <br /> Strange Assembly, like me and 25 Years, gives the book very high praise.<br /> <br /> EXAMPLE: <i>The Sabbat of V5 is in some ways a purer Sabbat, more reminiscent of the original conception of the sect. Gone are the byzantine political structures, the multiple ancient subsects, the pseudo-Masquerade, and the Camarilla-like politics that were added to make the Sabbat more functional for use as protagonists. The Sabbat has been ravaged by the Second Inquisition and flinging itself headlong into the Gehenna War. Mexico City has been abandoned. The title of Regent ostensibly exists, but is empty. Cardinals are just those Sabbat with a large enough war party and visions of grandeur. Instead, the Sabbat are stripped down to their antagonistic roots \u2013 a fanatical enemy hellbent on destruction and heedless of the Masquerade. It is not a coincidence that shifting the Sabbat away from the notion of being potential protagonists has also stripped them of many aspects that made that just another Camarilla \u2013 just another a worldwide political organization of vampires, albeit with a different sort of rhetoric and Blood Bonds.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This review you're quoting verges on feeling like, even in just this one paragraph, a lecture that V5 Sabbat is good because the way the Sabbat were written for some 19+ years of the game (I was going to cut it off at V20, but it's not like V20 changed the Sabbat especially, so, 19+ it is) was creatively bankrupt. If you don't feel like that's telling a bunch of people who had been playing VtM for that amount of time &quot;what you liked about the way this thing in the game was portrayed for the majority of its existence was wrong&quot;, I'm unsure of what to say there. It's less a review of why V5 Sabbat is good for any actual merit to do with the book in terms of quality or consistency of its own writing, or even value as a gaming aid, and more that it's good because it got rid of things the reviewer had a grudge against for some time. And that for me is one of the huge problems of 5th edition overall. It feels like vanishingly few people can actually talk about why it is a good edition on its own merits and quality, instead having to default to why they so very much disliked the VtM that came before it and explaining why it was wrong that people liked it. That makes it feel less like a game of its own and more like some fans (and fans who became writers) of vampire getting to feel vindicated on the internet and in LARPs, because the game now agrees with them.<br /> <br /> When people note that part of their problem with V5 is that it seems basically like saying &quot;almost everything significant after the corebook was a mistake and you didn't like or understand quality VtM gaming if you liked it&quot; and how stunningly insulting that is, reviews like this seem to be replying to that with &quot;well exactly!&quot;<br /> <br /> And it seems like when people point that out, the default then becomes trying to lecture that in fact in addition to being bad at gaming, it was also morally wrong to have enjoyed VtM for the past 19+ years or so as far as post 1e corebook material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 10-11-2021, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T16:26:22-07:00","id":1463489,"title":"","content":"Thanks for that nuanced response! Very well-written and informative as well as much appreciated.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T16:28:55-07:00","id":1463490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463487#post1463487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This review you're quoting verges on feeling like, even in just this one paragraph, a lecture that V5 Sabbat is good because the way the Sabbat were written for some 19 years of the game was creatively bankrupt. If you don't feel like that's telling a bunch of people who had been playing VtM for that amount of time &quot;what you liked about the game for the majority of its existence was wrong&quot;, I'm unsure of what to say there. It's less a review of why V5 Sabbat is good for any actual merit to do with the book in terms of quality or consistency of its own writing, or even value as a gaming, and more that it's good because it got rid of things the reviewer had a grudge against for some time. And that for me is one of the huge problems of 5th edition overall. <b>It feels like vanishingly few people can actually talk about why it is a good edition on its own merits and quality, instead having to default to why they so very much disliked the VtM that came before it and explaining why it was wrong that people liked it. </b>That makes it feel less like a game of its own and more like some fans (and fans who became writers) of vampire getting to feel vindicated on the internet and in LARPs, because the game now agrees with them.<br /> <br /> When people note that part of their problem with V5 is that it seems basically like saying &quot;almost everything significant after the corebook was a mistake and you didn't like or understand quality VtM gaming if you liked it&quot; and how stunningly insulting that is, reviews like this seem to be replying to that with &quot;well exactly!&quot;<br /> <br /> And it seems like when people point that out, the default then becomes trying to lecture that in fact in addition to being bad at gaming, it was also morally wrong to have enjoyed VtM for the past 19 years or so as far as post 1e corebook material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, the review says, &quot;It's utterly valueless for Sabbat PCs and running Sabbat games but I'm only judging it for its presentation of Sabbat as antagonists.&quot; Which feels like it acknowledges very much it is not a book for those looking for the other and doesn't make a judgement on that.<br /> <br /> Should it, though?<br /> <br /> The book never pretends to be a book for playing and doesn't judge past playstyles. It just presents one that doesn't include that. I don't think Strange Assembly makes a statement against the Sabbat but just says this does a good job of portraying what they clearly state is the goal.<br /> <br /> <b>Regarding the bolded text: </b>Actually, that would be the primary argument for this book. The book doesn't attempt to adapt previous material but presents its own thing to be judged on its own merits. It doesn't attempt to deal in nostalgia but actively tries to present the Sabbat concept in a new way. I think that is partially why I approve of the book because rather than split the difference, they present the rebooted Sabbat in a way that represents it as something to be held to its own standard and usefulness. It is an antagonists book and says so in the first page. It doesn't split the difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-11-2021, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T16:54:00-07:00","id":1463497,"title":"","content":"<b>My opinion of the Sabbat as a Sabbat ST and player</b><br /> <br /> I think I should share my opinion of someone who has run extensive amounts of Sabbat games and played multiple Sabbat characters. I have reviewed the book as a more general storyteller and someone who reviews books on their own artistic merits. But the visceral response of many people is not from the perspective of a neutral observer but someone who is heavily invested in Sabbat play and storytelling. I thought I would share my opinion from someone who has multiple characters from the Sword of Caine.<br /> <br /> The book is pretty damn useless.<br /> <br /> There's a few interesting tidbits here and there for Disciplines and angles for the Sabbat ritae as well as living with certain paths. I also like the idea of how the Sabbat might incorporate Thin Bloods and &quot;Antitribu are now more important than Clan--the Tzimisce and Lasombra are nothing special anymore either.&quot; However, there's only really one way to use this book and presentation of the Sabbat if you are a die hard Path of Caine follower like myself.<br /> <br /> This book is about how the Sabbat died.<br /> <br /> I can easily tell you how to run a Chroncile about how the Sabbat got taken over by shovel heads, religious fanatics, and the most degenerate Low Path followers. I've actually run that campaign a couple of times because the erudite Nietzschean ubermensch vampires that I tended to play have always struggled against the lowest common denominator of the Black Hand. Perhaps why I was prepped for it, unknowingly, that the Sabbat were going to die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I never objected to Lucita joining the Sabbat. I objected to the Lasombra Trilogy depicting her as joining the stupid-evil Sabbat. Lucita was already an evil Elder. She just didn't need to become a &quot;I kill orphans because I am BADASS&quot; dummy as well as evil. </div> </div> </div>However, this is not the story for someone who wants to see the Sword of Caine rise above its worst impulses. This is basically the story of Los Angeles by Night and the Anarchs where after they successfully acquired California, the Anarchs turned on each other to make a bunch of gang fiefdoms that are worse to live in as a Cainite than the Camarilla. I am 100% down to be able to tell the story of watching your faction become a parody of itself. However, there's no room for actual continued Sabbat play. It also is ONE story you can tell about the Sabbat. This is the Prequel Jedi period and rise of the Empire. If your ST isn't willing to let you kill Palpatine and Dooku/Anakin then it's going to be pretty depressing.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat of V5 are a parody of themselves. A not unbelievable parody that combines militia men, ISIS, gangs, and cultists but these are the Sabbat throwing away being Dracula and deciding to go all in on THIRTY DAYS OF NIGHT as well as VAMPIRE$. The 30 Days of Night and Vampire$ undead were always there. However, it is equivalent to the Brujah overthrowing Critias and becoming 100% iconoclasts. Which was actually kind of the story of V:TDA where the Brujah were getting dumber every century. I mean, Cristof is one of the smarter Brujah they embraced in the Dark Ages and Cristof is a moron.<br /> <br /> If you don't want/believe that the Sabbat's lowest common denominator will eventually overwhelm the secret manipulators then this will not be a story you want to tell. It's a story of the mob gaining control of the revolution and turning it into a Reign of Terror (and we were pretty Reign of Terror-y to begin with).<br /> <br /> Rats leaving a sinking ship is certainly a story arc to get with the PCs joining the Anarchs or the Camarilla (Or Ashirra or Inconnu) is there. I feel like a better story would have been to have given Blood Cult options to join. A &quot;True Sabbat&quot; that tries to rebuild what was lost or the Black Hand having become a separate organization from the swarm of locusts. I'm not afraid of tragedy in my vampire games, obviously, but if you're going to SINK a sect then you should include OPTIONS for past players.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat book should have had a whole ****ing chapter about, &quot;So what does your Sabbat PC do now?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-11-2021, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T17:01:56-07:00","id":1463501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463490#post1463490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, the review says, &quot;It's utterly valueless for Sabbat PCs and running Sabbat games but I'm only judging it for its presentation of Sabbat as antagonists.&quot; Which feels like it acknowledges very much it is not a book for those looking for the other and doesn't make a judgement on that.<br /> <br /> Should it, though?<br /> <br /> The book never pretends to be a book for playing and doesn't judge past playstyles. It just presents one that doesn't include that. I don't think Strange Assembly makes a statement against the Sabbat but just says this does a good job of portraying what they clearly state is the goal.<br /> <br /> <b>Regarding the bolded text: </b>Actually, that would be the primary argument for this book. The book doesn't attempt to adapt previous material but presents its own thing to be judged on its own merits. It doesn't attempt to deal in nostalgia but actively tries to present the Sabbat concept in a new way. I think that is partially why I approve of the book because rather than split the difference, they present the rebooted Sabbat in a way that represents it as something to be held to its own standard and usefulness. It is an antagonists book and says so in the first page. It doesn't split the difference.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually plunked down money for V5 Sabbat and read through it, because, I don't know, I've been into VtM for a while and keep hoping that I can salvage something out of V5 instead of feeling utterly pushed out of a game I got a lot of enjoyment from and there were all these posts from several writers to the tune of &quot;you just have to be patient&quot;. I'm not even that big a fan of the Sabbat but I certainly appreciated that the option of them existed as something playable. Feeling that the book doesn't judge past playstyles is not something that really jives with a book that functionally works pretty hard to make those past playstyles non viable. Even something simple like giving some rules for the vaudlerie of substance, which would have taken maybe a couple of paragraphs gets a nope. The book devotes space specifically to explaining why the Sabbat no longer works like it does (which, basically is pretty much using space in a book for &quot;here's why you can't play it like you did anymore&quot;), but cannot devote space to even some foundational rules stuff. The book itself makes the choice not to exist outside of its previous context.<br /> <br /> The idea that it &quot;presents the Sabbat in a new way&quot; when the praise for it, praise you yourself are quoting to compliment and note as yet another positive review, is being phrased as &quot;restoring the original feel of the Sabbat&quot; doesn't especially go together. Saying that the review you're trumpeting does not make a judgement doesn't feel possible when the very paragraph you quote of said revue comes off as pretty disdainful of how the Sabbat had been written post the core. Calling the V5 portrayal &quot;purer&quot; and statements like &quot;just another Camarilla&quot; are not things a person trying to sound benign about things says, as far as language. It's being judged just fine. You yourself devoted any number of posts in this thread to taking things to an outright moral dimension of why the Sabbat needed to be redone. There is an element of judgement that seems to unavoidably come with this praise, and it stands out. It makes the idea that people appreciate this book for building something up, instead of that they appreciate it for tearing something down, feel thin.<br /> <br /> It doesn't present the Sabbat in a new way, it mostly wants to present the Sabbat in the oldest way it possibly could with some added frills, and significant chunks of the book mostly exist as a Watsonian attempt to say why it makes sense to do so, as if to dodge the Doylist implications of what the underlying reasons come off as.<br /> <br /> The book doesn't add options, it takes them away, and puts visible effort into taking them away as far as if you wanted to opt into using V5 as someone into previous material. It was entirely possible to use the Sabbat as antagonists before, it was just also possible to use them in other ways. The idea that you can't possibly do both, that one excludes the other, comes off as deeply blinkered, and a statement that it's better when a game loses nuance and becomes basically about narrow absolutes, which, for VtM especially, is not great. Gaming doesn't actually have to be an either/or. It is in fact a lot easier to just not use extra material you don't like, than to have to come up with material out of nothing because the game has decided it no longer wants to help you out with that. In fact it's a pretty strong statement on that the energy and quality existed just fine to do both when &quot;the Sabbat as only antagonists&quot; is a markedly short, and thereby kinda painfully overpriced thing as a result.<br /> <br /> So, a related example: I used to hate the True Black Hand as something I found deeply moronic. Virulently hate it in that old, dumb, smug 90s gaming vibes way. I was even happy when they nuked it in revised. But after some time I realized that you know what? When it existed, I could have just ignored it. That blowing it up took away an option for people that liked that option. I realized that my getting to be right on the internet was mostly going &quot;you know this thing you were enjoying? I am happy because now you don't get to enjoy it in the game going forward as far as material that helps you play or run games. I am happy at your expense.&quot; When you state happiness or approval for a game thing getting blowed up, you are unavoidably also saying &quot;and thus I'm happy that people who enjoyed playing with their toy, got their toy taken away.&quot; That's just inescapable.<br /> <br /> So when V20 put it back? I realized that not only did I not really care, I actually thought &quot;you know what, good for the people who wanted some support for doing a thing they like with a game they like.&quot; And me? I could just ignore it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 10-11-2021, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T17:38:01-07:00","id":1463505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463501#post1463501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that it &quot;presents the Sabbat in a new way&quot; when the praise for it, praise you yourself are quoting to compliment and note as yet another positive review, is being phrased as &quot;restoring the original feel of the Sabbat&quot; doesn't especially go together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great response but an odd fact, I'd actually state that the Sabbat weren't really the antagonists of the setting until Revised. That was when suddenly they weren't EITHER mysterious boogeymen or a third player character sect.<br /> <br /> Revised went HARD on the idea, &quot;The Sabbat are coming for your cities! Anarchs and Cammies together to fight them!&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, it was the basis of the entire Clan Novel line after all.<br /> <br /> It also was the one who emphasized they were a bunch of meathead poseurs on Low Humanity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T17:55:46-07:00","id":1463506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463474#post1463474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, the point is that Paradox DOES recognize it as a problem and wanted to try to reverse it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a certain little green man said, &quot;Do or do not, there is no try.&quot;<br /> <br /> If Paradox wants there to be no Sabbat cities so nobody has to deal with their hometown being ruled by them, then there shouldn't be any Sabbat cities left. Period. Paradox has the final say in this. They could make it a demand to the writers that if they want to get paid, V5 Sabbat says no more Sabbat cities are left, end of that.<br /> <br /> So I don't buy that this is some sort of ideological stance on how VtM should be, because nothing is stopping them from making it that way. I can't help but say that if they left Sabbat ruled cities as a thing, they want that in the game. Which means the cities they pick for that are picked for a reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Notably, I wanted to also bring up OPP created the Drowned to address the Sabbat issue. The whole &quot;Native vampires taking back Latin America from the Sabbat.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that's really why OPP introduced them in BJD. South America wasn't Sabbat territory in the older books, and most of the Drowned Legacies are from South America. Mexico City was about as far as the Sabbat got in solid territorial control; farther South gets &quot;messy&quot; or at least undefined. It's worth remembering that in the fictional history of the setting, the Sabbat were the first wave of European vampires coming to the Americas, and they focused on North America rather heavily. For a while, what is now Canada, the USA, and Mexico was all Sabbat, and the Caribbean and South American territories were contested or controlled by others.<br /> <br /> So the Drown Legacies seem more to answer who are the vampires of Central and South America that seemed to have held off Sabbat and Camarilla rule, but nobody knows anything about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the Austrians don't believe that the buildings were blown up by the Austrian government (presumably as part of allied but member NATO relations) but they believe Al-Qaeda blew them up. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say they claimed the Austrian government blew anything up, but that Austrians would be protesting their government letting other countries pull a Waco in the middle of Vienna.<br /> <br /> Even blaming Al-Qaeda requires a rather low opinion of the intelligence of the Austrian citizenry since Al-Qaeda never managed any sort of attack like that in Christian Europe (and I only have to qualify that because of the series of Al-Qaeda bombings in Turkey included attacks on the European side of Istanbul). This was when Al-Qaeda had degraded so much that they were getting caught trying to sneak bomb making materials onto airplanes leading to all those silly TSA restrictions. How Al-Qaeda could have pulled off an attack like that without massive public demand for an explanation doesn't make a bit of sense. The entire Eurozone should have been in a flurry of trying to figure out how all the intelligence saying Al-Qaeda had no operational capabilities in Europe was so wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463479#post1463479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would actually be very interested in what WOULD be a very good way to address the issue and would love to hear pitches as its something I've struggled with myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't want to go with the method of keeping to the more nuanced Sabbat of Revised?<br /> <br /> You answered your own question by bringing up the Drowned Legacies. Latin America doesn't need Camarilla invaders. The few independent Domains turn out to be the tip of an iceberg that was waiting for the right time to kick everyone else out of power. Camarilla or Sabbat control in Latin America was always a mix of ruse or strategic ceding of territory to hide the vampires that truly ruled the nights and now is their time to claim their territory for themselves again.<br /> <br /> Especially with the V5 take on the Camarilla retreating from being vampire UN, this also expands to other parts of the globe. Iberia can be a haven for Lasombra that don't want to submit to the Cam but want out of the Sabbat. The Old Clan reasserts itself as a likewise independent territory in Eastern Europe, etc.<br /> <br /> This gives people places to play that aren't Cam or Anarch ruled. This adds dynamic politics that plays into the Cam no longer exerting the control it used to in areas without a history of Anarch control. There's lots of story fodder how successful any of these efforts are.<br /> <br /> The overarching meta-narrative is that areas formerly ignored by the game are now supported as places of opportunity to shape local vampire politics away from the existing factions and established Elders (even with the Beckoning). Empower players to make their local set games about local issues, not just stuff outsider narratives into local games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T18:00:58-07:00","id":1463507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463497#post1463497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[B]<br /> <br /> If you don't want/believe that the Sabbat's lowest common denominator will eventually overwhelm the secret manipulators then this will not be a story you want to tell. It's a story of the mob gaining control of the revolution and turning it into a Reign of Terror (and we were pretty Reign of Terror-y to begin with).<br /> <br /> The Sabbat book should have had a whole ****ing chapter about, &quot;So what does your Sabbat PC do now?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue it's the reactionary aspect of the movement ousting the reveltionary aspect, but other than that I agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T18:08:18-07:00","id":1463509,"title":"","content":"Thanks for that, Heavy Arms!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T18:32:19-07:00","id":1463511,"title":"","content":"I'm just glad they didn't make this a kickstarter like OPP did <i>Cult of the Blood Gods</i>. I'd almost certainly have contributed, and would now feel I'd been defrauded and robbed rather than just turned against and told &quot;we don't want your kind here.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T18:41:22-07:00","id":1463512,"title":"","content":"It's funny...for everything they took from requiem they didn't take the thing o really hoped for. Break down the sects into a covenant like system. Make the sabbat, camarilla, and anarchs not monolithic either or organizations. Sure they can have a world spanning culture and hierarchy...but here's the simple solution...just allow them to interact and play together. Think of the drama and intrigue that you could have. Heck make 2 new &quot;sects&quot; as player options. Have the Bahari be a full &quot;sect&quot; and I dunno...flesh out the inconnu to be something.. and yoy can always talk about other sects that exist in other regions that are unique to their culture. Present options...don't subtract.<br /> <br /> I really wish they had taken that from requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T19:15:48-07:00","id":1463515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463512#post1463512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's funny...for everything they took from requiem they didn't take the thing o really hoped for. Break down the sects into a covenant like system. Make the sabbat, camarilla, and anarchs not monolithic either or organizations. Sure they can have a world spanning culture and hierarchy...but here's the simple solution...just allow them to interact and play together. Think of the drama and intrigue that you could have. Heck make 2 new &quot;sects&quot; as player options. Have the Bahari be a full &quot;sect&quot; and I dunno...flesh out the inconnu to be something.. and yoy can always talk about other sects that exist in other regions that are unique to their culture. Present options...don't subtract.<br /> <br /> I really wish they had taken that from requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Damn, imagine what it would be like to have a group composed of an Anarch, a Sabbat, a Camarilla and a Hecata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T19:22:08-07:00","id":1463516,"title":"","content":"And, while I've probably said this a lot already, we don't need to make brand new things to have more complicated local politics in VtM. There's already four established &quot;local&quot; Sects (five if they figure out what to do with KotE). Imagine a Chicago where the Camarilla and Anarch conflict is highlighted not by the Sabbat threat, but additional conflicts from a group of Caribbean Drowned Legacy, and Laibon Legacies, that have followed their mortal groups to major US cities and bring their own multi-Clan organizations to vie for control instead of just being an Independent Clan trying to occupy a niche.<br /> <br /> Hell, the Ashirra might want to be in any major US city too.<br /> <br /> VtM has so much untapped potential in political conflicts that aren't two-sided hard-line antagonism.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T19:25:21-07:00","id":1463517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463511#post1463511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just glad they didn't make this a kickstarter like OPP did <i>Cult of the Blood Gods</i>. I'd almost certainly have contributed, and would now feel I'd been defrauded and robbed rather than just turned against and told &quot;we don't want your kind here.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You would have been able to read the material inside the book before the Kickstarter ended.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T19:25:59-07:00","id":1463518,"title":"","content":"They had the perfect opportunity to explain it too with the second inqusition...&quot;hey guys...look we aren't friends...but if we keep fighting like we did...we all die. So..um so we can survive we gotta learn to co exist&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T19:31:42-07:00","id":1463520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463518#post1463518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They had the perfect opportunity to explain it too with the second inqusition...&quot;hey guys...look we aren't friends...but if we keep fighting like we did...we all die. So..um so we can survive we gotta learn to co exist&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I have respect for the Sabbat who actually went, &quot;You know, screw it. No more hiding. We fight.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T19:34:57-07:00","id":1463521,"title":"","content":"Sure...those are called belials brood and could also be a thing lol. There's your pure antagonists. Some crazy young ex sabbat who have just collapsed to the beast and become monsters everyone fears. Just call them something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T19:46:01-07:00","id":1463522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463521#post1463521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure...those are called belials brood and could also be a thing lol. There's your pure antagonists. Some crazy young ex sabbat who have just collapsed to the beast and become monsters everyone fears. Just call them something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that's dismissive to Sabbat. Mind you, I like the infernalist Sabbat who revel in their own evil. I've played plenty of those as well. Sometimes you wish to cast down the veneer of humanity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T19:59:28-07:00","id":1463526,"title":"","content":"I mean...I find making sabbat watered down two dimensional insane vampire bad guys for pcs to deal with dismissive to the greater depth of the sabbat established over 20 years. I mean saying you can have your cake an eat it to. It's pretty easy to tell a story about a part of the sabbat that went done that route and became something else and have a functional sabbat for pc to play. Add...don't subtract","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T20:10:24-07:00","id":1463527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463526#post1463526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean...I find making sabbat watered down two dimensional insane vampire bad guys for pcs to deal with dismissive to the greater depth of the sabbat established over 20 years. I mean saying you can have your cake an eat it to. It's pretty easy to tell a story about a part of the sabbat that went done that route and became something else and have a functional sabbat for pc to play. Add...don't subtract</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think fanatics willing to die for the cause to be 2 dimensional if their motives as fleshed out as well. The book makes a lot of page count devoted to WHY they're fanatics and willing to die for the cause.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T20:13:08-07:00","id":1463529,"title":"","content":"You know that quote from Watchmen?<br /> <br /> &quot;Never compromise, not even in the face of Armageddon&quot;<br /> <br /> Thats the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T20:17:39-07:00","id":1463530,"title":"","content":"I've read it....it also tosses out all the OTHER aspects of the sabbat. Like all depth of the sect in say Mexico city by night, midnight siege, and many more. That whole all sabbat are fanatics to the cause...was never a fact across the whole of the sect. It just wasn't. The black hand was fanatics, not the whole of the sabbat. If this was the case...then how did they ever make it as a sect for 500 years and accomplish anything? It doesn't make much sense. <br /> <br /> We just have very different views of the sabbat. I prefer a deep sect made up of a variety of factions and beliefs...that are just like all other vampires...petty and political. The mask or lie is just different.<br /> <br /> THAT is vastly more interesting to me then &quot;so they crazy vampire monsters show up in your town and try to kill everyone muhabaha!&quot; Makes for a good movie, makes for a terrible game.<br /> <br /> Again...there is no reason why one could not have their cake and eat it too. Again, requiem just did this better. The lancea sanctum is basically the sabbat...all those crazy guys? Belials brood and the black hand is VII. They didn't need to alienate a chunk of their existing consumer base by breaking down the thing people enjoyed for 20 plus years. They could have just made new bad guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T20:25:35-07:00","id":1463533,"title":"","content":"Well, I feel like they are trying to have their cake and eat. You are right in that the Sabbat wasn't always like this, but others other aspects still technically still exist, jot not <i>as</i> part of the Sabbat. The cortieries who weren't all in on that type of fanatacism went to where they could continue what they did believe in, whether that was the Anarchs or Camarilla or one of the cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T20:25:39-07:00","id":1463534,"title":"","content":"Ya cept they do...a lot lol. See 3 civil wars. Like the true twist of horror was the sabbat...was just like all the others. Their lie was just different. They go into great detail the sabbat is great at preaching and saying ya we will die to kill the atendulvians. Truth was always, not so much. Turns out they are still vampires who largely concerned with their own agendas and plans. There's a reason in the books they say...there is very little difference between a sabbat elder and a camarilla elder. <br /> <br /> Look at the gehenna book and the sabbat. What happens? When gehenna comes they collapse just like everyone else. They loved to talk about taking the fight to the ancients...when given the chance they folded like a house of cards...just like everyone else lol. Lots of big talk...but the reality..before v5...they weren't fanatics on a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T20:32:38-07:00","id":1463535,"title":"","content":"Here's what I would have done. The beckoning happens and the sabbat gives a battle cry to middle east and go on a grand crusade. The sect elders say sure...go for it. The minority of the sect that were fanatics go. The elders of the sabbat shrug and sit down with anarchs and camarilla during the rise of the second Inquisition and go &quot;listen we gotta learn to co exist...all our crazies went off to die. So let's work that out&quot;. You have this intense cold war and treaty to bans open conflict. Imagine a world where you have a city where the anarchs, sabbat, and camarilla have to figure out how to exist in the same space or be destroyed by the Inquisition. The stories, rp, and drama from those kinda interactions? Amazing.<br /> <br /> Those former sabbat who were fanatics go off on the gehnna crusade and become something...something far worse and terrifying.<br /> <br /> Thats how I would have done it. Change and elevate the cam, sabbat, and anarchs to be distinct viable options. Then again, I suppose I could just play requiem and do the same thing...either way. Still said I'm not a welcomed consumer in V5 . I just think...missed opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T21:10:10-07:00","id":1463536,"title":"","content":"Like I said, as a Sabbat fan I have no problem with this as the end point of the Sabbat's story if that's what they wanted to do. The Sabbat CHANGING from a complex multifaceted group into the distilled essence of fury and fanaticism.<br /> <br /> However, they needed to do a lot more to build on that and there's very little info on that transformation as well as how to make use of that in RPGing terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T21:14:32-07:00","id":1463537,"title":"","content":"I mean I think you summed it up at one point previously when you used the term reboot lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T21:35:07-07:00","id":1463539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463535#post1463535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine a world where you have a city where the anarchs, sabbat, and camarilla have to figure out how to exist in the same space or be destroyed by the Inquisition. The stories, rp, and drama from those kinda interactions? Amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds really cool. I think that would create a far more interesting dynamic than just \u201cHey, there are some orcs, I mean Sabbat, in the city, pull out the d10s.\u201d A situation where the Sabbat and Camarilla don\u2019t have to kill each other on sight opens up so many options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T21:54:52-07:00","id":1463540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463487#post1463487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This review you're quoting verges on feeling like, even in just this one paragraph, a lecture that V5 Sabbat is good because the way the Sabbat were written for some 19+ years of the game (I was going to cut it off at V20, but it's not like V20 changed the Sabbat especially, so, 19+ it is) was creatively bankrupt. If you don't feel like that's telling a bunch of people who had been playing VtM for that amount of time &quot;what you liked about the way this thing in the game was portrayed for the majority of its existence was wrong&quot;, I'm unsure of what to say there. It's less a review of why V5 Sabbat is good for any actual merit to do with the book in terms of quality or consistency of its own writing, or even value as a gaming aid, and more that it's good because it got rid of things the reviewer had a grudge against for some time. And that for me is one of the huge problems of 5th edition overall. It feels like vanishingly few people can actually talk about why it is a good edition on its own merits and quality, instead having to default to why they so very much disliked the VtM that came before it and explaining why it was wrong that people liked it. That makes it feel less like a game of its own and more like some fans (and fans who became writers) of vampire getting to feel vindicated on the internet and in LARPs, because the game now agrees with them.<br /> <br /> When people note that part of their problem with V5 is that it seems basically like saying &quot;almost everything significant after the corebook was a mistake and you didn't like or understand quality VtM gaming if you liked it&quot; and how stunningly insulting that is, reviews like this seem to be replying to that with &quot;well exactly!&quot;<br /> <br /> And it seems like when people point that out, the default then becomes trying to lecture that in fact in addition to being bad at gaming, it was also morally wrong to have enjoyed VtM for the past 19+ years or so as far as post 1e corebook material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can speak plenty for why I like V5 on its own qualities. And I do not need to bash the way I played in the last 20 years. <br /> <br /> I started playing at 12, between 1999 and 2000: Revised was well on its way, but we in Italy of course had some &quot;buffer time&quot; with manuals arriving, so I started playing in a very gonzo mindset. <br /> <br /> I find things to be loved in every edition of Vampire so far: when I see huge problems and holes, I also try to contextualize them (and usually the answer I find is &quot;it's an homage to the genre by a 20-something american, written without extensive information availability at a time when the Internet was not so informative&quot;). <br /> <br /> What I wanted from a new edition wasn't V20.5, with some minor modifications to rules and setting. <br /> <br /> I wanted something bold and intriguing, as innovative as VtM was when it first came out. I've been following 5th edition since the playtest materials, and I've always felt new ideas and mechanics to be amazing. <br /> <br /> Marrying the Storyteller System with game design innovations of the last 30 years and some common sense practices, like &quot;take half&quot;, fail forward and similar? Useful to make the game flow smoother and reinforce the primacy of narration over dice. <br /> <br /> Streamlined combat rules have been a necessity since forever: some V5 choices needed polishing? Perhaps, but they delivered. My first V5 game was a 1-year long campaign with Ancillae characters and a lot of combat, and fights were quick and interesting, not agozining salvoes of dices. <br /> <br /> The Hunger mechanic is brilliant, it evokes feelings and color scenes, maintaining a consistent tone in the game while making it more interesting: again, I've read extensive rants over its crippling mathematics but I've played a many-dice, lots-of-rolls campaign and it severely impacted (for the better) in just a couple scenes. Again, Messy Criticals may need some polishing, but I just ruled out that if I don't have a ready-made effect, I use them as ST metacurrency to introduce complications later on. <br /> <br /> Mathematics are instead a strong point of the edition, as in the 5-dots cap / Blood Potency dynamics we now have a more balanced and mathematically consistent framework for building PCs and NPCs alike. <br /> <br /> &quot;You are what you eat&quot;: it's clear that at the beginning they meant something more far-reaching, but the final product, with Humors and Discrasyas, is fascinating and creepy, and, again, really reinforces the themes of the game giving greater player options. <br /> <br /> Morality rules give you the flexibility to adapt tone and pace of the game to your tastes. I admit that it took a while to give the proper game space to Touchstones, but when I managed to focus on them, in a Tzimisce game focused on abandoning Humanity nonetheless, they were again a huge plot opportunity. <br /> <br /> And don't let me start talking about Loresheets: is there a more fucking ingenious way to incorporate 30 years of metaplot into a chronicle?! <br /> <br /> <br /> I really like making Thin-Bloods characters, each one of them can be unique, and Thin Blood Alchemy is gory, messy and rich of plot hooks. <br /> <br /> I absolutely LOVE Disciplines as Power Trees, because in this way every PC and NPC can be absolutely unique, and you can easily port over powers from other editions or even Requiem. <br /> <br /> Speaking of, I could find of interest even the adoption of Requiem stats: to me, it was the promise of bridging edition wars and easily use a lot of interesting source materials. <br /> <br /> And change in the metaplot? Believe me or not, I loved the first presentation of source material even MORE than the final product. The mistery of the Beckoning, the idea that Camarilla elders were a powerful but frightened network in hiding, Anarchs finding themselves in government for the first time, Sabbat fighting the fight of their unlives, the Inquisition again a threat... <br /> <br /> I was and I still am very sad at the amount of vitriol leveraged against the game developers: when it first came out, the people working on it were accused of the most nefarious intentions. I frankly find shameful that a good chunk of the Internet fanbase would not be happy without Martin Ericsson losing his job. Like, it would be the dream of each and everyone of us to develop a new Vampire edition, and scores of people on Internet did everything they could to take it away from &quot;Dracula&quot; because... what, they didn't like his photo in the V20 corebook? Or it was just envy? He was called out daily as a nazi abuser, an allegation that just by looking at his Twitter would seem ridicolous. <br /> <br /> I do not regret the way I played, the books I bought or my first absurd characters: my first V5 campaign was gonzo action against Tzimisce Methuselas drawing on Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand. <br /> <br /> But I really think V5 has the best designed tools in the history of the game, and given choice I will never play with another ruleset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 10-12-2021, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T22:22:59-07:00","id":1463543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463530#post1463530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read it....it also tosses out all the OTHER aspects of the sabbat. Like all depth of the sect in say Mexico city by night, midnight siege, and many more. That whole all sabbat are fanatics to the cause...was never a fact across the whole of the sect. It just wasn't. The black hand was fanatics, not the whole of the sabbat. If this was the case...then how did they ever make it as a sect for 500 years and accomplish anything? It doesn't make much sense.<br /> <br /> We just have very different views of the sabbat. I prefer a deep sect made up of a variety of factions and beliefs...that are just like all other vampires...petty and political. The mask or lie is just different.<br /> <br /> THAT is vastly more interesting to me then &quot;so they crazy vampire monsters show up in your town and try to kill everyone muhabaha!&quot; Makes for a good movie, makes for a terrible game.<br /> <br /> Again...there is no reason why one could not have their cake and eat it too. Again, requiem just did this better. The lancea sanctum is basically the sabbat...all those crazy guys? Belials brood and the black hand is VII. They didn't need to alienate a chunk of their existing consumer base by breaking down the thing people enjoyed for 20 plus years. They could have just made new bad guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, the Sabbat are religious fanatics, but there is more than one way to be a religious fanatic. A group of monks who never speak and live in isolation farming peacefully are just as much religious fanatics as any Crusader or terrorist, yet they are wildly different from each other despite all fitting under the umbrella of &quot;religious fanatic&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T22:29:33-07:00","id":1463544,"title":"","content":"I'd agree with that. Their &quot;religion&quot; just takes the form of pack, faction, path, noddism, yes even clan for some of them (pre v5). Which is a wide variety of what that means exactly for each. Not all sabbat are &quot;religious fanatics&quot; in the sense they are ALL devoted solely to the death of the antedluvians. That's really more propaganda then fact. Of course that's all speaking pre v5. Religion is absolutely a theme of the sect. Its just not the ONLY one. IMO","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T01:03:12-07:00","id":1463549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463540#post1463540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can speak plenty for why I like V5 on its own qualities. And I do not need to bash the way I played in the last 20 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're a better reviewer than many (and I'm not counting <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> whose review I just disagree, don't find bad, and I know that reviewing professionally is a very different kind of animal).<br /> <br /> But let me comment on your points, and I'll actually agree with many of them, yet it won't make me like V5's current path.<br /> <br /> I wanted what I think everyone wanted from V5: an overhaul on the rules and a bg change in the setting. And I find extremely offensive the insistence in believing everyone's complains about the changes is because they wanted to play the same game as ever. VtM had bad rules forever. They missed every opportunity to make them even as they made better rules for their other products in the past. Time of Judgement put the setting into a crossroads, where it couldn't go on without dropping some themes to embrace new ones. Those were all things I expected and wanted.<br /> <br /> Most of the mechanics delivered, and I mean it. The new dice mechanics are interesting and flow smoother. The combat mechanics are easy and stay on what the game proposes instead of saying they won't be the focus and then diving into a rabbit hole of a simulationist mess. Hunger, Messy Criticals, Blood Potency, 5-dots cap, Humors and Dyscrasias, Convictions and Touchstones, Loresheets, those are all rules that are at least conceptually good and just need polishing, Touchstones more, Loresheets less, I'm not as excited about some as you, but I'm maybe even more excited about others.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I'll definitely try to convince my players to at least give the system a try, just some tweaks here and there. Thin Bloods became better in my opinion too. Their Alchemy is at least a good idea, although it needs some heavy tinkering. The same goes for Disciplines in general, to a lesser extend, I think the concept of the power tree is good, but the execution needs a lot of tinkering and Oblivion is objectively a bad idea. Oblivion, specifically.<br /> <br /> Requiem stats were a given, they would have to be too obnoxiously stubborn to not make this change, and wildly creative to find another change.<br /> <br /> And most of my thoughts apply to the metaplot in some way. As I said, I did wanted change, I wanted the end of the world to be delivered fully. But then we got the same problems but intensified: good concepts, bad executions, except this time it is a worse execution and, being the plot instead of the rules, polishing is harder. We also got the same stance of ditching things out, but plot development isn't the place to do this. You can simplify the setting by ignoring elements for now instead of actively butchering then.<br /> <br /> The Beckoning? Intriguing. But what's happening to those elders? Where are they going and what they're doing there? They went to the Middle East, not to another world, the lack of info isn't disturbing, it just sounds lazy. The Camarilla changing for its elders to survive? Excellent. The Camarilla turning into the GOP? Just what? The Anarchs rise to power in this vacuum is a good development. The Anarchs being regarded as the only sensible faction in the core and getting the treatment they got in their book, not so much. The Second Inquisition? With a proper blown up of the Masquerade as we know it would be a fantastic touch. As the same hunters from before, but nastier because lols and historical buildings in Vienna got &quot;casually&quot; blown up without the no one finding out it was a secret society? That's pretty much intellectually offensive. Sabbat fighting in their sacred war? Good. Becoming dumber and simpler under the justification that every sensible member went to other sects and we don't need the Sabbat anymore? No, thanks.<br /> <br /> We got V5 in the last half of the 2010's. This isn't a 20-something American with no proper research tools doing a semi-professional job anymore. Changing was a given, a necessity, but those changes should be well delivered. They should be good ideas with good executions, they didn't need to be awesome either, but good. The setting development ignored a big chunk of the same 30 years of game design innovations that made the rules deliver. Most changes were just focused on the already mentioned subtraction of play styles. The factions got individually dumber, important events went unexplored beyond their intended consequences, and the game is honestly shy from actual major changes, which makes the minor ones seem nonsensical. And they are still horrible at reaching for information and players from other places before writing about those places, making instead shallow references. The Chechnya incident was only the most prominent in the media, but the actual worse example is how they used the Middle East as the focal point of so many things and actually didn't even tried to describe it in any form.<br /> <br /> Now you want to blame the backlash on people being envious? Of course it can't have anything to do with context and reality being a complex place. Ericsson didn't loose his job because people freaked n the internet, he loose his job because Paradox freaked out, don't blame company decisions on fans. Yes, the whole debacle was a sorry mess, but unfortunately this is how public opinion works, sorry messes happen and companies need to navigate. In this case, it happened because WoD unfortunately already have a history with neo-nazi players, it isn't the company's fault, but is context.<br /> <br /> Please stop simplifying other people's positions for your own convenience. You're in your right to be well served by V5 and like it. You're in your right to defend it with good arguments and you do have them. You're on your right to be angry at what happened to Ericsson and I am too. But reality is this complex, nuanced place where things we like may have problems and people may have different opinions for a good reason, not just because they're envious (this REALLY pissed me off). You have a right to contextualize the game you like to see it under a better light, but not to demand others to do the same, and without contextualizing their opinion when it isn't convenient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T01:43:18-07:00","id":1463558,"title":"","content":"<br /> Thank you for your comment! As I've written elsewhere, I think that metaplot wasn't ignored, but they tried to downplay its amount to appease new players: I do generally agree with your remarks about where the presentation is lacking, especially in the Anarch book.<br /> <br /> Let me clarifiy a bit my remark about Ericsson<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463549#post1463549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now you want to blame the backlash on people being envious? Of course it can't have anything to do with context and reality being a complex place. Ericsson didn't loose his job because people freaked n the internet, he loose his job because Paradox freaked out, don't blame company decisions on fans. Yes, the whole debacle was a sorry mess, but unfortunately this is how public opinion works, sorry messes happen and companies need to navigate. In this case, it happened because WoD unfortunately already have a history with neo-nazi players, it isn't the company's fault, but is context.<br /> <br /> Please stop simplifying other people's positions for your own convenience. You're in your right to be well served by V5 and like it. You're in your right to defend it with good arguments and you do have them. You're on your right to be angry at what happened to Ericsson and I am too. But reality is this complex, nuanced place where things we like may have problems and people may have different opinions for a good reason, not just because they're envious (this REALLY pissed me off). You have a right to contextualize the game you like to see it under a better light, but not to demand others to do the same, and without contextualizing their opinion when it isn't convenient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ericcson's firing was of course a mix of complex instances and of the Chechinya incident.<br /> <br /> What I was referreing to, more precisely, were the early &quot;edition wars&quot; that happened just before the arrival of the corebook. Ericsson surely had some bad decisions, like involving Zak S. , but I feel he was subjected to an amount of slander that bordered on difamatory, in many Internet discussions. BTW, none of the current posters that I know were involved in this kind of warring.<br /> <br /> So, I wasn't really talking of the &quot;Chechinya mess&quot;, or of the current status of discussions here, but more of the pile-up of the earlier months: again, considering that he was the subject of considerable personal backlash way before publishing anything, I honestly have the doubt that at least some amount of bile was due to some sort of envy for this <i>&quot;wannabe LARPer who was not one of the established authors&quot;. </i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T02:23:34-07:00","id":1463562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463558#post1463558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I wasn't really talking of the &quot;Chechinya mess&quot;, or of the current status of discussions here, but more of the pile-up of the earlier months: again, considering that he was the subject of considerable personal backlash way before publishing anything, I honestly have the doubt that at least some amount of bile was due to some sort of envy for this <i>&quot;wannabe LARPer who was not one of the established authors&quot;. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>That early mess was about the Brujah write-up, I know the story, but it also was more complex than that.<br /> <br /> Many people were already complaining about a heavy White Supremacist presence in many WoD communities, including traditional forums and big LARPs. This was a big problem at the time. <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20180708153619/http://www.dogwithdice.com/whitewolfaredead/\" target=\"_blank\">Then one guy came and wrote one article, and that got big</a>. The link is to the article itself, and yes it was slander. But it was enough well written and under the whole context of 2018 to spark a shitstorm. In less than a week Paradox made a public statement about the incident, and the article didn't survived proper scrutiny. The author alleged to be receiving death threats from Paradox staff and other paranoid things and went off-line. Unfortunately this kind of shit happens in the internet from time to time, and the people that gave it undue credit aren't justified, but they didn't do this out of envy, it was far more complex.<br /> <br /> And before that, the pile-up of criticism on the developing of the system is, unfortunately, a part of any new edition of anything. Other RPGs that went through big new editions had to weather the same thing, including the pile-up on writers. It is less any specific emotion and more a storm of different reasons to be suspicious joining up and sharing (frequently half-assed) arguments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T03:51:26-07:00","id":1463567,"title":"","content":"AAAAAAARGH the crappy layout of the forums just deleted my 3 paragraph review of V5 sabbat so I'm just going to write my ratings having read it<br /> <br /> V5 alone product-6.0 out of 10, better than Anarch not enough crunch, not letting people play sabbat is a horrible diea<br /> Larger Context of 30 years of game-2.0 out of 10. Stick with Revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T03:57:25-07:00","id":1463568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463558#post1463558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What I was referreing to, more precisely, were the early &quot;edition wars&quot; that happened just before the arrival of the corebook. Ericsson surely had some bad decisions, like involving Zak S. , but I feel he was subjected to an amount of slander that bordered on difamatory, in many Internet discussions. BTW, none of the current posters that I know were involved in this kind of warring.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly dislike Zack to an......intense degree but it's pretty overt that some of the stuff said about him was completly made up. Which considering what he <b>has</b> done was really weird.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463562#post1463562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That early mess was about the Brujah write-up, I know the story, but it also was more complex than that.<br /> <br /> Many people were already complaining about a heavy White Supremacist presence in many WoD communities, including traditional forums and big LARPs. This was a big problem at the time. <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20180708153619/http://www.dogwithdice.com/whitewolfaredead/\" target=\"_blank\">Then one guy came and wrote one article, and that got big</a>. The link is to the article itself, and yes it was slander. But it was enough well written and under the whole context of 2018 to spark a shitstorm. In less than a week Paradox made a public statement about the incident, and the article didn't survived proper scrutiny. The author alleged to be receiving death threats from Paradox staff and other paranoid things and went off-line. Unfortunately this kind of shit happens in the internet from time to time, and the people that gave it undue credit aren't justified, but they didn't do this out of envy, it was far more complex.<br /> <br /> And before that, the pile-up of criticism on the developing of the system is, unfortunately, a part of any new edition of anything. Other RPGs that went through big new editions had to weather the same thing, including the pile-up on writers. It is less any specific emotion and more a storm of different reasons to be suspicious joining up and sharing (frequently half-assed) arguments.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole thing was a real splash of water in the face for me that a lot of the more.....assertive left wing people online may not be acting in good faith or worse, are just plain stupid. I recall i got buried and accused of being an alt right chud for appealing for calm and good faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-12-2021, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T04:20:57-07:00","id":1463571,"title":"","content":"Here was the biggest problem with Martin: He's a horrible PR face of a company. He's the kind of passionate, enthusiastic, and talented creative that shouldn't be let anywhere near the press, a blog, or a Twitter account while working on stuff. Why? Because he's so wrapped up in how cool he feels something is, that he forgets he's not a fan chatting with fans, but he's a brand representative who's words are going to get scrutinized. He said a lot of dumb things. Most of it was harmless. A lot of it would only take a few seconds of searching to put into context necessary to get what he was trying to say but stumbled around with the words. I'm pretty sure everyone here is guilty of that, but most of us have also likely been in a position where we had to turn off fans chatting on the Internet brain, and put on &quot;polite adult society&quot; brain instead without being the head of a company that's staking a lot on our personal creative vision.<br /> <br /> A lot of people fell into the hole of &quot;Does he keep making these weird comments and then correcting them because he's just bad at this part of the job, or did he mean it they way he first said it and someone at Paradox or within WW had to press him to do the right PR move?&quot; and then every future odd comment gets added to the &quot;maybe he really means this stuff...&quot; pile until they feel like that's the assumption to go with. The Zak S thing cannot be underestimated here in how much that whole mess put a lot of the public impressions of the early WW team in the negatives before they really did anything. <br /> <br /> I'm a pretty critical of V5 and WW/Paradox guy (even if monteparnas basically summed up my biggest problem with V5: lots of good ideas, with lots of poor execution). But I don't think anyone of the people I've sat around in private chats with cringing at the nWW's early missteps were ever envious of Martin. If anything quite the opposite. I remember talking about one of the first recorded public panels the WW team did at a convention and we pitied the man because it was painfully clear he was not ready to face hardcore fans in his new role. There was this whole awesome presentation about the new direction for the WoD in the 21st century, and then very confused looking Martin when the only questions related at all to what he'd just spent all that time talking about was the promise of a more diverse development and writing staff for the games to help avoid the mishaps of the oWW, and then just a slew of long standing WoD fan gripes. &quot;I'm jealous of that guy&quot; was pretty much the exact opposite of what reactions I saw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T05:34:38-07:00","id":1463578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463558#post1463558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for your comment! As I've written elsewhere, I think that metaplot wasn't ignored, but they tried to downplay its amount to appease new players: I do generally agree with your remarks about where the presentation is lacking, especially in the Anarch book.<br /> <br /> Let me clarifiy a bit my remark about Ericsson<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ericcson's firing was of course a mix of complex instances and of the Chechinya incident.<br /> <br /> What I was referreing to, more precisely, were the early &quot;edition wars&quot; that happened just before the arrival of the corebook. Ericsson surely had some bad decisions, like involving Zak S. , but I feel he was subjected to an amount of slander that bordered on difamatory, in many Internet discussions. BTW, none of the current posters that I know were involved in this kind of warring.<br /> <br /> So, I wasn't really talking of the &quot;Chechinya mess&quot;, or of the current status of discussions here, but more of the pile-up of the earlier months: again, considering that he was the subject of considerable personal backlash way before publishing anything, I honestly have the doubt that at least some amount of bile was due to some sort of envy for this <i>&quot;wannabe LARPer who was not one of the established authors&quot;. </i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ericsson's position was not helped by a series of what read as combative interviews that often came off as having as what bordered on open contempt for playstyles not his own, or for entire iterations of the game. Nor helped by frankly terrible mistakes being made in the game including the mess that is both the Camarilla and Anarch books, the ZakS mess before that, and what have you. Nor helped by an extremely poorly constructed/poorly received advanced playtest module release (whose material basically oozed that contempt along with a healthy chunk of what felt like edgelordism for the sake thereof), along with several other issues. Until this point I would have said very few people would have tried to argue that the initial launch of V5 was some smooth, well managed affair on the side of the people making the game, and ultimately he had a lot of responsibility for it, especially for what his place in the company was. To boil down the issue to &quot;envy&quot; ignores a lot of mistakes that the company themselves had to start even partially acknowledging/apologizing for some of them as they near completely changed the way they were going to even produce and run their VtM TTRPG division from that point on. That sort of thing doesn't happen when a project is going well.<br /> <br /> He made and helped make a big ol pile of goofs, to put it as kindly as possible, that seemed outright tailor made to cause a backlash. It can't be that shocking that one happened, and he did enough work on his own to provide for one happening. Someone was going to get some kind of consequences for rolling wave of mistakes and issues in the V5 opening, and the guy in a public place of authority tends to take the brunt there, especially when he was part of making those mistakes.<br /> <br /> To say that your own praise for V5 again doesn't come off with judgement of even just fans who don't like V5.. I mean your closing paragraph of your review is to talk about why people who didn't like V5 are the envious irrationals who drove a developer you liked out of a job. This is exactly the sort of thing I get at when I say it feels increasingly impossible to find discourse on why something about V5 is good without there almost needing to be some part about why fans who don't like V5 are in some way bad people, whether morally, or because they don't get good gaming. You've done a mix.<br /> <br /> You can't even talk about how you think a mechanic in V5 is good, without referring to people who have problems with it as &quot;ranting&quot;.<br /> <br /> But, more particularly:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wanted something bold and intriguing, as innovative as VtM was when it first came out. </div> </div> </div>There is not a lot of daylight between a statement like this and an implication that everything that came out after 1991 was none of these things.<br /> <br /> I would ask that people particularly look at the language they use for these sorts of things for even half a moment and what it says about the ability to talk about why you like a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 10-12-2021, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T06:00:53-07:00","id":1463581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463578#post1463578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To say that your own praise for V5 again doesn't come off with judgement.. I mean your closing paragraph of your review is to talk about why people who didn't like V5 are the envious irrationals who drove a developer you liked out of a job. This is exactly the sort of thing I get at when I say it feels increasingly impossible to find discourse on why something about V5 is good without there almost needing to be some part about why fans who don't like V5 are in some way bad people, whether morally, or because they don't get good gaming. You've done a mix.<br /> <br /> You can't even talk about how you think a mechanic in V5 is good, without referring to people who have problems with it as &quot;ranting&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, no, my last paragraph is not about &quot;<i>people who didn't like V5</i>&quot;: it's explicitly about &quot;<i>people who slandered Ericsson calling him a neonazi</i>&quot; and &quot;<i>people who generally insulted him with no particular regard for what he was going to write</i>&quot;. And some years ago there were lots of these people around. You don't hear from them a lot because in the meantime they mostly got banned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463578#post1463578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is not a lot of daylight between a statement like this and an implication that everything that came out after 1991 was none of these things.<br /> <br /> I would ask that people particularly look at the language they use for these sorts of things for even half a moment and what it says about the ability to talk about why you like a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, no again: I've just said that I wouldn't be interested in V5 if it had been a &quot;<i>V20 with some streamlined mechanics and a bit more metaplot</i>&quot;: for a 5th edition of the game to exist, I wanted some new rules and metaplot developments, especially after 30 years from its birth, and lots of new ideas in game design floating around.<br /> <br /> Without these elements, there wouldn't be any need of a 5th edition, you could just have more modules for V20, and it would have been perfectly fine, I would have bought them and played them nonetheless.<br /> <br /> I support the franchise in its entirety, I have no preference of editions: I even use a lot of Requiem materials in my game brainstorming.<br /> <br /> Come on, in this very post I praised &quot;Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand&quot;, and you call me judgemental on what was Vampire?! Sorry, but to me, this seems a little cherry-picking!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 10-12-2021, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T06:17:21-07:00","id":1463583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, no, my last paragraph is not about &quot;<i>people who didn't like V5</i>&quot;: it's explicitly about &quot;<i>people who slandered Ericsson calling him a neonazi</i>&quot; and &quot;<i>people who generally insulted him with no particular regard for what he was going to write</i>&quot;. And some years ago there were lots of these people around. You don't hear from them a lot because in the meantime they mostly got banned. </div> </div> </div>Your paragraph reads as an effort to say that any backlash against V5 was unearned and based in envious people slandering Martin Ericsson. To say that this doesn't read as &quot;V5 backlash was a result of this envy/bad fans and their terrible motives&quot;, I don't really know what to tell you there. It's a pretty strong statement that apparently no other possible mistakes could have been made to spark it. You refer to these people as &quot;a good chunk of the internet fanbase&quot;. Those are just your words. It's nice that you walked them back at least somewhat later, but that big ol review still chooses to close on the point that it does. If you didn't want to make the idea of disliking V5 into a moral issue, there was nothing that required you to include it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Come on, in this very post I praised &quot;Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand&quot;, and you call me judgemental on what was Vampire?! Sorry, but to me, this seems a little cherry-picking! </div> </div> </div>When you describe people saying how they don't like a game mechanic you like as &quot;extensively ranting&quot;, it's just your words. If you don't feel like calling people out for &quot;ranting&quot; isn't judging them, I frankly have absolutely no idea what to tell you there. Anything else mostly feels like deflection, honestly.<br /> <br /> To make it topical to this thread with an analogy, it would be like saying &quot;I really like the Sabbat! But also it's great how they were blowed up and are now unplayable&quot;. You might see how some statements are extremely difficult to reconcile with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T06:30:52-07:00","id":1463584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463583#post1463583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your paragraph reads as an effort to say that any backlash against V5 was unearned and based in envious people slandering Martin Ericsson. To say that this doesn't read as &quot;V5 backlash was a result of this envy/bad fans and their terrible motives&quot;, I don't really know what to tell you there. It's a pretty strong statement that apparently no other possible mistakes could have been made to spark it. You refer to these people as &quot;a good chunk of the internet fanbase&quot;. Those are just your words. It's nice that you walked them back at least somewhat later, but that big ol review still chooses to close on the point that it does. If you didn't want to make the idea of disliking V5 into a moral issue, there was nothing that required you to include it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> When you describe people saying how they don't like a game mechanic you like as &quot;extensively ranting&quot;, it's just your words. If you don't feel like calling people out for &quot;ranting&quot; isn't judging them, I frankly have absolutely no idea what to tell you there. Anything else mostly feels like deflection, honestly.<br /> <br /> To make it topical to this thread with an analogy, it would be like saying &quot;I really like the Sabbat! But also it's great how they were blowed up and are now unplayable&quot;. You might see how some statements are extremely difficult to reconcile with each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, again, I just said I was frankly ashamed that a lot of people were spending a lot of time and effort online asking for Ericsson resigning or being fired.<br /> <br /> Let me tell that, frankly, I'm feeling constantly morally judged for liking V5! <br /> <br /> But it's your cup of tea if you want to think that I was implying a general moral stance about criticizing the game.<br /> <br /> About the &quot;extensive rant&quot;, I confirm what I wrote: I remember statistical calculations done on the number of average conversation a Vampire would have in a Elysium, that each one would be a roll and thus there would be massive Frenzy and violence just for chatting. <br /> <br /> Considering the spirit and the letter of the Hunger rules, to me that was an excessive rant: however, English is not my native language, so if it is more appropriate we can agree to change &quot;rant&quot; into &quot;excessive and hyperbolical talking that had no constructive meaning&quot;.<br /> <br /> In any case, in these discussions, there are posters who regularly call V5 rules &quot;disgusting&quot;, I wonder why you are not telling them too that their behaviour is building walls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 10-12-2021, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T06:40:50-07:00","id":1463585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463584#post1463584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, again, I just said I was frankly ashamed that a lot of people were spending a lot of time and effort online asking for Ericsson resigning or being fired.<br /> <br /> Let me tell that, frankly, I'm feeling constantly morally judged for liking V5!<br /> <br /> But it's your cup of tea if you want to think that I was implying a general moral stance about criticizing the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're unhappy with a game discussion veering into the ideas of the morality of those involved with having preferences for a game one way or another, maybe don't write an entire paragraph commenting about the morality or your perceived lack thereof on people involved in not liking something or someone's involvement about a game that you like. In doing so you make that a topic of discourse.<br /> <br /> An easy way to avoid feeling morally judged for liking V5 would be not to start conversations on morally judging people for how they have interacted with V5, where again &quot;envy&quot; especially was a really reductionist and dismissive way to go about it in terms of Martin Ericsson having made a pretty sizable pile of gaffes and mistakes in his development role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 10-12-2021, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T06:51:41-07:00","id":1463586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About the &quot;extensive rant&quot;, I confirm what I wrote: I remember statistical calculations done on the number of average conversation a Vampire would have in a Elysium, that each one would be a roll and thus there would be massive Frenzy and violence just for chatting.<br /> <br /> Considering the spirit and the letter of the Hunger rules, to me that was an excessive rant: however, English is not my native language, so if it is more appropriate we can agree to change &quot;rant&quot; into &quot;excessive and hyperbolical talking that had no constructive meaning&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Okay, in the spirit of English not being your native language I'll try to say this as thoroughly as I can. &quot;Excessive and hyperbolic talking that had no constructive meaning&quot; is in fact even more judgmental than you were already in the context of English. Vastly more judgmental. In fact outright clinically judgmental. To the point that it now reads like you're calling people who don't like the rules you do intellectually inferior in some way for the views that they hold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In any case, in these discussions, there are posters who regularly call V5 rules &quot;disgusting&quot;, I wonder why you are not telling them too that their behaviour is building walls. </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between not liking a rule and saying that the people who don't like a rule don't understand or appreciate gaming. There's a further difference between finding a rule gross and saying that people who didn't like something a developer did couldn't have had legitimate reasons for doing so and were instead motivated by envy.<br /> <br /> But more to the point, if you're now saying that no one can comment on your posts unless they go back and comment on any single other post that's remotely previously relevant somehow, that's.. um.<br /> <br /> It's a thread, you posted some things. People can comment on the things you posted.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'll go further than that. You quoted me to respond to me. That's what started this entire conversation. If I'm not then allowed to respond to you based on how you responded to me because I haven't responded to every other post in this forum that alights in some way on this topic, that feels remarkably arbitrary.<br /> <br /> You replied to me to say &quot;I in fact can say why I like V5 without judging people as part of why I like it&quot;, I replied to this to say &quot;in reading your reply, you sure seem like you judged people&quot;, it went from there. Are you saying I wasn't allowed to reply to you? If that's the case, why quote me in the first place? &quot;I can disagree with you, you're not allowed to disagree with me&quot; feels perhaps a touch unfair as stances go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 10-12-2021, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T06:54:47-07:00","id":1463587,"title":"","content":"Ok, it's morally judgemental to criticise those who called Ericsson a neonazi and make an hypothesis on why he was so wildly attacked, I duly take note.<br /> <br /> Frankly, your tone is really condescending: if a rule is described as disgusting, it is fair criticism, but of if I say criticism is way excessive because the rule is bent well over its meaning, I'm insulting the intellect of my interlocutors. <br /> <br /> English may not be my native language, but let's not try to game with words: not understanding - or deliberately misunderstanding - a rule is not the same as not understanding gaming. <br /> <br /> I doubt this thread will get any more constructive, so I leave the discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 10-12-2021, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T07:14:50-07:00","id":1463588,"title":"","content":"It's definitely morally judgmental to say that the majority reason people had a problem with a game developer was that they were slandering him out of envy, yes and in doing so dismiss that he himself might have instead made a pile of mistakes. That's pretty much exactly what that is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Frankly, your tone is really condescending: if a rule is described as disgusting, it is fair criticism, but of if I say criticism is way excessive because the rule is bent well over its meaning, I'm insulting the intellect of my interlocutors. </div> </div> </div>You are literally right now saying that people critiqued a thing you liked because they were incapable of understanding the meaning of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> English may not be my native language, but let's not try to game with words: not understanding - or deliberately misunderstanding - a rule is not the same as not understanding gaming. </div> </div> </div>Why, when you want to talk about that you're not judging people for not liking V5, would you pile on to everything by now throwing in the suggestion that when someone doesn't understand a rule in V5, they're doing it on purpose as a willful effort not to understand that rule? That's basically... that's the equivalent of noting that someone expressing a problem with V5 rules is basically doing it with intention of malice, or certainly some undercurrent of dishonesty motivating them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I doubt this thread will get any more constructive, so I leave the discussion. </div> </div> </div>Hokay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  forgot an of 10-12-2021, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T09:38:46-07:00","id":1463597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463567#post1463567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AAAAAAARGH the crappy layout of the forums just deleted my 3 paragraph review of V5 sabbat so I'm just going to write my ratings having read it</div> </div> </div> </div>At my workplace forum we use the Discourse engine and I really miss it here, won't deny. Either way, I always ctrl+c my post before posting, clicking any buttons, or actually doing anything. Discourse has auto-save.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463584#post1463584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, in these discussions, there are posters who regularly call V5 rules &quot;disgusting&quot;, I wonder why you are not telling them too that their behaviour is building walls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't answer for others, but I personally do this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463587#post1463587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, it's morally judgemental to criticise those who called Ericsson a neonazi and make an hypothesis on why he was so wildly attacked,</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between criticizing a rule, an action or an argument, and judging the people behind them. There is some people that make judgement about the fans of V5 and that's objectively wrong.<br /> <br /> Wishing for Ericsson's firing was wrong. People should have calmed down. And Paradox should have removed him from PR, but that's no justification. Many fans let their prejudice guide them to unfair demands. What's judgemental isn't you pointing any of this out, but asserting that those fans did it out of envy. You jumped from criticism to attitudes you disagreed with to moral judgement on the people that had those attitudes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  typo 10-12-2021, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T10:27:57-07:00","id":1463599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463540#post1463540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was and I still am very sad at the amount of vitriol leveraged against the game developers: when it first came out, the people working on it were accused of the most nefarious intentions. I frankly find shameful that a good chunk of the Internet fanbase would not be happy without Martin Ericsson losing his job. Like, it would be the dream of each and everyone of us to develop a new Vampire edition, and scores of people on Internet did everything they could to take it away from &quot;Dracula&quot; because... what, they didn't like his photo in the V20 corebook? Or it was just envy? He was called out daily as a nazi abuser, an allegation that just by looking at his Twitter would seem ridicolous.<br /> <br /> I do not regret the way I played, the books I bought or my first absurd characters: my first V5 campaign was gonzo action against Tzimisce Methuselas drawing on Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> But I really think V5 has the best designed tools in the history of the game, and given choice I will never play with another ruleset.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This runs close to edition warring. Try not to attack fans even if you disagree with their point.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T13:16:26-07:00","id":1463608,"title":"","content":"I was put off for... a couple of years, I think? by the marketing around the V5 release and the various PR whoopsies Ericsson and the team made. Not the backlash to them, but the initial releases and interviews which seemed very unwelcoming to (and dismissive of) a lot of the tabletop gamers out there and caused said backlash. When I actually broke down and bought the core I found to my surprise that I really liked the atmosphere and the new take on the rules for the most part. Then OPP's work on <i>Chicago By Night</i> and <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i> built on that foundation and provided rich setting material that I could see enjoyable campaigns occurring in.<br /> <br /> A lot of that earned goodwill has been squandered by the treatment of the Sabbat and the concurrent abandonment of people who enjoyed playing Sabbat characters. I'd thought the new supplement might provide under-the-table support for playing Sabbat games while maintaining plausible deniability to avoid backlash, but instead it seems the development team bent over backwards to make sure they're unplayable. It's like a restaurant displaying innovative treats on a dessert cart but telling you that you're only allowed to order sugar-free yogurt because the other selections aren't good for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","user":"Matt the Bruins fan","date":". 10-12-2021, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T13:27:36-07:00","id":1463610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463608#post1463608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was put off for... a couple of years, I think? by the marketing around the V5 release and the various PR whoopsies Ericsson and the team made. Not the backlash to them, but the initial releases and interviews which seemed very unwelcoming to (and dismissive of) a lot of the tabletop gamers out there and caused said backlash. When I actually broke down and bought the core I found to my surprise that I really liked the atmosphere and the new take on the rules for the most part. Then OPP's work on <i>Chicago By Night</i> and <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i> built on that foundation and provided rich setting material that I could see enjoyable campaigns occurring in.<br /> <br /> A lot of that earned goodwill has been squandered by the treatment of the Sabbat and the concurrent abandonment of people who enjoyed playing Sabbat characters. I'd thought the new supplement might provide under-the-table support for playing Sabbat games while maintaining plausible deniability to avoid backlash, but instead it seems the development team bent over backwards to make sure they're unplayable. It's like a restaurant displaying innovative treats on a dessert cart but telling you that you're only allowed to order sugar-free yogurt because the other selections aren't good for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>The treatment of all the sects has been pretty disappointing as a primary carmarilla I'm frustrated at how cartoonishly evil and stupid the sect was written and anarchs have no were near enough material was provided to justify the emphasis on them as the editions protagonists. A lot of the clans havnt faired much better, pretty much the only ones I like what they did are the ones they did nothing with.<br /> <br /> Edit-actually I quite like the ravnos revisions. Although bizarrely the only romani I know doesn't","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-12-2021, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T15:23:47-07:00","id":1463628,"title":"","content":"Well, as someone that might have contributed to the &quot;V5 rules are disgusting&quot; thing?<br /> <br /> I've never intentionally said that as a broad generality. I do stand by that assessment of a few very specific rules (one in particular in the core book I think most V5 fans agree was a bad idea to include). As has been said, don't lose nuance on people's feelings about stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463610#post1463610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although bizarrely the only romani I know doesn't</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't surprise me too much, but the Romani that I know that are WoD fans that are still playing tend to fall into two categories regarding this: they haven't cared about VtM's official material on the Ravnos in decades and have their own fanon to replace it that they like better (sticking to pre-V5, or adapting it to V5), or they tend to like the transgressive nature of playing stereotypes about their our demographics (and not just being Romani) and tend to prefer the 2e gonzo era mentality on things rather than attempts to &quot;fix&quot; it.<br /> <br /> Though I can imagine that there's plenty of Romani that might have other reactions to the Ravnos changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T15:33:02-07:00","id":1463631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463610#post1463610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The treatment of all the sects has been pretty disappointing as a primary carmarilla I'm frustrated at how cartoonishly evil and stupid the sect was written and anarchs have no were near enough material was provided to justify the emphasis on them as the editions protagonists. A lot of the clans havnt faired much better, pretty much the only ones I like what they did are the ones they did nothing with.<br /> <br /> Edit-actually I quite like the ravnos revisions. Although bizarrely the only romani I know doesn't</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I am very happy the Anarchs are finally getting the coverage they deserve.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T15:45:42-07:00","id":1463634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463628#post1463628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't surprise me too much, but the Romani that I know that are WoD fans that are still playing tend to fall into two categories regarding this: they haven't cared about VtM's official material on the Ravnos in decades and have their own fanon to replace it that they like better (sticking to pre-V5, or adapting it to V5), or they tend to like the transgressive nature of playing stereotypes about their our demographics (and not just being Romani) and tend to prefer the 2e gonzo era mentality on things rather than attempts to &quot;fix&quot; it.<br /> <br /> Though I can imagine that there's plenty of Romani that might have other reactions to the Ravnos changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense, as a mega-Celt myself I've enjoyed leaning into the archetypes and occasionally stereotypes of my own culture when I've played fianna or verbena it's strangely comfortable to wear the trappings unapologetically. I know the russian guy I sometimes play with embraced the fangs, Lords and fiends with glee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-12-2021, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T15:47:24-07:00","id":1463635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463631#post1463631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit I am very happy the Anarchs are finally getting the coverage they deserve.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm surprised to hear you say that, v5 sabbat book may be controversial but v5 anarch was an outright stinker and probably were v5 starts to go south for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-12-2021, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T16:19:38-07:00","id":1463636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463635#post1463635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm surprised to hear you say that, v5 sabbat book may be controversial but v5 anarch was an outright stinker and probably were v5 starts to go south for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was terrible. However, LA By Night, Winter's Teeth, and Chicago by Night are much better.<br /> <br /> My opinion of V5 would much lower if not for the spinoff material.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T23:26:04-07:00","id":1463653,"title":"","content":"I personally think that the treatment of Ericsson by parts of the community and Paradox was shameful. This doesn't include justified criticism and dislike of rules or how Ericsson did PR. Bad faith groups throwing hyperbolic and/or wrong statements on social media around and media amplifying and validating them seems to be a problem in multimedia journalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T23:27:36-07:00","id":1463654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463653#post1463653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think that the treatment of Ericsson by parts of the community and Paradox was shameful. This doesn't include justified criticism and dislike of rules or how Ericsson did PR. Bad faith groups throwing hyperbolic and/or wrong statements on social media around and media amplifying and validating them seems to be a problem in multimedia journalism.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Let's avoid discussing this topic for a variety of reasons. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-13-2021, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T23:43:44-07:00","id":1463655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463549#post1463549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're a better reviewer than many (and I'm not counting <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> whose review I just disagree, don't find bad, and I know that reviewing professionally is a very different kind of animal).<br /> <br /> But let me comment on your points, and I'll actually agree with many of them, yet it won't make me like V5's current path.<br /> <br /> I wanted what I think everyone wanted from V5: an overhaul on the rules and a bg change in the setting. And I find extremely offensive the insistence in believing everyone's complains about the changes is because they wanted to play the same game as ever. VtM had bad rules forever. They missed every opportunity to make them even as they made better rules for their other products in the past. Time of Judgement put the setting into a crossroads, where it couldn't go on without dropping some themes to embrace new ones. Those were all things I expected and wanted.<br /> <br /> Most of the mechanics delivered, and I mean it. The new dice mechanics are interesting and flow smoother. The combat mechanics are easy and stay on what the game proposes instead of saying they won't be the focus and then diving into a rabbit hole of a simulationist mess. Hunger, Messy Criticals, Blood Potency, 5-dots cap, Humors and Dyscrasias, Convictions and Touchstones, Loresheets, those are all rules that are at least conceptually good and just need polishing, Touchstones more, Loresheets less, I'm not as excited about some as you, but I'm maybe even more excited about others.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I'll definitely try to convince my players to at least give the system a try, just some tweaks here and there. Thin Bloods became better in my opinion too. Their Alchemy is at least a good idea, although it needs some heavy tinkering. The same goes for Disciplines in general, to a lesser extend, I think the concept of the power tree is good, but the execution needs a lot of tinkering and Oblivion is objectively a bad idea. Oblivion, specifically.<br /> <br /> Requiem stats were a given, they would have to be too obnoxiously stubborn to not make this change, and wildly creative to find another change.<br /> <br /> And most of my thoughts apply to the metaplot in some way. As I said, I did wanted change, I wanted the end of the world to be delivered fully. But then we got the same problems but intensified: good concepts, bad executions, except this time it is a worse execution and, being the plot instead of the rules, polishing is harder. We also got the same stance of ditching things out, but plot development isn't the place to do this. You can simplify the setting by ignoring elements for now instead of actively butchering then.<br /> <br /> The Beckoning? Intriguing. But what's happening to those elders? Where are they going and what they're doing there? They went to the Middle East, not to another world, the lack of info isn't disturbing, it just sounds lazy. The Camarilla changing for its elders to survive? Excellent. The Camarilla turning into the GOP? Just what? The Anarchs rise to power in this vacuum is a good development. The Anarchs being regarded as the only sensible faction in the core and getting the treatment they got in their book, not so much. The Second Inquisition? With a proper blown up of the Masquerade as we know it would be a fantastic touch. As the same hunters from before, but nastier because lols and historical buildings in Vienna got &quot;casually&quot; blown up without the no one finding out it was a secret society? That's pretty much intellectually offensive. Sabbat fighting in their sacred war? Good. Becoming dumber and simpler under the justification that every sensible member went to other sects and we don't need the Sabbat anymore? No, thanks.<br /> <br /> We got V5 in the last half of the 2010's. This isn't a 20-something American with no proper research tools doing a semi-professional job anymore. Changing was a given, a necessity, but those changes should be well delivered. They should be good ideas with good executions, they didn't need to be awesome either, but good. The setting development ignored a big chunk of the same 30 years of game design innovations that made the rules deliver. Most changes were just focused on the already mentioned subtraction of play styles. The factions got individually dumber, important events went unexplored beyond their intended consequences, and the game is honestly shy from actual major changes, which makes the minor ones seem nonsensical. And they are still horrible at reaching for information and players from other places before writing about those places, making instead shallow references. The Chechnya incident was only the most prominent in the media, but the actual worse example is how they used the Middle East as the focal point of so many things and actually didn't even tried to describe it in any form.<br /> <br /> Now you want to blame the backlash on people being envious? Of course it can't have anything to do with context and reality being a complex place. Ericsson didn't loose his job because people freaked n the internet, he loose his job because Paradox freaked out, don't blame company decisions on fans. Yes, the whole debacle was a sorry mess, but unfortunately this is how public opinion works, sorry messes happen and companies need to navigate. In this case, it happened because WoD unfortunately already have a history with neo-nazi players, it isn't the company's fault, but is context.<br /> <br /> Please stop simplifying other people's positions for your own convenience. You're in your right to be well served by V5 and like it. You're in your right to defend it with good arguments and you do have them. You're on your right to be angry at what happened to Ericsson and I am too. But reality is this complex, nuanced place where things we like may have problems and people may have different opinions for a good reason, not just because they're envious (this REALLY pissed me off). You have a right to contextualize the game you like to see it under a better light, but not to demand others to do the same, and without contextualizing their opinion when it isn't convenient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks,<br /> <br /> I don't think that people who have an issue with V5's metaplot are complaining about change in general. I do think it boils down to the fact that a lot of the changes are things they specifically disagree with. To use a comparison, if you are a fan of Luke Skywalker and you hated his portrayal in THE LAST JEDI then you aren't being a bad fan of Luke Skywalker. You just don't like what was done to him and are expressing that opinion. It doesn't mean people who liked Luke Skywalker's treatment in said movie are wrong, it's a matter of taste and opinion. It just so happened the latter people are wrong.<br /> <br /> :rimshot:<br /> <br /> JK.<br /> <br /> I'm generally a big defender of V5 but I'm also going to admit that I also feel like OPP has been cleaning up a huge amount of what I perceived to be a mess. I feel the enthusiasm for V5 from the new book but I also feel like the original book had serious issues of lacking good rules for the Sabbat, very poor connection to the previous editions (HOW did it get to be like this), poor explanation of things like the Second Inquisition, and lacking rules for a good half of the clans. I feel like radical change was necessary for reasons listed below but we had a lot of statements without much explanation of what they MEANT.<br /> <br /> For example: The Beckoning was something that was stated to have gotten rid of the Elders. Given that a massive chunk of the game is based on the conflict with the Elders, this was a change that would have ruined my games. I feel like OPP carried a lot of water for Paradox by creating Chicago by Night and explaining: &quot;No, not every Elder went to the Middle East. Some stayed. Here's some reasons why.&quot; They also gave us examples of how the Anarchs and Camarilla interacted, how the technology ban was being dealt with [with great hypocrisy], and gave us the Lasombra.<br /> <br /> I'm going to be honest that I feel like OPP &quot;soft-rebooted&quot; 5th Edition by clarifying a lot of things that weren't necessarily WRONG by strict interpretation of 5th Edition, Anarchs, and Camarilla but they certainly gave us a lot of information that made things less radical than hinted at. My love of Chicago by Night might be blinding me but I feel like the 5th Edition of that book is what got me interested in V5 more than V20 because it managed to preserve a lot of what I loved about older editions while incorporating the best elements of V5's changes. In such a way that I felt it was superior to the initial V5 portrayal AND older editions.<br /> <br /> The thing is that people who experienced V5 only through the main book weren't going to get that full experience. I'm also a fan of LA by Night where Jason Carl also seemed to dial back some of the radical changes of V5 and present something closer to the classic Masquerade &quot;feel&quot; with a focus on relatively pleasant good-ish (Neutral-ish) vampires against a hostile Camarilla. Fans who were initially offput by the idea of V5 going &quot;all in&quot; on vampires being horrifying monsters got some reassurance there too.<br /> <br /> Cults of the Blood Gods also felt like they salvaged a bunch of dropped plots from Beckett's Jyhad Diary and canonized ideas that were worth salvaging. Throw in Let the Streets Run Red and the Chicago Folios and I'll be honest that my love of V5 is very much OPP's V5. It's not that I hate the &quot;main&quot; V5 but I think that a lot of the best stuff was done by people who were in love with the minutia of the Old World of Darkness that I feel was absent here. To use an example: I like Discovery, I really like Picard, but I am in LOVE with Lower Decks. The continuity of all the OPP books is what makes their V5 best and V5's &quot;main&quot; line seems determined to break with the past.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat book had a lot going for it but I feel like if OPP had done it then they probably would have had a lot more connective tissue to the past. V5 wanted a Sabbat book that presents them for entirely new audiences and I feel that will hurt some fans who want it to be full of a lot more information about the transition from 2004 to 2021. Those decades of the World of Darkness need to be filled in. The thing is that OPP has published 7 or 8 books on V5 while the main books are like 4 now.<br /> <br /> There's a reason my V5 is mostly defined by OPP and that's because they ARE the best parts of V5 for me. It's just a lot of fans will never experience that because they stopped at the main book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T01:13:22-07:00","id":1463663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463655#post1463655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a reason my V5 is mostly defined by OPP and that's because they ARE the best parts of V5 for me. It's just a lot of fans will never experience that because they stopped at the main book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As much as I may not like some of the choices made by the developers and writers I 100% agree that OPPs V5 books are heads and shoulders above Paradox/Modiphius/White Wolfs in terms of quality of writing, coherence and usefulness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T01:23:10-07:00","id":1463664,"title":"","content":"I think we're all agreed that the OPP books are the best. I think it comes from having lots of experience of the WoD, as well as being the heirs to the original WW. Rich T and his team know this game intimately, and they have cultivated a longstanding relationship with a varied collection of fans, so they know how to please a broader demographic. <br /> <br /> Obviously, they don't have the distribution in place that V5 needs, but I think a better idea from day one would've been to commission OPP to write V5 and outsource distro to Modiphius or Renegade. <br /> <br /> That way, you'd have the best of both worlds: writers and devs who really get the material and why fans love it, but international distro that reaches bricks and mortar stores. <br /> <br /> That was unlikely to happen, though, given that OPP probably wouldn't have the resources to take that plunge and print loads of books to make into market, since their primary model is to crowdfund the upfront costs. But Paradox could have fronted them the money, or outsourced that part to Modi, so that it was more of a partnership between the two companies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T01:33:53-07:00","id":1463665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463664#post1463664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we're all agreed that the OPP books are the best. I think it comes from having lots of experience of the WoD, as well as being the heirs to the original WW. Rich T and his team know this game intimately, and they have cultivated a longstanding relationship with a varied collection of fans, so they know how to please a broader demographic.<br /> <br /> Obviously, they don't have the distribution in place that V5 needs, but I think a better idea from day one would've been to commission OPP to write V5 and outsource distro to Modiphius or Renegade.<br /> <br /> That way, you'd have the best of both worlds: writers and devs who really get the material and why fans love it, but international distro that reaches bricks and mortar stores.<br /> <br /> That was unlikely to happen, though, given that OPP probably wouldn't have the resources to take that plunge and print loads of books to make into market, since their primary model is to crowdfund the upfront costs. But Paradox could have fronted them the money, or outsourced that part to Modi, so that it was more of a partnership between the two companies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, I don't think the writing talent is a problem.<br /> <br /> A lot of the same authors are working on this and great authors. They just seem to not want to do books that are heavily involved in past lore in the &quot;main&quot; line.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T01:47:35-07:00","id":1463666,"title":"","content":"I think the big issue is going to be how they go moving forward. A lot of the fluff changes are either badly written or underwritten. The Anarchs for the primary faction are criminally underdeveloped and are frankly, relying on poisoning the well for the other better developed sects. But this is a doomed strategy-stopping people from playing what they want isn't going to make them play what you want. <br /> If the anarchs are going to be the default protagonist faction (an idea I sincerely loathe incidently since I like the other two sects a lot more), then they're going to need a lot of fleshing out. Otherwise we're going to eventually saunter back to circa 1999 we're the better written sects are the primary. Something I'd actually prefer over the dumber carmarilla and the unplayable sabbat and I get the impression I'm not the only one. Time to shit or get off the pot.<br /> Also a lot of the mechanics need work. Oblivion is a total mess and feeding needs re-streamlining badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-13-2021, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T02:13:35-07:00","id":1463668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463666#post1463666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the big issue is going to be how they go moving forward. A lot of the fluff changes are either badly written or underwritten. The Anarchs for the primary faction are criminally underdeveloped and are frankly, relying on poisoning the well for the other better developed sects. But this is a doomed strategy-stopping people from playing what they want isn't going to make them play what you want.<br /> If the anarchs are going to be the default protagonist faction (an idea I sincerely loathe incidently since I like the other two sects a lot more), then they're going to need a lot of fleshing out. Otherwise we're going to eventually saunter back to circa 1999 we're the better written sects are the primary. Something I'd actually prefer over the dumber carmarilla and the unplayable sabbat and I get the impression I'm not the only one. Time to shit or get off the pot.<br /> Also a lot of the mechanics need work. Oblivion is a total mess and feeding needs re-streamlining badly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anarchs 4 Ever.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yes, I'd prefer a book like Anarchs Unbound. The Anarchs are by far the best sect but they're also not a sect but a loose alliance of gangs, sects, and groups.<br /> <br /> We need a book detailing the various Anarch factions like CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS.<br /> <br /> GANGS OF THE ANARCHS:<br /> <br /> * Marcus Vitel's Centurions<br /> * LA's Free Staters<br /> * Smiling Jack's Freebooters<br /> * The Brujah Council (COMMUNIST VILLAINS!)<br /> * The Church of Caine, Anarch (I admit, I made this)<br /> * Maldavis' Unionists<br /> <br /> And so on<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-13-2021, 05:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T02:43:00-07:00","id":1463670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463668#post1463668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anarchs 4 Ever.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yes, I'd prefer a book like Anarchs Unbound. The Anarchs are by far the best sect but they're also not a sect but a loose alliance of gangs, sects, and groups.<br /> <br /> We need a book detailing the various Anarch factions like CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS.<br /> <br /> GANGS OF THE ANARCHS:<br /> <br /> * Marcus Vitel's Centurions<br /> * LA's Free Staters<br /> * Smiling Jack's Freebooters<br /> * The Brujah Council (COMMUNIST VILLAINS!)<br /> * The Church of Caine, Anarch (I admit, I made this)<br /> * Maldavis' Unionists<br /> <br /> And so on</div> </div> </div> </div>Screw ups and hypocrites with no long term plan The minute the inquisition is gone and the other two pull their heads our their asses they're just real estate for the actual sects.<br /> They 'won' by being the only piece on the boards in an age of chaos that's not a sect that's a npc Rebel generation in strategy games <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway back out of character I'd also argue what they also need is a unifying manifesto and an idea of how they're going to go forward. Coherent institutions offices and checks and safeguards. Otherwise they're just going to end up being the carmarilla 2.0 or more likely a less functional sabbat. At the moment the anarchs are a joke and the punchline is &quot;they're winning&quot; but you can't just be 10 guys on motorcycles who constantly call the prince a fascist because he's annoyed you killed some cops","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T02:45:33-07:00","id":1463671,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> (to avoid a huge wall of text quote) For me V5 did a 'worst of both worlds' it made what would have been low Humanity mindless monster the default, but ditched the ability to do genuinely alien mindsets (as much as that is possible for a player to do anyway) and genuine Golconda seeker types as well, as well as the Sects becoming parodies of themselves, and the 'suggested' playstyle being basically mandatory, as the rule set really doesn't have as much freedom as it used to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 10-13-2021, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T02:48:45-07:00","id":1463672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463671#post1463671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> (to avoid a huge wall of text quote) For me V5 did a 'worst of both worlds' it made what would have been low Humanity mindless monster the default, but ditched the ability to do genuinely alien mindsets (as much as that is possible for a player to do anyway) and genuine Golconda seeker types as well, as well as the Sects becoming parodies of themselves, and the 'suggested' playstyle being basically mandatory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taggie, I think we all know you hate the Humanity system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T02:50:49-07:00","id":1463673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463670#post1463670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway back out of character I'd also argue what they also need is a unifying manifesto and an idea of how they're going to go forward. Coherent institutions offices and checks and safeguards. Otherwise they're just going to end up being the carmarilla 2.0 or more likely a less functional sabbat. At the moment the anarchs are a joke and the punchline is &quot;they're winning&quot; but you can't just be 10 guys on motorcycles who constantly call the prince a fascist because he's annoyed you killed some cops</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes the Anarchs cool is the fact they do not have a coherent ideology but are a variety of groups united by their desire to burn down the system.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I find it weird to argue that a Gothic PUNK game should not have, you know, punks.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T03:13:39-07:00","id":1463676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463673#post1463673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What makes the Anarchs cool is the fact they do not have a coherent ideology but are a variety of groups united by their desire to burn down the system.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I find it weird to argue that a Gothic PUNK game should not have, you know, punks.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> While this has a romantic appeal that's largely why they slowly lost ground in terms of popularity in previous editions. Fighting 'the man' on the street is fun sure but how long before you want to play someone actually interested in meaningful change, complex cultures or some actual personal ambition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T03:25:41-07:00","id":1463678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463673#post1463673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What makes the Anarchs cool is the fact they do not have a coherent ideology but are a variety of groups united by their desire to burn down the system.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I find it weird to argue that a Gothic PUNK game should not have, you know, punks.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yet you always seem to be disappointed that they don't write enough about... people who don't have a coherent ideology and really only want to burn down the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T03:26:31-07:00","id":1463679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463676#post1463676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While this has a romantic appeal that's largely why they slowly lost ground in terms of popularity in previous editions. Fighting 'the man' on the street is fun sure but how long before you want to play someone actually interested in meaningful change, complex cultures or some actual personal ambition?</div> </div> </div> </div>They slowly lost ground because they made the Sabbat the chief antagonists and portrayed them as incredible morons just shooting each other when we finally got the Anarch Free States.<br /> <br /> I also think the Anarchs are best played in Camarilla cities.<br /> <br /> It's silly to play in an Anarch city. What are you rebelling against then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T03:30:23-07:00","id":1463680,"title":"","content":"A new Anarch book would be a good idea. Compared to Cults of the Blood God I'd like more hard facts and way more informations about their political and social structure. When looking at the informations we have, their rise to power makes little sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T03:36:44-07:00","id":1463682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463679#post1463679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They slowly lost ground because they made the Sabbat the chief antagonists and portrayed them as incredible morons just shooting each other when we finally got the Anarch Free States.<br /> <br /> I also think the Anarchs are best played in Camarilla cities.<br /> <br /> It's silly to play in an Anarch city. What are you rebelling against then?</div> </div> </div> </div> No, that's a in game representation of out of game decisions, the anarchs got downplayed because their antagonists are better written. The free states are ironically an in game poster child of what my point v5 anarchs if they have hegemony will have exactly the same issues as the free states. No organization and a system without checks and balances ensures failure.<br /> <br /> Anarchs arnt morons but what they currently collectively propose is moronic. For me that's part of the charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T03:39:00-07:00","id":1463683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463676#post1463676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While this has a romantic appeal that's largely why they slowly lost ground in terms of popularity in previous editions. Fighting 'the man' on the street is fun sure but how long before you want to play someone actually interested in meaningful change, complex cultures or some actual personal ambition?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This so much. I don't want to restrict myself to a maladaptive self insert that can't stomach the realities of unlife. Part of the joyful satire of VTM is that you can actually <i>be &quot;The Man&quot; </i> , you can actually play the guy who benefits from and perpetuates systemic injustices. What better way to screw with Nazis than to actually play the guy who bankrolls them for his own insidious political ends that don't, in any way, benefit the lower class nazis who have championed him. Limiting yourself to an anarch on humanity is intellectually vapid and the farcical state of the nuCam as a moustache twirling foe is ideologically cancerous, nevermind the Sabbat and the &quot;all religions we don't like are bad&quot; attitude v5 has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T03:44:59-07:00","id":1463684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463673#post1463673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, I find it weird to argue that a Gothic PUNK game should not have, you know, punks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody is saying that the game shouldn't have punks. They were one of the core elements of the game from the beginning. You just don't like it when the early game portrayed them as an incoherent, disorganized rabble -- even though you say that's precisely the reason why we're supposed to think that the anarchs are cool.<br /> <br /> Compared to the old Camarilla and the Sabbat, anarchs have all the flavor of wet cardboard. Even with the current push toward making the anarchs the obvious player faction, they continue to have all the flavor of wet cardboard. That is what people are reacting to.<br /> <br /> The reason why the anarchs remain underdeveloped to this day is obvious: they are not a full-fledged sect. <i>They are a faction within the Camarilla.</i> You yourself admit that the anarchs only work in the context of the Camarilla. Splitting the anarchs and the Camarilla into separate sects only manages to diminish both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T04:18:18-07:00","id":1463690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463679#post1463679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's silly to play in an Anarch city. What are you rebelling against then?</div> </div> </div> </div>So what happens after Anarchs rebel?<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a common theme between most of communities described in \u201cAnarch\u201d: it\u2019s anarchy. If you start giving them an organisational framework, then they\u2019re not Anarchs, they\u2019re a new sect, just like how the old Anarchs decided to have bishops, fight the Antediluvians, reject humanity, etc.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t object to such a post-Anarch sect but what exactly would they stand for and how they agree upon that, let alone players?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T04:20:52-07:00","id":1463692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463683#post1463683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This so much. I don't want to restrict myself to a maladaptive self insert that can't stomach the realities of unlife. Part of the joyful satire of VTM is that you can actually <i>be &quot;The Man&quot; </i> , you can actually play the guy who benefits from and perpetuates systemic injustices. What better way to screw with Nazis than to actually play the guy who bankrolls them for his own insidious political ends that don't, in any way, benefit the lower class nazis who have championed him. Limiting yourself to an anarch on humanity is intellectually vapid and the farcical state of the nuCam as a moustache twirling foe is ideologically cancerous, nevermind the Sabbat and the &quot;all religions we don't like are bad&quot; attitude v5 has.</div> </div> </div> </div> Theirs also something to be said for the carmarilla as the lesser or more pragmatic of three evils. In Revised while an corrupting force in the world, the sect itself was far less destructive or dangerous than its counterparts and if you're a vampire and believe you have a right to exist then the ivory tower is pretty okay with its strong masquarade policies, strong support of humanity over paths and pragmatic approach.<br /> Say you've got your domain, a coterie at your back and show up at elysium once a month then spend the rest of your time doing whatever you want as long you don't throw a car at anyone. What appeal do the other sects have then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-13-2021, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T05:35:11-07:00","id":1463696,"title":"","content":"Ultimately there's a reason why Requiem changed the Camarilla into the Invictus, and the Anarchs into the Carthians.<br /> <br /> The Invictus are always &quot;The Man.&quot; Even if they're not in charge of a city, they're gunning for power, and they're going to hold on to the power they have. In power or out of power, they offer continuity and stability at the price of obedience. Playing and Invictus in an Invictus city actually means living up to your end of the bargain while vying with your fellow Covenant members for power. Invictus Oaths are seriously business (magically so), but also help push their more classic conservative political views on how vampires should conduct themselves. If the Invictus aren't in power, those Oaths and the ability to enforce them are still hella useful to whoever is, letting the Invictus to back up their offers of maintaining peace and order on behalf of the current crown even if everyone knows they're still trying to take it for themselves.<br /> <br /> The Carthians are always &quot;The Rebels.&quot; They map much more cleanly onto collectivist anarchist ideology because their goal is not rebellion, but fluidity. They want vampire governments that can adapt with the times instead of calcifying and becoming weak; and only local vampires making local agreements on how their local stuff should be handled can do that. Out of power, that's easy because nobody else agrees with them for the most part and run things their normal ways. When they're in power, they have to justify what they do to their fellow Carthians and other vampires. They need to prove their ideas actually work, and are actually good or even better... or internal revolt is as big of a threat as external opposition. Carthian Law makes sure the &quot;rabble&quot; are never voiceless, even if their own leaders are the ones with the power that need a talking too. Since static laws are weak laws, there's always a tension in Carthian cities between those that think the way things are is the best, and those that think they have a better idea, and that's never going to be settled permanently on purpose.<br /> <br /> While I don't want VtM to copy that setup, it's the sort of depth of design V5 could have really used more thought put into. The Sects needed work, and one thing that needed work was more thought about what members of that Sect look like in all the possible situations they can find themselves in so that you never have anyone saying, &quot;what's the point of playing an Anarch in an Anarch city?&quot; If that's a valid question for players to be asking of the game.... the game should have an answer somewhere already.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T09:12:31-07:00","id":1463706,"title":"","content":"I personally like the Anarchs, but also agree that this is in the context of a Camarilla city. The Anarchs as portrayed in VtM aren't a sect, they're the collective of kindred that on some level disagree with the powers that be. And their appeal is exactly the variety of people you can have in this situation, they're not an organized group but simply the common mass of the people. In a way, they ARE the check and balance of a &quot;healthy&quot; Camarilla-like city.<br /> <br /> And that's not a bad proposal in itself. Wherever you have a power structure you should describe the people on the bottom and, among them, the ones trying to call on the bullshit and have some change, for one reason or another. You need to depict the niche of the characters that don't want to accept the system as is. You have to do this both for NPCs and for PCs that feel like it, that may not exist on some tables, but do at others.<br /> <br /> What's lacking in the Anarchs is the post anarchy, and here the problem isn't not giving them enough depiction as a sect, but exactly <i>insisting in making them a sect</i>. Instead of discussing how new local systems can evolve when the rebellion start to win (and it doesn't have to mean overthrowing the system), the game stubbornly kept to the notion of them as a sect of, well, Anarchs. And that's stupid.<br /> <br /> Because on a ideological level they're not Anarchs. They're a multitude of ideas in varying levels of development, from the ones that have a clear picture of an Utopia to the ones that just want better feeding grounds without politicking. Anarchism is a very specific political ideology that depends on a very specific mindset to work even in theory, a theory few people ascribe to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T09:46:02-07:00","id":1463711,"title":"","content":"So I feel like a lot of people's criticism just boils down to &quot;revolution doesn't work, only reform does&quot; and... that's literally the opposite of what I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T10:27:22-07:00","id":1463719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463711#post1463711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I feel like a lot of people's criticism just boils down to &quot;revolution doesn't work, only reform does&quot; and... that's literally the opposite of what I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the criticism is more about &quot;what to do after the revolution&quot;, and how many people have the same idea.<br /> <br /> I don't believe in revolution anymore, despite being a communist myself. I'm for the collectivization of the means of production for real. But that is besides the point.<br /> <br /> Whatever you do with the system, what is your aim, and how will you get other people to work towards it with you? The game never answered it, instead it got half-assed depictions based on nothing but the idea that once the Cam is down everyone will just abide by the rule of this other guy and formalize nothing.<br /> <br /> You want true Anarchism? Is as valid a goal as any else. But define it and have some ideologues that can help. See if people buy it. What's your proposal?<br /> <br /> The Sabbat literally got there through a revolution, so it definitely works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T10:41:16-07:00","id":1463722,"title":"","content":"My take has been for a while that too make the Anarchs make sense you have to spend as much time thinking about the other sects as you do them and look at why they would rebel.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s easy to come into a kind of quasi-\u2018capitalist realism\u2019 with the Camarilla where it becomes the only system that works or could work and you don\u2019t analyze it and how oppressive it would be to dwell within. If a domain is simply a prince and sheriff who uphold the law and ignore everything else then the only real reason to be an Anarch is to want to replace the prince. You can already do what you like, so if you want to collectivize, you can.<br /> <br /> The necessity of the Movement comes about more when you demonstrate that the Camarilla is an organization run like a neo-manorial mafia. The prince and the sheriff rule through monopoly of violence, the elders hold the young in indentured servitude via prestation and quasi-feudalism through the allotment of feeding grounds as controlled by the elite of elysium. Society is maintained by a rigid and archaic social contract that does not allow for freedom of speech, thought, or expression. Life is held to be cheap behind a veil of human facades.<br /> <br /> This lenses allows one to understand why Anarchs would organize. To have justice be delivered not through the whims of a tyrant serving the interest of the elites but by a council jury of citizen peers and an elected judge. To have power over the many come from the many rather then an oligarchy of gerontocrats. To have the right to feed be distributed according to need so that all have freedom to do so without entering into a debtors contract with any landlord. To allow for systems where vampires may construct domains which are secure and comfortable without becoming chained by prestation.<br /> <br /> All of these are ideals which would be incredibly difficult to achieve and would suffer from the corruption of vampirism and humanity alike, though that doesn\u2019t make them not worth striving towards. They would come with their own complications and nuances if a group of anarchs do claim praxis in a domain.<br /> <br /> Thinking about how organizations like the Camarilla and Sabbat run and function are critical to understanding the dialectic of elder against youth which forms naturally out of it and what resolutions either side seeks to create.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T11:02:59-07:00","id":1463724,"title":"","content":"I mean at its core its...<br /> <br /> Camarilla: Feudalism<br /> Sabbat: Theocracy<br /> Anarch: Anarchy<br /> <br /> Reqiuem its<br /> <br /> Invictus: Fedualism<br /> Lancea Sanctum: Theocracy<br /> Carthian Movement: Anarchy, Communism, or modern Democracy<br /> <br /> Its all just twisted vampiric forms of government lol. At their basic core concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T11:27:20-07:00","id":1463726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463690#post1463690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what happens after Anarchs rebel?</div> </div> </div> </div>Among vampires the question is the goal making a new sect or being in charge. Because I'm cynical enough that most Anarchs object to the people rather than the government.<br /> <br /> Then again, I strongly think that vampires are very similar to mobsters.<br /> <br /> You ask, &quot;What happens when the Corleones are overthrown?&quot;<br /> <br /> The answer is, &quot;You don't have to deal with the Corleones anymore.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's lots of deep thought politically minded Anarchs but for a lot of them it's, &quot;The guy isn't trying to kill or oppress me anymore.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T11:31:42-07:00","id":1463727,"title":"","content":"&quot;&quot;What happens when we knock off Maranzano?&quot;<br /> &quot;We make the Commission, and its super successful and lasts decades&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T11:55:18-07:00","id":1463728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463711#post1463711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I feel like a lot of people's criticism just boils down to &amp;quot;revolution doesn't work, only reform does&amp;quot; and... that's literally the opposite of what I think.</div> </div> </div> </div> Assuming your talking about vtm because I personally don't think you believe anyone needs slotting for general administrative tinkering, no.<br /> The issue is the revolution has no objective or idea of how they're going to build a better society. The 2nd revolt started around 2012, covers a huge number of kindred and terrories and we havnt got a declaration of intent yet. By comparison most revolutions irl at least have a rough outline by now of what they want even if it's just ethnic territorial demands","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T11:57:35-07:00","id":1463729,"title":"","content":"ther issue with the anarchs is that they're defined as &quot;we don't like the cam&quot; which doesn't work as a political sect outside of binary politics and politics aren't a binary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T11:59:26-07:00","id":1463730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463719#post1463719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the criticism is more about &quot;what to do after the revolution&quot;, and how many people have the same idea.<br /> <br /> I don't believe in revolution anymore, despite being a communist myself. I'm for the collectivization of the means of production for real. But that is besides the point.<br /> <br /> Whatever you do with the system, what is your aim, and how will you get other people to work towards it with you? The game never answered it, instead it got half-assed depictions based on nothing but the idea that once the Cam is down everyone will just abide by the rule of this other guy and formalize nothing.<br /> <br /> You want true Anarchism? Is as valid a goal as any else. But define it and have some ideologues that can help. See if people buy it. What's your proposal?<br /> <br /> The Sabbat literally got there through a revolution, so it definitely works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, the criticism of the Anarchs not having any coherent aims or ideals? That I agree with 100%. But as part of the Camarilla? Regardless if you think reformation can work IRL it's essentially impossible when those in power cannot die. The only way to make a change is to roll out the guillotines and you just can't do that within the Ivory Tower. It's basically why my own Anarch faction has been built with things cobbled together from the Sabbat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T11:59:44-07:00","id":1463731,"title":"","content":"Yeah,<br /> <br /> My view of the Anarchs is that they can't actually win but they don't have to lose either. The Anarchs are a more literal version of the Dark Knight quote. They can die heroically resisting oppression against the local Prince and Elders or they can slowly become what they most despise. Attempts to make a new Carthage (or Libertalia or whatever) will always fail but the attempt has its own value.<br /> <br /> Besides, as mentioned, the Anarchs don't have to have high-minded ideals. If you're living in Chicago and the goal is to stop Lodin and Balathazar then stopping them is their own reward. Maybe you get your own territory or maybe you are forced to flee but you have one less enemy. Then again, I was oddly enough inspired for one Chronicle by THE WARRIORS where the protagonists attend a meeting of the Anarchs which is gathering a bunch of local Anarch gangs together to overthrow a brutal incompetant Prince. The legendary hero who gathered it gets killed mid-event? Why? Not because of a Camarilla plot but because one of the gang leaders felt like it.<br /> <br /> That is the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> I just play the Camarilla as every bit as dysfunctional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463728#post1463728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assuming your talking about vtm because I personally don't think you believe anyone needs slotting for general administrative tinkering, no.<br /> The issue is the revolution has no objective or idea of how they're going to build a better society. The 2nd revolt started around 2012, covers a huge number of kindred and terrories and we havnt got a declaration of intent yet. By comparison most revolutions irl at least have a rough outline by now of what they want even if it's just ethnic territorial demands</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on your grievance.<br /> <br /> I remembered one particularly talented player saying that a lot of critics of the Anarchs believed they were hypocrites because they didn't practice democracy. Said player instead said, &quot;In fact, the Anarchs practice a surprisingly efficient form of democracy. If there's 12 Kindred in a gang, the leader of the gang rules by their consent. If they object to him, they rip him apart. There's none of the Camarilla's enforcement by Elysium but direct mob rule. Perfect for vampires.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T11:59:51-07:00","id":1463732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463726#post1463726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Among vampires the question is the goal making a new sect or being in charge. Because I'm cynical enough that most Anarchs object to the people rather than the government.<br /> <br /> Then again, I strongly think that vampires are very similar to mobsters.<br /> <br /> You ask, &quot;What happens when the Corleones are overthrown?&quot;<br /> <br /> The answer is, &quot;You don't have to deal with the Corleones anymore.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's lots of deep thought politically minded Anarchs but for a lot of them it's, &quot;The guy isn't trying to kill or oppress me anymore.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And that's ultimatly a problem. Since all you're really doing is objecting to the fact you're not an elder, which is ultimatly self defeating and pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T12:06:13-07:00","id":1463733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463731#post1463731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends on your grievance.<br /> <br /> I remembered one particularly talented player saying that a lot of critics of the Anarchs believed they were hypocrites because they didn't practice democracy. Said player instead said, &amp;quot;In fact, the Anarchs practice a surprisingly efficient form of democracy. If there's 12 Kindred in a gang, the leader of the gang rules by their consent. If they object to him, they rip him apart. There's none of the Camarilla's enforcement by Elysium but direct mob rule. Perfect for vampires.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> That player is wrong in my case my objections with the anarchs is they don't appear to have anything resembling an idea of how the brave new world will work which is silly for a major sect and eventually boring in the long run from a player perspective. Meaningful conflict is the soul of drama","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T12:10:01-07:00","id":1463734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463733#post1463733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That player is wrong in my case my objections with the anarchs is they don't appear to have anything resembling an idea of how the brave new world will work which is silly for a major sect and eventually boring in the long run from a player perspective. Meaningful conflict is the soul of drama</div> </div> </div> </div>He said flat out what it would be like, a small bunch of vampires directly controlling their leader.<br /> <br /> It is a REJECTION of large sect vampire rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463732#post1463732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's ultimatly a problem. Since all you're really doing is objecting to the fact you're not an elder, which is ultimatly self defeating and pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if you have automatic weapons or a coterie enough to overpower one. You seem to be arguing that objection to unfair distribution of wealth and territory isn't one of THE most primal human reasons for revolution.<br /> <br /> What is better to fight for than survival and territory?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T12:15:34-07:00","id":1463736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463730#post1463730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as part of the Camarilla?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not <i>as part of the Camarilla</i>, but <i>as part of a Camarilla city</i>. That is, in terms of story structure this aimless Anarch work in the setting as a foil to the Camarilla in its own cities. It isn't that the Movement don't want revolution (although I don't think it must want revolution to be a good story element), but that the interplay between Anarch and Cam in the same city is what makes it work in the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T12:22:24-07:00","id":1463738,"title":"","content":"I really like the Cam and Anarchs pre-5 for one simple reason. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla is only as defined as it needs to be in order to get the setting to work and the core themes on the table. Why the Masquerade? Camarilla. Why aren't people taking things out of hand? Camarilla. Want an international conspiracy? Camarilla. Want a self contained city that's indicative of the wider vampire world? Camarilla. But it doesn't stop much, only enough to keep the setting together, a safety net. Want a Tyrant with all the power? Camarilla. Want a fragile council to rule? Camarilla. Want feuding bloodlines? Camarilla. Want Dave and his wife Sally? Camarilla. <br /> <br /> Not being well defined is a strength. Storytellers pre-5 have the optimum amount of leeway to do whatever they want with their cities whilst the Camarilla functions as just-enough-string for a safety net with a good dose of verisimilitude. It's a big sandbox with good walls. The Anarchs naturally fit into whatever you really want to do with the camarilla, they're intuitive resistance that don't need much defining. <br /> <br /> The Sabbat offer a smaller sandbox, but with very colourful sand and a lot of good non-sand props to work with <br /> '<br /> V5 tries too hard in defining the Camarilla. It's an even smaller sandbox with a few colours and a few mediocre non-sand props to work with. you just don't have the freedom and the context around the Cam (the SI) is very restricting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T12:26:20-07:00","id":1463739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463734#post1463734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He said flat out what it would be like, a small bunch of vampires directly controlling their leader.<br /> <br /> It is a REJECTION of large sect vampire rule.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not if you have automatic weapons or a coterie enough to overpower one. You seem to be arguing that objection to unfair distribution of wealth and territory isn't one of THE most primal human reasons for revolution.<br /> <br /> What is better to fight for than survival and territory?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about my objection not his solution, im.not saying the anarchs should believe in democracy I'm saying they should either believe in something or at least some ideas they want to implement.<br /> <br /> Also his solution is just the Sabbat again but it's going to get steamrolled by the other sects who brought 30 guys.<br /> <br /> No I'm arguing that if you're going to have one of major sects.in a major conflict have neither ideological or structural aspects then that's bad writing. Consider your argument about territory do the rebels have say a command structure? How is controlled territory governed? How do they deal with disciplinary measures or resources distribution? What happens when they win?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T12:43:48-07:00","id":1463740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463739#post1463739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also his solution is just the Sabbat again but it's going to get steamrolled by the other sects who brought 30 guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat have absolute control ove rtheir followers and are the opposite of any form of democracy. However, the Beast means that any form of change in leadership is inherently violent.<br /> <br /> There is no democratic reform or peaceful transition of power among vampires.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T13:05:23-07:00","id":1463743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463740#post1463740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Sabbat have absolute control ove rtheir followers and are the opposite of any form of democracy. However, the Beast means that any form of change in leadership is inherently violent.<br /> <br /> There is no democratic reform or peaceful transition of power among vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>So how do you remove a superior from a position of power the Sabbat? Which does occur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T13:54:35-07:00","id":1463745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463743#post1463743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So how do you remove a superior from a position of power the Sabbat? Which does occur.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a Pack level, it occurs via monomacy. A truly awful pack leader is going to face challenge after challenge until he either loses, or the whole pack just gets fed up and quietly offs him. On a larger level, leaders need the support of multiple packs to keep/ascend to power. So the potential leaders court the favor of the most powerful packs in the region, likely resulting in mini-civil-wars until someone is victorious. The very top guys seem to be elected Pope-style by elites, but those electing them need to consider whether that election would spark a larger civil war, so that election must at least keep in mind largescale appeal, meaning it won't be too far away from who would win a human style democratic election.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T14:11:41-07:00","id":1463747,"title":"","content":"That's the Revised answer where the Sabbat has some democratic trappings since the Code of Milan does say that leaders lead at the consent of those beneath them in its way. Not the answer to the situation that CT posits where the Sabbat have absolute control over their followers.<br /> <br /> If the leaders have absolute control, they don't have to worry about challenges from within.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T14:22:01-07:00","id":1463748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463747#post1463747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the Revised answer where the Sabbat has some democratic trappings since the Code of Milan does say that leaders lead at the consent of those beneath them in its way. Not the answer to the situation that CT posits where the Sabbat have absolute control over their followers.<br /> <br /> If the leaders have absolute control, they don't have to worry about challenges from within.</div> </div> </div> </div>here's a wild suggestion: maybe CT was wrong","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T14:43:56-07:00","id":1463749,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure CT is wrong in V5's take on the Sect. Though it creates the logical inconsistency Robin noted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T14:50:13-07:00","id":1463750,"title":"","content":"I always thought that was part of the Sabbat's &quot;joke.&quot; Monomancy is meant to make it seem like the Sabbat have a perfect way of resolving disputes and order. Except the nature of monomancy is that the Elders will always win in a one-on-one challenge. Which is why the Elders rule and the Neonates obey.<br /> <br /> An Anarch is a threat to the Elder only as a group.<br /> <br /> Part of what I loved about the Old Sabbat is they WERE every bit as hypocritical and corrupt as the Camarilla. They just lied about the whole freedom thing. The biggest twist for V5 for me is the idea that anyone over the age of 50 in the Sabbat believed in the whole, &quot;defeat the Antediluvians&quot; thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T16:13:17-07:00","id":1463757,"title":"","content":"If I could just interject to say that the archaic term for a duel is <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monomachy\" target=\"_blank\">monomachy</a>. Single combat. Not &quot;monomacy,&quot; like it was misspelled in <i>The Players Guide to the Sabbat,</i> and therefore carried over to every subsequent Sabbat-related product. And certainly not &quot;monomancy,&quot; which would be, what, &quot;single divination&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T16:20:08-07:00","id":1463759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463757#post1463757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I could just interject to say that the archaic term for a duel is <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monomachy\" target=\"_blank\">monomachy</a>. Single combat. Not &quot;monomacy,&quot; like it was misspelled in <i>The Players Guide to the Sabbat,</i> and therefore carried over to every subsequent Sabbat-related product. And certainly not &quot;monomancy,&quot; which would be, what, &quot;single divination&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the translations aren't great. As mentioned earlier in thread:<br /> <br /> Palla Grande also means &quot;The Grand (Soccer) Ball&quot; in Italian not the Grand Dance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T16:23:03-07:00","id":1463760,"title":"","content":"The triick with Sabbat monomancy isnt Steve the pander neonate vs Theoderic the Tzmisce elder, the danger/operunity is from your immediate superiors, subordinates and peers. If you're a Lasombra Bishop whose on the shit list, the monomancy you have to worry about is the guy whose next in line for your job or personally hates you. Likewise an inept ductus might find the rival packs ductus issuing challange after he fox-frenzies in a siege. The Lasombra (had) an entire system set up to kill bad Lasombra at any age.<br /> <br /> Which ironically brings me back to my original point as were discussion actual complex sect law and how they operated on a day to day Something the anarchs don't have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-13-2021, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T16:52:34-07:00","id":1463761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463760#post1463760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The triick with Sabbat monomancy isnt Steve the pander neonate vs Theoderic the Tzmisce elder, the danger/operunity is from your immediate superiors, subordinates and peers. If you're a Lasombra Bishop whose on the shit list, the monomancy you have to worry about is the guy whose next in line for your job or personally hates you. Likewise an inept ductus might find the rival packs ductus issuing challange after he fox-frenzies in a siege. The Lasombra (had) an entire system set up to kill bad Lasombra at any age.<br /> <br /> then again v5 Sabbat are orcs so maybe sauron tells them what to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression of the Pre-V5 Sabbat was basically the Elders of the Sabbat were every bit as hostile and inclined to oppression of their Neonates/Ancilla as the Camarilla but they have taken the Henry IV route:<br /> <br /> <i>To lead out many to the Holy Land,<br /> Lest rest and lying still might make them look<br /> Too near unto my state. Therefore, my Harry,<br /> Be it thy course to busy giddy minds<br /> With foreign quarrels;</i><br /> <br /> Or in Modern English: The Sabbat make sure no one attempts to overthrow the local Archbishop, Cardinals, Bishops, and Priscus by sending the excess Kindred all out on Crusades against Camarilla territories. If they succeed then they gain a new city to divide up among themselves as well as increase the Sabbat's power. If they fail then they lose the excess population their society can't sustain.<br /> <br /> The Elders still engage in all of their petty bickering and power jockeying but they have used this as a solution for their Anarch problem. Theoretically. As we've seen with the various Sabbat Civil Wars, the Antitribu and Loyalists have steadily gained more and more power that has eroded the traditional Clans of Lasombra and Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> As a Sabbat fan, I would want to know how the Loyalists have apparently TOTALLY destroyed the Old Order and replaced it with the mob that was previously a bunch of useful idiots. I'm not saying it couldn't happen but it deserved a trilogy or fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T17:47:32-07:00","id":1463765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463761#post1463761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My impression of the Pre-V5 Sabbat was basically the Elders of the Sabbat were every bit as hostile and inclined to oppression of their Neonates/Ancilla as the Camarilla but they have taken the Henry IV route:<br /> <br /> <i>To lead out many to the Holy Land,<br /> Lest rest and lying still might make them look<br /> Too near unto my state. Therefore, my Harry,<br /> Be it thy course to busy giddy minds<br /> With foreign quarrels;</i><br /> <br /> Or in Modern English: The Sabbat make sure no one attempts to overthrow the local Archbishop, Cardinals, Bishops, and Priscus by sending the excess Kindred all out on Crusades against Camarilla territories. If they succeed then they gain a new city to divide up among themselves as well as increase the Sabbat's power. If they fail then they lose the excess population their society can't sustain.<br /> <br /> The Elders still engage in all of their petty bickering and power jockeying but they have used this as a solution for their Anarch problem. Theoretically. As we've seen with the various Sabbat Civil Wars, the Antitribu and Loyalists have steadily gained more and more power that has eroded the traditional Clans of Lasombra and Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> As a Sabbat fan, I would want to know how the Loyalists have apparently TOTALLY destroyed the Old Order and replaced it with the mob that was previously a bunch of useful idiots. I'm not saying it couldn't happen but it deserved a trilogy or fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div> This Is certainly correct sabbat eldars are vile, but again this leads away from my point-sabbat and carmarilla politics have a depth the anarchs don't and this is going to be detrimental moving forward unless addressed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T17:52:52-07:00","id":1463766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463765#post1463765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This Is certainly correct sabbat eldars are vile, but again this leads away from my point-sabbat and carmarilla politics have a depth the anarchs don't and this is going to be detrimental moving forward unless addressed</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the issue is you want there to be complex labyrinthine games and the appeal of the Anarchs is that you don't have them. Even then, your character is an Anarch just by not wanting to be ground underfoot.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T19:01:13-07:00","id":1463771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463766#post1463766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think part of the issue is you want there to be complex labyrinthine games and the appeal of the Anarchs is that you don't have them. Even then, your character is an Anarch just by not wanting to be ground underfoot.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I want depth from a major sect which is apparently the settings primary protagonist group. Something the anarchs fundemently lack because they're incredibly underwritten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T19:02:10-07:00","id":1463773,"title":"","content":"I don't think there needs to be complex labyrinthine Anarch games as such, but the sect does need much more flavour.<br /> <br /> So for instance, my Anarch faction that's trying to take control of Glasgow is mostly made from some local gangs and ex-Sabbat packs led by a Child of the Dracon Tzimisce. They are trying to fulfill the Dream by making Glasgow the &quot;Carthage of the North.&quot; The way they plan to do this is to apply the Vaulderie to not just every kindred in the city, but also, eventually, when the time is right, apply it to every kine as well. Then there is also a bunch of Ministry influence (who claim to be the original religion of Carthage) and a bunch of conflict with the Camarilla in Edinburgh, which of course is all about the Cult of Mithras.<br /> <br /> Basically I'm trying to make the sect feel as flavourful and unique as possible, which tbf kind of ends up being a &quot;kinder&quot; Sabbat with the numbers filed off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T21:15:18-07:00","id":1463788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463765#post1463765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This Is certainly correct sabbat eldars are vile, but again this leads away from my point-sabbat and carmarilla politics have a depth the anarchs don't and this is going to be detrimental moving forward unless addressed</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that is kind of the problem. The Camarilla and Sabbat each have a long history with various practices, engagement with other groups, internal schisms and the like. Meanwhile... well there have been &quot;Anarchs&quot; around for a long time, but they're not any sort of unified faction. You don't really have this sense of history when dealing with the Anarchs. And Anarchs holding their own major territories and running things is a fairly recent phenomenon - previously most major metropolitan areas were under the control of the Camarilla, the Sabbat or were in parts of the world well outside of the Camarilla/Sabbat/Anarch conflict (the Middle East, India, China, Africa, etc). Anarchs might have technically held territory, but it was usually just some hole-in-the-wall place that neither the Sabbat nor the Camarilla was interested in. And if their territory did end up getting big and important the Sabbat or Camarilla would move in and that would be that.<br /> <br /> Then you got the the idea of the Anarch Free States and now the idea that the Anarchs can hold territory and are a fully equal faction to the Camarilla and the Sabbat. But that's an extremely modern idea. So there's not really any history or long-standing politics among the Anarchs. For all intents and purposes the Anarchs, as a political faction to rival the Camarilla and Sabbat, only started back in 1943 with the start of the Anarch Revolt, but realistically they only became a real faction in the 80's. So they have less than 40 years of history behind them.<br /> <br /> I think they just need to spin the fact that the Anarchs <i>don't</i> have that historical depth as a positive - here's a faction that's very new and that has all sorts of opportunities for newer, younger vampires who would largely be little more than gofers or worse in the Sabbat/Camarilla. Players will sort of be in on the &quot;ground floor&quot; and likely be helping to create the politics and depth of the Anarch faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T21:24:08-07:00","id":1463789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463788#post1463788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean that is kind of the problem. The Camarilla and Sabbat each have a long history with various practices, engagement with other groups, internal schisms and the like. Meanwhile... well there have been &quot;Anarchs&quot; around for a long time, but they're not any sort of unified faction. You don't really have this sense of history when dealing with the Anarchs. And Anarchs holding their own major territories and running things is a fairly recent phenomenon - previously most major metropolitan areas were under the control of the Camarilla, the Sabbat or were in parts of the world well outside of the Camarilla/Sabbat/Anarch conflict (the Middle East, India, China, Africa, etc). Anarchs might have technically held territory, but it was usually just some hole-in-the-wall place that neither the Sabbat nor the Camarilla was interested in. And if their territory did end up getting big and important the Sabbat or Camarilla would move in and that would be that.<br /> <br /> Then you got the the idea of the Anarch Free States and now the idea that the Anarchs can hold territory and are a fully equal faction to the Camarilla and the Sabbat. But that's an extremely modern idea. So there's not really any history or long-standing politics among the Anarchs. For all intents and purposes the Anarchs, as a political faction to rival the Camarilla and Sabbat, only started back in 1943 with the start of the Anarch Revolt, but realistically they only became a real faction in the 80's. So they have less than 40 years of history behind them.<br /> <br /> I think they just need to spin the fact that the Anarchs <i>don't</i> have that historical depth as a positive - here's a faction that's very new and that has all sorts of opportunities for newer, younger vampires who would largely be little more than gofers or worse in the Sabbat/Camarilla. Players will sort of be in on the &quot;ground floor&quot; and likely be helping to create the politics and depth of the Anarch faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, yes and no. One of the things I was very interested in (as introduced by ANARCHS UNBOUND) was the idea that the Brujah Council was an Anarch Free State before the California one because that really changes just about everything we know about the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> That for 100 years, the Soviet Union's vampire Illuminati were Anarchs.<br /> <br /> It's sort of like introducing the Romulans in Star Trek and then never following up on that. It changes the entire power dynamic of the setting and the Anarchs as a whole.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T23:42:05-07:00","id":1463797,"title":"","content":"Was that a retcon? From what I recall the Brujah Council explicitly never claimed to be an Anarch territory and their actions generally went against most of the typical Anarch ideals. The Camarilla labeled them all as Anarchs, but they always firmly rejected the label. They were closer to something like the Ashirra, a different sect entirely, rather than a group focused on rejecting the Camarilla (which is what distinguishes Anarchs from members of sects that are completely removed from the Camarilla/Sabbat).<br /> <br /> Though seeing as how the Brujah Council was utterly wiped out I suppose it's more of a historical footnote either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T00:13:30-07:00","id":1463800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463797#post1463797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was that a retcon? From what I recall the Brujah Council explicitly never claimed to be an Anarch territory and their actions generally went against most of the typical Anarch ideals. The Camarilla labeled them all as Anarchs, but they always firmly rejected the label. They were closer to something like the Ashirra, a different sect entirely, rather than a group focused on rejecting the Camarilla (which is what distinguishes Anarchs from members of sects that are completely removed from the Camarilla/Sabbat).<br /> <br /> Though seeing as how the Brujah Council was utterly wiped out I suppose it's more of a historical footnote either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Afaik they never called themselves Anarchs, the Cam called them that, but they didn't have much in common with 'mainstream' Anarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T00:15:07-07:00","id":1463801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463800#post1463800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Afaik they never called themselves Anarchs, the Cam called them that, but they didn't have much in common with 'mainstream' Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anarchs Unbound stated that the Brujah Council was financing the Anarch Movement in dozens of other countries and was heavily involved in shaping their ideology.<br /> <br /> So V20 made them Anarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T00:48:08-07:00","id":1463805,"title":"","content":"That's interesting and does push theAnarch timeline back by about 20 years. They're still very modern as a faction compared to the Camarilla, Sabbat, Ashirra, etc. Still, I guess the Brujah Council would serve as a historical inspiration for modern Anarchs, sort of like how Carthage does.<br /> <br /> That said there's some serious irony in the fact that in the US, at the time of the &quot;Red Scare&quot; people were terrified at the idea that the Russians were secretly funding and assisting people in America for the goal of overthrowing the government and overturning society. That was almost entirely bullshit. Meanwhile in vampiric society, that's <i>literally exactly what was happening.</i> \ud83e\udd23","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-14-2021, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T01:04:21-07:00","id":1463807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463805#post1463805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's interesting and does push theAnarch timeline back by about 20 years. They're still very modern as a faction compared to the Camarilla, Sabbat, Ashirra, etc. Still, I guess the Brujah Council would serve as a historical inspiration for modern Anarchs, sort of like how Carthage does.<br /> <br /> That said there's some serious irony in the fact that in the US, at the time of the &quot;Red Scare&quot; people were terrified at the idea that the Russians were secretly funding and assisting people in America for the goal of overthrowing the government and overturning society. That was almost entirely bullshit. Meanwhile in vampiric society, that's <i>literally exactly what was happening.</i> \ud83e\udd23</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, is it weird I think this means the Anarchs seem less useless? I say that as an Anarch fan but conquering LA is not enough for 600 years of work.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, they also were but the Communist Party funded by the Soviet Union in the USA collapsed before WW2 when they ordered them to not support the New Deal. (They assumed that Roosevelt reforming capitalism would hurt them)<br /> <br /> The Americans locals thought this was....well, stupid.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oddly, I suppose this means Salvador Garcia probably WAS an agent of the Russians in the Anarch Free State.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-14-2021, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T01:36:07-07:00","id":1463809,"title":"","content":"I don't know &quot;useless&quot; is a word I'd use to describe the Anarchs. The thing is, for most of history the Anarchs weren't a sect or organization. Individual cities had Anarchs, and those Anarch groups may have had politics and such, but those were all about local issues. For most Anarchs their beef was with the local Prince. There wasn't some global Anarch conclave where Anarchs got together once every twenty years to chat and hash out plans.<br /> <br /> So the Anarchs in Berlin didn't necessarily have much to do with the Anarchs in Paris. There would have been some ideological sense of solidarity in the way both were &quot;sticking it to The Man&quot; but for the most part, Berlin's Anarchs weren't going to to be directly interacting with or helping Paris' Anarchs. And if the Anarchs did manage to overthrow a Prince it was only a matter of time before the Camarilla or Sabbat would move back in because the Anarchs lakes those sorts of global resources. I don't think that's really a problem. In fact trying to turn the Anarchs into a major sect like the Camarilla, Sabbat, Ashirra, etc is more problematic and awkward because, again, there's not really a sense of the Anarchs as a distinct sect. <br /> <br /> So again, I think the best thing to do is to play up that sense that this sect is basically just now getting its legs under it, it doesn't have a strongly defined ideology other than rejecting the Camarilla and Sabbat, so the sect could end up going anywhere and becoming anything and, oh yeah, the PCs are in on the ground floor and can try to help raise this thing into something they like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-14-2021, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T01:59:26-07:00","id":1463810,"title":"","content":"To put it another way the most distinguishing and defining aspect of the Anarchs is that power and prestige are determined by deeds, not by blood or age. In the Camarilla in 10 years someone could go from being Prince's Lacky #27 to being Prince's Lacky #19. If you've just been turned into a vampire and have very high generation, it's going to be a long, long time before you can realistically get power. <br /> <br /> In the Sabbat power is determined by survival. If you survive long enough you deserve power. But of course age and generation equal survival. The Sabbat make a big show about equality but it's all a lie.<br /> <br /> With the Anarchs even some high generation vampire who just turned a few weeks ago can start amassing political and social power depending on what he does. I think the Bloodlines game highlights that. If the Protagonist had chosen to side with the Anarchs and stick around she'd easily be a leading figure even though she just became a vampire a few nights before. That's what the game needs to highlight and push, that player Anarchs are going to have a large amount of self-determination, and as a result the Chronicle is going to be very different from a Camarilla or Sabbat one.<br /> <br /> Yeah the Anarchs don't have the history or politics of other sects, but the players and their ST are the ones who will be creating that to some degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-14-2021, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"t