20:32:19-07:00","id":1464143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1464141#post1464141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thiiiink I need to trouble tickets this, but all my posts seemed to vanish from the thread for like 5 seconds, then when I refreshed, they were back. I don't suppose anyone else noticed that?</div> </div> </div> </div>That happens to me sometimes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T20:38:20-07:00","id":1464144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1464128#post1464128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to chime in about the &amp;quot;1st edition = Anarch edition&amp;quot; bit.<br /> As someone who owns and has read 1st edition, I can say.... Um, <b>no?</b><br /> <br /> Camarilla was still very much the default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anarchs are in the Camarilla. Back then it wasn\u2019t two separate organizations like the Sabbat and Camarilla. The Anarchs were there within Camarilla cities, opposing the rulers mostly within the system. I think that the assumed default was playing an Anarch aligned vampire within the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T20:42:33-07:00","id":1464146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1464080#post1464080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to point out but you basically are saying, &amp;quot;Anarchs aren't cool because I play them as poseurs and losers&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> Also, I hate to point this out but if you're playing a Thin Blood out to survive and kill the guys in power then that's pretty much an Anarch. One of my all time favorite Anarchs is Jenna Cross and she's a Thin Blood revolutionary trained by Smiling Jack.<br /> <br /> But I don't disagree yours is a valid interpretation either as dealing with poseurs and hypocrites is something every Anarch should deal with. The PCs are usually the only Anarchs who are 100% true to the cause because it's their job to be the protagonists and guiding voice in the Movement. It's why Mark Rein Hagen made the first Anarch we meet in V:TM be Juggler, the ultimate in poseur rebels with the possible exception of Gengis.<br /> <br /> Indeed, funnily, V5 gives Juggler MORE dignity than he initially had as a rebel.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Some bits by Justin Achilli:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1449013445647548417\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://abs.twimg.com/x-web/assets/og/default-og.a2e144f0cf66.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1449013445647548417\" target=\"_blank\"> Post Not Found - X | 404 Error </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1449013445647548417\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1449013445647548417 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The post you're looking for could not be found or may have been deleted. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1449013931515813891\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://abs.twimg.com/x-web/assets/og/default-og.a2e144f0cf66.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1449013931515813891\" target=\"_blank\"> Post Not Found - X | 404 Error </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1449013931515813891\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1449013931515813891 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The post you're looking for could not be found or may have been deleted. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Weird that a faction set up to mock and denigrate the civil rights movement became the forced protagonists..while mpcking and denigrating civil rights even more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T20:53:47-07:00","id":1464149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1464138#post1464138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that is flat abuse of power, you did lie about what he said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since people decided to talk about it, as someone who liked and agreed to Archderd's comment, he shouldn't have fought over it publicly with moderation. He could and should have talked this through PMs, with CT and other mods. At this point the original comment isn't the problem anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1464146#post1464146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird that a faction set up to mock and denigrate the civil rights movement became the forced protagonists..while mpcking and denigrating civil rights even more.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as the authors may not have had a complete grasp of those movements, I don't think the Anarchs were set up to mock anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T21:17:07-07:00","id":1464151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1464144#post1464144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anarchs are in the Camarilla. Back then it wasn\u2019t two separate organizations like the Sabbat and Camarilla. The Anarchs were there within Camarilla cities, opposing the rulers mostly within the system. I think that the assumed default was playing an Anarch aligned vampire within the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Moving the goal post still doesn't guarantee the score.<br /> Once again, as someone <i>who literally has read the 1st edition book</i> I can tell you that is not the case. The Camarilla was the assumed default (and technically, the only playable option). <br /> Whether or not you joined the Anarchs or the authors wanted you to, is irrelevant to the fact that the book as-written has you playing a Camarilla member by default. <br /> <br /> Also, just to prod Achilli's statements even more:<br /> <br /> It's curious how in his mind 5th Edition is &quot;Anarch Edition&quot;, and yet the book seems to be just as cool with you playing Camarilla.<br /> Let's start with some small bits, aside from the fact that it lays everything out for Camarilla chronicles and characters same as it does for anarchs: <br /> <br /> * The Relationship Map example shows a Camarilla coterie as the PCs (they are the Prince's marechal coterie).<br /> * The Camarilla is the first mentioned option in the Sect selection bit in the character creation.<br /> * The Chronicles chapter lays out Camarilla chronicles equally to Anarch ones.<br /> * The examples in the Chronicles chapter are also written about a group playing a Camarilla chronicle.<br /> * There are Camarilla Lore Sheets in the corebook.<br /> <br /> If the authors wanted to make this an &quot;Anarchs FIRST&quot; edition, they have a strange, &quot;let's-eat-the-cake-and-leave-it-whole&quot; attitude.<br /> I guess it's that attitude that gave us playable Lasombra and Tzimisce <i>&quot;but not <b>Sabbat</b>, you guys!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Heavy sigh, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T21:26:37-07:00","id":1464153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1464146#post1464146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weird that a faction set up to mock and denigrate the civil rights movement became the forced protagonists..while mpcking and denigrating civil rights even more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting interpretation. Please tell me more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T21:56:32-07:00","id":1464155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1464149#post1464149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since people decided to talk about it, as someone who liked and agreed to Archderd's comment, he shouldn't have fought over it publicly with moderation. He could and should have talked this through PMs, with CT and other mods. At this point the original comment isn't the problem anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> As much as the authors may not have had a complete grasp of those movements, I don't think the Anarchs were set up to mock anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think all of the factions had an element of mockery to them, in all the gamelines. There's always been a lot more &quot;Family Guy&quot; in the WOD than people seem to see these days.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T21:57:00-07:00","id":1464156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1464153#post1464153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting interpretation. Please tell me more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, we have the OG Chicago By Nights real life civil rights activists as vampires being at best hypocrites and more usually straw characters. Then we have the vast majority of Anarchs we see being gangsters, thugs etc.to a cartoonish degree. Mind you this isn't unique to Anarchs we know the issues Ravnos and Assamites had/have as well.<br /> <br /> As an aside the movements being full of spies/agent provocateur is sadly realistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 10-16-2021, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T01:43:44-07:00","id":1464163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1464151#post1464151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, as someone <i>who literally has read the 1st edition book</i> I can tell you that is not the case. The Camarilla was the assumed default (and technically, the only playable option).</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not the only one, so you'll have to live with the idea that people can interpret the same books in different ways.<br /> <br /> This is not about mechanics or about straightforward telling the reader how to play, of course they didn't do that neither here or there. Instead, it is about plot structure and narrative roles.<br /> <br /> First edition don't talk about Anarchs as a sect. Instead, they're a phenomenon. The only two sects are Sabbat (unplayable on core) and Camarilla, the Anarchs are a subculture of the young vampires in the Camarilla. It is about Neonates and Ancillae vs Elders. As the book unfolds you can grasp what are the narrative expectations for each one: who'll have a better chance at maintaining Humanity, who'll have a shot at a &quot;happy end&quot;, who'll find out more truths or make a more meaningful impact on the setting.<br /> <br /> Put on V5 terms, where they're effectively distinct sects, one embraces modern society, have space for sensible decisions and at least may understand the problems of common people, the other are mustache twirling villains that forbid their young from using computers and try to live as feudal lords in the 21st century while one of their most well defended secret places literally got bombed the other day.<br /> <br /> Sure, the game lets you chose freely between &quot;blank canvas for your self-insert&quot; and &quot;your grognard granpa but Evil\u2122&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1464155#post1464155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think all of the factions had an element of mockery to them, in all the gamelines. There's always been a lot more &quot;Family Guy&quot; in the WOD than people seem to see these days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having an element of mockery is different from being setup as mockery. As I see it, the authors played them mostly straight.<br /> <br /> \u200bKeep in mind that some interpretations too silly for us to take seriously today were thought seriously at the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1464156#post1464156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you this isn't unique to Anarchs we know the issues Ravnos and Assamites had/have as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is precisely the point, they're not mocking with stereotypes, they're playing the stereotypes straight.<br /> <br /> A lot of people believed those were real, faithful representations of those people. Sometimes even with good intentions. At the time this wouldn't even fly as a joke, as no one would get it as ironic. People who believed that would say it aloud no problem, people who didn't were still a minority. Even among more progressive minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T03:24:55-07:00","id":1464168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1464155#post1464155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think all of the factions had an element of mockery to them, in all the gamelines. There's always been a lot more &quot;Family Guy&quot; in the WOD than people seem to see these days.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Looking <span style=\"color:#494949\">at designer notes for </span><span style=\"color:#494949\">an</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">arch indic</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">ate its being pl</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">ayed straight.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#494949\">To jump b</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#494949\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">ack to the Sabbat book did anyone else notice it contradicted itself......sometimes mid paragraph, for example saying the sabbat doesnt have territory then explaining how it's territories work?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-16-2021, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T09:25:22-07:00","id":1464204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1464168#post1464168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Looking <span style=\"color:#494949\">at designer notes for </span><span style=\"color:#494949\">an</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">arch indic</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">ate its being pl</span><span style=\"color:#494949\">ayed straight.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#494949\">To jump b</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#494949\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">ack to the Sabbat book did anyone else notice it contradicted itself......sometimes mid paragraph, for example saying the sabbat doesnt have territory then explaining how it's territories work?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>It's being played straight now, but there was a much stronger Family Guy style mockery to the early stuff. Everyone was rather cartoony and just wrong about a lot of stuff, and goofilly wrong at that. It was a game about cartoony straw conservatives and cartoony straw liberals and cartoony straw feminists and cartoony straw misogynists and so forth. It was like watching a war between Stan and Hayley on American Dad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T11:52:23-07:00","id":1464210,"title":"","content":"I always got the impression that the Anarchs were the intended protagonists because the writers of the game liked the idea of the powerless fighting against the powerful. It was the punk part of the gothic punk aesthetic. The authors were largely sympathetic to the underdog and thought that they were cool. Sure, some silly elements were thrown in by intent or through carelessness, but I don\u2019t think that mockery was a significant motive.<br /> <br /> Even when we talk about the ethnic stereotypes in the older books, we have to keep in mind that all of fiction is full of stereotypes, some might even say archetypes. For the most part, people like those. We see a tough biker and make a bunch of assumptions about that character. We see a religious rural southerner and make another set of assumptions. When someone plays D&amp;D and have a paladin character, the player has all kinds of ideas (stereotypes) about what a knight in shining armor is supposed to be like.<br /> <br /> In many regards, the ethnic stereotypes in WoD are like that. Toreador are associated with France because the French are stereotypically seen (in the USA) as artsy and hedonistic. Get of Fenris are these berserker warrior pseudo-Nazis because that is a Germanic/Norse stereotype.<br /> <br /> The Ravnos are an entire Clan based (originally) off of the Romani stereotype. Not as an attempt to insult or ridicule Romani people, but because they were just one of hundreds of other stereotypes being used for storytelling back then and in the early 1990\u2019s they weren\u2019t as sensitive about a lot of ethnic stereotypes as we are now. We still actually have plenty of other stereotypes in fiction now (including WoD) that most people seem alright with that maybe in the future will be regarded as insensitive or offensive.<br /> <br /> Well, that is a bit of a tangent, but my main point is that I don\u2019t think that satire was the intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T16:15:51-07:00","id":1464228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1464151#post1464151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heavy sigh, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sigh a lot when it comes to this stuff, you don't need to ask, just assume I am. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ---------------------<br /> <br /> Also, on the satire bit: The WoD has always had a heavy dose of satire to it, but in a very literary definition of satire rather than what most people think of when you use the word in general conversation.<br /> <br /> There's three traditional schools of satire. I think most people think satire = Horatian satire, as the most directly comedic school of satire. Horace's approach to mockery was to make light and jest, and to point out flaws in a blunted fashion as to mollify the target's with the humor so they'd be more receptive to the criticism. The Colbert Report is a great modern example.<br /> <br /> The WoD leaned heavily into Juvenalian or Menippean satire depending on the game line. VtM is very Juvenalian: it's not funny, but mocks through caricature and hyperbole to tear down those it sees as wrong, and like any good Juvenalian satire aims to make its targets look absurd in their delusions that they could possibly be right. This is also very old-school punk. Mage or CtD could have a whole book written on which is the more Menippean satire. Horatian and Juvenalian satire usually has easily identified targets (either specific people, or specific groups of people). Menippean satire is about targeting ideas, cultural norms, national mythologies, and other social constructs. It tends to appear more light hearted and comedic, but only to lead into very dark absurdity. The now fairly common tropes around stories that go, &quot;this community seems like some blissful utopia, but you soon find out it's a horrific dystopia that the characters desperately need to escape,&quot; tend to be the more down to Earth incarnations of Menippean satire. A Clockwork Orange is more of what the WoD does: take an already absurdly dark take on humanity and then show how much worse it can get.<br /> <br /> Probably more rambling than the topic needed on the tangent, but hopefully useful for interpreting why some people call the WoD satire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T16:59:50-07:00","id":1464232,"title":"","content":"I think the big difference of CBN's Anarchs (1st Edition) vs. later ones is the fact that they seemed to be largely sincere in their social convictions. Gengis was the only one who was a complete poseur as he was a &quot;champagne punk&quot; and conformist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T12:45:57-07:00","id":1464619,"title":"","content":"I am lowering my score to 4/5. I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> made some very good points about how the absence of player rules is a significant issue. The size of it is also bugging me after an initial few weeks of enthusiasm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T12:47:20-07:00","id":1464620,"title":"","content":"I am writing up another review for GRIMDARK MAGAZINE that I thought I'd share since, well, I'm an indie contractor and they won't mind:<br /> <br /> SABBAT: THE BLACK HAND is a supplement for Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition. For those unfamiliar with the roleplaying game, it was extraordinarily popular during the Nineties and one of the biggest influences on LARP as well as several media franchises. Elements were incorporated into Blade and the Underworld movies plus cropped up in True Blood's later seasons. It is set in a horror themed version of our world where vampires live among us and secretly pull humanity's strings. Grimdark Magazine reviewed the 5th Edition core book of the game and was mostly very positive (link: <a href=\"https://www.grimdarkmagazine.com/review-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.grimdarkmagazine.com/rev...e-5th-edition/</a>)<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, there was one serious flaw with the book and that was the absence of one of the main sects of the game. It's a bit like doing The Lord of the Rings and forgetting to include Sauron's people. The Sabbat are not the &quot;evil&quot; vampires since most vampires are some kind of bastard or another but they're certainly the evilest. Without them, the game felt significantly less than complete and many people felt like one of their favorite player character options was missing. Storytellers were also denied one of the most popular antagonists that could easily be thrown in a game to wreck havoc.<br /> <br /> This book, written by long time V:TM writer Justin Achilli, goes a long way to rectifying that absence. It also has serious flaws of its own but successfully does, at least, fill a hole that was extremely noticeable in V5 games. Those who are seeking rules for how to play Sabbat are still going to be disappointed, though. Not only does the book state that it is only meant for antagonists but it specifically precludes any rules that would make Sabbat playable in V5. There are no rules for Path followers, Loresheets, or series staples like the Vaulderie.<br /> <br /> I generally don't judge books by what they don't offer but I should note this absence is something that shouldn't be glossed over either. Vampire: The Masquerade is a game about playing monsters and acting like the Sabbat are a &quot;bridge too far&quot; is a strange choice. Yes, they're the most absolute scummiest of all vampires with regular massacres of humans and Hannibal Lecter being how one of the smarter members of their group would act. However, it's all make-believe anyway and being worried about games with them as protagonists is like worrying about metal god and devout Christian Alice Cooper acts in his private life.<br /> <br /> But what does the book provide? It does update the Sabbat to 2021 with descriptions of how the sect has changed in the past fifteen years. In many ways, it's a significantly simpler sect (not quite dumbed down) with various factions having all been expelled or killed. There's no more False Hand, Inquisition, Loyalists, or Clan factions. Instead, the Sabbat have all become Antitribu with Paths as their primary guiding influence. They are at their most feral and united, all ready to wage war on the Antediluvians with those who want to stay behind forced to defect to the Camarilla and Anarchs or become food.<br /> <br /> The gameplay rules are rather light with some material on how to create horrifying ghoul abominations, zombie Thin Bloods, and EVIL Disciplines. The biggest complaint I have about the book, related to my one that it doesn't have player character options, is the fact that it is incredibly expensive for its 134 pages. The Camarilla and Anarch guides were over 200 pages each and a similar cost, which is a difference of (using basic math), 70 pages of content. These 70 pages could have been used to talk about Path rules, Loresheets, how the Sabbat got to be in its current state, or other useful material.<br /> <br /> I give the book a lot of credit that it is a direly necessary one and one that I am happy to have in my library. The descriptions of Paths, changes to the Sabbat, and visceral horror on page is all top notch. However, I feel like this book could have easily been paired with the V5 Companion (that was free) to fill out the page count. As it is, the book is overpriced for its size. Its something I recommend for Storytellers, though, because V5 without the Sabbat is just not the same animal as previous editions. Antagonists or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T14:29:58-07:00","id":1465439,"title":"","content":"I haven't read the PDF as I'm waiting for the book to hit local brick and mortar shops. While on one hand, I'm sad that there's no info on making PC Sabbat characters, the reasoning behind it seems sound. Given the huge amount of turmoil surrounding that sect in the last few years, it's no surprise they'd do what every extremist group does when pushed against the wall ... they purge those elements they feel are not 'ideologically pure'. I totally understand why the Lasombra leadership have chosen to leave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T15:03:45-07:00","id":1465442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465439#post1465439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read the PDF as I'm waiting for the book to hit local brick and mortar shops. While on one hand, I'm sad that there's no info on making PC Sabbat characters, the reasoning behind it seems sound. Given the huge amount of turmoil surrounding that sect in the last few years, it's no surprise they'd do what every extremist group does when pushed against the wall ... they purge those elements they feel are not 'ideologically pure'. I totally understand why the Lasombra leadership have chosen to leave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if the Sabbat is pushed against the wall and is effectively dying, this is no reason to not let players chose to play them, and not even give us loresheets to represent those purged elements that got out alive.<br /> <br /> This is a massive lack, and one that could be easily corrected by the 70 or so pages of content it have below the other similarly priced supplements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T16:06:28-07:00","id":1465446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465439#post1465439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read the PDF as I'm waiting for the book to hit local brick and mortar shops. While on one hand, I'm sad that there's no info on making PC Sabbat characters, the reasoning behind it seems sound. Given the huge amount of turmoil surrounding that sect in the last few years, it's no surprise they'd do what every extremist group does when pushed against the wall ... they purge those elements they feel are not 'ideologically pure'. I totally understand why the Lasombra leadership have chosen to leave.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't care if they came up with a plausible sounding reason for dumping the Sabbat. It's fiction: they can come up with a plausible sounding reason for the Sabbat all growing rockets on their feet and flying to Mars if they really wanted to. I love the Sabbat, I didn't want them dumped as a playable faction, and I don't give the slightest hint of a damn what in-story reason they invented for dumping them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T16:31:41-07:00","id":1465447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465439#post1465439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read the PDF as I'm waiting for the book to hit local brick and mortar shops. While on one hand, I'm sad that there's no info on making PC Sabbat characters, the reasoning behind it seems sound. Given the huge amount of turmoil surrounding that sect in the last few years, it's no surprise they'd do what every extremist group does when pushed against the wall ... they purge those elements they feel are not 'ideologically pure'. I totally understand why the Lasombra leadership have chosen to leave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but that's stuff they wrote in themselves it's not an event that occurred irl they decided the Sabbat would implode. I can't say it didn't happen but I can critique it as a bad idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T16:45:53-07:00","id":1465448,"title":"","content":"It's just weird to me that they keep trying to defend the destruction of the Sabbat by saying it was well-written. As if Sabbat players are complaining about the writing-quality and would be appeased if you could just convince us that our sect's destruction was well-written. We don't care. You could write the destruction of the Sabbat so well that a light shines down from Heaven and God himself compliments you on your writing skill, and we still wouldn't care. We want the Sabbat to continue to be a playable sect. The End.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T16:46:16-07:00","id":1465449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465447#post1465447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but that's stuff they wrote in themselves it's not an event that occurred irl they decided the Sabbat would implode. I can't say it didn't happen but I can critique it as a bad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>A very important point:<br /> <br /> They didn't made the Sabbat unplayable because the Sabbat was pressed.<br /> <br /> They pressed the Sabbat to make it unplayable.<br /> <br /> I would rather have the Camarilla threatened by Rocket-Feet-Sabbat-From-Mars than have V5's Sabbat in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T16:58:26-07:00","id":1465451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465448#post1465448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just weird to me that they keep trying to defend the destruction of the Sabbat by saying it was well-written. As if Sabbat players are complaining about the writing-quality and would be appeased if you could just convince us that our sect's destruction was well-written. We don't care. You could write the destruction of the Sabbat so well that a light shines down from Heaven and God himself compliments you on your writing skill, and we still wouldn't care. We want the Sabbat to continue to be a playable sect. The End.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I hope they rectify this.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't impact the book's utility for what it was meant to be.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T19:17:09-07:00","id":1465459,"title":"","content":"Extreme groups don\u2019t always, or necessarily even frequently, purge \u201cimpure\u201d elements when they are in trouble. The SS, for example, through the course of WWII began to relax their standards for recruitment as the war progressed - eventually accepting Slavic or even non-white members. If the Sabbat is having problems, it seems like they would have even more trouble remaining ideologically pure. They would probably have more shovel heads who don\u2019t end up being as indoctrinated or strictly controlled. Sabbat members who might not be desirable in times of relative safety might be tolerated if they are still fighting with the Sabbat despite their other objectionable qualities. I can see plenty of in-setting justifications why the Sabbat would be just as appropriate for player characters as ever, maybe even more so.<br /> <br /> Though outside of storytelling, writing, or realism - role playing games are there for people to have fun. I imagine that a high percentage of people who wanted the new Sabbat book wanted to play Sabbat characters, because that would be cool and fun for them, and if the book doesn\u2019t facilitate Sabbat PCs, then that seems like a significant problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T19:19:38-07:00","id":1465460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465459#post1465459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extreme groups don\u2019t always, or necessarily even frequently, purge \u201cimpure\u201d elements when they are in trouble. The SS, for example, through the course of WWII began to relax their standards for recruitment as the war progressed - eventually accepting Slavic or even non-white members. If the Sabbat is having problems, it seems like they would have even more trouble remaining ideologically pure. They would probably have more shovel heads who don\u2019t end up being as indoctrinated or strictly controlled. Sabbat members who might not be desirable in times of relative safety might be tolerated if they are still fighting with the Sabbat despite their other objectionable qualities. I can see plenty of in-setting justifications why the Sabbat would be just as appropriate for player characters as ever, maybe even more so.<br /> <br /> Though outside of storytelling, writing, or realism - role playing games are there for people to have fun. <b>I imagine that a high percentage of people who wanted the new Sabbat book wanted to play Sabbat characters, because that would be cool and fun for them, and if the book doesn\u2019t facilitate Sabbat PCs, then that seems like a significant problem</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that's definitely something to give them credit for. They made no attempt to falsely advertise the book and literally the first page explains what the book is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T19:33:59-07:00","id":1465461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465460#post1465460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, that's definitely something to give them credit for. They made no attempt to falsely advertise the book and literally the first page explains what the book is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still it is a disrespect to those people to decide to make the book like that in the first place when they know it is not what most people eager for the book's release wanted. It is a dick move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T20:10:21-07:00","id":1465466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465461#post1465461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still it is a disrespect to those people to decide to make the book like that in the first place when they know it is not what most people eager for the book's release wanted. It is a dick move.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely a significant minority wanted playable Sabbat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T20:34:35-07:00","id":1465468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465466#post1465466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely a significant minority wanted playable Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, unless you have data to back up your claim, you can't say if it was a minority.<br /> <br /> Second and more important, I purposefully said &quot;<i>eager for the book's release</i>&quot;, not any V5 player.<br /> <br /> <br /> Camarilla-only players and STs aren't eager for such releases, at least in my experience. They either don't care or buy the books more for the sake of completeness of their library/understanding of the official lore.<br /> <br /> How many people were <b>eager</b> for this release, <b>only</b> to use them as antagonists?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T20:53:19-07:00","id":1465471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465468#post1465468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, unless you have data to back up your claim, you can't say if it was a minority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the majority of people play Sabbat, which I don't think anyone has ever claimed ever, it would be a minority. Next why would being a minority make their desires less relevant?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T20:54:15-07:00","id":1465472,"title":"","content":"I think it is fair to say we've always been a minority of the player base. Here's the thing, though: giving us what we want doesn't hurt the Cammy players at all. It's like french-fries versus onion rings: most people may like fries, but it's not like having onion rings on the menu hurts the people who like fries. No one is going to rip the fries out of your hands because onion rings are also on the menu.<br /> <br /> Those of you who prefer to play Cammies have zero need to destroy the Sabbat. I've been running/playing Sabbat off-and-on for 30 years. My doing so has never stopped a single person from playing Cammies. I have never had the slightest desire to force the destruction of the Camarilla into the metaplot for the sake of my Sabbat games, because I have never had the slightest need to do so. I don't need to destroy your games in order to play mine. Yet it feels like Cammy players can't offer me the same courtesy, and feel a need to destroy my games for no reason beyond distaste. It feels like someone in charge looked at us and went &quot;ew&quot; and destroyed us like they were Toreadors and we were Nossies at their mercy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T21:00:04-07:00","id":1465473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465461#post1465461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still it is a disrespect to those people to decide to make the book like that in the first place when they know it is not what most people eager for the book's release wanted. It is a dick move.</div> </div> </div> </div>The owners of the IP, Paradox, have a specific vision for V5. They've made that very clear, both from interviews with Achilli prior to Sabbat being released, and also in discussions elsewhere. The specific interview can be found on the WoD youtube, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v_JiRakxa5M&amp;t=2s\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v_JiRakxa5M&amp;t=2s</a>, about 20 or so minutes in, but they've talked about the TTRPG providing the baselines for everything else many times before, as well as their vision for V5 and what it needs to do.<br /> <br /> As far as other discussions, from the Dark Pack ST Vault Discord when asked about the 'direction of the WoD' we have this answer:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>STV Discord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>What\u2019s the official statement on the direction of World of Darkness franchise?</b><br /> <br /> We gave an interview to VentureBeat about a year ago that goes in detail into that subject, and I would say it didn\u2019t age badly at all! Please check it out here: <a href=\"https://venturebeat.com/2020/08/02/for-world-of-darkness-the-future-of-tabletop-rpgs-is-increasingly-digital/\" target=\"_blank\">https://venturebeat.com/2020/08/02/f...ingly-digital/</a><br /> <br /> The keywords are \u201cmedia-agnostic\u201d and \u201ctransmedia\u201d. Since then, we\u2019ve announced our Hollywood-adjacent partnership and plans of bringing WoD to small and big screens, which also explains it further. Our stories need to work at the TTRPG table just like they need to work in a video game, comic book, actual play, immersive experience or on the silver screen - and our approach to IP development treats this as a baseline. TTRPG corebooks become guides for our partners on how to work with our IPs, and when we write these materials, we keep this firmly in mind.<br /> <br /> To give a live example - explanations on how antagonists in V5 Sabbat behave in detail, what sounds or gestures they would make - this is super helpful for storytellers at the tables, but also it would help TV writers nail this down in a script, or video game designers develop them well for in-game worlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not 'disrespect' or 'destroying something because of Cammy players' or anything like that. It's just their business model for the IP, nothing more and nothing less. They're building things that support the reason they bought the IP in the first place: video games and TV shows and other media than a TTRPG, which also dovetails into building things from a 'new player' standpoint to an extent, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 10-27-2021, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T22:01:07-07:00","id":1465477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465472#post1465472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't need to destroy your games in order to play mine. Yet it feels like Cammy players can't offer me the same courtesy, and feel a need to destroy my games for no reason beyond distaste. It feels like someone in charge looked at us and went &quot;ew&quot; and destroyed us like they were Toreadors and we were Nossies at their mercy.</div> </div> </div> </div>IC it's the duty of anyone to destroy their enemy sects. <br /> <br /> But OoC, it feels really shit. <br /> <br /> Especially since the old system was Cam&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;Sab/Indies&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;Ana but someone felt that this didn't align with their preferences and real world political ideal so they wrote things as Ana&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;Cam&gt;&gt;Hecata&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;Sab, and they did so at the complete expense of the values that actually made up these organizations. What are the Anarchs rebeling against if they're now the no.1 faction and their enemies are jokes who willfully gave up their monopoly? How does the Camarilla purge dissent when they've decided to let so many people go and do their own thing? How can the Sabbat fight the antes (weak as they may be mechanically in V5, they still are legendary figures who can carry mountains in the minds of Sabbat) when they've purged their most useful members and have decided not to hold territory. <br /> <br /> It's not like any of this is necessary or good for the game. This is just someone's highly specific wishlist manifesting at the expense of players and the setting at large.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T23:06:44-07:00","id":1465480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465473#post1465473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The owners of the IP, Paradox, have a specific vision for V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of that. I've discussed this <i>ad nauseam</i> here. So I'll keep the reply short this time.<br /> <br /> Their goals at being transmedia and attracting new players aren't affected by including nuance in the games. I don't know if their decisions have to do with it and they're plain bad if they do.<br /> <br /> A TTRPG supplement may be relevant for their other goals, but's still a TTRPG supplement. If it is made in such a way as to not attend the needs of its paying public, this is a dick move.<br /> <br /> Having a reason behind your dick move doesn't make it less dickish, believing your idea is brilliant doesn't make it brilliant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T00:27:56-07:00","id":1465484,"title":"","content":"Additionally:<br /> <br /> Pretend I'm a studio writer for the TV show.<br /> <br /> Which is a more useful text to me? Rev. Guide to the Sabbat, or V5 Sabbat?<br /> <br /> I would argue GttS for a simple reason: the second I want to write a big bad Sabbat that's meant to carry a season's worth of plot and intrigue. V5 is fine for largely nameless antagonists that are scary because of what the represent as a group. It even works fine for a leadership character like Andrei from VtMB1. But it's not going to help me craft someone half as horrifying as Vykos. Someone horrible enough on the surface, but has layers upon layers of history to uncover; aka the kind of stuff writers love to help make characters more interesting and engaging.<br /> <br /> This is why so many WoD antagonists books have enough rules to be playable even if the creators don't want them to be playable: to give the STs the rules-as-context to make them compelling. The ST, and as such writers in other media, have to understand the Sabbat on that level to portray them past a certain level of depth.<br /> <br /> What does such a vital ceremony as the Vaulderie do? How does it make vampires feel? How far does it go? How reliable is it? What can test its effects? Can a spy in the Sabbat endure a ceremony or two and still betray the Sabbat, or do you need more potent protections for espionage?<br /> <br /> If you want a consistent transmedia franchise, these sorts of details are really useful to have set down. Even for antagonists that the players will never get to use in video games, that the writers of books and shows will never make too sympathetic, etc. You don't have to like a character as a person to find them compelling, but you need to understand them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T02:40:19-07:00","id":1465489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465480#post1465480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware of that. I've discussed this <i>ad nauseam</i> here. So I'll keep the reply short this time.<br /> <br /> Their goals at being transmedia and attracting new players aren't affected by including nuance in the games. I don't know if their decisions have to do with it and they're plain bad if they do.<br /> <br /> A TTRPG supplement may be relevant for their other goals, but's still a TTRPG supplement. If it is made in such a way as to not attend the needs of its paying public, this is a dick move.<br /> <br /> Having a reason behind your dick move doesn't make it less dickish, believing your idea is brilliant doesn't make it brilliant.</div> </div> </div> </div> The weird part is it isn't even particulary clear if that's the root of success since re release has seen a surge of advertising, community building and native advertising. <br /> Its also worth noting they didn't really promote or legitimise the Anarchs as poison the well with the other two sects.<br /> I also feel the lack of nuance may eventually cause issues moving forward as the lack of depth decentavizes ongoing play. As I've mentioned &quot;on the street fighting the man.&quot; Is fun but how long can you really run that for everyone everywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-27-2021, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T03:51:52-07:00","id":1465491,"title":"","content":"<i>Here are six rules, one is extremely important, the other five can be ignored or interpreted as the writer/head vampire pleases. Feel free to add in your own rules at will.</i><br /> <br /> That's 90% of vampire's political landscape within the Camarilla. The other 10% is clans, elysium, and the specific archaic terms vampires use.<br /> <br /> I don't know why you'd want a &quot;specific vision&quot; to apply globally when the global vision is so broad and accommodating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T04:11:41-07:00","id":1465492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465489#post1465489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I've mentioned &quot;on the street fighting the man.&quot; Is fun but how long can you really run that for everyone everywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, it depends a lot on the play-loop in the game. D&amp;D has been coasting by on, &quot;get quest, have combat and other obstacles, finished quest, get rewards, get new quest and repeat with more toys and bigger numbers&quot; for along time, because the play loop keeps people going.<br /> <br /> Lots of games copy that core loop with different dressings for different genres. Shadowrun could easily be called &quot;on the street fighting the man&quot; even if usually it involves taking money from a different The Man in the process. But you can keep people into the same essential loop of &quot;Mr. Johnson gets you a mission, have combat and other obstacles, finish mission, get rewards, get new mission and repeat with more toys and bigger numbers.&quot;<br /> <br /> VtM's game loop just isn't good for keeping that &quot;Anarch&quot; edge. While VtM's game loop does vary from that D&amp;D original a bit, it's hard to loop a lot with the Anarchs. The Cam loops easier because however much it's a scam, some vampires claw their way up the pyramid scheme. The loop feels like it's progressing even as it's repeating because it doles out what feels like advancement within the context of the setting. It would take lots of loops, but players can theoretically progress all the way to the Cam Inner Circle; the same also applied to the pre-V5 Sabbat where you could fight to take over as Regent if you put in the effort.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs thematically fight against the application of political machinations and favor trading that alter the &quot;important NPC gives you a job&quot; loop to something different. Fighting the man, in VtM, doesn't get you anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T04:20:43-07:00","id":1465493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465489#post1465489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The weird part is it isn't even particulary clear if that's the root of success since re release has seen a surge of advertising, community building and native advertising.<br /> Its also worth noting they didn't really promote or legitimise the Anarchs as poison the well with the other two sects.<br /> I also feel the lack of nuance may eventually cause issues moving forward as the lack of depth decentavizes ongoing play. As I've mentioned &quot;on the street fighting the man.&quot; Is fun but how long can you really run that for everyone everywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the idea the Anarchs are getting a big push at the expense of other sects is questionable. I feel that is mostly a product of fanon. They also have had a lot of things changed about them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">VtM's game loop just isn't good for keeping that &quot;Anarch&quot; edge. While VtM's game loop does vary from that D&amp;D original a bit, it's hard to loop a lot with the Anarchs. The Cam loops easier because however much it's a scam, some vampires claw their way up the pyramid scheme. The loop feels like it's progressing even as it's repeating because it doles out what feels like advancement within the context of the setting. It would take lots of loops, but players can theoretically progress all the way to the Cam Inner Circle; the same also applied to the pre-V5 Sabbat where you could fight to take over as Regent if you put in the effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that's very much a matter of how you choose to play. There's always assholes trying to oppress you in V:TM. If you manage to beat, conquer, and crush them all then you become the oppressor. Which means that you've lost just as well as if your enemies had succeeded. It's not a mistake but part of Gothic Punk ideology that if you win, you become part of the system.<br /> <br /> That was there as back in Forged in Steel with Juggler being every bit as bad as Modius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-27-2021, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T04:59:38-07:00","id":1465499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465493#post1465493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel that's very much a matter of how you choose to play. There's always assholes trying to oppress you in V:TM. If you manage to beat, conquer, and crush them all then you become the oppressor. Which means that you've lost just as well as if your enemies had succeeded. It's not a mistake but part of Gothic Punk ideology that if you win, you become part of the system.<br /> <br /> That was there as back in Forged in Steel with Juggler being every bit as bad as Modius.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is a theme that is often portrayed, this is far from a rule. Princes are often depicted less gruel or more gruel than other ones, the Sabbat was overall depicted as more gruel than the Camarilla etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T05:29:03-07:00","id":1465503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465493#post1465493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like the idea the Anarchs are getting a big push at the expense of other sects is questionable. I feel that is mostly a product of fanon. They also have had a lot of things changed about them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Naturally personal interpretation applies but the Carmarilla has been made so evil as to be cartoonish and the Sabbat has been explicitally exluded from play, at the same time the Anarchs have shifted from an minority sub-sect to 4 clans and 2 clans. I mean when you're shoving the Clan &quot;we're way better suited to the Sabbat&quot; Tzmisce into the sect somebodies clearly playing favourates.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T06:07:28-07:00","id":1465506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465503#post1465503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Naturally personal interpretation applies but the Carmarilla has been made so evil as to be cartoonish and the Sabbat has been explicitally exluded from play, at the same time the Anarchs have shifted from an minority sub-sect to 4 clans and 2 clans. I mean when you're shoving the Clan &quot;we're way better suited to the Sabbat&quot; Tzmisce into the sect somebodies clearly playing favourates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Tzimisce have joined the Anarchs have they? I think they just have been acknowledged as having Anarch members. They presumably also have Camarilla members.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce are now an independent Clan in V20 terms.<br /> <br /> As for the Camarilla, I don't think they've shown themselves as any more evil than they were in previous editions. They made some STUPID moves like triggering the Second Inquisition and exiling the Brujah but the Camarilla hasn't shown anything particularly bad unless I'm missing something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T06:37:49-07:00","id":1465507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465506#post1465506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think the Tzimisce have joined the Anarchs have they? I think they just have been acknowledged as having Anarch members. They presumably also have Camarilla members.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce are now an independent Clan in V20 terms.<br /> <br /> As for the Camarilla, I don't think they've shown themselves as any more evil than they were in previous editions. They made some STUPID moves like triggering the Second Inquisition and exiling the Brujah but the Camarilla hasn't shown anything particularly bad unless I'm missing something.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books seems to go back and forth on this, Companion says they're still Sabbat with Some Anarchs, Sabbat says any Sabbat member is considered Anti which makes the clan De facto Anarch, Their isnt much indication of independants being a prominant force.<br /> <br /> Highlight Carmarilla blooper wheel<br /> -Methusulah worship, terrible idea for a number of reasons. Not in the least because the Assamites just joined because they were fleeing their methusulah's and the Tremere ones just got ashed<br /> -Exclusivatory policy undermines masquarade and explictly endorses both Sabbat and Anarchs.<br /> -Not accepting Setites despite being very much their kind of people, especially with the Ancient worship<br /> -Weird theocratic aspects.<br /> -Asking clan Lasombra to self implode to join the sect....or more likely not immediatly explaining the terms were an implicit &quot;no&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T07:08:22-07:00","id":1465508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465493#post1465493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the idea the Anarchs are getting a big push at the expense of other sects is questionable. I feel that is mostly a product of fanon. They also have had a lot of things changed about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat has been completely gutted. Most of the factions that existed within the Sabbat are essentially gone. The Camarilla has lost a significant amount of power and influence, the Brujah, the Tremere are in shambles, etc. Plus both sects lost a lot of their elders, whereas the Anarchs never really had any. The Anarchs went from a loose collection of whatever to now having multiple clans effectively pledge loyalty to them. They're a full sect on the same level as the Sabbat and the Camarilla, and most of the Anarch's rise has come as a result of the Camarilla and the Sabbat getting torn apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T07:17:40-07:00","id":1465510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465507#post1465507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books seems to go back and forth on this, Companion says they're still Sabbat with Some Anarchs, Sabbat says any Sabbat member is considered Anti which makes the clan De facto Anarch, Their isnt much indication of independants being a prominant force.<br /> <br /> Highlight Carmarilla blooper wheel<br /> -Methusulah worship, terrible idea for a number of reasons. Not in the least because the Assamites just joined because they were fleeing their methusulah's and the Tremere ones just got ashed<br /> -Exclusivatory policy undermines masquarade and explictly endorses both Sabbat and Anarchs.<br /> -Not accepting Setites despite being very much their kind of people, especially with the Ancient worship<br /> -Weird theocratic aspects.<br /> -Asking clan Lasombra to self implode to join the sect....or more likely not immediatly explaining the terms were an implicit &quot;no&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1. Methusaleh Worship has always been a thing in secret. Its just in the open now. Remember all the Ancestor worship and Gehenna cults in Elysium.<br /> <br /> 2. The Camarilla is writing off the Anarchs. They were never accepting the Sabbat anyway. They're leaving the others for the wolves.<br /> <br /> 3. The Setites and Assamites were never going to share a sect. Besides, the Anarchs accepting the Setites makes the Anarchs look like morons.<br /> <br /> 4. I always hated the Camarilla's persecution of Noddists. It came from nowhere in Revised.<br /> <br /> 5. The Lasombra were always going to have to kill a bunch of Sabbat on the way out. The Lasombra will probably rule the sect in a few decades. Besides, why is destroying the Lasombra evil? Its one of the better moral things the Camarilla does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T07:49:11-07:00","id":1465512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465510#post1465510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Methusaleh Worship has always been a thing in secret. Its just in the open now. Remember all the Ancestor worship and Gehenna cults in Elysium.<br /> <br /> 2. The Camarilla is writing off the Anarchs. They were never accepting the Sabbat anyway. They're leaving the others for the wolves.<br /> <br /> 3. The Setites and Assamites were never going to share a sect. Besides, the Anarchs accepting the Setites makes the Anarchs look like morons.<br /> <br /> 4. I always hated the Camarilla's persecution of Noddists. It came from nowhere in Revised.<br /> <br /> 5. The Lasombra were always going to have to kill a bunch of Sabbat on the way out. The Lasombra will probably rule the sect in a few decades. Besides, why is destroying the Lasombra evil? Its one of the better moral things the Camarilla does.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) speculations not conformed by resources<br /> 2)that's a massive chunk of kindred pop and that's before you consider autarkis and other groups. It isn't leaving the others for wolves, vampires are the wolves and they've decided that the shepard is going to forget wolves exist if while he's constantly shooting them.<br /> 3) as opposed to pre 5th tremere and anyone but especially assamites? And those people apparently praying to ul shugi<br /> 4) it makes sense to avoid mass panic, its also is only part of the sects weird theocratic leanings. There also the distinction between noddist scholar and antideluvian worshipping crackpot<br /> 5) it isn't evil, it's dumb. If it was a serious offer the carmilla are idiots more likely it was a weak bluff the lasombra were pathetic enough to go for. Thinking on it getting the lasombra to obliterate themselves for 2nd class citizen carmarilla membership was pretty smart even if I think it was a happy accident for the sect.<br /> <br /> Edit-i actually forgot the all time greatest hit for thr ivory tower: causing the 2nd inquisition and the 2nd anarch revolt. This isn't even a subjective issue the corebook directly says they did it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-27-2021, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T08:31:26-07:00","id":1465515,"title":"","content":"Man, this place sure feels like groundhog day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T09:27:25-07:00","id":1465518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465506#post1465506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Camarilla, I don't think they've shown themselves as any more evil than they were in previous editions. They made some STUPID moves like triggering the Second Inquisition and exiling the Brujah but the Camarilla hasn't shown anything particularly bad unless I'm missing something.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what happens when you never play Camarilla characters. Along with everything <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> mentioned there's just... so much more. One of the more notable ones: <br /> <br /> The Luddite, anti-tech idea is stupid on so many levels It's difficult to get round to the idea that I actually have to explain why it's stupid. <br /> 1: All vampires have to do is not mention specific terms when they're on the phone. <br /> 2: The NSA isn't omniscient. It isn't global and there aren't many similar organizations. NSA evidence has apparently been useful in initiating less than 2% of terrorism investigations. It's far too much of a stretch to say that level of ineffeciency is because the real bulk of the NSA's effort has gone to finding vampires. <br /> 3: Having couriers run around with beautiful handcrafted letters in this day and age is the height of fucking stupidity. What's the alternative to electronic communication that doesn't make people turn their heads? <br /> <br /> I feel like the cam saw some dirty sheets so they decided to fix the problem by shitting the bed, wrapping the sheet around themselves, and then setting the sheet on fire while they're looking like a cigarette.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T09:31:23-07:00","id":1465519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465472#post1465472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet it feels like Cammy players can't offer me the same courtesy, and feel a need to destroy my games for no reason beyond distaste.</div> </div> </div> </div>My only problem is with this line. Please, I'm as pissed off at unplayable Sabbat as you, but I'm still primarily a Camarilla player.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465492#post1465492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Anarchs thematically fight against the application of political machinations and favor trading that alter the &quot;important NPC gives you a job&quot; loop to something different. Fighting the man, in VtM, doesn't get you anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I don't think the Anarchs really work as a different sect, but can work well within the Camarilla, as then you can work the loop as something that isn't a 0-1 situation.<br /> <br /> Instead of Fight the Man &gt; disrupt the system &gt; there's no system, it can (and should) be Fight the Man over an issue &gt; solve the issue, making life a little better &gt; in a better environment find next issue.<br /> <br /> Keeping only the end of the Princedom itself as goal will keep you from ever perceiving advancement until you achieve it, and then what? Then you would need a new play style entirely for creating and defending the new status quo, which isn't a bad thing per se, but can't be the default loop.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465506#post1465506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Camarilla, I don't think they've shown themselves as any more evil than they were in previous editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because you keep conflating <i>things that happens at some cities</i> with <i>Camarilla Policies</i>. No matter how many times we tell you that hunting Thin Bloods, executing Anarchs, and other general asshole behaviors aren't Camarilla policies, you insist they are because to you if a Prince does something it can only be because the Camarilla as an institution wants it, and so it all happens simultaneously all the time in every Camarilla city.<br /> <br /> What the Camarilla does give pre-V5 is a lot of freedom for a Prince to run the city however they want as long as the Masquerade is kept, because organizations like that don't work top-down. It isn't the Inner Circle that empower Princes, but the Princes that either recognize the Camarilla or not. Being too intrusive would just implode the sect.<br /> <br /> In the end, the point is that the Camarilla is a loose association with a few strong demands, and not a closed club. You refuse to understand this as the V5 authors also did, that's why you can't comprehend our criticism on what they did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T09:42:17-07:00","id":1465520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465519#post1465519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's because you keep conflating <i>things that happens at some cities</i> with <i>Camarilla Policies</i>. No matter how many times we tell you that hunting Thin Bloods, executing Anarchs, and other general asshole behaviors aren't Camarilla policies, you insist they are because to you if a Prince does something it can only be because the Camarilla as an institution wants it, and so it all happens simultaneously all the time in every Camarilla city.<br /> <br /> What the Camarilla does give pre-V5 is a lot of freedom for a Prince to run the city however they want as long as the Masquerade is kept, because organizations like that don't work top-down. It isn't the Inner Circle that empower Princes, but the Princes that either recognize the Camarilla or not. Being too intrusive would just implode the sect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like that is a distinction without a difference and is a weird one to make in the first place. &quot;No, it's not officially Camarilla policy but the Princes that the Camarilla appoints and approves of are able to do so. It's also common enough that there is an official designated title for the position of torturing and murdering people that has fallen into common parlance.&quot; There are certainly exceptions to the rule of Princes that are engaged in mass murder of Thin Bloods and Princes that are better than others but it's weird to act like the ones with Scourges and carrying out crackdowns like this are the outliers.<br /> <br /> Also, the persecution of Thin Bloods and torture is primarily a REVISED thing not a V5 thing. Indeed, the Thin Bloods being persecuted is probably less in V5 because they're no longer considered the Camarilla's responsibilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the end, the point is that the Camarilla is a loose association with a few strong demands, and not a closed club. You refuse to understand this as the V5 authors also did, that's why you can't comprehend our criticism on what they did </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla has always been a group that centered around an oligarchy that enforced its rules on everyone else. Why they're fun. The big difference is now they can't try to enforce their power on Anarchs so they decided not to even try.<br /> <br /> It's a minor change, IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T09:46:43-07:00","id":1465524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465512#post1465512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) speculations not conformed by resources</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally cited Elysium, a 2nd edition book about Elders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2)that's a massive chunk of kindred pop and that's before you consider autarkis and other groups. It isn't leaving the others for wolves, vampires are the wolves and they've decided that the shepard is going to forget wolves exist if while he's constantly shooting them. </div> </div> </div>This isn't exactly new. The Anarchs had their own territory and sect from the beginning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) as opposed to pre 5th tremere and anyone but especially assamites? And those people apparently praying to ul shugi </div> </div> </div>The Assamites joined the Camarilla in Revised. It's not a 5th Edition change. The Followers joining the Camarilla was always a longshot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) it makes sense to avoid mass panic, its also is only part of the sects weird theocratic leanings. There also the distinction between noddist scholar and antideluvian worshipping crackpot </div> </div> </div>All it did was cause more Gehenna madness and it was always Hardelstadt's insane thing. It was also invented for Revised as previously you had Ventrue reciting their lineage back to Caine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) it isn't evil, it's dumb. If it was a serious offer the carmilla are idiots more likely it was a weak bluff the lasombra were pathetic enough to go for. Thinking on it getting the lasombra to obliterate themselves for 2nd class citizen carmarilla membership was pretty smart even if I think it was a happy accident for the sect. </div> </div> </div>The Lasombra Antitribu are probably the ones who made it happen. Now the Lasombra defectors and they are on even terms and it's strong enough to be the core of a new clan.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T10:18:50-07:00","id":1465527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465520#post1465520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like that is a distinction without a difference and is a weird one to make in the first place. &quot;No, it's not officially Camarilla policy but the Princes that the Camarilla appoints and approves of are able to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you have a tendency to only think on those things at extremes. They either condone or condemn, with no middle ground.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465520#post1465520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also common enough that there is an official designated title</div> </div> </div> </div>No, there is not, another nuance you refused to get, and I say refused because I already saw it be pointed to you and you ignore.<br /> <br /> <b>The Scourge isn't an official title. It isn't. It just isn't.</b> People create names when they have things to name, that's what we call <i>common parlance</i>. <u><i>Princes that engage in Thin Blood hunting have this office</i></u>. It have to do with the fact that a Prince may have whatever office they want within their cities. And the name got &quot;common&quot;.<br /> <br /> It isn't an official Camarilla title in any capacity and this is plainly said in the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465520#post1465520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are certainly exceptions to the rule of Princes that are engaged in mass murder of Thin Bloods and Princes that are better than others but it's weird to act like the ones with Scourges and carrying out crackdowns like this are the outliers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is? Can you point out any actual canonical pre-V5 lore that says so?<br /> <br /> Something being common can mean a lot of things. Some things are common in the sense they happen to one out of 10 people. The murder of homosexuals is still unfortunately common, but not in the sense that most homosexuals will die from murder. &quot;Common&quot; is a word that depends on context.<br /> <br /> Nowhere I ever saw is said just how common exactly this batshit crazy behavior is. The two things that are said, though, are that the Camarilla accept it at least informally, and that the official stance is that it is a batshit crazy behavior.<br /> <br /> Why the Camarilla says one thing and does other? Any interpretation is valid. They can informally endorse it or just be incapable of doing shit about it. No interpretation is more official or even more likely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465520#post1465520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a minor change, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't, because it is a major MO change.<br /> <br /> Even if we assume the Camarilla as an oligarchy (which is true, but extremely simplistic), posing as government and claiming that everyone is a member by default is a huge part of its MO and how it works.<br /> <br /> Actually it is also a part of its horror, as the Camarilla wasn't meant to be just a fraternity, but The System. You yourself loves to point out how the game is about fighting The Man. Well, The Man is only The Man because they are legitimized as such by the system.<br /> <br /> There is no major system for vampires, though, the system is the sect. If the Camarilla expels everyone they're not gaming the system against others, they're just deluding themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T10:36:49-07:00","id":1465528,"title":"","content":"Hey,<br /> <br /> I understand fully if I am wrong and I appreciate you taking the chance to response. Still, I am mostly going by the GUIDE TO THE CAMARILLA regarding the commonality of Scourges. Here's what I got.<br /> <br /> <b>Guide to the Camarilla</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Scourge</b><br /> <br /> Page 32-33<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some claim the position of scourge is a relic of medieval times, an older form of the sheriff, while others believe that the post was created only within the last decade (with an equally new-minted pedigree). <b>However the scourge came to be, the office is now part of the landscape of many Camarilla cities. From Bern to Portland, scourges take their mandate to scour the borderlands and barrens of the major metropolises. </b>Their targets arc fledgling vampires created without permission, anarchs and those thin-blooded mules of the 14th and 15th Generations.<br /> <br /> Proceedings regarding the scourge vary from city to city. Some princes grant their scourges the right of destruction to speed the process of purging along, while ocher princes demand that the scourge bring the night's &quot;catch&quot; to Elysium for judgment. This last comes in light of some recent tales of over-enthusiastic scourges attacking and killing vampires who had followed protocol and were known in the city, but happened to be in the wrong place at the wrong time. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not every prince makes use of the scourge- indeed, a number of princes <b>(usually of smaller or less &quot;prestigious cities)</b>sec it as a dangerous and unnecessary office. The legality of the scourge is still under debate in a number of circles, particularly with regard to granting these gendarmes the right of destruction. </div> </div> </div>I mean, it is absolutely an official title of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Oddly, this seems to imply Anarchism was a death sentence as early as Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-27-2021, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T10:43:04-07:00","id":1465529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465466#post1465466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely a significant minority wanted playable Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm primarily a Camarilla fan, but I want the books to support playable Sabbat characters. It doesn't hurt my Camarilla games if other people are playing Sabbat games, in fact giving enough details to make Sabbat PCs also gives Camarilla or Anarch STs more material for nuanced antagonists. Also, even if I prefer Camarilla games, I might still want to play Sabbat once in a while, it's not as though I have real life loyalty or animosity to fictional vampire organizations.<br /> <br /> I'm moderately interested in Sabbat book, but I'm sure that people who were really interested in a Sabbat book almost all wanted playable Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I really don't see any downside to supporting Sabbat PCs and I see plenty of downsides to not supporting them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T11:43:00-07:00","id":1465540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465528#post1465528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand fully if I am wrong and I appreciate you taking the chance to response.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me demonstrate how the very text you quote have more than one interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Some claim the position of scourge is a relic of medieval times, an older form of the sheriff, while others believe that the post was created only within the last decade (with an equally new-minted pedigree).</i> </div> </div> </div>The jurisprudence of the title is in question. This isn't a closed question, or a rare one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>However the scourge came to be, the office is now part of the landscape of many Camarilla cities.</b> </div> </div> </div>Just how many? &quot;Most&quot; is by definition more than half, &quot;many&quot; can be any quantity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>From Bern to Portland, scourges take their mandate to scour the borderlands and barrens of the major metropolises.</b> </div> </div> </div>This defines area, but not how common it is in the area. Also hints that you don't find it so much at minor cities, but doesn't say at how many big cities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Their targets arc fledgling vampires created without permission, anarchs and those thin-blooded mules of the 14th and 15th Generations.</i> </div> </div> </div>Their targets are defined by their Princes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Proceedings regarding the scourge vary from city to city.</i> </div> </div> </div>That pretty much says that the Scourge doesn't mean the exact same thing everywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Some princes grant their scourges the right of destruction to speed the process of purging along, while ocher princes demand that the scourge bring the night's &quot;catch&quot; to Elysium for judgment.</i> </div> </div> </div>And that confirms that the process isn't always as straightforward. You're welcome to treat those judgments are just for show, but it isn't in the text, so it is open just how serious or lethal they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>This last comes in light of some recent tales of over-enthusiastic scourges attacking and killing vampires who had followed protocol and were known in the city, but happened to be in the wrong place at the wrong time.</i> </div> </div> </div>And that reinforces Camarilla law. No matter what are the Scourge's targets, vampires that followed proper law shouldn't be killed and it did caused problems for overzealous Princes.<br /> <br /> So the Caittif, Anarch, unauthorized Embrace or Thin Blood that presented themselves to the Prince earlier <b>are</b> exempt of persecution and it <b>must</b> be remembered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Not every prince makes use of the scourge- indeed, a number of princes </i><b>(usually of smaller or less &quot;prestigious cities)</b><i>sec it as a dangerous and unnecessary office.</i> </div> </div> </div>Pay attention to the line. Let me rephrase it without breaks:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>a number of princes </i><i>see it as a dangerous and unnecessary office.</i> </div> </div> </div>This is not about the princes that don't use the Scourge. This is about the Princes that are vocal against it. Huge difference. Your bold parenthesis only qualifies that vocal opposition.<br /> <br /> How big of a difference it is? Let me give you a RL example.<br /> <br /> Less than 6% of Taiwan's population is vocal in favor of declaring their independence from China. Does that mean that most Taiwanese want Chinese dominion?<br /> <br /> Well, just little more than 1% of them are vocal in favor of Chinese annexation of Taiwan. The people that want to keep the status quo where the island is kind of independent and kind of not and just say they don't care one way or another when questioned are almost 90% (yes, there are other answers).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>The legality of the scourge is still under debate in a number of circles, particularly with regard to granting these gendarmes the right of destruction.</i> </div> </div> </div>Here it straight out says that the question isn't settled. It isn't a discussion if the Scourge should be expanded, it is a discussion if it is even legal, or if there should be a crackdown on the entire idea.<br /> <br /> This line alone means that opposition to the office of Scourge is big enough for there to be open talks about intervening on Princes' policies. This is big.<br /> <br /> Of course, it is bigger on the matter, already not universal among &quot;Scourge users&quot;, if the Scourge themselves should be able to carry out execution. But it is big nonetheless, and it is focused but not limited to this.<br /> <br /> Even assuming that Revised Cam is the go to for Cam, which is an assumption by itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T12:08:16-07:00","id":1465544,"title":"","content":"I think a problem with Revised era books is that many times they make a sudden new announcement of how things are that was never the case previously simply because for Revised Metaplot purposes, that's what they wanted.<br /> <br /> Before the concept was introduced in Revised, I don't remember there ever being a Scourge. It certainly wasn't something shown in any of the By Night books. Now, it's always been the case that vampires illegally embraced without permission from the Prince get destroyed. That's simple enforcement of the Tradition of Progeny. It can't be done any other way. (In fact, in almost all the Anarch games I've played in, even Anarchs understand you simply can't have people embrace whomever they want. It needs to be regulated in some way. And if someone is embraced illegally, destroying the sire and childe is OK because that's what's needed to prevent people from overpopulating a domain with too many vampires.) And it is entirely conceivable the Prince might want to dump such a task on a particular individual. But that is very different than a new position called the Scourge simply killing Caitiff and Thin Bloods because the Revised Metaplot requires lots of those kinds of characters to be destroyed in order to fulfill the Revised Metaplot that destroying thin bloods would be one of the reasons the antedeluvians would rise.<br /> <br /> It was an arbitrary decision. It's perfectly legitimate to say that this is nonsense and reject it. Most players I know rejected the Metaplot at their table top games and LARPs, or only incorporated specific ideas of it.<br /> <br /> So now in V5 which has the strange position of saying some of the Revised Metaplot happened, but not all of it, does it even make sense that this portion should have been kept when other things have been rejected? Again, I think it's perfectly reasonable to say this doesn't make sense and shouldn't be the default going normal.<br /> <br /> As I've said on this forum many times before, I think it's best to reject the idea that there is one canon anymore. We're in an old DC Comics style having an Earth-1, Earth-2, etc. We have the standard setting as laid out in early 2e when everything was originally defined. V20 was essentially a call back to this. Then we have the late Greenberg era world that has a lot of gonzo elements that aren't essential to the standard setting, but represents one style of play (essentially these are the secrets revealed in Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand). Then we have the late 2e era where some of the over-the-top Greenberg stuff is not mentioned or even dropped. Then we have the Revised/Achilli era of the Metaplot which made massive changes to the setting. Now we have the V5 setting which builds on some of the Revised stuff, but not others and no longer represents the standard setting. There's essentially no continuity between these worlds even though they are based (to varying degrees) on the core setting originally introduced.<br /> <br /> The idea that the Scourge is an institution found everywhere in Camarilla cities is an artifact of &quot;WoD-Achilli&quot;. If someone wants to play in that, that's fine. I don't think it's actually that popular. I don't know anyone who actually used all the Metaplot introduced in that era as the basis for the setting. I've only ever seen certain things taken from it used. STs should be empowered to take whatever they like and reject the rest. So if you want the Scourge to be the default, go ahead. If you want it to be a rare exception, that's fine too. If you don't want to use it at all, that's great. All can be conceivably justified. But the Scourge obviously is not part of the core setting of VtM. It's part of this variant version created in Revised to serve a particular metaplot need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T12:16:57-07:00","id":1465547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465544#post1465544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a problem with Revised era books is that many times they make a sudden new announcement of how things are that was never the case previously simply because for Revised Metaplot purposes, that's what they wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>White Wolf has a history of retconning things left and right. However, that wasn't the case with the Scourge in that it wasn't a thing that had always been there. The Scourge was specifically a new addition to the Camarilla in Revised. Later, it would be added to the Dark Ages portion of Vampire: The Masquerade but in-universe the idea was the Scourge was a Medieval concept of vampire society that had been revived in the 1999-2004 period of time rather than something that had always been there off camera like the Sheriff.<br /> <br /> The thing about the addition of the Scourge was that it was meant to represent a response from the Camarilla to fears of Gehenna as well as the rising number of Thin Bloods, Caitiff, as well as illegally Embraced Progeny. Too many vampires were also not announcing themselves in the courts of the Princedom as well as spreading Anarch dogma. The Scourge was meant to represent the Camarilla resorting to draconian measures to try to regain control of their cities but it was to show things changing versus the idea the Camarilla was always like that.<br /> <br /> Justin Achilli had the view in Revised that the game had gotten too far away from its horror roots. As such, the book represented a direct attempt to make vampires more evil. The old jokes of trenchcoats and katanas and superheroes with fangs. I personally disagree with this and you can and should play V:TM <i>however you have fun doing so</i> but I believe that was a design decision. One of the things Justin focused on was making the Camarilla as evil as the Sabbat. Hence there was a lot of emphasis on the Camarilla being a parasitic organization that increased the crime, homelessness, wealth disparity, and more among mortals.<br /> <br /> It also formalized titles like Prince, Primogen, Harpy, Herald, Sheriff, and Scourge. Well before people started complaining about V5, Justin Achilli had helped set the groundwork for the &quot;evil global conspiracy&quot; version of the Camarilla. Whereas 2nd Edition had the Camarilla be a much looser and less organized group. THAT was a retcon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea that the Scourge is an institution found everywhere in Camarilla cities is an artifact of &quot;WoD-Achilli&quot;. If someone wants to play in that, that's fine. I don't think it's actually that popular. I don't know anyone who actually used all the Metaplot introduced in that era as the basis for the setting. I've only ever seen certain things taken from it used. STs should be empowered to take whatever they like and reject the rest. So if you want the Scourge to be the default, go ahead. If you want it to be a rare exception, that's fine too. If you don't want to use it at all, that's great. All can be conceivably justified. But the Scourge obviously is not part of the core setting of VtM. It's part of this variant version created in Revised to serve a particular metaplot need. </div> </div> </div>I generally agree with this and think everyone's table is its own alternate universe. At the end of the day, the ST is always right. Generally, I use the Scourge as a &quot;designated asshole&quot; in the setting and someone loathed by the rest of the court. One of the funniest things I ever had in my game was where one of the PCs was made the Scourge as a punishment/reward and everyone started treating them as a psychopath despite being nicer than the Sheriff.<br /> <br /> It was a source of much amusement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-27-2021, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T12:23:40-07:00","id":1465549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465540#post1465540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This line alone means that opposition to the office of Scourge is big enough for there to be open talks about intervening on Princes' policies. This is big. Of course, it is bigger on the matter, already not universal among &quot;Scourge users&quot;, if the Scourge themselves should be able to carry out execution. But it is big nonetheless, and it is focused but not limited to this. Even assuming that Revised Cam is the go to for Cam, which is an assumption by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for responding. This is a lot of interesting new perspective on the subject. I am surprised at how controversial the Scourge is with some fans. Mind you, it was always meant to represent the darkest side of the Camarilla and a sign a domain had gone to Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T12:54:58-07:00","id":1465553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465549#post1465549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for responding. This is a lot of interesting new perspective on the subject. I am surprised at how controversial the Scourge is with some fans. Mind you, it was always meant to represent the darkest side of the Camarilla and a sign a domain had gone to Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome. And just to be sure I want to make it clear that when I said things like <i>you refuse to understand</i>, it is not that I think you do so on purpose, but bias and discourse method and all that. I know I was harsh, but I sincerely wish to not have been offensive, it was not my intent.<br /> <br /> The Scourge <b>does</b>, indeed, represent the darkest side of the Camarilla, but that doesn't say just how prevalent or institutional this dark side is. And I think this is a good thing, as I said before in another place, nuance creates versatility, where I can have my Camarilla and you can have yours, and both be right under the lore.<br /> <br /> And as someone who works in a huge company with lots of institutional policies and organizational culture, frequently at odds, I can say for sure that the difference between official and unofficial isn't moot. They may have similar goals, but play out in very different ways. And sometimes their difference involves a lot of inner struggle in management.<br /> <br /> Remember when I talked about Upper and Middle Management in another thread about the Technocracy? The most common situation isn't that official policies are a facade and unofficial ones are for real. The most common situation is that official policies come from Upper Management or with their blessing and unofficial ones come from Middle Management and are too hard for Upper Management to fight.<br /> <br /> Justin Achili's personal take aside (which I firmly disagree with), Revised put it that way. The Scourge is a sign of Gehenna, <b>as Princes get scared enough to do it and damn the consequences</b>, but it is still far from a well defined policy. Middle Management is taking things in their own hands and Upper Management is still trying to figure out how to respond, as responding this isn't simple either, even if they have an agreement one way or the other, which isn't said if they have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T13:12:50-07:00","id":1465556,"title":"","content":"Why would upper management care, though? They may find the slaughter of caitiffs pointless and vaguely distasteful, but it's not like creatures that old are capable of genuine moral outrage. They are too busy scheming against other ancient creatures. The only reason to act on something like this is to weaken their rivals, which is just as likely to involve discouraging caitiff-slaughter as it is to involve encouraging it, or ignoring it entirely in favor of some tactic completely unrelated to the treatment of caitiffs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T13:39:55-07:00","id":1465560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465556#post1465556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why would upper management care, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the same reason behind the entire Camarilla scheme: survival.<br /> <br /> 1- Allowing wanton violence against any group increases the risks for the Masquerade. Not only you risk being too blatant with your actions but your victim is likely to break the Masquerade to save their lives.<br /> <br /> 2- It is even worse if your violence encourages organization for protection. An all out war on the streets is pretty bad for the Masquerade. It can also engulf Upper Management or their assets.<br /> <br /> 3- General mood is a thing. Enforcing the idea that everything is fine or that we have a war on the scum out there affects how subjects go through their nightly lives and generate more profit or more problems.<br /> <br /> 4- The means matter, especially if it isn't an isolated thing. Princes empowering Scourges to hunt their enemies as judge, jury and executioner sends a very bad message that can come back to bite them.<br /> <br /> 5- Politics. Appearances matter, even if they're just a facade. Alliances matter, but having sway over certain people does, too. The elders may be the big players in the Cam, but the opinions of Neonates and Ancillae do matter in a broader scope as the whole point is to keep them in check through politics instead of simple brute force.<br /> <br /> 6- Finally, things evolve. If a Prince establishes a Scourge today and that goes completely unchecked, what will this Prince do tomorrow? The Upper Management's role is to think those things through in the long run, just being ok now is far from enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T14:09:43-07:00","id":1465566,"title":"","content":"given the distance (rules wise) between thinbloods and their progenitors, would it be relatively easy to modify things to create and play sabbat born thinbloods with this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T14:38:32-07:00","id":1465568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465566#post1465566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">given the distance (rules wise) between thinbloods and their progenitors, would it be relatively easy to modify things to create and play sabbat born thinbloods with this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not easier than playing anyone as Sabbat. All the important rules for playing Sabbat do not relate to Generation in any capacity.<br /> <br /> So no, it isn't meant to let you play as Sabbat no matter what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T15:25:29-07:00","id":1465571,"title":"","content":"As a side I don't really have a problem with the Scourge as an office in the camarilla. Gehena panic aside, it's pretty easy to justify fromm pragmatic viewpoint. Unsanctioned embraces are a massive masquarade risk for a number of reasons and any contested territory is going to want to have someone looking for anarch/Sabbat trespassers. I just like my carmarilla kingpin rather than dick dastardly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465529#post1465529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm primarily a Camarilla fan, but I want the books to support playable Sabbat characters. It doesn't hurt my Camarilla games if other people are playing Sabbat games, in fact giving enough details to make Sabbat PCs also gives Camarilla or Anarch STs more material for nuanced antagonists. Also, even if I prefer Camarilla games, I might still want to play Sabbat once in a while, it's not as though I have real life loyalty or animosity to fictional vampire organizations.<br /> <br /> I'm moderately interested in Sabbat book, but I'm sure that people who were really interested in a Sabbat book almost all wanted playable Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I really don't see any downside to supporting Sabbat PCs and I see plenty of downsides to not supporting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a cam primary myself Its probably worth noting as a gm its a lot easier to remove the dumb writing for carmarilla than re-build sabbat mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-28-2021, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T22:30:03-07:00","id":1465604,"title":"","content":"An Official scourge position is unnecessary, you just need to ensure territory is properly allocated and vampires will hand over anyone who doesn't belong. You're really just designating someone as a bad guy by giving them the title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T01:01:28-07:00","id":1465607,"title":"","content":"The Scourge is basically the Prince making it clear they plan to kill a lot of people without the desire to investigate or hold trials (that's what the Sheriff does). The Scourge is just there to kill people. Only Prince's supremely confident in their power can appoint one since just the act of declaring this guy will be judge, jury and executioner in your domain and will answer to nobody but you will likely drive some vampires to being Anarchs. <br /> <br /> And yeah, that's about it Scary. Everyone hates the Scourge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T01:12:24-07:00","id":1465610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465604#post1465604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Official scourge position is unnecessary, you just need to ensure territory is properly allocated and vampires will hand over anyone who doesn't belong. You're really just designating someone as a bad guy by giving them the title.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would disagree with this as the idea that you are going to get your Toreador Primogen to turn over the Thin Bloods feeding in their territory is ridiculous. The Scourge is not law enforcement. A Scourge is an EXTERMINATOR. You don't get the holders of the domain to remove the people feeding in their territory. That's the whole reason you're a part of the Camarilla. They have PEOPLE for that.<br /> <br /> And the Scourge is not for &quot;real&quot; Kindred. They're for the dregs and vermin of Kindred society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T02:59:16-07:00","id":1465616,"title":"","content":"Just ask the Sherrif to do that. <br /> <br /> For all you know it could be someone's sanctioned childe they haven't introduced to everyone yet. Accounting periods can be rough. requesting for a scourge rather than a sherrif is a nice way to make an enemy out of a potentially powerful and now bereaved sire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T03:13:18-07:00","id":1465617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465616#post1465616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just ask the Sherrif to do that.<br /> <br /> For all you know it could be someone's sanctioned childe they haven't introduced to everyone yet. Accounting periods can be rough. requesting for a scourge rather than a sherrif is a nice way to make an enemy out of a potentially powerful and now bereaved sire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that's literally listed as something that happened and why a lot of people hate the Scourge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 32 of the Guide to the Camarilla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This last comes in light of some recent tales of over-enthusiastic scourges attacking and killing vampires who had followed protocol and were known in the city, but happened to be in the wrong place at the wrong time. The story currently circulating through Elysium describes a feral Gangrel scourge who encountered three Kindred in a derelict building in the barrens of Milwaukee. As he had been given full authority to destroy any Kindred he did not recognize, the scourge made quick work of the trio, who were unable to give much resistance. He brought back trophies of his work, to the consternation of the Tremere primogen, who recognized the personal effects of three recently acknowledged neonates; apparently they had gone looking for a private place to perform a ritual. The prince initially refused to disbar the scourge, but the outrage of the primogen council and the wrath of the united Tremere clan forced him to reconsider.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, the simple fact is the Sheriff is not the best person you want for slaughter. You don't want to humanize Thin Bloods after all.<br /> <br /> Just...remove them.<br /> <br /> The simple fact is the Camarilla sometimes needs someone who does induce pants wetting fear. The Sheriff and Deputies can be brutal and cruel but they are meant to represent the Traditions and be enforcers for the Prince. A Scourge is meant to be something extra and useful for the darker most sadistic of Kidnred. The stick and the nailed stick if you will. With the rising tide of Anarchs, Thin Bloods, and other things you need to have someone who is the designated monster<br /> <br /> I imagine a lot of ex-Sabbat and Banu Haqim will end up in Scourge roles in the New Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-28-2021, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T04:41:37-07:00","id":1465619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465617#post1465617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I imagine a lot of ex-Sabbat and Banu Haqim will end up in Scourge roles in the New Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>The worst possible choices? Wouldn't put it past the idiocy of the nuCam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T06:17:49-07:00","id":1465630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465619#post1465619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The worst possible choices? Wouldn't put it past the idiocy of the nuCam.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well your argument would reduce the Sheriff to 0 Humanity in a short while. If you need a job that can be done by a monster you need to have someone who is a monster do it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T06:25:26-07:00","id":1465635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465610#post1465610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the idea that you are going to get your Toreador Primogen to turn over the Thin Bloods feeding in their territory is ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Turning over doesn't mean the Primogen will personally catch the dregs in their territory. It means they'll complain and the Prince will send the Sheriff.<br /> <br /> A Scourge does sends a very hostile message, and the very same Primogen that keeps their own business in their territory may not like the idea of some goon being empowered to come without asking, poking around and offing people without satisfaction in their territory.<br /> <br /> Just how many of their Ghouls and retainers can the Prince have executed in absolute silence that way? Why should they trust?<br /> <br /> You're forgetting this point: as a rule of thumb, even the Princes faithful allies wouldn't trust the Prince that far. It is not just about what Scourge is supposed to do, but about how much leeway they have to abuse their powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465617#post1465617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, the simple fact is the Sheriff is not the best person you want for slaughter. You don't want to humanize Thin Bloods after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's not how it works.<br /> <br /> To begin with, I'll always repeat that pre-V5 Camarilla don't have the Scourge as an official sect position and this change in nuCam is idiotic. I won't buy those arguments for the Scourge if I don't buy their premises.<br /> <br /> Assuming the Prince just want to get rid of Thin Bloods, the first thing to look up is how other Kindred in the domain look upon them. If they see a Thin Blood as an easy to control servant, as a safe citizen, or what. Remember that Thin Blood hatred is based on a very specific reading of a very specific legend. To buy into it you have to both believe in the prophecy and in the specific interpretation. After all, they're given as a sign, not a cause.<br /> <br /> For many (how many no one knows) Thin Bloods aren't worse than any other high generation. Which means they're actually good as they can't raise to your power level even with time, and being unable to sire is just icing on the cake as they won't compete with you for this right, ever.<br /> <br /> Second, Thin Bloods don't have rat faces and five arms. No one is stupid to think you can just look at someone and say if they're a Thin Blood. Someone walking around and offing people first, justifying later they were &quot;Thin Blood&quot; isn't really helping your cause. This is not about humanizing them, this is about trust.<br /> <br /> In third, the Scourge isn't just about Thin Bloods. It is about everyone the Prince deems &quot;undesirable&quot;. Of those, only the Thin Bloods may be &quot;dehumanized&quot;, all the others are pretty much Kindred. So it's still empowering someone to execute people without proper judgment. By the way a judgment that was explicitly considered proper protocol specifically for unsanctioned Embraces until yesterday.<br /> <br /> You totally can have the Sheriff doing this stuff. You'll just be giving a little more work for them, inside their obligations anyway. It is not like a Kindred domain have a huge population where the police's phone never stops ringing. You can also have an executioner that isn't also judge and jury, and/or an investigator that acts as &quot;sanitary authority&quot; and dehumanize Thin Bloods without raising so many concerns for everyone else's safety.<br /> <br /> Now, can I picture some Princes going forward with that idea? Absolutely. Especially powerful tyrants that do rule even other elders by fear alone, or wannabe tyrants too stupid for their position. Those Princes do exist, for various reasons. Can I picture this becoming an official Camarilla policy regardless of very specific local circumstances? Only in a version of the setting where the Inner Circle went through dramatic brain surgery and are still too drugged to think straight with the neurons left.<br /> <br /> Which is my precise impression of the nuCam.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465630#post1465630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well your argument would reduce the Sheriff to 0 Humanity in a short while. If you need a job that can be done by a monster you need to have someone who is a monster do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if the idiot executes everyone through diablerie. Otherwise they'll stop at 2, falling from planned murder, but as they're following orders it isn't casual murder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T06:39:08-07:00","id":1465640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To begin with, I'll always repeat that pre-V5 Camarilla don't have the Scourge as an official sect position and this change in nuCam is idiotic. I won't buy those arguments for the Scourge if I don't buy their premises.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to have to state I don't think this is remotely true. Even if you argue that Scourges aren't in every city, they're absolutely an official sect position. You can certainly argue it's a dumb idea but it's every bit as much a title as Sheriff or Seneschal or Herald. There's nothing wrong with thinking it's a dumb thing to include and counter-productive to dealing with the issue or that you hate it as something the Camarilla would endorse but I think if you have an entry in the Guide of Camarilla then it's beyond the point of denying that it is a part of the official Revised changes to the Camarilla. It is not an invention of V5.<br /> <br /> It also shows up in V20. It's on page 25 of the Core Book.<br /> <br /> People refer to the Scourge in NEW YORK BY NIGHT as an actual job title held by someone.<br /> <br /> NYBN is a Revised city book.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying.<br /> <br /> The Scourge exists as a weapon of fear and to restore the Camarilla's respect in a very specific time of decreasing power. After the Sabbat sieges of 1999 and Week of Nightmares, the Gehenna fever is sweeping the land. The Scourge is a way for the Camarilla to restore order by beginning a purge of the excessive number of overpopulated high generation Kindred that have weakneed their power base. It is an intimation tactic to create an office that does not have to abide by the social contract of the Traditions or, perhaps, more properly, enforces them much-much stricter.<br /> <br /> Your argument that &quot;only people who believe in Gehenna will want to destroy Thin Bloods&quot; fails I think due to the fact that <i>Thin Bloods arne't considered vampires</i> by a significant chunk of the Kindred population. They have no Clan and are innately Caitiff. There is no reason to accord them the status of Cainite and if they are not Cainites then they are, by nature, a living threat to the Masquerade. It means they should all be destroyed to protect the Masquerade. It is not an argument without merit if you are an asshole.<br /> <br /> And yes you are right, Humanity 2-3 is about where I consider most Scourges will be.<br /> <br /> Maybe 1 if they've taken the occassional nibble of unwanted blood.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, I'd argue the Scourge creates an outlet for sufficienly ambitious Kindred as well. It's a new title and power to those psychotic and zealous in the pursuit of the Camarilla's power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T07:06:45-07:00","id":1465645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465619#post1465619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The worst possible choices? Wouldn't put it past the idiocy of the nuCam.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it would be a great position for people like that. The Scourge goes around dealing with people who aren't in the Camarilla - thin-bloods, people who have refused to introduce themselves to the prince for whatever reason, unsanctioned vampires, the Sabbat, Anarchs, etc. <br /> <br /> The Scourge doesn't really operate within the Camarilla hierarchy, he can't make demands of other vampires in the city and most people just generally view the Scourge as the Prince's lapdog and hate him. This means that politically the Scourge has no future, and moreover is pretty much forever tied to the Prince. If the Prince were to perish the his Scourge would probably get killed too. At best maybe the Scourge could become the new Prince's Scourge. Further the Scourge is pretty disposable - if the Prince wants to kill the Scourge he can do it, come up with some semi-plausible reason (&quot;We caught the Scourge engaging in unauthorized diablerie&quot;) and nobody is going to cry for the Scourge. No one with a decent understanding of Camarilla politics is going to volunteer for that shitshow of a job, so there are two people the Prince will pick. <br /> <br /> The first group are people who honestly enjoy going around killing others. The very real monsters and bullies who don't mind being a a killer. These guys could even be serial diablerists (and as long as they're snacking on people who aren't a part of the Camarilla the Prince can look away and dispose of them if they fuck up and get caught). These people don't mind or don't care that they're going to spend unlife working for the Prince and getting no real respect from anyone else. <br /> <br /> Alternatively the Prince will take someone he doesn't necessarily trust or someone that he doesn't want to see rise in the city's politics and &quot;make them an offer they can't refuse,&quot; essentially forcing them into being his Scourge. This is where you might put an Assamite or an ex-Sabbat. It keeps them occupied and away from the levers of power in the city and ensures that nobody is really going to want to work with them. It also ensures that they have to present a modicum of loyalty to the Prince, since if the Prince dies they'd likely be next (plus the Prince has an easier time of disposing of them if he feels it's necessary). <br /> <br /> Meanwhile with the Sheriff, the Prince is only going to want to appoint someone he can trust to the position (it's likely the Sheriff will eventually find out some of the skeletons in the Prince's closet) and further the Sheriff very much is not disposable. If the Scourge dies it's easy to pick a new guy and tell him, &quot;Go find unsanctioned vampires and kill them.&quot; If the Sheriff dies it could take years or even decades for a new one to get up to speed on what's going on in the city, especially if the previous one didn't leave any records behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T07:23:44-07:00","id":1465648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465619#post1465619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The worst possible choices? Wouldn't put it past the idiocy of the nuCam.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Why yes I am very loyal to the sect my liege like all the lasombra who jumped ship. No I'm not overtly a Sabbat plant, I'm totally loyal now. That's why I havnt fallen to the beast see?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T07:32:48-07:00","id":1465649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465648#post1465648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Why yes I am very loyal to the sect my liege like all the lasombra who jumped ship. No I'm not overtly a Sabbat plant, I'm totally loyal now. That's why I havnt fallen to the beast see?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, what better use for a ex-Sabbat than doing the dirty work?<br /> <br /> No one's going to want you at parties, so why not torture and kill for your bosses? It's a position of power and prestige.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T07:43:25-07:00","id":1465650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465640#post1465640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to have to state I don't think this is remotely true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, and since I'm not convinced what I'm asking is that we put this aside and accept that two readings are possible, as I'm trying to do, engaging with each other's basic view. Otherwise you'll just have me repeating myself over and over for no reason.<br /> <br /> I know you and some people read Revised's GttC as formalizing the Scourge, you know I and some people read it as not doing it. Lets leave it at that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465640#post1465640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not an invention of V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I didn't said it was, this is a very fair point to remember. V5 goes with it, but didn't invented it. It could have gone with any of our interpretations on what GttC meant, and it could have changed the take on the matter anyways, either with the Scourge being dropped after a few years or made even more important and prevalent.<br /> <br /> We can debate V5's decisions on their merits when this is relevant to the argument, but V5 pretty much didn't created the Scourge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465640#post1465640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also shows up in V20. It's on page 25 of the Core Book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Where i is described that way:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a position most often found in paranoid<br /> domains where elders believe that fighting the symp-<br /> toms of the Final Nights will stave off the coming of<br /> Gehenna. </div> </div> </div>This sums up that it isn't necessarily a common position and pretty much depends on that very specific interpretation of a very specific prophecy.<br /> <br /> Also that list is about common titles in the sect, not going in the merit if it is endorsed or not by the upper echelons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465640#post1465640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People refer to the Scourge in NEW YORK BY NIGHT as an actual job title held by someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Princes give whatever title they want. It isn't official for the Camarilla as an institution, but it sure is official in their city. This only proves that it exists in NYC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465640#post1465640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Scourge exists as a weapon of fear and to restore the Camarilla's respect in a very specific time of decreasing power.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's your interpretation, not what any pre-V5 book at least says. They all agree, without exception, that the Scourge exists to appease the fears of elders that think that killing Thin Bloods will stave off Gehenna.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465640#post1465640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After the Sabbat sieges of 1999 and Week of Nightmares, the Gehenna fever is sweeping the land. The Scourge is a way for the Camarilla to restore order by beginning a purge of the excessive number of overpopulated high generation Kindred that have weakneed their power base.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gehenna fever is sweeping the land indeed, and that is what caused the creation of the Scourge. But your conclusion after that isn't backed by any book I ever read.<br /> <br /> What is written there is that the Scourge is the creation of individual Princes, not of upper echelons, and they did it because they buy in the Gehenna fever, and not to fight it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465640#post1465640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your argument that &quot;only people who believe in Gehenna will want to destroy Thin Bloods&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The book actively says, right there on V20 page 25 for example, that only people who believe killing Thin Bloods will stave off Gehenna want to destroy them.<br /> <br /> Everything else you said on the matter explains why people may not <b>care</b> about the Thin Blood culling, but <i><b>not caring</b></i> isn't the same as <b><i>wanting</i></b>. Especially because Caitiff face prejudice, but they're pretty much still considered Kindred and used as low-cost labor by many. Nothing makes a Thin Blood particularly a Masquerade threat just because they're there.<br /> <br /> Oh, no, wait, there is one thing: <b>hunting them so badly they'll fuck the Masquerade to defend themselves</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T08:08:41-07:00","id":1465653,"title":"","content":"I imagine that it's rarely a terror tactic and rather a quick and simple means of keeping illegitimately embraced and migrated kindred/thin-bloods out of trouble and half enforcing the Tradition of Progeny. The victims shouldn't be kindred of whom most of the community knows, let alone values. If a sanctioned fledgling gets killed, either somebody screwed up the sanctioning process royally by failing to add them to the scourge's legitimate residents list or the scourge has simply broken the Tradition of Destruction and has no defence for the act.<br /> <br /> In tightly regulated domains, they're obsolete. When the targets already have a community, it risks turning into a war. It's best for when illegitimate embraces and arrivals are frequent, but isolated and not yet established.<br /> <br /> Curiously, Valerie Duval, from the New York visual novels, travels around the world scourging. So she doesn't appear to be fixed agent of the prince of New York. I don't recall any hints as to whether she answers to somebody else or if she's an independent volunteer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T08:30:27-07:00","id":1465656,"title":"","content":"I was more refering to the stupidity of enabling likely diablerists to run amok with the pretext of peace keeping. They get addicted, they bite off more than they should chew, you the prince are now facing an angry mob because you employed a homicidal fiend to thin the population as he pleases. Assamites win awards for <i>the most dangerous canidate for state authorized violence </i> by a good few miles, and former Sabbat? Is <i>former </i>a useful distinction here? Oh yes. They might jump at the job, in the same way a junkie might like to run a pharmacy or a child rapist may be overly enthused about running an orphanage; a good prince makes sure that doesn't happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-28-2021, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T08:47:26-07:00","id":1465658,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'll have to agree with MWIS on this one. Making an Assamite or former Sabbat a scourge is one of the most unwise things a Camarilla prince could do.<br /> <br /> Actually, letting the Assamites into the Camarilla at all strikes me as extremely foolish and the entire role of scourge is pretty questionable. Making the Assamites into scourges is in the overlapping Venn Diagram region of bad decisions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T08:51:49-07:00","id":1465660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465649#post1465649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, what better use for a ex-Sabbat than doing the dirty work?<br /> <br /> No one's going to want you at parties, so why not torture and kill for your bosses? It's a position of power and prestige.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes I suppose that is the line of reasoning the defiantly not a infiltrator lasombra would be hoping you'd go for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T09:22:09-07:00","id":1465665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465656#post1465656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assamites win awards for <i>the most dangerous canidate for state authorized violence </i> by a good few miles,</div> </div> </div> </div>I can clearly picture an Assamite or ex-Sabbat looking at the Prince as if they were a lunatic just for proposing that. And probably denying the job if they can, as it is obviously stupid for their future, unless they're really lost to the addiction by now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T10:14:07-07:00","id":1465666,"title":"","content":"The way the Scourge got fixed by the Prince in my campaign was they made it an office under the Sheriff and essentially made it akin to an on-staff bounty hunter. The scourge is only sent after specific individuals after the Sheriff and/or Prince has determined they were a problem. Similarly, kill orders were for specific individuals for specific offenses and not a blanket policy.<br /> <br /> They were still a mad dog, but the fact they appeared to be on a chain quelled a lot of the discontent amid the court. The Scourge was also required to be on hand for all presentations and spend their non-hunting time in court so as to be familiar with those recognized by the Prince.<br /> <br /> The Prince still tended to go harder on thinbloods though as he had a blanket ban on siring for those of the 13th Generation* in his city (he tried to control all embraces, but this was a \u201cthe answer for you will always be \u2018No\u2019 so don\u2019t annoy me by asking\u201d policy) and gave out of town thinbloods who presented themselves 24 hours to leave his city; so by definition any thinblood in his city was either an unsanctioned embrace, had failed to present themselves or ignored the Prince\u2019s order to vacate; but only the last one would be a kill-on-sight order for the Scourge (a complete unknown would be dragged in to determine their sire or why they\u2019d failed to present themselves before execution\u2026 all of these offenses being actual violations of the Traditions rather than <i>just</i> because they were thinbloods).<br /> <br /> Basically; Sheriff = investigative branch, Scourge = enforcement branch. It still made the Scourge an asshole no one liked, but it prevented a lot of blowback onto the Prince.<br /> <br /> * side-bar: the Prince also put a population limit on creating ghouls just so his subjects would have one more thing they needed to curry his favor for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T15:20:31-07:00","id":1465700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465660#post1465660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes I suppose that is the line of reasoning the defiantly not a infiltrator lasombra would be hoping you'd go for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it's a weird thing to worry about infiltrators among the refugees from Gehenna. It's possible but suicidal from the Lasombra perspective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465665#post1465665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can clearly picture an Assamite or ex-Sabbat looking at the Prince as if they were a lunatic just for proposing that. And probably denying the job if they can, as it is obviously stupid for their future, unless they're really lost to the addiction by now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, what exactly <i>are they going to do</i> in the city power structure then?<br /> <br /> What does a Sabbat defector DO that a Prince should let them in?<br /> <br /> Mind you, we've already got canonical examples of the Sabbat defectors being made into Scourges. Aurora and her brother in LA BY NIGHT were made the Scourges of Los Angeles because Vannevar Thomas needed people to kill Anarchs. The Lasombra Ancilla were dependent on Vannevar Thomas' favor and needed his protection, so he unleashed them on the Anarchs as well as the dissenters of his court. Their reputation as monsters and terrifying killers meant that they rapidly became a whip that forced the Anarchs on the backfoot as well as made the Camarilla look reasonable by comparison.<br /> <br /> It also gave them significant power in the court while solidifying Vannevar's position.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-28-2021, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T15:34:52-07:00","id":1465702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465700#post1465700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then they're morons? I mean, what exactly <i>are they going to do</i> in the city power structure then?<br /> <br /> What does a Sabbat defector DO that a Prince should let them in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not something that will solidify their reputation as untrustworthy monsters. THAT is moronic.<br /> <br /> Act as a defector. You don't arrive eager for a good position in a power structure, you arrive eager to do simple work that'll prove you're a trustworthy citizen ready to adapt to a new life.<br /> <br /> If you're a defector, you already know that your first years, maybe decades for vampires, will be dedicated to building a reputation as a citizen in good standing. You'll have it harder, yet will do it better than others, because you knew that was the price.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you're <b>really, incredibly good</b> <b>at something</b>, then you can use it right away, especially if your defection was facilitated precisely for your specialized know-how and abilities, and you either weigh in the pro and con of asserting yourself so early or you don't have a choice. But it is for personal specialization, not for a broad group. It isn't the case with the Assamites and Lasombra. Most of them should just keep low profile and bide their time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T15:46:30-07:00","id":1465704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465702#post1465702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not something that will solidify their reputation as untrustworthy monsters. THAT is moronic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they not want a reputation as monsters? I mean, that kind of reputation has power in Kindred society. Mind you, I think the issue is we're coming at it from different perspectives on how the Camarilla prefers to be perceived. You definitely seem to lean into the idea want good publicity while I think a lot of their agents prefer to be terrifying. Madame Guil and Karl Screkt made their bones as Justicars because Princes would quake in their presence.<br /> <br /> A Sabbat defector knows that they are going to arrive with a reputation as a blood soaked monster, diablerist, and murderer. Now you can definitely try to state that reputation is undeserved like Sierra in Chicago by Night but you can also lean into that terror in order to accumulate power. If you're going to have a reputation as a monster then you should have that reputation in the service of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Act as a defector. You don't arrive eager for a good position in a power structure, you arrive eager to do simple work that'll prove you're a trustworthy citizen ready to adapt to a new life.<br /> <br /> If you're a defector, you already know that your first years, maybe decades for vampires, will be dedicated to building a reputation as a citizen in good standing. You'll have it harder, yet will do it better than others, because you knew that was the price.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you're <b>really, incredibly good</b> <b>at something</b>, then you can use it right away, especially if your defection was facilitated precisely for your specialized know-how and abilities, and you either weigh in the pro and con of asserting yourself so early or you don't have a choice. But it is for personal specialization, not for a broad group. It isn't the case with the Assamites and Lasombra. Most of them should just keep low profile and bide their time. </div> </div> </div>The Lasombra aren't going to do that as their opportunity for seizing power in the Camarilla is going to be one they can't play the long game for. The Camarilla is a wounded animal and incredibly weakened by all the recent events. So much so that they're willing to accept the Lasombra in the first place. In that situation, now is the best time for Lasombra to carve for themselves a place in the power structure.<br /> <br /> It's after all the Lasombra's hat that they push themselves right until they fall huge.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T16:58:13-07:00","id":1465715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465704#post1465704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Madame Guil and Karl Screkt made their bones as Justicars because Princes would quake in their presence.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>As Justicars</i>. Politics, social standing and reputation aren't things that exist in a vacuum. Not only that, their reputation wasn't just as monsters.<br /> <br /> Guil got the job after 2 <i>centuries</i> of work helping to rebuild the Camarilla in France, definitely building a lot of trust way before building reputation as merciless.<br /> <br /> Schrekt is merciless, but is far more known for his absolute loyalty to the Camarilla as an institution in defense of every Kindred. He simply loves the Camarilla, he worship the law, he believes in every Kindred having a right for protection as long as they follow the law, and THAT is the reason Schrekt is among the most respected Justicars in sect's history. The guy created many of the best practices for Justicars, including maintaining a multi-clan body of Archons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465704#post1465704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going to have a reputation as a monster then you should have that reputation in the service of the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can't do anything about it, sure. But if this reputation is just as a monster, what have you to gain from it? You'll be the Scourge forever and that's all.<br /> <br /> The Scourge is a politically dead position, except in extremely specific circumstances if ever. There may be one or two Lasombra that can actually make a good use of the position in their cities, but for the most part they won't have use for it. It is a dump.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465704#post1465704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you can also lean into that terror in order to accumulate power.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your reputation is <i>just</i> as a monster and a criminal, the only thing you'll reap out of that terror is a Blood Hunt on your head at the first opportunity, especially if you hold an office hated and disposable as is the Scourge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465704#post1465704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra aren't going to do that as their opportunity for seizing power in the Camarilla</div> </div> </div> </div>Their opportunity to seize power in the Camarilla is zero as Scourge. If they want to build a quick power base while the Cam is weakened they must go big in the sect problems, so they can use the situation to create trust fast.<br /> <br /> You know, like Guil did in the aftermath of the French Revolution, or how Schrekt did during e Inquisition, helping with the big problems, and building a fast reputation of reliability and passion for the work that must be done, instead of working as janitors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T16:59:29-07:00","id":1465716,"title":"","content":"I don't think they can bank on their scary rep considering they just completely discredited themselves with defection. If anything threats of big bad lasombra are going to be laughed at by the not-loser clans.<br /> I'd also avoid the office of Scourge like the plague, anything which indicates you're still on a path or will create personal enemies in sect is not what you want to do. If anything your position might be subtly re enforced by not looking power hungry.<br /> If there is a job for the lasombra its general street muscle in sect battles. Pity oblivion is a lousy discipline compared to obtenerbration but potence is okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T17:06:29-07:00","id":1465718,"title":"","content":"I guess I am surprised you don't think being a Scourge is a source of power in the Camarilla but I think we've exhausted that line of conversation, Sabbat-wise. Thanks for discussing it.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow I'm going to be doing a podcast as the PRO-Sabbat: The Black Hand guy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T17:08:38-07:00","id":1465719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465716#post1465716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they can bank on their scary rep considering they just completely discredited themselves with defection. If anything threats of big bad lasombra are going to be laughed at by the not-loser clans.<br /> I'd also avoid the office of Scourge like the plague, anything which indicates you're still on a path or will create personal enemies in sect is not what you want to do. If anything your position might be subtly re enforced by not looking power hungry.<br /> If there is a job for the lasombra its general street muscle in sect battles. Pity oblivion is a lousy discipline compared to obtenerbration but potence is okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. What morons they would be to do so but we know the Lasombra are smarter and deadlier than most vampires.<br /> <br /> 2. I find the idea that the Lasombra are leaving their Paths to be silly. They're all still irredeemable monsters. Mind you, a lot of Lasombra will have never gotten on Paths in the first place according to Revised.<br /> <br /> 3. I imagine the Lasombra will get whatever position they want but I guess I think that they proved themselves the superior vampires by abandoning the Sabbat. They showed, at the end of the day, that they had no loyalty to anything and really did walk the walk of their social darwinist ideals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T17:23:17-07:00","id":1465720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465719#post1465719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. What morons they would be to do so but we know the Lasombra are smarter and deadlier than most vampires.<br /> <br /> 2. I find the idea that the Lasombra are leaving their Paths to be silly. They're all still irredeemable monsters. Mind you, a lot of Lasombra will have never gotten on Paths in the first place according to Revised.<br /> <br /> 3. I imagine the Lasombra will get whatever position they want but I guess I think that they proved themselves the superior vampires by abandoning the Sabbat. They showed, at the end of the day, that they had no loyalty to anything and really did walk the walk of their social darwinist ideals.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) they've just decisively proven they're not. Well they are very good at dying I suppose that counts as deadly.<br /> <br /> 2) ah so you agree the defection and v5s attitude to Sabbat Paths is absurd?<br /> <br /> 3) why do you think that? What is it about &quot;we were wrong about everything and have trashed everything we touched.&quot; that proves anything except lasombra shouldn't rule or be listened to all? That isn't social darwinism except if they're admitting they're the lower order to the ventrue and the brujah who still have there sects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-28-2021, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T17:28:31-07:00","id":1465721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465720#post1465720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) they've just decisively proven they're not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe your perspective is supported by canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) ah so you agree the defection was absurd? </div> </div> </div>It's hard to take any Lasombra seriously who would remain in the Sabbat. I mean, the idea of a Sabbat LOYAL to the sect is a betrayal of what the Lasombra are about. The Sabbat failed, they were abandoned. Proof the Lasombra are the superior vampires. It's that epic Game of Thrones/Red Wedding moment where the Lasombra show this isn't the kind of story where loyalty and virtue win.<br /> <br /> &quot;I told you that you shouldn't trusted me!&quot; - Littlefinger<br /> <br /> Mind you, the idea you have to be on HUMANITY in the Camarilla is so incredibly weird that I wonder who wrote the idea. Only a Sabbat shovelhead would believe such a thing and the Black Hand book flat out has them admit, &quot;Yeah, they're probably not on Humanity.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) why do you think that? What is it about &quot;we were wrong about everything and have trashed everything we touch.&quot; that proves anything except lasombra shouldn't rule. That isn't social darwinism except if they're admitting they're the lower order to the ventrue and the brujah who still have there sects. </div> </div> </div>The Lasombra managed to move from the Sabbat to the Camarilla and now are in a position to take over their old rivals. The Tremere were number 2# for most of the Camarilla's history but I'm pretty sure the Lasombra are going to be from now on.<br /> <br /> At least until they can move on no. 1#<br /> <br /> My perspective is the Lasombra will suffer for a bit but are probably stronger than the Tremere, Loyalist Brujah, Loyalist Gangrel, and Malkavians in terms of influence in the sect. The Nosferatu and Toreador still probably have more pull but that won't be for long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-28-2021, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T17:34:00-07:00","id":1465722,"title":"","content":"Basically, I believe the Sabbat defection of the Lasombra is the Golden Parachute of vampire politics.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra leadership has escaped with all the Sabbat's money, influence, power, and prestige while leaving the rest of the sect to burn. They've offered up those who wouldn't get with the program as sacrifices as well as the Antitribu of the sect. As such, the 500 or so Lasombra defectees are sitting nice and pretty on the burning corpse of their former friends, playing golf.<br /> <br /> Yes, Endron Oil has gone bankrupt but it's not the executives who have lost their pensions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":