y stronger than the Tremere, Loyalist Brujah, Loyalist Gangrel, and Malkavians in terms of influence in the sect. The Nosferatu and Toreador still probably have more pull but that won't be for long.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) pretty much yeah but that's bad writing. Irl if I was to do what the lasombra did how much respect would you really get?<br /> <br /> 2) that's not what I asked, the Sabbat failed because the writers decided it would. also little finger died a failure the world improved by his absence as did everyone involved in the Red weddings instigation. You'd have to be ferociously stupid to put him and position of authority by season 2.<br /> <br /> 3) no that'd be the toreador a clan which isnt a massive liability. lasombra numbers are low, they're ferociously incompetent and by the appallingly low bar of Vampire society: untrustworthy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T17:59:01-07:00","id":1465725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465724#post1465724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) pretty much yeah but that's bad writing. Irl if I was to do what the lasombra did how much respect would you really get?<br /> <br /> 2) that's not what I asked, the Sabbat failed because the writers decided it would. also little finger died a failure the world improved by his absence as did everyone involved in the Red weddings instigation. You'd have to be ferociously stupid to put him and position of authority by season 2.<br /> <br /> 3) no that'd be the toreador a clan which isnt a massive liability. lasombra numbers are low, they're ferociously incompetent and by the appallingly low bar of Vampire society: untrustworthy.</div> </div> </div> </div>1:] Why wouldn't they have respect? You don't respect someone for loyalty in vampire society.<br /> <br /> 2:] The Sabbat only do anything because they are written that way. The Sabbat suffered a massive gain in 1999 and washed over all of the Camarilla in the East Coast because they were written this way. Now in an age of massive social media and being watched constantly, the Sabbat are being portrayed as suffering a reversal of fortune.<br /> <br /> 3:] Are the Lasombra's numbers that low compared to other clans? The defection murders are not going to do that much difference compared to the Beckoning and Second Inquisition. There's 1800 Ventrue versus, what, 1500 Lasombra in the Camarilla? Not numbers that should really matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T18:13:51-07:00","id":1465729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465725#post1465725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1:] Why wouldn't they have respect? You don't respect someone for loyalty in vampire society.<br /> <br /> 2:] The Sabbat only do anything because they are written that way. The Sabbat suffered a massive gain in 1999 and washed over all of the Camarilla in the East Coast because they were written this way. Now in an age of massive social media and being watched constantly, the Sabbat are being portrayed as suffering a reversal of fortune.<br /> <br /> 3:] Are the Lasombra's numbers that low compared to other clans? The defection murders are not going to do that much difference compared to the Beckoning and Second Inquisition. There's 1800 Ventrue versus, what, 1500 Lasombra in the Camarilla? Not numbers that should really matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) because they just just wasted 500 years fighting a war then admitted their primary rivals were right about everything after the sect they built imploded under the weight of their incompetence. Then they betrayed all the members of the sect they led and got a load more of them killed.<br /> <br /> 2) correct but the main issue of contention with v5's writing. It's bad. I can't contend what happens but I can point out the gaping plotholes.<br /> <br /> 3) almost certainly, they suffered heavy casualties in the gehenna war they went off to fight and 2nd inquisition which the Sabbat was especially hard hit by then then probably lost a lot more with the defection conditions and the massive bloodbath which would follow and the lasombra who stayed in the Sabbat anyway. Optimistically I'd say maybe 250-500 tops, more of a bloodline than clan really and it really really does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T18:20:16-07:00","id":1465732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465721#post1465721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe your perspective is supported by canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither is any of your many assumptions about the Lasombra being in a good situation and going to grow big.<br /> <br /> On the other side, while the authors write whatever they want and that is truth, so they decide if the Lasombra are successful or not, we can have an opinion about whatever the authors do being well written or not, making sense or not.<br /> <br /> I do not see the Lasombra defection as well written and do not see them in a good position. If the authors make them successful after that it will be canon and fact in the setting, yet it will make the setting weaker to me because it will be even worse writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T23:11:57-07:00","id":1465741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465722#post1465722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, I believe the Sabbat defection of the Lasombra is the Golden Parachute of vampire politics.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>In the sense that Gold is a really terrible material for a parachute? Sure. <br /> <br /> I don't really know how to deal with your insistance that the Lasombra are doing well. It's like if someone got mutilated to the point where a doctor barely managed to save their now permanently crippled life and some fool in the background is saying things like &quot;Oh he was a masochist, he probably liked it&quot; or &quot;all that pain must be forcing the weakness from the body, he's better off&quot; <br /> <br /> The official writer can say shit like that, but if 1+1 doesn't equal 2 then they're lying out of their arse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T23:16:57-07:00","id":1465742,"title":"","content":"I don't think the defection was even necessary to give the Lasombra a presence in the Camarilla. Individual Lasombra have been in the Camarilla since the beginning, some of them quite potent in blood. They could have simply said that their childer have reached sufficient number to be considered a playable clan without a special backstory. Done. It didn't require some special backstory involving gutting the Sabbat. They just wanted to gut the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T03:03:09-07:00","id":1465751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465742#post1465742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the defection was even necessary to give the Lasombra a presence in the Camarilla. Individual Lasombra have been in the Camarilla since the beginning, some of them quite potent in blood. They could have simply said that their childer have reached sufficient number to be considered a playable clan without a special backstory. Done. It didn't require some special backstory involving gutting the Sabbat. They just wanted to gut the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div> As I've mentioned before the way I ran it was their was a big defection centered around the King's and Queens of shadow and frustrated neonates who hook it with the small number of lasombra already there. The clan is still majority sabbat but now theirs a prominent antitribu in the carmarilla. That way everyone wins.<br /> I figure they're probably going to be used as street muscle while trying build up powerbases. Probably trying to wring domains and ghouling right out of prince whenever a siege goes down or he needs to persecute anarchs. They're kind of hamstrung in the carmarilla in v5 because the clan flaw is particulary awkward for power accumulation/masquarade and oblivion sucks but previous mechanics lasombra are downright brutal in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-29-2021, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T03:10:10-07:00","id":1465752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465741#post1465741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the sense that Gold is a really terrible material for a parachute? Sure.<br /> <br /> I don't really know how to deal with your insistance that the Lasombra are doing well. It's like if someone got mutilated to the point where a doctor barely managed to save their now permanently crippled life and some fool in the background is saying things like &quot;Oh he was a masochist, he probably liked it&quot; or &quot;all that pain must be forcing the weakness from the body, he's better off&quot;<br /> <br /> The official writer can say shit like that, but if 1+1 doesn't equal 2 then they're lying out of their arse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, it's because I'm a huge Lasombra fanboy.<br /> <br /> As much as the Tzimisce? No.<br /> <br /> As much as the Malkavians? No.<br /> <br /> But the Lasombra are up there and I tend to view them with the lens of being the biggest bestest most ruthless Sith Lords out there. As such, I might be biased toward viewing anything they do as automatically succeeding and being a political masterstroke. Even so, I feel like the Lasombra as written are people that have managed to ride a very terrible series of choices and emerge on top of a difficult situation. I perhaps am also taking the view that I think some of the side-eye they're getting is because people who dislike the way the Sabbat were treated in V5 are trying to frame the Lasombra defection with the most contempt/scorn as possible.<br /> <br /> They don't ike the development and thus it is influencing whether they think it was a smart move or not in-universe. That is entirely fair because if your table has the Lasombra being part of the Sabbat as the bestest thing ever for them then it will never be a round peg in a round hole to say that leaving them was a good idea.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I am influenced by the following factoids:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>The Lasombra got out before the Sabbat went to shit</b>.<br /> <br /> In-universe, the Sabbat have become even more radicalized and ready to give themselves entirely up to the Gehenna Crusade as well as suicidal self-sacrifice. The Lasombra look smarter for being the one people not to drink the Kool-Aid.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>The Lasombra were the ones who made the Treaty of Chicago's provisions</b><br /> <br /> Kevin Jackson is a new Prince, an Ancilla and it is very clear from the beginning that Makarov (wait, no that's the villain from Call of Duty) was sent there to be executed from the beginning. It was a deal they chose to make and manipulated Jackson into following up on. Their reasoning? Purging their Clan and eliminating Sabbat Elders is a way to remove their enemies and get paid for it.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Yes, the Lasombra have taken a hit but so everyone else</b><br /> <br /> If the Lasombra were the only people to do a purge of their Sabbat loyal members (plus other Sabbat Elders of the Tzimisce and Antitribu). yes, it would be devastating to them. However, the rest of Kindred society has also been beaten badly. The Second Inquisition and Beckoning is supposed to have inflicted massive casualties on everyone.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>The Lasombra already had a decent-sized Camarilla presence</b><br /> <br /> The Antitribu were only a Bloodline in the Camarilla but that doesn't mean they've not had any influence or power (Montano, the Prince of Venice, and so on). The Sabbat defectees are joining another group that makes them large enough to be the &quot;main&quot; Clan.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>The Camarilla needs the Lasombra</b><br /> <br /> The Camarilla fucked up by exiling the Brujah and losing the Gangrel so them recruiting the Banu Haqim into their ranks/the entirety of the Ashirra and now the Lasombra is a good way of making up their losses. The Camarilla for all the talk of it being in a bad place is now back up to 7 clans and controls much of the Middle East since it's merger.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>There's a lot of open real estate lately</b><br /> <br /> The Sabbat becoming a mobile army and the losses of so many Kindred means there's a lot of spaces for surving Lasombra to move up in the Camarilla. Princedoms, Seneschals, Scourges, and Sheriffs. They're not going to be the dregs of Camarilla society because a Lasombra who goes to Detroit and sets up a new Princedom is going to be the top dog there and undoubtedly knows plenty of people already.<br /> <br /> 7. <b>The Lasombra know their Antediluvian is alive now</b><br /> <br /> As per BJD, they have their reasons for defecting to the side of the Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> Basically, the fact the Lasombra are able to escape the Sabbat's sinking ship with all of its treasure makes them look badass to my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T03:27:19-07:00","id":1465754,"title":"","content":"Yeah but it makes them look pathetic in everyone else's and overtly antagonizes Sabbat fans. Consider how much the stupidity and weakness of 3rd ed anarchs overtly annoys you and I think you'll see were we're coming from.<br /> I'm a huge lasombra fangirl as in they're my number 1 clan in modern nights and the current approach makes me think the writers hate the clan.<br /> <br /> Edit:to push this point further how do you reconcile the fact everything they did over the last 700 years was a complete failure and anyone who followed them most likely just died horribly with idea of them being impressive or formidable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-29-2021, 07:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T04:59:53-07:00","id":1465756,"title":"","content":"I prefer Lasombra as they're presented in V5, but you have to admit, joining the Camarilla is hardly a victory compared to what they could be doing if they either joined it in the first place or they stayed in the Sabbat and it didn't run off the rails. After all, they used to direct the Sabbat more than any other clan. Whose fault is it if the Sabbat no longer serves their purposes?<br /> <br /> And yes, the Second Inquisition and Beckoning have affected every clan (except Hecata for the latter) but does that not include the Lasombra? In which case Lasombra have been lost to the Second Inquisition, the Beckoning <i>and</i> killing each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T07:15:30-07:00","id":1465766,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Lasombra were in charge of the Sabbat. They fucked up. They fucked up bad. So bad, in fact, that the Sabbat ended up getting completely out of their control and they had no choice but to flee the sect they created and led, slaughter their own clan members in the process, and then go beg the same guys they spent the last 700 years trying (but failing) to destroy to let them join their sect. At the end of the day the Lasombra objectively and absolutely failed as leaders of their sect.<br /> <br /> I don't feel it's possible to spin that as any sort of victory of the Lasombra.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, the Sabbat went to shit because we were shit leaders and we completely fucked everything up, but I guess maybe it's possible we could have somehow fucked up even worse? Maybe? So way to go us! We're the best!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T07:43:43-07:00","id":1465768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465766#post1465766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Lasombra were in charge of the Sabbat. They fucked up. They fucked up bad. So bad, in fact, that the Sabbat ended up getting completely out of their control and they had no choice but to flee the sect they created and led, slaughter their own clan members in the process, and then go beg the same guys they spent the last 700 years trying (but failing) to destroy to let them join their sect. At the end of the day the Lasombra objectively and absolutely failed as leaders of their sect.<br /> <br /> I don't feel it's possible to spin that as any sort of victory of the Lasombra.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, the Sabbat went to shit because we were shit leaders and we completely fucked everything up, but I guess maybe it's possible we could have somehow fucked up even worse? Maybe? So way to go us! We're the best!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget they also failed to kill lasombra and the brujah have managed to rally 2.5 clans to their 1 in under 20 years while going from strength to strength and the ventrues 4 as they fight on despite the increasingly bleak situation.<br /> <br /> To quote a PC &quot;I'd sooner put the Tremere in charge.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-29-2021, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T07:56:38-07:00","id":1465769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465742#post1465742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the defection was even necessary to give the Lasombra a presence in the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me correct you, there were individual Tzimisce in the Cam since always (and that's canon). The Lasombra had enough of a presence to be called an <i>Antitribu</i> Bloodline.<br /> <br /> They have been playable in the Camarilla for quite some time.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465752#post1465752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As such, I might be biased toward viewing anything they do as automatically succeeding and being a political masterstroke.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465752#post1465752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I perhaps am also taking the view that I think some of the side-eye they're getting is because people who dislike the way the Sabbat were treated in V5 are trying to frame the Lasombra defection with the most contempt/scorn as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, I must say you have good taste. Not the best, but certainly good taste.<br /> <br /> But the problem here is that you have your own bias <i><u>and</u></i> assumes everyone that disagrees with you sharing a bias, and so <b>kind of</b> disregarding the actual arguments. You're thinking that anything the Lasombra does is genius because it's the Lasombra and anything that happens in V5 we all will think is dumb just because it is V5. You can't really get out of this cycle that way.<br /> <br /> Many of the people arguing against the <i>defection as written </i>already said they could accept another version of it. No one is arguing that, <i>assuming the Sabbat metaplot</i>, <b>a</b> defection was a good idea. We argue the metaplot and the defection, <u><b>but they're distinct arguments</b></u>.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, the Lasombra are a fictional construct. They do what the author wants them to do, and it succeeds if the author wants it to succeed. It is the author's job to then convince the reader that the actions and outcomes are believable. So remember that you can't write the <i>author's</i> plan as genius because of the <i>characters</i> involved.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465752#post1465752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. <b>The Lasombra got out before the Sabbat went to shit</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which in itself is a sign of failure. The good thing is that it is a <i>recognition</i> of failure, but failure nonetheless.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat was their biggest clan project in the last 1 thousand years at least. A huge investment of time and resources. A huge <i>opportunity cost</i>, as they pretty much made a humongous lot of enemies and burned so many bridges to make it work.<br /> <br /> Yet, it didn't. And instead of trying to salvage it, they cut their losses and got out. This isn't a dumb move in itself, by the way, shit happens and trying to much to save what's lost can cost even more, a good investor must know when to accept fate and leave. But it is loss, nonetheless.<br /> <br /> So keep in mind that they're acting out of a loss. It isn't a win. The goal isn't to become more powerful than before, is to lose as little as possible. When you try to frame it as the best possible situation you are just deluding yourself because it isn't supposed to be so, it wasn't written as such, it isn't seen as that from any perspective.<br /> <br /> And yes, social darwinists don't mind it so much. They see it as other challenge to overcome. Something that will make them stronger <i>in the long run</i>. But still not a desirable situation and not a win.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465752#post1465752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. <b>The Lasombra were the ones who made the Treaty of Chicago's provisions</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Keep two things in mind. First, that they're doing it out of a very bad position. They need to leave the Sabbat ASAP. They also need to break a treaty that will convince the rest of the Camarilla, no matter who's at the table. Doing it with a weak negotiator is actually bad, as it means others will be less likely to buy into the Princes' ability to get a good deal. They may be very shrewd, but they still don't hold a winning hand and everyone at the table knows it.<br /> <br /> Second, as said before, we're arguing bad writing. <b>This is not about the Lasombra's intelligence, is about the author's</b>. We have to analyse the deal itself and not just the characters involved. A hidden agenda can only do so much in making an obviously bad deal better than it seems, and for now this is too obviously a bad deal.<br /> <br /> And there's actually a third: <b>you</b> are assuming their intentions with the deal, they're not only also up to scrutiny from an OoC perspective, but they're not actual canon either.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465752#post1465752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. <b>Yes, the Lasombra have taken a hit but so everyone else</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Yet no one else <b>choose</b> to take that beat. By the way, a beat the Lasombra took twice. If they were better off than others after the two-hit SI + Beckoning, they could take the opportunity to act from a stronger position.<br /> <br /> Instead they decide to impose even more loses on themselves. How is this getting stronger? How does this help? You can justify it on cutting loses, but then it is cutting loses, again not winning, or staying even. They <b>literally</b> butchered the clan.<br /> <br /> And that after suffering the same or similar loses as everyone else. They also got hit by the SI and the Beckoning, and at this point it is moot if they got just as bad or not. They basically made sure they would be in an even worse position.<br /> <br /> Because, you know, even in the best interpretation possible of their conditions they had to butcher at least 1 Lasombra for every 3 defectors, and probably it was way worse, not 1:1 but close, especially considering the scale, as they can't conceivably have done every kill silently, undetected and undefended with so many murders. So a chunk of the wannabe defectors actually died trying and there was a huge fight.<br /> <br /> This necessarily means that the defectors are coming to the Camarilla seriously weakened by the fight <b>plus</b> other reasons everyone had.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465752#post1465752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. <b>The Lasombra already had a decent-sized Camarilla presence</b></div> </div> </div> </div>It have no bearing on the quality of the defection and only means that such horrendous conditions were probably unnecessary as you don't need as huge a defection to begin with, and you have insiders to ease things out.<br /> <br /> Of course, that assuming the two groups are in good relations, as the Camarilla Lasombra are known to be hunted by their kin and not very fond of the Sabbat ones. It could very well be that the shitfest on the defectors is the old <i>Antitribu</i> vengeance.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465752#post1465752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. <b>The Camarilla needs the Lasombra</b></div> </div> </div> </div>No, the Camarilla needs a new clan. And not that badly. The Cam did lose a lot, as everyone else, but their needs aren't equal. The Cam got to the table needing to recover some power, the Lasombra got there needing to survive. The Cam have other potential prospects, the Lasombra only have the Cam.<br /> <br /> Still, as was also said before, those conditions are plain dumb, not just dumb for the Lasombra. You are right that the Camarilla have a lot to gain from the defection, regardless. <b>But then why the fuck they asked for that!?</b> It makes no sense. They got a new clan and thoroughly butchered that new clan in the process, for what?<br /> <br /> Granted, <i>a list of targets would make sense</i>. Saying that the defectors can come if those names are offed or brought to the Cam is all god and well. Then it would sound like a tough but good negotiation where both parties get reasonable outcomes and the Cam gets rid of key problematic Lasombra. This is not what happened.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465752#post1465752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. <b>There's a lot of open real estate lately</b></div> </div> </div> </div>What we strongly doubt is that the Lasombra are in the best position to get it. All good positions are based on trust in some level. The Prince may not have illusions that their followers want their power, but they trust key followers to do a good job and behave in the Prince's best interest because it is a common interest.<br /> <br /> No matter how hard the combination of problems have hit, in most cities the Prince have a list of better options to fill any position before resorting to newcomers with a reputation as elder's diablerists.<br /> <br /> And founding your own domain isn't easy, either. Others will try with greater support, and the defectors are coming to established cities first, not receiving an approval letter from the Camarilla to colonize the wild lands. Even in a bad abandoned domain, a Lasombra will get at least a lot of suspicious eyes for even trying, and will have to bring other &quot;colonizers&quot; as those domains are probably empty, or else they would already have their own new Princes.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465752#post1465752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with all of its treasure</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really care about the Ante part, but where did you insist in getting this?<br /> <br /> This isn't the Iron Age when you can simply kill the king and loot the castle. Kindred resources aren't that simple to get, <b>much less when you're evacuating a sinking ship</b>. You know, both literally and figuratively the bulk of the treasure goes down with the ship.<br /> <br /> A number of Lasombra stayed on the Sabbat. They are both best positioned to actually grab any resource of the dead ones and any resource abandoned by the defectors. They are the ones likely to be individually better off in this mess.<br /> <br /> You are totally ignoring the means of cutting loses because you want to see anything the Lasombra does as necessarily the best move imaginable regardless of circumstances.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465752#post1465752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As per BJD, they have their reasons for defecting to the side of the Antediluvians.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is arguing that leaving the Sabbat was a bad idea for the Lasombra. The Sabbat sinking in the first place is a bad idea for the <i>game</i>, but given it is happening, leaving is a good idea for the Lasombra.<br /> <br /> What we're arguing is the merit of the <i><b>conditions</b></i> imposed. They're plain stupid for everyone involved. They are ridiculous, mean a huge amount of extra loses for both parties for no tangible gain and don't follow what uses to happen at similar situations.<br /> <br /> They could and should have a detailed plan of escape, with a defined price for the defectors, but an actual, sensible price that makes the Cam stronger instead of making the clan weaker for the giggles. They could have a list of names that must go down, a list of assets to be transferred or brought with them, another of assets that must be destroyed in their way out. They could have a check list of sabotages to be carried with proof.<br /> <br /> More than anything, it should be tough but doable. The Cam have nothing to gain insisting on a ludicrous price because a ludicrous price would just be unlikely to be paid. The Lasombra have nothing to gain accepting a ludicrous price because as successful bastards they know both what their limits are and when they can get a better offer at the table, they know a joke when they hear it.<br /> <br /> <b>It isn't absurd because it was the Lasombra, or V5. It is absurd because we know the Lasombra can do better.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T14:32:59-07:00","id":1465831,"title":"","content":"I came in late, but I would throw my opinion in the ring that the Scourge isn't simply a dog catcher, taking out clanless vampires. For me the Scourge is also acting like a border police, and threat assessment through the city. While the Sheriff might be all suit and tie, be on limousine, talk all polished and well-spoken like, the Scourge seems like it got to put their feet on the ground. The more posh Sheriffs; that may act like a justice official who might not even carry a weapon, and who deal more with high echelons and society than the streets might demand a Scourge from the Prince to do the more 'dirty work'. If he/she doesn't, he/she might just endeavor one Hound to act like it. Besides, Primogens now have the Clan Whip, who might just be their own personal Scourge/Sheriff (only without the killing sanction in the vast majority of cities). So yeah, I can imagine most big cities, be it power scale or size scale, having a Scourge, cuz it is a lot of ground to cover.<br /> And yeah, giving the position is an easy way to give a dirty &quot;low-clan&quot; vampire something to bite, or maybe it is a heavy duty you kind of curse the vamp with having. So it is the perfect position for the Prince to make mistakes; like giving to a Banu Haqim who wants &quot;very much, sir&quot; to prove themselves (and lo and behold, we got a junkie). And yeah, the Scourge can also be a nice person, who most often than not lends a hand to the disenfranchised (like in Vampire Coteries of New York's sheriff). <br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> Now, about Lasombras in Camarilla, it makes sense for me, in a meta and universe perspective. I mean, they are the Clan who will do ANYTHING to survive, even Gangrel might have some more pride than desire to survive than Lasombras. So yeah, a great number of them dispatching some others of their own to get a place in the most secure club Vampires have nowdays? &quot;Sign me in&quot;. Like, hell, I imagine being a vampire with all talks of Gehenna going on, of Elders Beckoning, weird Cults popping up everywhere, the SECOND INQUISITION hitting hard.... A network of security, who has a tad of distaste for the technology that sometimes doesn't work with you, with a society that even as though it might hate and distrust you exists for you to abuse and manipulate... that seems like a good challenge for the Lasombra. Besides, they are the grey eminence, the power behind the throne, they don't need no position as Sheriff, Primogen or Prince, no sir. <br /> Either way, even if you think the contextualization in the writing isn't as smooth as it could be, I believe there is a very fun territory to explore with the Lasombra marked for suspicion and barred from positions in the most elitist Camarilla has ever been. And hell! I can assure you if they can't get power in the secular structure, they will have a handful of cults to do so through. Besides, imagine how pissed the Sabbat will be with the Lasombra traitors! And since very few will lend a hand to the Shadow Clan, they will also have to look after themselves... let's see their Darwinism take them from between a rock and this hard place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T16:45:19-07:00","id":1465843,"title":"","content":"The big question with the changes to Sabbat and its clans is who really benefits? On a practical level it doesn't really make much difference to carmarilla and anarch coteries and Sabbat players are aggressively discouraged to play and more importantly for the company-buy.<br /> So who actually benefits from this reductive approach?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-29-2021, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T17:14:08-07:00","id":1465847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465843#post1465843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big question with the changes to Sabbat and its clans is who really benefits? On a practical level it doesn't really make much difference to carmarilla and anarch coteries and Sabbat players are aggressively discouraged to play and more importantly for the company-buy.<br /> So who actually benefits from this reductive approach?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm against the change so I'm probably not the person to argue it. The Sabbat are my 2nd favorite sect after the Anarchs and their complexity as well as alien morality is important to me. I also have enjoyed many good games about their Byzantine conflicts. The Fall of the Sabbat to the Beast is a worthwhile metaplot but the people who would primarily benefit from it like Sabbat defectors, people wanting to rebuild the Sabbat, and so on are as discouraged from being played as anyone else.<br /> <br /> Still, it's not hard to understand why the Sabbat was done this way. Much of the setting in 5th Edition seems to have been streamlined. The Sabbat as depicted in the 5th Edition supplement for them are very similar to their depiction in Bloodlines. They're a ravening horde with a few very intelligent and alien morality monsters looming over them.<br /> <br /> This is probably the result of the books being used as a &quot;bible&quot; for game developers going forward as we have BLOOD HUNT. That game would have made a lot more sense if you weren't battling Anarchs but instead a Sabbat siege as they're the guys who have no respect for the Masquerade battling it out on the streets and should it succeed, I have no doubt that future games will incorporate the Sabbat similarly as enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-29-2021, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T17:48:03-07:00","id":1465851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465831#post1465831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me the Scourge is also acting like a border police, and threat assessment through the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sheriff can do that or send a Hound. Two things define the Scourge:<br /> <br /> 1- It hunts Thin Blood. It may be and frequently is tasked with &quot;border policing&quot;, but what really defines it is hunting Thin Bloods;<br /> <br /> 2- It answers only to the Prince. And <b><u>that</u></b> is the crux of the question. The Scourge doesn't respond to no one else and is supposed to not never give satisfaction to no one else, no matter their position. They are empowered by the Prince to go anywhere and do anything, and only the Prince can judge the actions of the Scourge.<br /> <br /> So, those two things are what distinguishes a Scourge from a Hound or Sheriff. If you want a border patrol that properly follow protocol and don't need to raise eyebrows at an alarming rate, you don't need a Scourge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465831#post1465831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Scourge isn't simply a dog catcher.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they're the Prince's personal dog catcher, and the Prince have no need for a Scourge that tries to be more than that.<br /> <br /> But, yes, the Scourge as a person may be a likable person, even. It is unfortunately stuck with being hated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465831#post1465831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, even if you think the contextualization in the writing isn't as smooth as it could be</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the problem. The problem is specifically with the defection terms. No less, no more.<br /> <br /> Oh, of course, and with the Sabbat becoming unplayable, which is just tangentially related as there was no need for the defection to actually change the Lasombra's position in the sect. It would just be a matter of changing who's called <i>Antitribu</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465847#post1465847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably the result of the books being used as a &quot;bible&quot; for game developers going forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still have a hard time believing that because it is a dumb bible. There is nothing to gain for a developer from a streamlined setting. No writer of other media benefits from this. There must be another explanation, even if it is simply &quot;they like it that way&quot;, otherwise I'll have to conclude they're really blind to the actual media market and following dated theories.<br /> <br /> Not that it isn't possible, but I prefer to think they're a little smarter than that if they're putting so much money in the project and keeping their idea of the setting so airtight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T18:08:12-07:00","id":1465854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465851#post1465851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still have a hard time believing that because it is a dumb bible. There is nothing to gain for a developer from a streamlined setting. No writer of other media benefits from this. There must be another explanation, even if it is simply &quot;they like it that way&quot;, otherwise I'll have to conclude they're really blind to the actual media market and following dated theories.<br /> <br /> Not that it isn't possible, but I prefer to think they're a little smarter than that if they're putting so much money in the project and keeping their idea of the setting so airtight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we'll just have to disagree because I don't think the Nu Sabbat are poorly written. They're not very flexibly written and have lost a lot of benefits but they are well-defined for what they are and their role in the current metaplot.<br /> <br /> As the hammer meant to take to traditional power structures and shake up the status quo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, they're the Prince's personal dog catcher, and the Prince have no need for a Scourge that tries to be more than that.<br /> <br /> But, yes, the Scourge as a person may be a likable person, even. It is unfortunately stuck with being hated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember a Scourge is not only someone who can exterminate Thin Bloods, though that is the group which has the least protection in Kindred society. The Scourge's mandate can also apply to Caitiff and Anarchs as a rule. The breaking of the latter from the Camarilla was already occurring in 1999 until 2004 and a sign the Camarilla was adopting a zero-tolerance policy to dissent. The Sabbat's antics, the destruction of the Ravnos, and the Kuei-Jin meant hat Kindred society was greatly destabilized.<br /> <br /> The Scourge is someone I'd describe, without hyperbole, as the executioner or torturer of the Prince. Their role is to be a source of fear in the court and someone who puts bite in the Camarilla's threats. The Sheriff and Hounds COULD do all this but you don't want them viewed as a mindless attack dog and dealer of final death. The Scourge wears their brutality as a badge of honor and it creates its own enforcement.<br /> <br /> The Sheriff is the dirty cop, the Scourge is the Secret Police Captain.<br /> <br /> &quot;Are you hiding any Anarchs in your haven?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-29-2021, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T18:40:44-07:00","id":1465861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465854#post1465854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we'll just have to disagree because I don't think the Nu Sabbat are poorly written. They're not very flexibly written and have lost a lot of benefits but they are well-defined for what they are and their role in the current metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going into the merit of being well or poorly written, just about the streamlining and simplification, regardless of writing quality.<br /> <br /> The decision of making the Sabbat less nuanced as an example, makes the Sabbat less versatile. This is as true for STs as it is for a movie script or a computer game. The caveat being that the ST actually can alter and adapt anything they want for their games, while licensees must keep the IP as is, only adding approved alterations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465854#post1465854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember a Scourge is not only someone who can exterminate Thin Bloods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and it makes sense that in the current situation its role as Anarch catcher is growing. But I was stressing the definition <i>per se</i>, and what defines the Scourge in this regard is the hunting of Thin Bloods.<br /> <br /> Basically, in any city where the Prince declared a Scourge you know it was for Thin Bloods. The Prince may hide behind many justifications and the Scourge may have many other obligations, for show or for real. But you know they're there to hunt Thin Bloods, or else the Prince would just empower a Hound with a couple new duties.<br /> <br /> This isn't the more important problem, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465854#post1465854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Scourge is someone I'd describe, without hyperbole, as the executioner or torturer of the Prince.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is.<br /> <br /> Like, you empower someone to go anywhere, do anything to anyone and answer to you and only to you, no matter what.<br /> <br /> No, you're not just appointing border police.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465854#post1465854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sheriff is the dirty cop, the Scourge is the Secret Police Captain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only disagree here. I think they're more a field agent than a captain. The Scourge's role isn't to make complex policy decisions. They must be able to make a lot of decisions on the field, but never define the mission or how it is carried off.<br /> <br /> That's why it is an end-job, despite working at the feet of the Prince. It is non-prestigious, hated, ties you tightly to one person, and you don't even get to help with big decisions or ask the reason behind your mission. You're not helping decisions, just causing pain and destruction.<br /> <br /> Even your information-gathering is kind of secondary, as the Prince have the Sheriff already to do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T20:39:44-07:00","id":1465865,"title":"","content":"Well, yes, it is surely true that from the Dark Ages there would be a difference between the Sheriff and the Scourge. Cuz NOBODY wanted to be dirty and stained executioner, it is a bloody and thankless job, that makes you feared and avoided. If the vampires replicated this in their own courts is a matter of region by region, ruler by ruler I guess. So yeah, if the Sheriff acts more like a clean justice officer, he/she probably will let the Scourge be the CIA waterboarding agent.<br /> The thing is, the best part about the Scourge job is that hardly anyone will be spying on your work (there is nothing interesting to see mostly), you don't have (and probably isn't called) to go to social and ceremonial events, you only answer to the Prince (and yeah, it seems there isn't a degree of subservice to the Sheriff so rock and roll), and the most important thing here is 'you have a mandate of death penalty, a <i>carte blanche</i> to kill those who you deem (by the laws of the domain) a pariah, invader, clanless, undesirable and etc.'. Power of life and death is really powerful, even if it is just over the poacher, the Anarch or Sabbat, the Thinblood and other downtrodden. I imagine that the smart Scourge has a lot of little and big favors with the small fish, and maybe they were payed off by some Camarilla citizen to let someone slide... So there is a lot of potential for fun stories with the Scourge, and it can be a versatile position. It can also just be a mad dog hunting down the Blood Hunted (which basically all Thinbloods are de facto, but maybe banished Clans might be as well). <br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> The Sabbat matter, well, for me it is a pretty sticky point. I liked the sect, but it seemed that every person from which I heard a Sabbat game being told played as something very different from what I liked about Vampire. It was all war games and darkness-city dwelling, guns blazing and bazookas. Call it a bad impression, but the communities with which I interacted left a taste of &quot;Sabbat isn't Vampire the Masquerade but a different game in the same setting&quot;. And we are defined by impressions, so I've never felt interested with Sabbat games, finding much of it like a murder hobo's wet dream draped in the Vampire melodrama; which is okay for me, the entire setting doesn't need to work for me. What I can say for me is that V5, with all its chinks and rough edges here and there has a very well defined vision and core. It is a battle against or with the Beast, a crashing and tidings of morality, it is Humanity against the very nature of vampire, including all the needs of the blood drinkers and their political or power ambitions; it is a sympathetic game. So it a game about vampires who struggle with their own Humanity and the failing Humanity from the elders and power hungry (be you one of the later or the formers). I might be wrong of course. Either way, the Sabbat is a bit too distant from this kind of game, even if it is VERY close setting wise, thematic and mechanically it works differently. So yeah, V5 made me want to play Sabbat, even if it doesn't give me the tools for the job; but I also don't think the game (not the setting) has the sect as an essential component of its player options. <br /> The option would be great yes, but it seems the developers didn't want to open this can of worms, so they decided to make their own can of worms; they made something new, even if smaller. Something that got me off guard and it might have had something to do with this option removal is the liberation for the Storytellers Vault to have V5 fan-material. And hell, it seems like just in the first week we got 3 books just to let us play with Paths of Enlightenment; some of these made with the expressed purpose of a Sabbat game. Call this whatever you want, but it seems like these two releases were made as a pair. But I might be getting crazy.<br /> All and all, I liked the direction it took, but I feel for the people who loved to play as the sect and were expecting to do it more in the new edition with new material but didn't have it. Even if I don't expect my PCs to go Sabbat in my current games or other ones, for the fun of it I'm making my own ways of having the Sabbat as a playable faction. We'll see how it goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T21:57:55-07:00","id":1465867,"title":"","content":"The Lasombra care so much about &quot;brand recognition&quot; that they kill any member who they deem unworthy. <br /> This whole deal is really, really, really bad for brand recognition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T22:39:25-07:00","id":1465869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465867#post1465867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra care so much about &quot;brand recognition&quot; that they kill any member who they deem unworthy.<br /> This whole deal is really, really, really bad for brand recognition.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one can stop them from taking over the Camarilla. Certainly not the weak Ventrue. Their blood will invigorate the new Kings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T23:51:16-07:00","id":1465871,"title":"","content":"The more you share nonsense, the more I think the writers are on a similar page and want to destroy the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T00:32:47-07:00","id":1465873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465869#post1465869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one can stop them from taking over the Camarilla. Certainly not the weak Ventrue. Their blood will invigorate the new Kings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I expect that if the Lasombra took over the Camarilla, the sect would implode just like the Sabbat. Probably much faster since so many of the Lasombra in the Camarilla are the ones who're the first to cut and run when things take a bad turn. At least with the Ventrue, they'd stick around to the bitter end if their sect started going sideways rather than jump ship at the first opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T00:59:38-07:00","id":1465874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465871#post1465871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more you share nonsense, the more I think the writers are on a similar page and want to destroy the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a huge Lasombra fanboy. The problem is they were always held back by the Sabbat and frankly were regulated to being the literal Keepers of their brothers. A bunch of ravening madmen. They, by contrast, never got to be the kind of all-pervasive all-powerful Illuminati that the Camarilla is on its best days. The Lasombra were always best in the Camarilla and it was a shame they never had a bigger role in the sect.<br /> <br /> But let's face it, they're also flat out cooler than the Ventrue. There's nothing the Ventrue do that the Lasombra don't do better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T01:54:54-07:00","id":1465877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465874#post1465874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But let's face it, they're also flat out cooler than the Ventrue. There's nothing the Ventrue do that the Lasombra don't do better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Earn trust<br /> Organize<br /> Cooperate<br /> Form meaningful relations that aren't based on fear.<br /> They have better manners, and dress better.<br /> They can take a hit.<br /> And they can certainly lead sects and global conspiracies a lot better.<br /> <br /> &quot;cooler&quot; =/= &quot;better&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-30-2021, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T05:19:07-07:00","id":1465887,"title":"","content":"Also, lets remember, that the Ventrue were never really designed to have to compete to be the &quot;cold bastard leadership Clan.&quot; They were that first, and then the Tzimisce and Lasoombra got expanded on and took all their &quot;cool&quot; narrative stuff from the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> There's a reason why most of the things MWIS pointed to are made to really pop in the DA line that was designed to have all the Clans interact more openly without Sects dividing them up. When mot of the Clans weren't dreaming of the idea of having organization above the level of Prince, the Vetnrue formed military and trade leagues so that if you tried to mes with one Ventrue Prince, you had to deal with dozens of them. They were the masters of medieval warfare, and knew how to use mortal troops and tactics to out siege or out maneuver Clans relying on flashy Disciplines for major conflicts. <br /> <br /> The problem in the modern nights, is there's no real equivalent to a lord getting on his horse decked out in awe inspiring armor, and leading an army of vampires, ghouls, and conditioned mortals into formation warfare on open battlefields for the Ventrue to keep that mode of cool (plus the games don't have great mechanical support for it). The Ventrue focusing on political and financial warfare and without the militaristic edge of feudal lords past, made them too easy to co-opt.<br /> <br /> It's one of the shames of V5's directions: they actually created a space where the Ventrue could be those warlords of the night again, ruling war, money, and power, had the Camarilla taken a more militaristic (if defensive) stance over what was written. It would have also made more room to have the Ventrue and Lasombra in the same Clan. While maybe too close to the Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords for some, that dynamic has a lot of resonance across lots of genres for a reason. Someone thinks they wields the power of the throne by sitting in it, and someone thinks they can wield whoever sits on the throne.<br /> <br /> But sitting on a Camarilla throne in V5 doesn't have the might of the Fiefs of the Black Cross to make the Venture cooler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T05:27:42-07:00","id":1465888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465877#post1465877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Earn trust<br /> Organize<br /> Cooperate<br /> <b>Form meaningful relations that aren't based on fear.</b><br /> They have better manners, and dress better.<br /> They can take a hit.<br /> And they can certainly lead sects and global conspiracies a lot better.<br /> <br /> &quot;cooler&quot; =/= &quot;better&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay now you're just making up words that don't make any sense in vampire society.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T07:30:27-07:00","id":1465891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465865#post1465865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, the best part about the Scourge job is that hardly anyone will be spying on your work (there is nothing interesting to see mostly),</div> </div> </div> </div>No one have a reason to believe you're not abusing your powers, so I'd say anyone that thinks they can get away with it will pretty much be spying on your work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465865#post1465865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and maybe they were payed off by some Camarilla citizen to let someone slide...</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible, but remember that an office with so many dirty jobs and at the direct service of the Prince also means that going against the Prince's wishes may not be very smart.<br /> <br /> A Scourge that defies the Prince's orders is playing a very dangerous game at every turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465865#post1465865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood Hunted (which basically all Thinbloods are de facto, but maybe banished Clans might be as well).</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's officially true it only highlights how much the Camarilla went dumb in V5, as before it was only true in some domains, not necessarily most of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465865#post1465865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but it seemed that every person from which I heard a Sabbat game being told played as something very different from what I liked about Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which doesn't matter in the least. Not for you, not for the designers. Saying that a play style supported by the same rules and same setting doesn't have a place because it is against your personal vision of the correct way to play the game is gatekeeping and stupid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465865#post1465865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a battle against or with the Beast, a crashing and tidings of morality, it is Humanity against the very nature of vampire, including all the needs of the blood drinkers and their political or power ambitions; it is a sympathetic game. So it a game about vampires who struggle with their own Humanity and the failing Humanity from the elders and power hungry (be you one of the later or the formers).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you just defined Vampire: the Masquerade in all of its editions. Yet the Sabbat's presence never kept it from being that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465865#post1465865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they made something new, even if smaller. Something that got me off guard and it might have had something to do with this option removal is the liberation for the Storytellers Vault to have V5 fan-material.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they made something new by not making something, because not creating rules made space for fans to create rules instead?<br /> <br /> Why don't we go one step further and make a 6th edition without rules, so the fans can make all the rules?<br /> <br /> You can't seriously pretend that a bad design decision is good because it encourages people to correct it...<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465874#post1465874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra were always best in the Camarilla and it was a shame they never had a bigger role in the sect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here now, this line is actually true. And it is also true for the Tzimisce. When they wrote the Sabbat they created an interesting sect and two interesting clans, but not a good marriage between them.<br /> <br /> One thing I think V5 did well was to formalize the Sabbat as the sect of the <i>Antitribu</i>, covering all clans and being bound to none. Which does not change the roles of those two in the sect, but does define them better in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T07:38:47-07:00","id":1465892,"title":"","content":"<i>Brushes it off with humour. </i><br /> <br /> But for realsies: The OG seven clans were the best at what they did. The Ad-on clans aren't competitive with them outside of the extremely specific fields that these clans excel in. Judging by discipline spread and weakness, the original clans have three things they're good at or two things and a widely applicable power (Protean/Thaumaturgy) the later clans are largely defined by two things they're good at and... a very specific power with a limited range of applications. Obtenebration is only good for physical conflict and has almost no wider application that couldn't be done better by another discipline. Vicissitude is surgery, Chimestry is too costly for regular use, Quietus isn't particularly good for anything. They're imbalanced. Unwieldy. They need to be more selective with their childer as they both have a higher barrier for entry while also their highly specific skills are more easily devalued by competition, which in turn harms their organization. In most cases there's a OG cam clan that can do things better than them 4 times out of 5.<br /> <br /> Malks&gt; Set (probably the strongest in terms of ease-of unlife of the non original clans)<br /> Gangrel&gt;Ravnos<br /> Nosferatu&gt;Assamites/Giovanni<br /> Ventrue&gt;Lasombra/Tzmisce<br /> Tremere&gt;Anyone who can cast a spell.<br /> <br /> Toreador= They're not particularly good at anything specific, but nobody can equal them in diversity or quantity, they have the lowest barrier of entry of all clans.<br /> Brujah, In combat, they only really lose to high level lasombra (a clan specializing in crushing their foes) but still have a higher quality of life than all these clans<br /> <br /> The Lasombra can't compete with the Ventrue in anything except direct combat. The Malkavians also trounce the Lasombra in every aspect other than combat. The Tremere also trounce the Lasombra. The Brujah are very much favoured in direct social competition with Lasombra.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra are very much one of the best clans for the position of Sherriff or scourge, <i>but you really don't want to be giving these positions to a load of ex-sabbat now, do you?</i><br /> <br /> And Look, I love the Lasombra<br /> But they sure as fuck aren't going to be ruling the Camarilla with anything short of an act of god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-30-2021, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T07:43:55-07:00","id":1465893,"title":"","content":"I mean the Toreador are absolutely the best at social combat. How do you know you're the best? You're the one no one thinks is the ruler but dictates what they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T08:06:29-07:00","id":1465896,"title":"","content":"&quot;Social combat&quot;<br /> Because with all that charisma, everyone expects the Toreador to be assholes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T08:28:24-07:00","id":1465900,"title":"","content":"This is pretty much a case of MyWifeIsScary writing down his headcanon. It is well written, but if you think about for more than one minute, you begin to see the flaws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T08:47:40-07:00","id":1465902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465892#post1465892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for realsies: The OG seven clans were the best at what they did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree that the OG seven are the best, at the very least, at being the default options for players. And indeed it seems the main reason to keep the Gangrel out and kick the Brujah from the Cam is just to put them on the Anarchs, so the Cam doesn't have monopoly over the main body of the Big Seven.<br /> <br /> They have nice Discipline spreads and versatile concepts. They cover all your bases on main Vampire tropes, with the ad-on clans making for specialized subtropes.<br /> <br /> Some of your arguments don't add up so well, as you have an exceedingly strict view on the role of Disciplines in a Kindred's existence and clan effectiveness, but I know where this line of argument goes, so I'll focus on just a few picks here.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't brush off the Toreador so easily. The combination of Auspex and Presence is extremely powerful as a social weapon. It is less controlling, but actually more powerful than Presence + Dominate, or even than Auspex + Dominate, for their role in Kindred society. Celerity is also the most versatile physical Discipline even if you take out the broken rules on multi-action, as it can be easily both defensive and offensive. They simply excel at setting and riding social mood like no one else.<br /> <br /> Lasombra represent a different and interesting approach to leadership if compared to Ventrue. I wouldn't brush them off so easily, although the past as Sabbat is certainly a huge problem now. But were them in the original Cam, I totally see them and the Ventrue working together, as rival or allies interchangeably. More probable than any of the two controlling the Camarilla is the two being always disputing it but being collectively a <i>de facto</i> diumvirate, maybe a <i>triumvirate </i>with the Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T08:54:03-07:00","id":1465903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465892#post1465892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Toreador= They're not particularly good at anything specific, but nobody can equal them in diversity or quantity, they have the lowest barrier of entry of all clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that after the Tremere, they arguably have the strongest Disciplines set. Auspex and Presence is an especially potent combination, covering a lot of bases. Celerity is there to make sure that they cannot easily be directly threatened, making them able to use their social prowess more extensively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T09:07:13-07:00","id":1465905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465900#post1465900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is pretty much a case of MyWifeIsScary writing down his headcanon. It is well written, but if you think about for more than one minute, you begin to see the flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is just headcanon, it's headcanon that I completely agree with, and is in accord with the view of the clans that the creator of the game has. The original seven clans are the most important for the game and the best at what they do. They were carefully chosen out of all the concepts that were floating around during the development of the game, and embody common archetypes that are instantly recognizable to everyone. Consequently, there is never a convention where one of the seven is not played, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Of1JmwBlmNc&amp;t=2274s\" target=\"_blank\">as Mark Rein-Hagen is eager to point out.</a><br /> <br /> My personal view is that the Ventrue should typically run rings around the Lasombra. Portraying the former as incompetent nincompoops to hype up the latter not only goes against the original design intent, but is a failure to recognize which character concept has the broader appeal and is thus more useful for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T09:17:46-07:00","id":1465907,"title":"","content":"Eh if you heard the phrase &quot;an entire clan of bitches&quot; and didn't think Toreador, there's something wrong with you.<br /> <br /> Disciplines are, until V5, a great indicator of what Attributes a clan values. It's also very easy to make broad statements about the character of clans who share disciplines. There are some extremely strong correlations:<br /> <br /> The Clans with Dominate are depicted as more organized than the clans without Dominate. (Exceptions: Nosferatu are very well organized without dominate, perhaps animalism acts as a surrogate? )<br /> Clans with Auspex are known for intelectual pursuits than those who don't have Auspex. (You could argue they're often obsessive)<br /> Clans with Potence are violent and fond of brute force (exceptions: Assamites, though you can argue poison and finess is more their modus operandi)<br /> Clans with Presence are good at making friends and winning allies, at least among mortals.<br /> Clans with Fortitude... ehm, it's difficult to articulate. We can say they're more reliable, or more responsible, or more... burden able. Perhaps more predictable?<br /> Clans with Celerity are arsehats, by vampire standards. (I'd say fickle, but once again Assamites ruin that notion)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-30-2021, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T09:46:05-07:00","id":1465910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465907#post1465907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disciplines are, until V5, a great indicator of what Attributes a clan values. It's also very easy to make broad statements about the character of clans who share disciplines. There are some extremely strong correlations:</div> </div> </div> </div>My point isn't that it isn't true, but that you have a tendency to overplay this aspect. And that's particularly problematic when a discipline can be interpreted in a way you didn't thought of before, or with clans meant to be trope inversions, for example.<br /> <br /> It is also complicated by gimmicky Disciplines, as they're not supposed to play into the same tropes to begin with.<br /> <br /> But that's besides the point. Even if it is debatable if the ad-on clans are weaker in the setting, they are weaker as broad archetypes, being more limited in narrative scope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T09:54:36-07:00","id":1465911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465903#post1465903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that after the Tremere, they arguably have the strongest Disciplines set. Auspex and Presence is an especially potent combination, covering a lot of bases. Celerity is there to make sure that they cannot easily be directly threatened, making them able to use their social prowess more extensively.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Auspex is just <i>strong </i>as a suplementary discipline. But thinking about it more deeply, it's primarly an investigative discipline, not a social one (though it is certainly very helpful with social cues, depending on the edition.) One physical discipline, one social discipline, and one mental discipline. <br /> In no particular order, here's some reasons why Ventrue&gt;Toreador socially. <br /> 1- Toreador disciplines are expensive in OG VTM. Celerity and Presence are blood guzzlers whereas most disciplines aren't. <br /> 2- Ventrue have better combo disciplines. <br /> 3- Toreador are poorly organized and fight as much among themselves more than they fight outsiders. Ventrue are famously rather supportive of one another.<br /> 4- The directness of Dominate is a lot better on mortals than Auspex. Auspex may be more useful against vampires, but You've got less need for going against other vampires when you're much better at acquiring wealth from mortals and, really, if you really think you've got enemies, Dominate's a lot more fun to abuse. <br /> 5- Dominate is front-loaded with goodness. Auspex has it's best stuff at the back. <br /> 6- Until V5, Dominate was very competitive with Auspex when it comes to investigations. <br /> 7- In V5, Fortitude has social resistance powers. A big point up for Ventrue. <br /> <br /> Most importantly<br /> The Toreador don't have much of a weakness.<br /> The Ventrue have a crippling one. Potentially the harshest in the game. <br /> <br /> This actually give the Ventrue a much stronger social impetus. The Toreador make enemies because they're <i>bored</i>. The Ventrue, more than any other clan, Avoid enemies because their lives depend on the stable development of their herd. They're driven to be socially responsible, to care about reputation, to band together with their clanmates. The Toreador just want to see something beautiful so they can become jaded and temper their weakness with apathy. Socially speaking, you can predict what a Ventrue is going to do, and it's much harder to predict a Toreador. That sounds like a weakness, but from an outsider perspective it makes them the better choice for an ally by a good mile. Dependability &gt;&gt;&gt; Sas. (the mountain range of resources help) <br /> <br /> (I'm not trying to say the Ventrue are nicer than the Toreador. They'll totally crush you if a cost-benefit analysis tells them to. The Toreador may be bitches, but they might spare you with enough abstract reasoning)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T10:21:19-07:00","id":1465915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465896#post1465896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Social combat&quot;<br /> Because with all that charisma, everyone expects the Toreador to be assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet even the Ventrue will beg for them not to say mean things about them. Everyone is stockholm syndromed for their approval. Which doesn't exist in RL but exists among vampires.<br /> <br /> Toreador are the true masters of the Camarilla and always have been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7S