eonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465905#post1465905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is just headcanon, it's headcanon that I completely agree with, and is in accord with the view of the clans that the creator of the game has. The original seven clans are the most important for the game and the best at what they do. They were carefully chosen out of all the concepts that were floating around during the development of the game, and embody common archetypes that are instantly recognizable to everyone. Consequently, there is never a convention where one of the seven is not played, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Of1JmwBlmNc&amp;t=2274s\" target=\"_blank\">as Mark Rein-Hagen is eager to point out.</a><br /> <br /> My personal view is that the Ventrue should typically run rings around the Lasombra. Portraying the former as incompetent nincompoops to hype up the latter not only goes against the original design intent, but is a failure to recognize which character concept has the broader appeal and is thus more useful for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the Ventrue look like fools for the fact they didn't beat the Lasombra in 600 years. The Lasombra have their own flaws but have purged their weak members by leaving the Sabbat.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\