<div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465916#post1465916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then the Ventrue look like fools for the fact they didn't beat the Lasombra in 600 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ventrue didn't tried. They weren't even playing the same game for 600 years.<br /> <br /> For all they cared the only Lasombra worth of mention were the few one's in the Camarilla, and they were pretty much a footnote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465924#post1465924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra are safe, secure, rich, and powerful while their employees burn. Seems legit to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please point out a source, not your weird reasoning, an actual source that states that they're secure, rich and powerful.<br /> <br /> Safer they are, sure. They're not in sinking Sabbat. But that's true for everyone that's not in sinking Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T11:05:07-07:00","id":1465928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465927#post1465927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please point out a source, not your weird reasoning, an actual source that states that they're secure, rich and powerful.<br /> <br /> Safer they are, sure. They're not in sinking Sabbat. But that's true for everyone that's not in sinking Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>SHADOWS OF NEW YORK has your sire shown that way.<br /> <br /> PARLIAMENT OF KNIVES states the Lasombra are already infiltrating dozens of cities (just came out).<br /> <br /> We see the Lasombra also wielding significant influence in LA BY NIGHT (two Scourges and the Sheriff).<br /> <br /> Sierra obviously is one in CHICAGO BY NIGHT as is Rabbi Basaras.<br /> <br /> CHILDREN OF THE BLOOD and LET THE STREETS RUN RED also show high ranking powerful Lasombra in the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Which is to say: every single post-Chicago by Night book and resource. <i>Where are the suffering Lasombra</i>? Is there any evidence they are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T11:42:26-07:00","id":1465932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465891#post1465891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one have a reason to believe you're not abusing your powers, so I'd say anyone that thinks they can get away with it will pretty much be spying on your work.<br /> <br /> <br /> Possible, but remember that an office with so many dirty jobs and at the direct service of the Prince also means that going against the Prince's wishes may not be very smart.<br /> <br /> A Scourge that defies the Prince's orders is playing a very dangerous game at every turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> If that's officially true it only highlights how much the Camarilla went dumb in V5, as before it was only true in some domains, not necessarily most of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which doesn't matter in the least. Not for you, not for the designers. Saying that a play style supported by the same rules and same setting doesn't have a place because it is against your personal vision of the correct way to play the game is gatekeeping and stupid.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, you just defined Vampire: the Masquerade in all of its editions. Yet the Sabbat's presence never kept it from being that.<br /> <br /> <br /> So they made something new by not making something, because not creating rules made space for fans to create rules instead?<br /> <br /> Why don't we go one step further and make a 6th edition without rules, so the fans can make all the rules?<br /> <br /> You can't seriously pretend that a bad design decision is good because it encourages people to correct it...<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> Here now, this line is actually true. And it is also true for the Tzimisce. When they wrote the Sabbat they created an interesting sect and two interesting clans, but not a good marriage between them.<br /> <br /> One thing I think V5 did well was to formalize the Sabbat as the sect of the <i>Antitribu</i>, covering all clans and being bound to none. Which does not change the roles of those two in the sect, but does define them better in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, Scourges will always be playing a dangerous game, if they will defy their Princes or not is a matter of risk and principle; one that make stories and gives one more knot in the web of intrigue in the city scene. <br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> Well, it seems like instead of raising points and talking out with me, having a healthy discussion, you just called me stupid and gamekeeper, and used sarcasm to not argument and just swoosh away the question. Also, calling something dumb without giving the alternative or at the very least reason isn't very helpful to the discussion if you don't state that it you are just putting out your opinion out there, which for me is super okay, because we are here to hear opinions and share our ideas. This type of prickly response is quite unnecessary, and I always try to state in my replies that mine are personal visions, and that I hope don't invade or attack the experience of others, for I'm simply giving context to the vision I have as to support what I endorse or not in the game. When people state how all mightly terrible V5 does something or another, so many times I simply don't agree, but hey, when there is a good point I understand even when there is a lot of moments when there is just statements that he/she/them are so stupid and morons for doing this or that which is pitiful and aggressive for no reason other than putting out frustration. <br /> I just think we keep the more constructive talk, instead of bouts of outrage sometimes, cuz there is a lot of awesome discussions and threads throughout here and the forum; people sharing their fun and bad experiences, putting out there theories and concocting together better views and ways to do things in the game and setting than the book themselves. Well, I've already talked enough, I know I'm in the minority here about V5, but it isn't about that, everybody has the right do dislike everything it puts out, I just think we could keep a more friendly environment, its a forum about a game we all love or loved after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T11:53:41-07:00","id":1465934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465915#post1465915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet even the Ventrue will beg for them not to say mean things about them. Everyone is stockholm syndromed for their approval. Which doesn't exist in RL but exists among vampires.<br /> <br /> Toreador are the true masters of the Camarilla and always have been.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It looks to me that Toreador make the Camarilla acceptable and &quot;charming&quot;, alluring perhaps, polishing the rough edges and giving it a &quot;marketable&quot; form in a way. Not only to outsiders, but the inside as well. They keep the veneer of a social club of security, luxury and power, instead of a bastion of the backstabbing, money grubbing and political filth that it mostly is. Ventrues to me kind of need the drapes of the Toreador to have wide acceptance, otherwise they'll look like pure tyrants and dictators. I'm talking, of course, in really broad strokes and general flows, cuz Toreador also are some of the most backstabbing and manipulators there are. And Ventrues value their image a lot, like the kings of the Old Regime, who made their aura of grandeur by their image more than anything. So we could say softly that Toreadors give &quot;life&quot; and &quot;comfort&quot; to the Camarilla, even if that might not be true lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T12:32:53-07:00","id":1465935,"title":"","content":"Lasombra are like one of the goofy side characters that views the hero (Ventrue) as their chief rival, while Ventrue barely recognizes Lasombra's existence and spends the plot trying to outpace the competitive Brujah and his untrustworthy ally and main rival, Tremere while doing his best to keep Malkav by his side and the Nos and Toreador on his team despite their hatred for eachother. Gangrel shows up on occasion to lend a helping hand. Lasombra really wants to set himself apart from the recurring villains Like Ravnos and Assamite but his gimick is too edgy to be taken that seriously. He can only look at the the big guy and copy him as best he can whilst also asserting his supperiority from the shadows of the the closet. Everytime he wakes up, he takes a good long look in the mirror. He just needs to find himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T13:19:25-07:00","id":1465937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465919#post1465919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra lost in the same way the Enron executives who escaped with 100+ million did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you should find a better example here... two of Enron's top executives went to jail, and a third killed himself.<br /> <br /> It's not exactly, &quot;and all the rich and powerful people got richer after destroying their company,&quot; like you're making it out to be... and the example perhaps supports the other side of the argument a bit more than you realize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T13:29:18-07:00","id":1465938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465928#post1465928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> SHADOWS OF NEW YORK has your sire shown that way.<br /> <br /> PARLIAMENT OF KNIVES states the Lasombra are already infiltrating dozens of cities (just came out).<br /> <br /> We see the Lasombra also wielding significant influence in LA BY NIGHT (two Scourges and the Sheriff).<br /> <br /> Sierra obviously is one in CHICAGO BY NIGHT as is Rabbi Basaras.<br /> <br /> CHILDREN OF THE BLOOD and LET THE STREETS RUN RED also show high ranking powerful Lasombra in the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Which is to say: every single post-Chicago by Night book and resource. <i>Where are the suffering Lasombra</i>? Is there any evidence they are?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The very same Chicago by Night you are talking about notes Princes in other cities already subjecting Lasombra to harsh terms of entry or verging on. The same Chicago by Night is the one you acknowledged previously as the book where the clan cuts itself off from one of its best representatives and operatives (Talley) as part of getting into Chicago. If you don't feel that Sierra and Basaras are a really bad trade for Talley, as far as gain vs loss to the clan, I'm not really sure what to tell you. You seem to have taken the idea that *some* Lasombra are now doing okay in the Camarilla and decided it means the clan has achieved some brilliant masterstroke over the apparent drooling fools of the Camarilla, who they will totally also conquer, and that they have not lost anything of consequence for doing so, despite noting themselves they have suffered losses of consequence for doing so. They had to kill off, banish or blood hunt, a variety of established, valuable members of their own clan. That is by definition a loss to their clan. The clan itself acknowledges they had to pay an actual, significant price for their gains. There is a difference between your particular bias towards a clan and the actual state of that clan. Chicago by Night goes repeatedly out of its way to have the Lasombra themselves acknowledge they have paid significant cost for what they have obtained and I don't know why you continuously try to minimize that, you seem to be unable to recognize it mostly makes you sound like the reverse of what you're griping about. You seem to feel that the only way to respond to what you think is considerable underplaying of the Lasombra defection as reasonable is to vastly overplay it as some brilliant master move that tricked an entire sect, while ignoring the distortions that requires of its own.<br /> <br /> Also in LA by Night, the LA Camarilla just got borderline obliterated as a political presence of note in the city, presenting the Lasombra there as having achieved some notable power within the sect is... a choice. They exist on the Camarilla's fringe at best. Why not let them claim whatever position at this point?<br /> <br /> While we're there, which Lasombra in Children of the Blood and Let the Streets Run Red are you talking about?<br /> <br /> Just to be more specific, here are the terms the Lasombra themselves note they have been given by some of &quot;the cities they want to get into&quot;, from Chicago by Night, as in, this is a thing they already had to do:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The conservative<br /> domains? The ones we want to get in on? They\u2019ve been<br /> known to ask for the following:<br /> \u2022 For every Lasombra joining the Camarilla, an elder<br /> Lasombra must be presented as sacrifice.<br /> \u2022 Lasombra intending on joining the Camarilla must<br /> submit to a Blood Bond.<br /> \u2022 A maximum of three Lasombra may exist in any<br /> one Camarilla domain.<br /> \u2022 Lasombra are to receive no warnings regarding the<br /> Traditions; just punishment.<br /> \u2022 The practice of our particular brand of blood arts is<br /> forbidden on pain of final death.<br /> \u2022 No Lasombra may hold title in Camarilla domains<br /> for at least 50 years. </div> </div> </div>While they don't specify which cities did this? There are enough for these domains to be noted in plural. Lasombra suffering strict conditions is enough of a thing that the noted Amici Noctis strategy boils down to &quot;eventually the Camarilla will get tired of doing this.&quot; If you think the Lasombra who got into these cities aren't suffering.. okay.<br /> <br /> Going by actual game material and not treating context to derive from it as optional, it boils down to that some Lasombra are presented as having managed to achieve position and place, or at least security and station. Others are suffering. Others are dead. And that overall? This was not a decision that left the clan unscathed or some unstoppable master move. As though V5 at least made an attempt to portray this as a situation with as much drawback as benefit for those involved. What several people are arguing is that V5 badly wrote this attempt to portray that situation as such as far as that narrative logic. To attempt to counter that with not &quot;no it made sense fine as far as the narrative logic&quot;, but instead &quot;in fact the Lasombra are unstoppable super geniuses who suffered nothing of consequence&quot; is again, certainly a choice. One that puts you at odds in several places with both the game material, and as someone else just pointed out, some instances of real world events. And also again requires nailing things into these absolutist binaries where nuance cannot exist, as though you feel that if anyone deigns to question it, the Lasombra defection can't possibly be defended in the writing by noting it as a conflicted move taken in response to dire circumstances that may or may not play out, presenting it as having arguments both for and against, no, it can only be defended by referring to it as the most brilliant thing ever. Do you really think the writers intended to portray the Lasombra defection in the way you described it as far as a barely impeded mega victory over morons, given what the game material itself inculdes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 10-30-2021, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T13:50:59-07:00","id":1465941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465932#post1465932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it seems like instead of raising points and talking out with me, having a healthy discussion, you just called me stupid and gamekeeper</div> </div> </div> </div>That was not on you, that was on the authors for making the decision. You said it yourself that you didn't agreed to the decision.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry if it wasn't clear on that and sounded offensive, it was not my intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465932#post1465932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and used sarcasm to not argument and just swoosh away the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did used sarcasm, but I'm not sure what question exactly went unanswered. Can you re-frame it, then?<br /> <br /> My sarcasm, by the way, is partially due to the length of the conversation, partially due to my own problems, and although I did felt it was ok on context, I may have missed it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465932#post1465932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, calling something dumb without giving the alternative or at the very least reason isn't very helpful to the discussion if you don't state that it you are just putting out your opinion out there, which for me is super okay, because we are here to hear opinions and share our ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deciding to cut off a sizable population of players and optional stories by choosing first to not present a previously important sect, then simplifying it and making it officially unplayable, <i>as a design decision taken by a company with multimedia in mind</i>, is dumb.<br /> <br /> Cutting off people because they don't fit in a given concept of how the game should be played is gatekeeping.<br /> <br /> I am not stating those things are my opinion because I don't see them as merely my opinion, but as objective, demonstrable facts based on my knowledge on the subject and verifiable by hard data.<br /> <br /> Of course, by doing that I am opening myself to fact-checking and hard responses, by those allegations are presented as facts by design. If it was just an opinion, I would present them as such.<br /> <br /> That said, I tend to tone down my exigence on this regard, both on me and on others, for ease of communication, but you did raised a valid point, hence my explanation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465932#post1465932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This type of prickly response is quite unnecessary,</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. I'm sorry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465932#post1465932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always try to state in my replies that mine are personal visions, and that I hope don't invade or attack the experience of others, for I'm simply giving context to the vision I have as to support what I endorse or not in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I write a lot without stating those things all the time, so I need to rely on context to trim my texts as much as possible. At the same time, I can't read context perfectly, so it is a risk I knowingly assume after weighing both options.<br /> <br /> Happens to be the case that I'm Autistic, and as such I struggle with many communication issues even when they're not apparent. I can only apologize when my calculations go off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465932#post1465932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When people state how all mightly terrible V5 does something or another, so many times I simply don't agree, but hey, when there is a good point I understand even when there is a lot of moments when there is just statements that he/she/them are so stupid and morons for doing this or that which is pitiful and aggressive for no reason other than putting out frustration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting out frustration is, unfortunately, one of the roles of human communication. Although it isn't always fair, it is a fact of life. In that regard, the changes in V5 created a lot of frustration in many senses.<br /> <br /> In this particular thread, the main sore point is the lack of playability for the Sabbat, and it is a sore point for a lot of people. Some have been playing Sabbat for the last 29 years, which for many others is pretty much a lifetime.<br /> <br /> So it may not be such a big deal for you, but it is a huge deal for a lot of people that invested themselves emotionally in this game for almost three decades.<br /> <br /> And at this point I have to point something for you: when you try to tone down other's frustration and say that things aren't that bad, you sometimes sounds dismissive of the root causes of that frustration. You don't have the intent of hurt, but you cause it nonetheless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465932#post1465932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think we could keep a more friendly environment,</div> </div> </div> </div>The frustration and built up anger doesn't necessarily cause it to be an unfriendly environment, hence my sincere apologies for offending you. As far as I can tell, I pretty much enjoy discussing with many here even when I'm not so friendly towards their arguments.<br /> <br /> One last thing I would like to ask you is to put more spaces in your posts. They're frequently hard and slow to read, and sometimes I have to stop to avoid a headache. Break paragraphs more frequently and use double Enter between paragraphs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465934#post1465934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ventrues to me kind of need the drapes of the Toreador to have wide acceptance, otherwise they'll look like pure tyrants and dictators.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how the Ventrue strike me at all.<br /> <br /> Even La Croix tried as much as possible to seem like a reasonable person, and indeed avoided using Dominate as first option to convince even the Protagonist, an extremely fresh Neonate. And that because he had to play far harder as he was in an extremely bad situation.<br /> <br /> Ventrue are managers, organizers. They are negotiators. Their style is convincing people and helping them work as a group instead of bossing around unnecessarily.<br /> <br /> Now, they do need the Toreador to keep the social environment running smoothly. That part I pretty much agree. But Tyrants? I don't see them playing like that frequently if they can avoid at all, and they do have the means to avoid it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T16:08:03-07:00","id":1465946,"title":"","content":"Made a new thread for discussing the roles of individual Clans: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465949-world-building-how-do-you-use-certain-clans\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-certain-clans</a><br /> <br /> I think it'll be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-30-2021, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T22:36:10-07:00","id":1465971,"title":"","content":"After reading V5 I don't see how Ventrue isn't tyranical under the coating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T22:47:21-07:00","id":1465972,"title":"","content":"Well you've convinced me guys. The Lasombra are making the best of a crappy situation and have lost a lot. Conceded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T05:23:47-07:00","id":1465999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465911#post1465911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Auspex is just <i>strong </i>as a suplementary discipline. But thinking about it more deeply, it's primarly an investigative discipline, not a social one (though it is certainly very helpful with social cues, depending on the edition.) One physical discipline, one social discipline, and one mental discipline.<br /> In no particular order, here's some reasons why Ventrue&gt;Toreador socially.<br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that Auspex is more than a strong supplementary Discipline. It comes late, but Auspex 4 Telepathy is incredibly powerful. There is this quote &quot;<i>This is one of the most potent vampiric abilities, since, given time, a Kindred can learn virtually anything from a subject without him ever knowing.</i>&quot;<br /> Astral Projection is immensely useful for spying, and it allows the use of other Disciplines while active.<br /> I see the perspective that the level 1-3 powers are not that potent compared to the sheer usefulness of Dominate. However, there the fact that if a Vampire already has Presence for influencing the minds of others, then Dominate does not bring in that much. Thus having Auspex is better, especially once the potency of levels 4 and 5 is taken into account.<br /> Also, the Elder Powers of Auspex are distinctly better than those of Dominate in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T07:09:56-07:00","id":1466006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465941#post1465941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even La Croix tried as much as possible to seem like a reasonable person, and indeed avoided using Dominate as first option to convince even the Protagonist, an extremely fresh Neonate. And that because he had to play far harder as he was in an extremely bad situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's generally how I see the difference between the Ventrue and the other &quot;leader clans&quot; of V:tM. When a Ventrue wants someone to do something, they start off negotiating, then turn on Presence and only turn towards using Dominate as a last resort. Meanwhile with the Lasombra, Dominate is going to be the first choice, and if that doesn't work, then they'll try to use Obteneration to terrify the person into obedience or use Potence to make them comply through brute force. The Lasombra are more like bullies whereas the Ventrue tend to be more affable. Same thing with the Brujah - if their Presence doesn't work, out come the fists. The Ventrue have other options than physical violence and fear when it comes to getting others to do what they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T07:56:55-07:00","id":1466010,"title":"","content":"In the webcomic Strong Female Protagonist (about a supergirl-esque flying brick), the primary villain is a telepath. Not a mind-controller.<br /> <br /> He said something that I liked about the utility of being able to read minds, though, and why Auspex is the best Discipline for Toreador.<br /> <br /> &quot;If you can't control someone after knowing their every hidden desire and want then you aren't very smart.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T08:15:58-07:00","id":1466011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466010#post1466010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the webcomic Strong Female Protagonist (about a supergirl-esque flying brick), the primary villain is a telepath. Not a mind-controller.<br /> <br /> He said something that I liked about the utility of being able to read minds, though, and why Auspex is the best Discipline for Toreador.<br /> <br /> &quot;If you can't control someone after knowing their every hidden desire and want then you aren't very smart.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you also need to at least be able to pretend that you have the means to fulfill those desires? Come to think of it, Tremere probably can in a lot of cases. Although they can also control minds. Which makes to it easier for them to offer dreams. Also, it's funny that the Ministry like to do things that way without natural Auspex.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T08:17:15-07:00","id":1466012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466011#post1466011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you also need to at least be able to pretend that you have the means to fulfill those desires? Come to think of it, Tremere probably can in a lot of cases. Although they can also control minds. Which makes to it easier for them to offer dreams. Also, it's funny that the Ministry like to do things that way without natural Auspex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presence certainly helps the Toreador in their claims to fulfill your ever desire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yes, you'd think the Ministry would do better with Auspex than Obfuscate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T08:39:17-07:00","id":1466014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466012#post1466012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Presence certainly helps the Toreador in their claims to fulfill your ever desire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And it certainly helps when the tables are turned and it is the Toreador's every desire being taken into account <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466012#post1466012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yes, you'd think the Ministry would do better with Auspex than Obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disciplines are so very useful, but there's also the idea that nothing beats a well-planned, carefully performed deception, gaslighting, or temptation done through completely mundane means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T08:49:16-07:00","id":1466017,"title":"","content":"Resources 5 are the ultimate discipline, sphere of magic, gift, what have you. Syndicate had it right all along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T09:53:16-07:00","id":1466025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466017#post1466017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resources 5 are the ultimate discipline, sphere of magic, gift, what have you. Syndicate had it right all along.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that I use the standard \u201cbackgrounds increase through play not XP\u201d I found that I had to start imposing Resources costs whenever the PCs used it to solve problems like getting information or acquiring other backgrounds using it. And I let them know when what they want would ding their resources to acquire it.<br /> <br /> Ex. Resources 5 can let you pay a large personal security detail (effectively multiple retainers or the utterly broken Military Force background), but that\u2019s going to drop your Resources by one or more levels depending on the size because that\u2019s a brand new expense and you won\u2019t have that free cash available for other things until you figure out a way to increase your revenue.<br /> <br /> In some ways it feels like Resources needs an overhaul akin to how Havens and such have multiple sub-elements (size, security, luxury) so that it\u2019s not just \u201cI have Resources so I solve everything by throwing money at it\u201d (aka the Bruce Wayne/Tony Stark school of problem solving)\u2026 like properties, personnel and pretty cash with a system for shifting the categories around with time as you reinvest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T11:07:30-07:00","id":1466033,"title":"","content":"As we spin off various tangents:<br /> <br /> The CofD (though it charges XP for such things) has a pretty good system for keeping Resources in check. Items, and (very important to the point) services have an Availability rating. You need Resources &gt;= Availability + 2 to be able to basically freely afford something.without bumping into number of uses over time restrictions. Most average skilled professionals are an Availability 3 service for a single prearranged instance (+1 Availability to get one right away).<br /> <br /> So even at Resources 5, you can't just snap your fingers and make skilled people appear. Getting someone else a good bodyguard on short notice for a single event is going to eat up your normal purchasing power. Though you can easily take the time to arrange to pay for a few rent-a-cops through a standard security agency if you're not in a rush.<br /> <br /> This means that Backgrounds that represent specific individuals are more valuable to cultivate, as they're not taking away from your Resources purchasing power, and don't have the same issues like being on-call rather than needing to worry about complications if you need them now. Even without the XP factor, it helps balance things out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T13:04:51-07:00","id":1466045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1465999#post1465999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see the perspective that the level 1-3 powers are not that potent compared to the sheer usefulness of Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I disagree that even the first levels of Auspex are less potent.<br /> <br /> Information is a big advantage in any situation, and that's the first big thing Auspex gives you, the inherent versatility of information.<br /> <br /> Even at level 1 your ability at catching clues, hearing things, etc. increases and that's immensely useful, always. At level 2 you get to read auras, and that is far more useful on a variety of situations than reading minds, as you can screen several people with ease, for many bits of relevant information.<br /> <br /> The only power truly situational is the level 3 Spirit Touch, and even then it makes for a great way to get information through indirect sources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466011#post1466011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you also need to at least be able to pretend that you have the means to fulfill those desires? Come to think of it, Tremere probably can in a lot of cases. Although they can also control minds. Which makes to it easier for them to offer dreams. Also, it's funny that the Ministry like to do things that way without natural Auspex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing is already an advantage, especially when you can use it both to fulfill desires or to threat impeding them.<br /> <br /> On the Ministry, their thing is precisely less about knowing and more about getting things. They're brokers, they don't need to know what you want, you'll tell them yourself under the promise that they can deliver, no questions asked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466025#post1466025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In some ways it feels like Resources needs an overhaul akin to how Havens and such have multiple sub-elements (size, security, luxury) so that it\u2019s not just \u201cI have Resources so I solve everything by throwing money at it\u201d (aka the Bruce Wayne/Tony Stark school of problem solving)\u2026 like properties, personnel and pretty cash with a system for shifting the categories around with time as you reinvest.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> that CofD's take on it already addressed many of the issues (not only with Resources, by the way), As someone that works with economy and finances irl, the idea of breaking Resources that way does appeal to me. I'm not sure if it would be an interesting thing or not, but at least merits some attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T13:16:32-07:00","id":1466046,"title":"","content":"As far as my own gaming experience, Spirit's Touch has been hugely useful for campaigns with even moderate political/investigation, even occult mystery angles, it's a great power for getting even some basic context to work from in a &quot;what happened with this thing or this person?&quot; way if you can angle its use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T13:38:56-07:00","id":1466048,"title":"","content":"Sometimes it is just a starting point to make sense out of things. But starting points are extremely important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T17:00:28-07:00","id":1466063,"title":"","content":"\u200b&quot;The person who last held this keys was a man. Period.&quot;<br /> <br /> Spirit's Touch is only strong if you ST go full fluffy and ignore system rules. It need five successes before getting really useful information, with high difficulty if its not an object closely linked to the last owner.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T17:23:46-07:00","id":1466064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5#post1461282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/p7oJCPU.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Link: <a href=\"https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/2322-sabbattheblackhand\" target=\"_blank\">https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/...attheblackhand</a><br /> <br /> There is no Regent of the Sabbat and <b>it is controlled by a loose alliance of warring Cardinals.</b> <br /> <br /> No Sabbat remain on the Path of Humanity and<b> infighting is practically nonexistent.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for a good review, but this does not add up. How can you have warring cardinals when infihting is nonexistent?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T17:57:57-07:00","id":1466073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466064#post1466064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for a good review, but this does not add up. How can you have warring cardinals when infihting is nonexistent?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cardinals aren't warring with each other. They're engaged in constant battle with the sect's enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T18:01:47-07:00","id":1466074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466064#post1466064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for a good review, but this does not add up. How can you have warring cardinals when infihting is nonexistent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Best guess? These Cardinals are mostly getting ignored by the many Sabbat packs. Without widespread pack support, the war amounts to a couple of guys hurling insults at each other from different cities.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're excommunicated!&quot;<br /> &quot;No, YOU'RE excommunicated!&quot;<br /> &quot;Nuh-uh, YOU are!&quot;<br /> &quot;No way!:<br /> &quot;Yes, way!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T18:09:01-07:00","id":1466075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466074#post1466074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Best guess? These Cardinals are mostly getting ignored by the many Sabbat packs. Without widespread pack support, the war amounts to a couple of guys hurling insults at each other from different cities.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're excommunicated!&quot;<br /> &quot;No, YOU'RE excommunicated!&quot;<br /> &quot;Nuh-uh, YOU are!&quot;<br /> &quot;No way!:<br /> &quot;Yes, way!&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It was a poor choice of words on my part.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T18:21:12-07:00","id":1466076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466064#post1466064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for a good review, but this does not add up. How can you have warring cardinals when infihting is nonexistent?</div> </div> </div> </div>The book has a couple of internal contradictions like that, my personal favourite was the bit were they said the Sabbat doesn't hold territory and then went in a blow by blow of its how territories work and its desire to capture more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T18:28:28-07:00","id":1466077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466076#post1466076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The book has a couple of internal contradictions like that, my personal favourite was the bit were they said the Sabbat doesn't hold territory and then went in a blow by blow of its how territories work and its desire to capture more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I mean they've abandoned most of their territory but have a few but they should have emphasized how territory <i>doesn't matter.</i><br /> <br /> After all, you don't need domain if you just grab people off the street whenever you need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T18:40:31-07:00","id":1466078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466077#post1466077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I mean they've abandoned most of their territory but have a few but they should have emphasized how territory <i>doesn't matter.</i><br /> <br /> After all, you don't need domain if you just grab people off the street whenever you need.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was part of there back to basics mindset they tried to go for but doesn't really take into account cainite ecology or the logistics of jihad. <br /> There were a couple of other ones I recall &quot;ranks don't exist now here are the ranks.&quot; Is the one which stuck with me It occurs its something of a paradox trying to sell a minimalist approach to sect and then realising that it wouldnt work and this books supposes to be 40 quids worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-02-2021, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T18:50:43-07:00","id":1466079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466078#post1466078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it was part of there back to basics mindset they tried to go for but doesn't really take into account cainite ecology or the logistics of jihad.<br /> There were a couple of other ones I recall &quot;ranks don't exist now here are the ranks.&quot; Is the one which stuck with me It occurs its something of a paradox trying to sell a minimalist approach to sect and then realising that it would work and this books supposes to be 40 quids worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean what they're describing is a Sabbat in mid-evolution.<br /> <br /> They could have worked better with that, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Sections I feel that were missing:<br /> <br /> * Path rules<br /> * Loresheets<br /> * A much longer history for those who like lore<br /> * A discussion of the sabbat's breakdown in heirarchy to become almost entirely Loyalists<br /> * What happened to the Black Hand and Inquisition<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T19:03:52-07:00","id":1466081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466079#post1466079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean what they're describing is a Sabbat in mid-evolution.<br /> <br /> They could have worked better with that, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Sections I feel that were missing:<br /> <br /> * Path rules<br /> * Loresheets<br /> * A much longer history for those who like lore<br /> * A discussion of the sabbat's breakdown in heirarchy to become almost entirely Loyalists<br /> * What happened to the Black Hand and Inquisition<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Devolution really, but I'm getting snarky.<br /> <br /> If anything they should probably re-establish the infrastructure. On a practical level Johnny anarch and lady carmarilla wouldnt really see any practical difference between 2nd/3rd/20th Ed Sabbat and the modern one anyway. He's still just a lunatic with a machete and &quot;kill god&quot; carved into his forehead when push comes to shove.<br /> Yeah the book needed more crunch badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-31-2021, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T20:16:32-07:00","id":1466082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466063#post1466063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSpirit's Touch is only strong if you ST go full fluffy and ignore system rules. It need five successes before getting really useful information, with high difficulty if its not an object closely linked to the last owner.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're mistaking overwhelmingly broken with useful. If Spirit's Touch could give all the good information by grabbing anything the subject touched, it would be downright broken.<br /> <br /> It is on you to choose the object you're analyzing, so if you're trying it on random stuff it is indeed likely that you'll have consistently high dif and a bunch of useless information. But if you're careful with the object you want to use, then you're likely to have a reasonable or low dif and a context for whatever glimpse of information you get.<br /> <br /> Now, what may be true is that not all STs know how to handle Spirit's Touch. It's RAW can be read in many ways, so the ST may choose to simply be stingy with it, always erring on the side of high dif and choosing the most shitty information possible. I do like the V5 version in which it lets the player choose the information beforehand, but the perfect rendition to me is VtR 2nd ed's, where each success lets the user ask a question from a list to the ST.<br /> <br /> An ST that isn't a jerk, though, should know to measure the value of the information and err on the middle ground dif at least, 6 or 7.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466079#post1466079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean what they're describing is a Sabbat in mid-evolution.<br /> <br /> They could have worked better with that, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Sections I feel that were missing:<br /> <br /> * Path rules<br /> * Loresheets<br /> * A much longer history for those who like lore<br /> * A discussion of the sabbat's breakdown in heirarchy to become almost entirely Loyalists<br /> * What happened to the Black Hand and Inquisition</div> </div> </div> </div>Although it wouldn't solve the complains about the Sabbat losing nuance, it would certanly make for a more useful and interesting book, and those are badly needed information.<br /> <br /> Especially the Loresheets, if they still wanted to make it unplayable, they would at least be useful to play with its legacy elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T13:15:04-07:00","id":1466159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466045#post1466045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I disagree that even the first levels of Auspex are less potent.<br /> <br /> Information is a big advantage in any situation, and that's the first big thing Auspex gives you, the inherent versatility of information.<br /> <br /> Even at level 1 your ability at catching clues, hearing things, etc. increases and that's immensely useful, always. At level 2 you get to read auras, and that is far more useful on a variety of situations than reading minds, as you can screen several people with ease, for many bits of relevant information.<br /> <br /> The only power truly situational is the level 3 Spirit Touch, and even then it makes for a great way to get information through indirect sources.<br /> <br /> <br /> Knowing is already an advantage, especially when you can use it both to fulfill desires or to threat impeding them.<br /> <br /> On the Ministry, their thing is precisely less about knowing and more about getting things. They're brokers, they don't need to know what you want, you'll tell them yourself under the promise that they can deliver, no questions asked.<br /> <br /> <br /> While I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> that CofD's take on it already addressed many of the issues (not only with Resources, by the way), As someone that works with economy and finances irl, the idea of breaking Resources that way does appeal to me. I'm not sure if it would be an interesting thing or not, but at least merits some attention.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really like this view, because it made me realize an important point about some of the clans that seem like... they should be put away or get dunked, because they aren't dominating or martial. It kind of reminds me of CK3 too.<br /> <br /> But to be simple let's just use the Toreador example (and yeah Celerity can be an excellent Discipline to evade the martial Clans), for they surround themselves by those who like or are allured by them (Presence), and maybe everybody wonders if it is just the social charms or the Presence that make the Toreador so hard to hate, even when they are little bastards. <br /> <br /> Most importantly, Auspex... in a game where everyone has dirt, everyone, and if they don't have they have other weakness, retainers, touchstones.... To know this is to hold people in your hand. Will somebody try to attack your stuff if they know (or fear) that you know a good reason why the Prince or Sheriff should come knocking on their haven? Just the fear of the Auspex using Clans must be real, especially for the paranoid vamps.<br /> <br /> Malks, Toreadors, Hecata, Tremere.... they seem so many times protected from the threats of other Clans, especially the first two (Hecata and Tremere have their own history, twists, diableries and etc., but not entirely negligible). They must have very specific dirt on people (not as much as Nosferatus of course), and if they don't they don't dig dirt, they are great bodyguards and threat assessment agents, and seekers too. All of this make them dear or untouchable in big webs of politics, which is more predominant or clear in the Camarilla. <br /> <br /> And yeah, Auspex users can be great brokers and &quot;cutters&quot; (threatening or cutting off their desires as well, which I never thought about till now). Salubri are the Auspex users that got the less out of their discipline, given the situation of the Clan and its members, except if you believe &quot;it was their plan all along&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T13:27:59-07:00","id":1466160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466079#post1466079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean what they're describing is a Sabbat in mid-evolution.<br /> <br /> They could have worked better with that, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Sections I feel that were missing:<br /> <br /> * Path rules<br /> * Loresheets<br /> * A much longer history for those who like lore<br /> * A discussion of the sabbat's breakdown in heirarchy to become almost entirely Loyalists<br /> * What happened to the Black Hand and Inquisition<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would so love these sections... Gezus, I was itching for them when I read it. &quot;perhaps the archives are incomplete&quot; I thought.<br /> More history would be good, because the additions to the lore (like the talks about esbats) were very nice. It really made me see one more particle that in time made the Sabbat whole. Even if not in the book, this adds to the old lores. Like... Heresies, esbats, Lost Tribe, TalMaheRa, Anarchs... etc. <br /> <br /> More on what occurred with the Inquisition and Black Hand (even if it states &quot;before, the Black Hand was the top of the Sabbat, the elite; now, there is no bigger hand over the Sabbat, every pack is part of the bigger Hand&quot; or something to context the name questions). Not even some fiction with some little 'hey, hey, did you noticed that? did you get it?'. Besides, Inquisition would be awesome! Because they are the best Sabbat characters who might lend a hand to hunt down another Sabbat in a V5 setting; also, somebody gotta go around slapping and hunting Sabbats that are running from the Crusade or turning lax and holding territory and politicking instead of helping the Sect's war. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T14:19:16-07:00","id":1466169,"title":"","content":"The Loresheets alone would already help with snippets of lore, if they didn't wanted to dive into it.<br /> <br /> For me, the minimum amount of crunch would be a loresheet for each <i>Antitribu</i>, another for each faction and another for each Path. Even if they were all geared exclusively at ex-Sabbat Camarilla or Anarch. It would already be some official information, and would help contextualize things a lot better. And almost justify the price.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T14:29:14-07:00","id":1466171,"title":"","content":"Always found that the Sabbat Inquisition made the Black Hand redundant anyway. The player pack is there to either handle military stuff, or manipulate a more militant pack into doing the military stuff. The Inquisition is there to be The Man that the player characters have to worry about offending. I don't need two versions of The Man within the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T15:00:05-07:00","id":1466176,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Antitribu need individual loresheets (except maybe for those Ventrue knights), but loresheets for notable sabbat members would be pretty sweet. Descendant of Vykos? Descendant of Goratrix? Give some loresheets to clans other than the Hecata, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T15:27:58-07:00","id":1466180,"title":"","content":"At the very least for the <i>Antitribu</i> that have some distinction in either Disciplines and/or Weakness, but preferably for everyone even if based on individual members.<br /> <br /> Those Loresheets would help to ground how the Sabbat affects your view or station in your clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T15:54:52-07:00","id":1466190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466180#post1466180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very least for the <i>Antitribu</i> that have some distinction in either Disciplines and/or Weakness, but preferably for everyone even if based on individual members.<br /> <br /> Those Loresheets would help to ground how the Sabbat affects your view or station in your clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loresheets suffer the issue that they are a fun tax, Venture antis having a different discipline spread shouldn't cost points at character crea