additional Discipline you can purchase at Clan cost.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the loresheets I have seen so far, I would not count on it, though I haven't seen everything ofc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T16:02:10-07:00","id":1466193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466192#post1466192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given the loresheets I have seen so far, I would not count on it, though I haven't seen everything ofc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well we have NO loresheets for Sabbat canon so it wouldn't matter.<br /> <br /> I am curious to see what the Vault has already released, though, and if any of them are any good.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T16:15:23-07:00","id":1466198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466193#post1466193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well we have NO loresheets for Sabbat canon so it wouldn't matter.<br /> <br /> I am curious to see what the Vault has already released, though, and if any of them are any good.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Path of Enlightenment loresheets in &quot;Long Road Out Of Hell&quot; are outstanding.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T16:48:46-07:00","id":1466204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466190#post1466190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loresheets suffer the issue that they are a fun tax, Venture antis having a different discipline spread shouldn't cost points at character creation, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand, but they are the rule we have, and it is too simple to correct this. Even if it isn't corrected, since we're talking about what they should have done, it just makes sense to presume it would be in their own way. The system they have in place for this, good or bad, is the Loresheet. And it isn't a bad system <i>per se</i> even if not as well used as it could be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T20:10:16-07:00","id":1466218,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I forgot to put that out too. Loresheets were missing and it was a shame!... this is was really weird cuz I think not counting the Starter Pack and the Companion, all V5 books had Loresheets. I'm almost expecting a 2nd companion with Sabbat and Anarch or Independent content in there. Because, although not essential, some koldun sorcery would be very neat; and that is especailly true since we would be playing (according to the official availability) with the Old Clan Tzimisce, and not so much the antitribu part of the Clan (by V5 usage of antitribu). <br /> <br /> I also think Loresheets would be so much fun if they had Flaws too... but that's okay. Funny thing is, they gave an individual Clan overview in Camarilla and Anarch book, which I don't actually remember anything interesting beside Ipsissimus (but it seems like the beginning of an idea, not the entirety of it). But with antitribu, even if you're just gonna say how much they aren't like the Clan orthodoxy, and how they oppose it, even if it is just a little, before the indoctrination into a Path or the &quot;hivemind&quot;, it would've been swell. <br /> <br /> But it is too true, we are getting a ton of Hecata loresheets, very little of anything else. I know that it seems a Hecata game is basically a Hecata-only PC chronicle, so a lot of options is a great thing, but we have more than enough now. There is no Ravnos, Tzimisce or Salubri loresheet, and Lasombras have very little (one or two maybe?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T00:14:51-07:00","id":1466231,"title":"","content":"Even though the V5 changes made my own Tzimisce character far more mainstream where he had been a rare outlier in previous editions, I would like some information about the practices of the koldun to use with the new edition. Maybe some archtypical powers rendered as rituals the way The Lure of Flames was, but for controlling the weather or finding buried treasure on Walpurgis Night as in the novel <i>Dracula</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T03:29:46-07:00","id":1466241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466169#post1466169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Loresheets alone would already help with snippets of lore, if they didn't wanted to dive into it.<br /> <br /> For me, the minimum amount of crunch would be a loresheet for each <i>Antitribu</i>, another for each faction and another for each Path. Even if they were all geared exclusively at ex-Sabbat Camarilla or Anarch. It would already be some official information, and would help contextualize things a lot better. And almost justify the price.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really missed the cultural aspects of antitribu, especially as they seem to treat the paths as pseudo clans anyway. The lasombra and tzmisce being considered anti's was just outright silly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T03:35:30-07:00","id":1466242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466241#post1466241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really missed the cultural aspects of antitribu, especially as they seem to treat the paths as pseudo clans anyway. The lasombra and tzmisce being considered anti's was just outright silly</div> </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't they be? Bluntly, one thing that is good about V5 and absolutely a good idea is the removal of the Tzimisce and Lasombra from a privileged position in the sect. It's hard to believe the Antitribu would have tolerated it as long as they did anyway. Since neither of them killed their Antediluvian, it's also good to bring them down a peg in-universe.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I may be influenced by the fact I play a lot of Antitribu and consider it a badge of honor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T04:44:45-07:00","id":1466257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466242#post1466242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why wouldn't they be? Bluntly, one thing that is good about V5 and absolutely a good idea is the removal of the Tzimisce and Lasombra from a privileged position in the sect. It's hard to believe the Antitribu would have tolerated it as long as they did anyway. Since neither of them killed their Antediluvian, it's also good to bring them down a peg in-universe.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I may be influenced by the fact I play a lot of Antitribu and consider it a badge of honor.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's debatable but also not my point. My point is neither clan have much incentive to consider themselves anti, especially the Tzmisce who are still considered majority sabbat and the clans culture meshes very will with the sects<br /> I've always portrayed the Sabbat as more 'enlightened' when it comes to clan/bloodline heritage in that the institutions are there but its understood that some people will consciously choose to opt out. Especially as mass embraces will ensure some vampires are just a bad fit. Lasombra who arnt personally ambitious, toreador who are crude and stupid etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T04:50:14-07:00","id":1466258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466257#post1466257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's debatable but also not my point. My point is neither clan have much incentive to consider themselves anti, especially the Tzmisce who are still considered majority sabbat and the clans culture meshes very will with the sects<br /> I've always portrayed the Sabbat as more 'enlightened' when it comes to clan/bloodline heritage in that the institutions are there but its understood that some people will consciously choose to opt out. Especially as mass embraces will ensure some vampires are just a bad fit. Lasombra who arnt personally ambitious, toreador who are crude and stupid etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the existence of the Tzimisce Antediluvian is a good reason to consider them enemies of their Clan isn't it? I thought the reason that the two Clans considered themselves Clans was because they claimed to have destroyed their Antediluvians. Which is now known to be false in-universe. The reason the Antitribu is because they are against their founders.<br /> <br /> Or did I miss the reasoning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T05:20:11-07:00","id":1466264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466190#post1466190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Loresheets suffer the issue that they are a fun tax, Venture antis having a different discipline spread shouldn't cost points at character creation, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is why I wouldn't tie Loresheets to XP, but to story progression. But I am pretty liberal with the use of the V5 rule set. I didn't GM VTM since Cults of the Bloodgods released, but I would certainly allow different bloodlines/discipline spreads within the main clans, if there is a good reason for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27028,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","user":"Ignithas","date":". 11-02-2021, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T05:20:35-07:00","id":1466265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466258#post1466258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, the existence of the Tzimisce Antediluvian is a good reason to consider them enemies of their Clan isn't it? I thought the reason that the two Clans considered themselves Clans was because they claimed to have destroyed their Antediluvians. Which is now known to be false in-universe. The reason the Antitribu is because they are against their founders.<br /> <br /> Or did I miss the reasoning?</div> </div> </div> </div>The eldest doesn't appear to care either way. definitions of clans are tricky. Ventrue and set are known to be dead so nobody really knows what they want in terms of clan legitimacy. Personally I've always gone with an aggressive rejection of standard clan values hence why sabbat salubri are antitribu despite outnumbering the clan at leady 20:1. The tzmisce and to a lesser degree the lasombra don't really have this issue since the Sabbat ideology synergies with there's very well, largely because they're the ones who shaped it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T05:37:23-07:00","id":1466268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466265#post1466265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The eldest doesn't appear to care either way. definitions of clans are tricky. Ventrue and set are known to be dead so nobody really knows what they want in terms of clan legitimacy. Personally I've always gone with an aggressive rejection of standard clan values hence why sabbat salubri are antitribu despite outnumbering the clan at leady 20:1. The tzmisce and to a lesser degree the lasombra don't really have this issue since the Sabbat ideology synergies with there's very well, largely because they're the ones who shaped it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is definitely a reason why they would be Clans and not Antribu. Still, of changes I had the least problem there because the book emphasizes the Sabbat antitribu is explictly due to the hatred of the Antes.<br /> <br /> It depends really how much you consider that to be THE purpose of the Sabbat to oppose them in all things, I suppose.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T06:39:43-07:00","id":1466279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466258#post1466258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, the existence of the Tzimisce Antediluvian is a good reason to consider them enemies of their Clan isn't it? I thought the reason that the two Clans considered themselves Clans was because they claimed to have destroyed their Antediluvians. Which is now known to be false in-universe. The reason the Antitribu is because they are against their founders.<br /> <br /> Or did I miss the reasoning?</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's a bit complicated. At least as per the Revised Guide to the Sabbat, the antitribu were the vampires who had turned their backs on their clans, but this was a conscious political decision rather than an absolute objective definition and it's a label some groups chose to take or chose to reject. Take for example the Salubri antitribu.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revised Guide to the Sabbat page 28</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the Sabbat seems like a strange place for those who take offense at the destruction of Elders (at least to other Sabbat) the Salubri antitribu seem to regard the sect's larger philosophy with only lip service. In their minds, their allegiance with the sect begins and ends with the war on the Camarilla. In the tradition of the antitribu, the Sabbat Salubri have turned utterly away from the &quot;clan&quot; that spawned them, regarding their progenitors with antipathy for what they consider weakness and fatalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Salubri Sabbat considered themselves antitribu and called themselves antitribu. But they were not trying to kill their Antediluvian as he was widely believed to already be dead (in fact that was the reason they were part of the Sabbat, because the Camarilla had given the Tremere the de facto okay to Blood Hunt the Salubri). They called themselves antitribu because they had turned their backs on the peaceful philosophy that was the predominant concept to their Clan.<br /> <br /> So note that in this case, the Salubri antitribu weren't out to kill Saulot. He was dead and if anything they were out to take vengeance for him. The Salubri antitribu don't even hate or try to kill regular Salubri. They pity them and view them as weaklings and cowards, but they don't necessarily want to wipe them out. If anything they want to take vengeance for their deaths at the hands of the Tremere. So for them, they considered themselves antitribu because of the way their goals and actions went against the more typical clan beliefs of fatalism and pacifism, not because they were opposed to Saulot.<br /> <br /> We can also take a look at the Serpents of Light who were, defacto antitribu. They rejected the clan, they wanted to kill Set, by any definition they <i>are</i> antitribu, but they reject the label and don't call themselves antitribu. Instead they tended to consider themselves almost more like a new Clan, choosing to completely cut their ties with their forebearers and instead and create a new identity for themselves rather than call themselves &quot;Followers of Set antitribu&quot; because fuck Set (and also it's kind of a mouthful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).<br /> <br /> And of course, you had the Lasombra in the Camarilla who called themselves antitribu because they recognized that the Sabbat Lasombra had functionally taken control of the Clan's identity, and so they wore the &quot;anti-tribe&quot; badge as one to vocally and clearly note their rejection of the Sabbat Lasombra - which was an important political distinction to make in Camarilla society. After all, you don't want people getting confused over where your loyalties lay, so you call yourself a Lasombra antitribu so that the other Camarilla guys go, &quot;Oh he's antitribu. He's okay, he's one of <i>our</i> Lasombra.&quot;<br /> <br /> Note that they absolutely did not call themselves &quot;Lasombra antitribu&quot; because they opposed their Antediluvian. That had nothing to do with why they called themselves antitribu. It was simply a political label they used to draw a clear distinction between themselves and the Lasombra in the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> So who is antitribu and who is not and why they call themselves that or choose not to call themselves antitribu is a pretty complicated topic and there's no definite, absolute rule. Ultimately if a group considers themselves antitribu then they recognize that they form an off-shoot of the &quot;main&quot; clan and oppose it in some way, whether that opposition is philosophical or physical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-02-2021, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T06:43:55-07:00","id":1466280,"title":"","content":"Very true.<br /> <br /> Oddly, I suppose the Tzimisce and Lasombra becoming Antitribu as a fig-leaf toward parity with the other Antitribu strikes me as a change that is actually justifiable in-universe. Ir's not one of the changes that I think actually harms the sect and makes sense in-universe.<br /> <br /> But I can see why people feel its a change for change's sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T07:27:36-07:00","id":1466281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466257#post1466257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's debatable but also not my point. My point is neither clan have much incentive to consider themselves anti, especially the Tzmisce who are still considered majority sabbat and the clans culture meshes very will with the sects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that true tho? I belive it was said all of the Tzimisce fledglings and neonates were Anarch and most of the Ancilla and Elders were Autarkis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T10:02:08-07:00","id":1466294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466280#post1466280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very true.<br /> <br /> Oddly, I suppose the Tzimisce and Lasombra becoming Antitribu as a fig-leaf toward parity with the other Antitribu strikes me as a change that is actually justifiable in-universe. Ir's not one of the changes that I think actually harms the sect and makes sense in-universe.<br /> <br /> But I can see why people feel its a change for change's sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>The change in name is a meh, the utter obliteration of the Sabbat as anything but orcs is the main issue <br /> <br /> I just wish..well honestly that they had let the setting die, rather than this, because no matter the claims it is impossible to get a pre V5 game now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T10:27:23-07:00","id":1466296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466294#post1466294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The change in name is a meh, the utter obliteration of the Sabbat as anything but orcs is the main issue<br /> <br /> I just wish..well honestly that they had let the setting die, rather than this, because no matter the claims it is impossible to get a pre V5 game now</div> </div> </div> </div>You can always do a home game, friend.<br /> <br /> I really recommend the Storyteller's Vault alternatives to canon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T10:28:23-07:00","id":1466297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466281#post1466281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that true tho? I belive it was said all of the Tzimisce fledglings and neonates were Anarch and most of the Ancilla and Elders were Autarkis</div> </div> </div> </div>It's metaphorically true because there are no Tzimisce or Lasombra in the Sabbat anymore. Just Tzimisce and Lasombra antitribu. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T11:07:06-07:00","id":1466301,"title":"","content":"I never liked the <i>Antitribu</i> label because I never liked to see the clans as tightly united politically to begin with. They are families, not political parties. I very much prefer VtR's take on not equating clan to Covenant, and that was my stance since the beginning of VtM.<br /> <br /> So for me at least the new labeling process make more sense, with the word <i>Antitribu</i> effectively becoming a Sabbat moniker to highlight that now you live in a sect where your clan isn't politically important. You're <i>Antitribu</i> because you don't pay allegiance to your clan in any form, not even within your sect.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> does have a very good point on what it meant back them. Not one definition that I like that much, but certainly a definition that existed already and made sense for its adherents.<br /> <br /> What do they do, now? Do the old Lasombra <i>Antitribu</i> really simply dropped the moniker and see as kin the people that just last week was hunting them and shitting on their way of life? Do the Salubri <i>Antitribu</i> agree with all this nonsense, or did they left the Sabbat <i>en masse</i> as their point was always pretty much about kinship? The Serpents of Light will be required to call themselves <i>Antitribu </i>despite being the whole of the bloodline (if they're still on the Sabbt)?<br /> <br /> For me it is a better use of the term, OoC it <b>is</b> change for change's sake. But above all that, names are socially and politically significant. IC it can't simply change out of nothing and have no impact. I don't see everyone agreeing, either. At the very least we should see all over the place people arguing over those things and taking stances. And I for one <b>don't</b> think the old Lasombra <i>Antitribu</i> will want to be seen as the same as the defectors.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat's Tzimisce, though, if this movement was forwarded as sect agenda, I pretty much see much of them answering more to the lines of <i>&quot;yeah, sure, whatever&quot;</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T11:31:47-07:00","id":1466305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466296#post1466296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can always do a home game, friend.<br /> <br /> I really recommend the Storyteller's Vault alternatives to canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly not, the only RPers I know in real life don't care about the WoD, and as I live in a small town, online is the other option, that brings up the point that online games are usually RAW, which makes the Vault a moot point. But this is just an old grognard tilting at windmills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T11:40:48-07:00","id":1466306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466305#post1466305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sadly not, the only RPers I know in real life don't care about the WoD, and as I live in a small town, online is the other option, that brings up the point that online games are usually RAW, which makes the Vault a moot point. But this is just an old grognard tilting at windmills.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're not the only person who observes this kind of thing, for what it's worth.<br /> <br /> For a considerable number of people, especially as time rolls along, online gaming is their only viable option, and when that basically mostly means various groups of strangers trying to arrange into a game, the easiest and default way of doing that is almost always going to be the most recent version of a game, and its most straightforward reading.<br /> <br /> It's why &quot;well then you can run&quot; or &quot;well then just ask for X, Y, Z house rule&quot; always feels so disingenuous/dismissive as far as what boils down to saying &quot;well then always be the ST and never play&quot;. And if you wanted to play? And if you don't really have a temperament for STing? And if the idea of having to basically always lobby whatever group you try to join to make changes that make a game experience more playable for you more or less turns the whole thing into a chore just to play a game you like? Well sucks to be you, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-02-2021, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T12:00:18-07:00","id":1466310,"title":"","content":"A thought occurs that remaining Sabbat lasombra will probably overtake carmarilla lasombra in terms of numbers quite quickly considering Sabbat vs Carmarilla embracing policies. It's unlikely the lasombra will get much permission to embrace in the ivory tower so that unless attrition keeps them down the Sabbat is probably going to eventually be the de facto keeper clan again.<br /> <br /> Could provide an easy handwave after the tepid and embarissing lasombra defection of v5 .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T13:00:44-07:00","id":1466317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466310#post1466310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thought occurs that remaining Sabbat lasombra will probably overtake carmarilla lasombra in terms of numbers quite quickly considering Sabbat vs Carmarilla embracing policies. It's unlikely the lasombra will get much permission to embrace in the ivory tower so that unless attrition keeps them down the Sabbat is probably going to eventually be the de facto keeper clan again.<br /> <br /> Could provide an easy handwave after the tepid and embarissing lasombra defection of v5 .</div> </div> </div> </div>It would still be Antitribu and not the actual Lasombra. They're set against the Lasombra Antediluvian and he's returned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466306#post1466306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You're not the only person who observes this kind of thing, for what it's worth.<br /> <br /> For a considerable number of people, especially as time rolls along, online gaming is their only viable option, and when that basically mostly means various groups of strangers trying to arrange into a game, the easiest and default way of doing that is almost always going to be the most recent version of a game, and its most straightforward reading.<br /> <br /> It's why &quot;well then you can run&quot; or &quot;well then just ask for X, Y, Z house rule&quot; always feels so disingenuous/dismissive as far as what boils down to saying &quot;well then always be the ST and never play&quot;. And if you wanted to play? And if you don't really have a temperament for STing? And if the idea of having to basically always lobby whatever group you try to join to make changes that make a game experience more playable for you more or less turns the whole thing into a chore just to play a game you like? Well sucks to be you, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also a response to, &quot;I would rather there be no new edition at all.&quot;<br /> <br /> I am not pleased with the Sabbat's depiction from a player standpoint. I'm glad they've updated the Sabbat but I was hoping they would have given a lot more information from a player, ex-Sabbat, and Gehenna War perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-02-2021, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T13:17:48-07:00","id":1466318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466317#post1466317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would still be Antitribu and not the actual Lasombra. They're set against the Lasombra Antediluvian and he's returned.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's also a response to, &quot;I would rather there be no new edition at all.&quot;<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't really what antitribu are as we've explored earlier. Furthermore their isn't any actual indication la-som-bara actually wants the clan to join the carmarilla or even views them as anything more than dinner and this in turn works on the presumption it was lasombra they met and not just some 4th gen nightmare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-02-2021, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T13:24:38-07:00","id":1466319,"title":"","content":"Based on past treatment I assume Montano (and likely his loyal progeny) could be considered safely off the dinner menu. Joining the sect that he's been a member of for half a millennium and reconciling with him wouldn't be the most foolish steps to take from a <i>now</i>-what-do-we-do-about-the-King-of-Shadows? perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T13:27:49-07:00","id":1466320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also a response to, &quot;I would rather there be no new edition at all.&quot;<br /> <br /> I am not pleased with the Sabbat's depiction from a player standpoint. I'm glad they've updated the Sabbat but I was hoping they would have given a lot more information from a player, ex-Sabbat, and Gehenna War perspective. </div> </div> </div>As far as it goes, when an edition comes along and goes &quot;of the three previously major playable groups that were playable right until 2018 or so, one of them is now the assumed default, and referred to in almost heroic terms for being so. Of the other two, one of them is having their entire thematics and play emphasis changed to a point of almost unrecognizability from what was being done with it until 2018 or so, will overall come off as incompetently evil, there will be repeated off hand developer and writer comments that playing them in previous ways was mistaken incorrect gaming and almost made you morally bad as a person to want to play them as you did. And as far as the remaining group of those three, they will not be officially supported as playable going forward. At all. And largely rumbled anyway. Also the overall game mechanics will basically be meant for a particular type of playstyle that we wanted to emphasize over others and at times said mechanics feel like they actively fight the idea of being used any other way.&quot; The people put off by that don't really have a new edition to play anyway, y'know?<br /> <br /> I mean, for anyone who really likes Anarchs and is really into a usually low level, night to night life, street level game generally focused on hunger, I imagine V5 is awesome. And for people who have never experienced really Vampire before 2018 (and remember, that's still 3 years ago) and don't really have any notion of VtM being capable of being any different anyway, I'm sure that's perfectly fine too. And certainly from the way most people who visibly talk about liking this version of the game talk about it, as far as what they actually praise about it, and the like, that is indeed what they're into. And that's entirely fine for what it is.<br /> <br /> Anyone outside of that framework doesn't really have a place in this edition (and it feels thin when people act like they do anyway). And that sucks, at least for those people.<br /> <br /> I'm not myself saying I'd rather there be no game going forwards, certainly. I am noting that for a chunk of people, there basically is no game going forwards anyway as far as getting to have some part of it, and that's not great. That might be bumming them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-02-2021, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T13:48:32-07:00","id":1466322,"title":"","content":"I never liked the GOT YA, with the lasombra antediluvian being not dead. And here's why. I prefer my Antediluvians to be able to foiled due to being insane alien monsters full of hubris. Example.<br /> <br /> Lasombra: Yes Gratiano kill my mortal form so I might fully become one with abyss and become a god! wait..what do you mean the abyss is way older then me..more powerful and just consumes me into being one with it...noooooo<br /> <br /> Salout: Yes Tremere Diablerize me so I might make a new clan for me for when I become Demon Emperor! wait...who else is in here...OH COME ON<br /> <br /> Tzimisce: Spoiler...im becoming a virus!<br /> <br /> Malkav: THATS MY THING TZIMISCE!<br /> <br /> Cappadcious: Pfft yo Augustus kill me so I can become a wraith and then take over god's throne...wait whats a Maelstrom? <br /> <br /> Brujah: Jokes on all of you...I just went to future times so I can see flying cars!<br /> <br /> Remember, even Cthulhu was beaten by a boat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T13:53:24-07:00","id":1466323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466319#post1466319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on past treatment I assume Montano (and likely his loyal progeny) could be considered safely off the dinner menu. Joining the sect that he's been a member of for half a millennium and reconciling with him wouldn't be the most foolish steps to take from a <i>now</i>-what-do-we-do-about-the-King-of-Shadows? perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plausible but unlikely, he hasn't lifted a finger as the antitribu camarilla got slaughtered over 700 years and pretty much all gehenna prophecies don't have a &quot;except the ones I like&quot; clause. Plus lasombra is genrally depicted as an asshole even by 3rd gem standards","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T13:55:08-07:00","id":1466324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466322#post1466322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never liked the GOT YA, with the lasombra antediluvian being not dead. And here's why. I prefer my Antediluvians to be able to foiled due to being insane alien monsters full of hubris. Example.<br /> <br /> Lasombra: Yes Gratiano kill my mortal form so I might fully become one with abyss and become a god! wait..what do you mean the abyss is way older then me..more powerful and just consumes me into being one with it...noooooo<br /> <br /> Salout: Yes Tremere Diablerize me so I might make a new clan for me for when I become Demon Emperor! wait...who else is in here...OH COME ON<br /> <br /> Tzimisce: Spoiler...im becoming a virus!<br /> <br /> Malkav: THATS MY THING TZIMISCE!<br /> <br /> Cappadcious: Pfft yo Augustus kill me so I can become a wraith and then take over god's throne...wait whats a Maelstrom? <br /> <br /> Brujah: Jokes on all of you...I just went to future times so I can see flying cars!<br /> <br /> Remember, even Cthulhu was beaten by a boat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well stunned technically but I get your point. Inevitable invincible 3rd gen are boring for the same reason ur shulgi is-no stakes and no tensio.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T13:55:47-07:00","id":1466325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Brujah: Jokes on all of you...I just went to future times so I can see flying cars! </div> </div> </div>I am 1000% on board with Brujah being the guy from the Key and Peele Sexy Vampires skit.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T13:58:54-07:00","id":1466326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466322#post1466322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malkav: THATS MY THING TZIMISCE!</div> </div> </div> </div>My headcanon is that Malkav is the only Ante who genuinely pulled off an immortality by becoming the Madness Network. But, there is no &quot;Malkav&quot; anymore. It's not an entity you can talk to or interact with, it doesn't control any of its childer or flash cool disciplines. Clan Malkavian in aggregate is Malkav the way cells in aggregate are a human being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T14:04:15-07:00","id":1466327,"title":"","content":"I don't think Antes really play that kind of role in politics one way or another, so their being alive or not is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> To me it makes sense for the Sabbat to forward the <i>Antitribu</i> moniker as meaning you don't have loyalty to your clan. That's it. Saying it has to do with the Ante still existing? It never had anything to do with it and it doesn't make sense. This is a statement to your clan, not to your Ante.<br /> <br /> A bunch of clans either think their Ante is already dead or don't care one way or the other. The Ventrue and Salubri <i>Antitribu</i> don't call themselves like that to piss off dead people. Ennoya and Absimiliard couldn't care less, as one is indifferent and the other is an enemy to his clan anyway. Arikel and Malkav aren't supposed to be great leaders of their clan, at most an inspiration.<br /> <br /> Only Haqim and Set are really all that into being the overlords of their clans, at least from the PoV of their descendants. They're pretty much the only ones that could feel offended by the whole <i>Antitribu</i> thing. None other. No Ante cares. <b>The clans care</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T14:07:28-07:00","id":1466328,"title":"","content":"I mean in Gehenna the book<br /> <br /> Set: Why did you call me back from Duat...you all arent worthy of my blood! :<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />roceeds to eat his entire clan<br /> <br /> Haqim: OH YOU ARE ALL SO UNWORTHY! &quot;&quot;proceeds to turn into a sandstorm to hunt down and kill his entire clan::","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T14:11:49-07:00","id":1466329,"title":"","content":"As a side I've always tried to 'run' 3rd gen as having differing personalities and agendas. With some of them outright dead my thoughts on Toreador is she's borderline almost pleasent for example especially in comparison to Tzmisce.<br /> Another point I made was that a lot of them have agendas which don't really relate to their clans such as sets desire to become the new apothis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T14:15:18-07:00","id":1466330,"title":"","content":"out of all the Antediluvians, Toreador got like the least amount of materiel beyond &quot;was a bull dancer&quot; &quot;was real pretty&quot; &quot;might have dated Nosferatu but eww&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T14:21:51-07:00","id":1466331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466330#post1466330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">out of all the Antediluvians, Toreador got like the least amount of materiel beyond &quot;was a bull dancer&quot; &quot;was real pretty&quot; &quot;might have dated Nosferatu but eww&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I heard she killed herself rather than degenerate into a complete horror like her siblings. I can't remember were but I like the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T14:24:44-07:00","id":1466332,"title":"","content":"My take is actually that Gehenna is as much a losing situation for the Antes as it is for their descendants, and so many of them already get out of this game. Power is good, but protect one's own Ego and getting rid of problematic needs like low-gen blood takes precedence. So they're actively trying to NOT be blood-sucking heralds of the end of the world.<br /> <br /> That also means any Ante is either limited by the effects of their Transcendence, by being in the process of achieving it yet, or by being a dumb loser that actually turned into what their childer fear.<br /> <br /> Cappadocius turned into a Wraith to diablerize God. If he achieved it, he's for all purposes Ego-dead. If not, he found whatever else to do as a happy ghost.<br /> <br /> Lasombra is a big jerk, mustache-twirling villain, an pretty much trying to eat an energy field bigger than his head. Anyone can see from a long way that his plan is stupid. He's either Ego-dead, dead-dead, enslaved, or simply failed and is a &quot;common&quot; vampire again, powerful as may be, ready to fulfill his role in the Gehenna prophecy and maybe enter Wassail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T14:43:00-07:00","id":1466333,"title":"","content":"I always thought Dirty Secrets of the Black hand was a silly book with the idea that Timisce now is a clan of super-alien HIV vampires infested by Chtulu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T15:09:52-07:00","id":1466343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466332#post1466332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lasombra is a big jerk, mustache-twirling villain, an pretty much trying to eat an energy field bigger than his head. Anyone can see from a long way that his plan is stupid. He's either Ego-dead, dead-dead, enslaved, or simply failed and is a &quot;common&quot; vampire again, powerful as may be, ready to fulfill his role in the Gehenna prophecy and maybe enter Wassail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, have you considered how delicious an energy field larger than your head might look? Who among us can say they haven't had a hankering for such things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T15:22:16-07:00","id":1466347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466343#post1466343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, have you considered how delicious an energy field larger than your head might look? Who among us can say they haven't had a hankering for such things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just imagined a barely-transformed Lasombra cursed with a new weakness. Instead of the mirror/camera thing, he have eternal stomachache.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T15:27:01-07:00","id":1466348,"title":"","content":"And so every Lasombra, when using Obtenebration, swears sometimes to themselves in moments they dare not speak of aloud, that they can almost hear echoing from within the shadows a sort of whinging groan. &quot;... it was worth it I tell you! like chocolate but better! oh god bring me all the antacids on Earth you stupid minions....&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T15:36:34-07:00","id":1466349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466280#post1466280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very true.<br /> <br /> Oddly, I suppose the Tzimisce and Lasombra becoming Antitribu as a fig-leaf toward parity with the other Antitribu strikes me as a change that is actually justifiable in-universe. Ir's not one of the changes that I think actually harms the sect and makes sense in-universe.<br /> <br /> But I can see why people feel its a change for change's sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just have a really hard time seeing it. For the Sabbat in the Lasombra to don on the antitribu label would mean that they accept that their position as author of their clan has slipped from their fingers. That functionally they're the losers, big losers, and now the fate of Clan Lasombra lays with the Camarilla, at least for the foreseeable future. I just can't see the Lasombra being willing to admit that they failed and lost everything they spent the last 700 centuries building and working towards. Now that could be true from an objective viewpoint, but I just can't see them embracing that.<br /> <br /> For me the most likely scenario is that the Sabbat Lasombra insist that they're the &quot;real&quot; Lasombra and that they're ones who control the destiny of the clan. And that all of the traitors who ran off to join the ranks of the Lasombra antitribu in the Camarilla are now also Lasombra antitribu. And then the turncoat Lasombra new to the Camarilla would insist that no, they're the &quot;real&quot; Lasombra and it's the Sabbat who are now the antitribu due to the fact that the Camarilla Lasombra have the most bodies and and that therefore the Camarilla Lasombra are now the &quot;main branch&quot; of the clan.<br /> <br /> Funny enough I would expect that the only Lasombra who would choose to call themselves antitribu would be the old-school Lasombra antitribu who were always a part of the Camarilla and never a part of the Sabbat. While 5e gives us a sort of &quot;Kumbaya&quot; view in which the ex-Sabbat Lasombra are largely accepted by the Camarilla, in reality they would face a lot of weariness and even discrimination from members of the Camarilla who might not be willing to let bye-gones be by-gone or, at the least, have a tough time entirely trusting their backs to some guy who spent the last couple of hundred years on a Path drinking other vampires souls and trying to destroy the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> So the actual Lasombra antitribu, the ones who have always been part of the Camarilla, might find it useful to keep that distinction in order to draw a line between themselves (who have spent centuries proving their loyalty to the Camarilla) and the newcomers who only just joined up a few months ago. So they'd call themselves antitribu and you'd have other Camarilla vampires calling them that (&quot;What? You think Fred can't be trusted because he's a Lasombra and that means he's ex-Sabbat? No no, Fred's one of them antitribu Lasombra. He's been part of the Camarilla since he was embraced 90 years ago. He's not some monster.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Something would be fairly similar with the Tzimisci which has never really had an antitribu group and I really can't see the Sabbat Tzimisci being willing to gracefully accept the fact that they are no longer in control of the future of their clan either. People might call Tzimisci Sabbat &quot;antitribu&quot; but I can't see them calling themselves that.<br /> <br /> I think ultimately this is just goes towards v5's desire to simplify things and having the Lasombra fight over who is and isn't antitribu is felt to be too complicated, so the authors decided to just make all of the Sabbat clans antitribu in order to make a clearer distinction between the factions.<br /> <br /> * Edit* Out of curiosity, as I haven't read the new Sabbat book, are the Serpents of Light now called &quot;antitribu&quot; or do they at least keep their non-antitribu label? Because rejecting the label of antitribu entirely was a pretty important part of their identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-02-2021, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T16:34:44-07:00","id":1466352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466349#post1466349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny enough I would expect that the only Lasombra who would choose to call themselves antitribu would be the old-school Lasombra antitribu who were always a part of the Camarilla and never a part of the Sabbat. While 5e gives us a sort of &quot;Kumbaya&quot; view in which the ex-Sabbat Lasombra are largely accepted by the Camarilla, in reality they would face a lot of weariness and even discrimination from members of the Camarilla who might not be willing to let bye-gones be by-gone or, at the least, have a tough time entirely trusting their backs to some guy who spent the last couple of hundred years on a Path drinking other vampires souls and trying to destroy the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> So the actual Lasombra antitribu, the ones who have always been part of the Camarilla, might find it useful to keep that distinction in order to draw a line between themselves (who have spent centuries proving their loyalty to the Camarilla) and the newcomers who only just joined up a few months ago. So they'd call themselves antitribu and you'd have other Camarilla vampires calling them that (&quot;What? You think Fred can't be trusted because he's a Lasombra and that means he's ex-Sabbat? No no, Fred's one of them antitribu Lasombra. He's been part of the Camarilla since he was embraced 90 years ago. He's not some monster.&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely my take. The Sabbat Lasombra wouldn't call themselves <i>Antitribu</i> unless they're really weakened to the point of bowing to the will of others, and the old-school <i>Antitribu</i> are the ones that really pride themselves in the moniker.<br /> <br /> To me the defector are called exactly that: the Lasombra <i>Defectors</i>. And no <i>Antitribu</i> will accept to be confused with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T16:55:13-07:00","id":1466353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466352#post1466352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Precisely my take. The Sabbat Lasombra wouldn't call themselves <i>Antitribu</i> unless they're really weakened to the point of bowing to the will of others, and the old-school <i>Antitribu</i> are the ones that really pride themselves in the moniker.<br /> <br /> To me the defector are called exactly that: the Lasombra <i>Defectors</i>. And no <i>Antitribu</i> will accept to be confused with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing abiout SABBAT: THE BLACK HAND is that it actually does have a lot of really fascinating and interesting ideas for Sabbat culture that are worth talking about. Unfortunately, they've been overshadowed by the larger controversy of them being regulated to being an antagonist sect. It kind of makes discussing the intricacies of it all hard as the antagonist only element is the 800 lb gorilla in the room. This isn't me dismissing the element as you're not going to be able to have much opportunity tio discuss these intricacies with a Sabbat trying to diablerize you.<br /> <br /> However, getting back on topic (SHOCK - I am terrible at this), <b>The Paths replacing Clan</b> is something that I actually really like and am glad that the Sabbat are going for. In a way, the Lasombra and Tzimisce ANtitribu elements don't really matter because the &quot;New&quot; Sabbat are a group that is fully molding into a single post-clan sect. Being Lasombra as a concept no longer will matter in the Sabbat because all of the traditional Lasombra power structures, cultures, and beliefs will cease to exist.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra who actually CARE about being Lasombra and their 13,000 year heritage dating back to Enoch are the people who have moved over to the Camarilla. The Lasombra who were actually in charge of maintaining their traditional Clan based structure are explictly the ones who were the first to leave--perhaps noting that the Anti-Clan fervor that was part of the Gehenna War would ultimately destroy what kept the Lasombra unique.<br /> <br /> The funny thing is this has happened before in the sect. The Assamite Antitribu almost entirely left the Sabbat and rejoined the mainstream clan when Ur-Shulgi broke the Tremere Curse.<br /> <br /> The stronger identity of the Sabbat are the Paths of Cathari, Death and Soul, and other ideologies. So it goes:<br /> <br /> 1. Sabbat<br /> 2. Path<br /> 3. Clan<br /> <br /> In importance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T16:58:39-07:00","id":1466354,"title":"","content":"So, apart from the discussions the thread has had going on, I wanted to know if some basic realities of the Sabbat are adequately explained/explored in this book: <br /> <br /> 1) What is the Gehenna War? Materially speaking? Who are the Sabbat fighting, exactly? Why? Why does the Camarilla/Anarch not also do anything about these enemies? <br /> <br /> 2) How does cyclical Gehenna work? When was the last Gehenna before this? Was there one before that? How did it start, and why does it happen? <br /> <br /> 3) (The bit about the Sabbat that never made sense to me) How does the Sabbat's modus operandi of Mass Embraces and flouting the Masquerade to embrace their inner Beast work, especially in a post-SI world? Is that addressed at all? <br /> <br /> Some, or all, of these have probably been covered, but it's a 60-page thread, so I hope it's alright to ask them again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/480-blind-dragon","name":"Blind Dragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T17:05:48-07:00","id":1466355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blind Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466354#post1466354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, apart from the discussions the thread has had going on, I wanted to know if some basic realities of the Sabbat are adequately explained/explored in this book:<br /> <br /> 1) What is the Gehenna War? Materially speaking? Who are the Sabbat fighting, exactly? Why? Why does the Camarilla/Anarch not also do anything about these enemies?<br /> <br /> 2) How does cyclical Gehenna work? When was the last Gehenna before this? Was there one before that? How did it start, and why does it happen?<br /> <br /> 3) (The bit about the Sabbat that never made sense to me) How does the Sabbat's modus operandi of Mass Embraces and flouting the Masquerade to embrace their inner Beast work, especially in a post-SI world? Is that addressed at all?<br /> <br /> Some, or all, of these have probably been covered, but it's a 60-page thread, so I hope it's alright to ask them again.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. <b>The Gehenna War is absolutely nothing different</b>: Justin Achill basically says that it was misinterpred as some great mass migration of the Sabbat to fight Ancients. However, it's actually them fighting the exact same war they were always fighting. They just added the Ashirra to the list of people they want to murder.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Cynical Gehenna</b>: This isn't detailed here but in LA by Night, Jason Carl had Beckett explain it as &quot;The Antediluvians awaken, eat their progeny, Embrace new ones, and go back to sleep.&quot;<br /> <br /> 3. <b>How does their violation of the Masquerade work</b>? According to the book? Shitily. SABBAT: THE BLACK HAND says the Sabbat have suffered the vast majority of casualties to the Second Inquisition and take it as a badge of pride they're fighting them head on. It has also influenced the SI's assumptions about vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-02-2021, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T17:30:52-07:00","id":1466356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blind Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466354#post1466354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3) (The bit about the Sabbat that never made sense to me) How does the Sabbat's modus operandi of Mass Embraces and flouting the Masquerade to embrace their inner Beast work, especially in a post-SI world? Is that addressed at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>The older editions explained this quite well: the Sabbat don't actually break the masquerade in their own territories. Instead, they commit minor breaches of the masquerade in enemy territory, forcing the Cammies to scramble to fix things, thereby exposing themselves and their resources.<br /> <br /> The thing about sieges is, it's always been a problem for both sides to find each other. It's basically 20 guys in a city of millions laying siege to 20 other guys hiding in a city of millions.<br /> <br /> So here's what you do: you embrace a group of homeless people or whatever. You send them to attack a location. Being newborns, they flaunt their new powers a bit, but they barely have powers so it's nothing that isn't fixable. The Camarilla scramble to fix this, exposing their resources and minions in the process, and maybe even their faces. They likely slaughter the shovelheads, but who cares, they are shovelheads. The true Sabbat watch from the shadows and use this intell for quiet, targeted assassinations.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Sabbat breeches of the masquerade never amounted to anything that couldn't be dismissed as some homeless people on drugs going crazy in enemy cities.<br /> <br /> It's only in this edition that the Sabbat suddenly became idiots blatantly violating the masquerade in their own cities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T17:36:23-07:00","id":1466357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466356#post1466356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The older editions explained this quite well: the Sabbat don't actually break the masquerade in their own territories. Instead, they commit minor breaches of the masquerade in enemy territory, forcing the Cammies to scramble to fix things, thereby exposing themselves and their resources.<br /> <br /> The thing about sieges is, it's always been a problem for both sides to find each other. It's basically 20 guys in a city of millions laying siege to 20 other guys hiding in a city of millions.<br /> <br /> So here's what you do: you embrace a group of homeless people or whatever. You send them to attack a location. Being newborns, they flaunt their new powers a bit, but they barely have powers so it's nothing that isn't fixable. The Camarilla scramble to fix this, exposing their resources and minions in the process, and maybe even their faces. They likely slaughter the shovelheads, but who cares, they are shovelheads. The true Sabbat watch from the shadows and use this intell for quiet, targeted assassinations.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Sabbat breeches of the masquerade never amounted to anything that couldn't be dismissed as some homeless people on drugs going crazy in enemy cities.<br /> <br /> <b>It's only in this edition that the Sabbat suddenly became idiots blatantly violating the masquerade in their own cities.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhhhh.<br /> <br /> This isn't quite the distinction you make it out to be. The Sabbat were always engaged in far more overt and noticeable behavior than the Camarilla. No, they didn't (and still don't) go around going, &quot;booga booga booga!&quot; However, they always dropped a lot more bodies and had less influence among mortal authorities. They also had big vampire rituals the Camarilla didn't. As such, the Sabbat were always going to be bigger targets than the sect literally founded to keep the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Besides, we know the Camarilla was feeding the SI information on the Sabbat. It's stated this is why Montreal fell in PARLIAMENT OF KNIVES.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-02-2021, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T17:54:15-07:00","id":1466358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466353#post1466353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, getting back on topic (SHOCK - I am terrible at this), <b>The Paths replacing Clan</b> is something that I actually really like and am glad that the Sabbat are going for. In a way, the Lasombra and Tzimisce ANtitribu elements don't really matter because the &quot;New&quot; Sabbat are a group that is fully molding into a single post-clan sect. Being Lasombra as a concept no longer will matter in the Sabbat because all of the traditional Lasombra power structures, cultures, and beliefs will cease to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't a bad thing <i>per se</i>, I actually tend to agree with you. The problem is historical context. As much as it makes sense, the Sabbat Lasombra never did this before, while the Camarilla ones did. Why would they change attitudes now?<br /> <br /> I do get that as much as the Sabbat had some of this tendency before, the two founding clans <i>were</i> exceptions. They had pride in &quot;completely&quot; subverting their old institutions and now being fully Sabbat instead of needing to be <i>Antitribu</i>. Now even them are pressed to set clan aside in favor of identifying as Sabbat above all else before being of clan <i>X</i> or <i>Y</i>.<br /> <br /> But then again, why bother with the moniker? They can still rub in the face of others they are the clans that fully converted. They are the leadership of the sect. Unless both of those two things changed, they have no reason to embrace the moniker of <i>Antitribu</i>.<br /> <br /> Well, I for one don't care if they're in such situation. I <b>am</b> a fan of both clans, but never liked their too firm association with the Sabbat. I also think the Sabbat works better without them as so obviously at the helm. I think both making them present elsewhere and making the Sabbat more independent from them are good things (coupled with the bad things of making the badly written defection, that I can easily change in my games, and going-to-Hell Sabbat, which is less simple).<br /> <br /> Yet, the change of the moniker just for the sake of it (yeah, I know it is to make things simpler, actually) is something I think doesn't add to the setting without consideration being paid to its history.<br /> <br /> Or even, if they really wanted to do it, this is the one single thing they could just retcon and it would make more sense. Would be bad, but would be less bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T18:00:01-07:00","id":1466359,"title":"","content":"I've never been a fan of the word &quot;antitribu&quot; myself, for anyone. I tend to think that citizens of each sect would consider themselves to be the real Gangrel/Nosferatu/Ventrue/etc, and members of the other sect to be the antitribu. In other words, both sides would use it as an insult for the other side. I've never bought that someone would call themselves something as cringey and self-demeaning as antitribu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 11-02-2021, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T18:09:45-07:00","id":1466362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466357#post1466357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't quite the distinction you make it out to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is exactly the distinction he make it out to be. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> didn't said the Sabbat was as good with the Masquerade as the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> What was addressed was the impression that many players have that the Camarilla's description of the Sabbat is accurate. It isn't, until V5 decided it is, actualizing the Straw Man to punch it. Very mature game it is.<br /> <br /> Prior to V5 the Sabbat simply isn't a bunch of idiots. It just have a particular strategy that involves Embracing a bunch of idiots, but they're meant to die anyway. The big rituals involve less than two dozen vampires, they <b>are</b> easy to conceal. They are more overt, but they're not nearly a fraction of a blatant as the Camarilla describes them.<br /> <br /> As much as I have my problems especially with early descriptions of Sabbat cities in Latin America, I have to recognize the sect simply wasn't so stupid. It was a lot of propaganda, until in V5 the authors themselves drank the Kool-Aid and decided to make it real and start to kill the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> One thing is certain. Their goal is to snuff out the Sabbat in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T18:12:04-07:00","id":1466363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466362#post1466362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is exactly the distinction he make it out to be. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> didn't said the Sabbat was as good with the Masquerade as the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> What was addressed was the impression that many players have that the Camarilla's description of the Sabbat is accurate. It isn't, until V5 decided it is, actualizing the Straw Man to punch it. Very mature game it is.<br /> <br /> Prior to V5 the Sabbat simply isn't a bunch of idiots. It just have a particular strategy that involves Embracing a bunch of idiots, but they're meant to die anyway. The big rituals involve less than two dozen vampires, they <b>are</b> easy to conceal. They are more overt, but they're not nearly a fraction of a blatant as the Camarilla describes them.<br /> <br /> As much as I have my problems especially with early descriptions of Sabbat cities in Latin America, I have to recognize the sect simply wasn't so stupid. It was a lot of propaganda, until in V5 the authors themselves drank the Kool-Aid and decided to make it real and start to kill the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> One thing is certain. Their goal is to snuff out the Sabbat in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhh.<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat were originally EXACTLY THAT but it was retconned as being that they WEREN'T that way because it was stupid. Some context in that element is important because the idea the Sabbat were being unfairly maligned by the Camarilla is something that was added to make the sect look better. I feel like acting like the better written version was always true is something that undermines any argument.<br /> <br /> Especially since it was JUSTIN ACHILLI who wrote the better written version and certainly knows what he wrote previously.<br /> <br /> Justin Achilli made the retcon that the Sabbat kept the Masquerade rather than reveling in their own evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T19:26:07-07:00","id":1466371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466363#post1466363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehhhh.<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat were originally EXACTLY THAT but it was retconned as being that they WEREN'T that way because it was stupid. Some context in that element is important because the idea the Sabbat were being unfairly maligned by the Camarilla is something that was added to make the sect look better. I feel like acting like the better written version was always true is something that undermines any argument.<br /> <br /> Especially since it was JUSTIN ACHILLI who wrote the better written version and certainly knows what he wrote previously.<br /> <br /> Justin Achilli made the retcon that the Sabbat kept the Masquerade rather than reveling in their own evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here are some lines from The Player's Guide to the Sabbat, a book that long predates both Revised and Justin Achilli's presence, in Vampire the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When hunting humans for blood or sport, Sabbat will<br /> not hesitate to kill their prey. They love to drink victims to<br /> death and will even drink them dry when they do not need<br /> any blood. However, they usually kill only in cities they do<br /> not control. They know killing on a regular basis in their own<br /> cities would lead to trouble </div> </div> </div>The book goes on to introduce the idea that the Sabbat are in the end like most vampires, hypocrites, because while officially they ridicule the Masquerade, unofficially their leaders are engaged in regular efforts to cover up the crap their younger or more dedicated members engage in. That while *less effective* and subtle at concealment than a sect that, say, openly champions the Masquerade, like the Camarilla, they nevertheless do successfully in the end cover things up and work to do so.<br /> <br /> For instance, on Sabbat games:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Sabbat have a number of games they enjoy. They<br /> play them mainly in enemy territory, but occasionally within<br /> their own. </div> </div> </div>As though the Sabbat actually does have an understanding that there are limits to the crap they can get away with on their own turf. Certainly missing persons cases will ramp up when the &quot;ocassionally&quot; circumstances happen, or the loyalists slip the leash of control, but even these Sabbat are noted as understanding that there have to be what are referred as &quot;cool down periods&quot;.<br /> <br /> The idea that the Sabbat get up to most of their nonsense in *other people's territory not their own* is introduced because...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sabbat are known to<br /> stir up a great deal of trouble, especially when they are not in<br /> their own territory. That way someone else will have to clean<br /> up the mess. </div> </div> </div>Now, certainly, some of the other ideas and writing in the book will contradict these things, even shortly within the writing of others. I won't argue this was the best written book evar as far as being entirely coherent with itself, much as I wouldn't argue a lot of early VtM is what I would call well written. But to suggest that the ideas that the Sabbat in fact understood they needed some measure of restraint and self control in their own territory are retcons and the sole responsibility of Justin Achilli is..... interesting. The ideas existed well early in the existence of the Sabbat as a playable entity and certainly under different writers/developers. People thought these things long before revised as far as &quot;how does the Sabbat work then?&quot; and the books offered material that supported doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-02-2021, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T19:38:25-07:00","id":1466372,"title":"","content":"Actually while I'm there, on specifically this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Justin Achilli made the retcon that the Sabbat kept the Masquerade rather than reveling in their own evil.</i> </div> </div> </div>It takes all of 8 pages for, going to a different book, the Storyteller's Handbook to the Sabbat, a book from... 1993, to say this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Sabbat see the Camarilla as the evil<br /> establishment. Though the Sabbat has its own hierarchy of<br /> leaders, titles, rules and intrigue, most sect members still see<br /> themselves as rebels. They often do things that Camarilla<br /> Kindred consider flagrant violations of the Masquerade.<br /> Despite this, the Sabbat hypocritically maintains a Masquerade<br /> of its own, though it tends to rely more on intimidation<br /> and violence than does the Camarilla. </div> </div> </div>As though again, the idea that the Sabbat in fact keeps the Masquerade is pretty old, predating both revised and Achilli alike. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T19:47:23-07:00","id":1466373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466372#post1466372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As though again, the idea that the Sabbat in fact keeps the Masquerade is pretty old, predating both revised and Achilli alike.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They do keep the Masquerade but I guess I still believe the point is not lost because they were a lot more overt than the Camarilla and Anarchs.<br /> <br /> But you're right, I was overstating matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-03-2021, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T19:59:02-07:00","id":1466377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466373#post1466373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ummm...<br /> <br /> <i>The Sabbat see the Camarilla as the evil<br /> establishment. Though the Sabbat has its own hierarchy of<br /> leaders, titles, rules and intrigue, most sect members still see<br /> themselves as rebels. <b>They often do things that Camarilla<br /> Kindred consider flagrant violations of the Masquerade.</b><br /> Despite this, the Sabbat hypocritically maintains a Masquerade<br /> of its own, though it tends to rely more on intimidation<br /> and violence than does the Camarilla. </i><br /> <br /> Just saying.<br /> <br /> But you're right, I was overstating matters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd like to be try and clear this looks like you are straight up ignoring the words &quot;the Sabbat hypocritically maintains a Masquerade of its own&quot; because you are bolding the words that the Sabbat does things the Camarilla consider to be flagrant violations. Is that what you're doing? It's really hard to read that some other way as far as your intent, especially given the bold for emphasis and the &quot;Just saying.&quot; I'm seriously asking.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you feel you gain from treating words and context optional like this. The entire point of the paragraph in the book in question is to talk about the Sabbat's hypocrisies. The very book that proceeded on this sect that this one is a companion to on the Sabbat talks a bunch of times about the Sabbat understanding their own need to self control some things. As though the ST guide is refining ideas introduced in the Player's guide. You are at a point where you can say &quot;this one sentence lets me ignore the point of an entire paragraph&quot;. Context matters. The entire point of this paragraph is to call out the Sabbat's hypocrisy. That they call themselves rebels against the establishment, yet themselves maintain a hierarchy. That they do things that violate the Camarilla's Masquerade, even at the same time that they maintain one of their own. The previous Sabbat book before this, on top of that, notes them having the basic wisdom to understand that they need to mostly contain their worst Masquerade breaches to *other people's cities* in those exact words. The sentence you are bolding to try and hold onto the completely incorrect thing you said while ignoring multiple others doesn't really change this.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm not sure if you know this, but the same dude wrote both of these books. It's as if there is a continuation of ideas from one to the next. Now, again, I don't personally find either book well written for how they come together, but these ideas in them are all the same pretty clearly expressed and connect to each other.<br /> <br /> Context matters. It's not actually optional.<br /> <br /> Once again, you said this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <i>Justin Achilli made the retcon that the Sabbat kept the Masquerade rather than reveling in their own evil.</i> </div> </div> </div>This is objectively wrong by repeated content published for the game Vampire the Masquerade, as opposed to what you say that content is. This isn't &quot;an overstatement&quot;, it's just straight up wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-02-2021, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T20:13:49-07:00","id":1466379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466377#post1466377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is objectively wrong by repeated content published for the game Vampire the Masquerade, as opposed to what you say that content is. This isn't &quot;an overstatement&quot;, it's just straight up wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said I overstated things. I'm confused.<br /> <br /> What are you objecting to?<br /> <br /> Yeah, you're right, the Sabbat keep a Masquerade. Just far looser and more flagrantly than the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-02-2021, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T20:17:01-07:00","id":1466380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466373#post1466373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just saying what? You're not only ignoring most of what the book says to highlight only what you want, you're also ignoring what the people you're arguing with actually said.<br /> <br /> No one here said the Sabbat does a better job at Masquerade keeping than the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> No one here said the Sabbat does as good a job at Masquerade keeping as the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> What was said is that the Sabbat does a job at Masquerade keeping. It isn't as overt and stupid as is described in books written from the Camarilla's perspective.<br /> <br /> <b>And this is not Achili's creation</b>. The cautious Sabbat predates Revised. You may not like to read previous books like that, which is totally an option, but is there anyways for anyone who wants to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T20:19:11-07:00","id":1466381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466379#post1466379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I said I overstated things. I'm confused.<br /> <br /> What are you objecting to?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The use of the word &quot;overstate&quot; is to refer to that something that exists was to some degree exaggerated. Whereas the use of the word wrong refers to something that is incorrect.<br /> <br /> The idea that Justin Achilli made the retcon that the Sabbat kept the Masquerade rather than revelling in their own evil, is not an overstatement, because there's no element of it that is correct to overstate, or indeed, exist in any meaningful sense. It's just wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T20:20:09-07:00","id":1466382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466380#post1466380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just saying what? You're not only ignoring most of what the book says to highlight only what you want, you're also ignoring what the people you're arguing with actually said.<br /> <br /> No one here said the Sabbat does a better job at Masquerade keeping than the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> No one here said the Sabbat does as good a job at Masquerade keeping as the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> What was said is that the Sabbat does a job at Masquerade keeping. It isn't as overt and stupid as is described in books written from the Camarilla's perspective.<br /> <br /> <b>And this is not Achili's creation</b>. The cautious Sabbat predates Revised. You may not like to read previous books like that, which is totally an option, but is there anyways for anyone who wants to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I said I overstated things. I don't disagree with that. Which brings us back to the point the Sabbat have always kept the Masquerade much worse than the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466381#post1466381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The use of the word &quot;overstate&quot; is to refer to that something that exists was to some degree exaggerated. Whereas the use of the word wrong refers to something that is incorrect.<br /> <br /> The idea that Justin Achilli made the retcon that the Sabbat kept the Masquerade rather than revelling in their own evil, is not an overstatement, because there's no element of it that is correct to overstate, or indeed, exist in any meaningful sense. It's just wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. I stand corrected.<br /> <br /> Props for using quotes from the books and I appreciate the effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T20:25:51-07:00","id":1466384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466382#post1466382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I said I overstated things. I don't disagree with that. Which brings us back to the point the Sabbat have always kept the Masquerade much worse than the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No it really doesn't, because there's a huge difference between &quot;not as well as the Camarilla&quot; and &quot;were bad/incompetent at it&quot;. I'm not sure again why everything with you can only exist in some binary state where nuance dies a miserable death. You seem to need or want to present every disagreement with how you view the game in the starkest terms possible and it really does a number on the possibility of discussing things with you.<br /> <br /> The idea, before V5, was that the Sabbat were in fact functional enough at keeping the Masquerade in their own cities that they could thus, y'know, function, and this as an idea was pretty much as old as the notion of the Sabbat being a playable sect. The idea is that the Sabbat in fact had some understanding of that they needed to not be overt and stupid in their own cities, and this idea actually existed in several published books for the game Vampire the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Look.. do you know what the fallacy of the excluded middle is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T20:26:05-07:00","id":1466385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466379#post1466379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I said I overstated things. I'm confused.<br /> <br /> What are you objecting to?<br /> <br /> Yeah, you're right, the Sabbat keep a Masquerade. Just far looser and more flagrantly than the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are also ignoring that Achilli's contribution to the Sabbat was to destroy them as an interesting faction, whether with the dumpster fire of revised or spitting in the face of Sabbat players with V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T20:31:25-07:00","id":1466386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466382#post1466382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I said I overstated things. I don't disagree with that. Which brings us back to the point the Sabbat have always kept the Masquerade much worse than the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>A big part of my tone is because yo ninja'd me.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say t was much worse than the Camarilla, though, as much as that it included counting on the Camarilla to clean things up.<br /> <br /> Which brings us full cycle in their hypocrisy: they fought the Camarilla, but the Camarilla's presence near them was actually by design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T20:31:35-07:00","id":1466387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466385#post1466385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are also ignoring that Achilli's contribution to the Sabbat was to destroy them as an interesting faction, whether with the dumpster fire of revised or spitting in the face of Sabbat players with V5.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't personally go so far as to say Revised destroyed the idea of the Sabbat as an interesting faction. Compare it for instance to Vampire 5th, where they are straight up unplayable boogeymen. The Sabbat can still at least be played in revised, and really several ideas, like having the Sabbat not be so choked with hidden infernalism up down and all around the town (to the point where it takes up a lot of oxygen otherwise when wanting to instead just deal with the Sabbat's main thematics), or giving the Black Hand subsect their own distinct culture and pseudo religious secret doctrine to give them more personality, or cleaning up some of the paths that had some janky writing, were solid choices that offered more options, without compromising previous options when offering them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T20:37:39-07:00","id":1466389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466387#post1466387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I wouldn't personally go so far as to say Revised destroyed the idea of the Sabbat as an interesting faction. Compare it for instance to Vampire 5th, where they are straight up unplayable boogeymen. The Sabbat can still at least be played in revised, and really several ideas, like having the Sabbat not be so choked with hidden infernalism up down and all around the town (to the point where it takes up a lot of oxygen otherwise when wanting to instead just deal with the Sabbat's main thematics), or giving the Black Hand subsect their own distinct culture and pseudo religious secret doctrine to give them more personality, or cleaning up some of the paths that had some janky writing, were solid choices that offered more options, without compromising previous options when offering them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I was completely wrong about early 2nd Edition Sabbat. However, I think infernalism is something that gets ignored too much.<br /> <br /> After all, demon worship isn't any worse than what Sabbat do normally. I think they could have really expanded on it and made it a viable path for the Sabbat. After all, fight fire with fire. The Antediluvians are all powerful so maybe you need a Demon Lord to fight them. Of course, I love DEMON: THE FALLEN and the irony that some demons are better than Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T20:48:55-07:00","id":1466393,"title":"","content":"So.. to still be topical and to try to put things another way since it's coming up, right, so, the revised Sabbat and opinions on that, both in contrast to V5 and otherwise. Honestly there were some good moves there in my view.<br /> <br /> Take otherwise for example something pre revised like Montreal by Night (I do not mean to harsh anyone who enjoyed Montreal By Night, but on the other hand, to me personally, woof). Anything else you could say about it besides, it certainly does have more of the Sabbat portrayal that seems to influence where CTPhipps' understanding of the sect came from (on the other hand it does also have some npcs who clearly understand 'we can't just be an overt dumb freeforall' so, it's a mix).<br /> <br /> One of the things that aggravated me about this book was that the entire whole story and plotline of it boils down to infernalism shenanigans. Which just for me completely sucks all the air out of doing things with it, if I wanted to have a focus that isn't infernalism shenanigans and get use out of this book. Cripes there's an outright Decani under the city, and most of the plot boils down to the rivalry between it and another Decani. That's so huge it is almost unignorable. It touches almost every npc in some way or other. It's not even a hidden methuselah type rivalry. It's demons playing shenanigans with vampires. And this is basically kind of the signature Sabbat city as far as the underlying plot being that.<br /> <br /> Whereas in revised, the central plot around Montreal instead shifted to Cardinal Strathcona attempting to slowly and carefully encourage a Camarilla siege of the city that while not succeeding (or so he hopes), does succeed *enough* to spark a renewed spirit of unity and dedication in the sect (or so he hopes) by threatening its religious heart, because he feels the Sabbat are falling short of their ideals in the modern nights (and the idea that, hey, maybe he's not wrong, is something that can be thereby explored/debated). There's politics in that, potential direct conflict, philosophical debate, a bunch of stuff.<br /> <br /> That to me was pretty neat, and left a lot more room to play around with a lot more things. Certainly it had more depth as a concept than, y'know, demons warring for influence over each other with vampires as pawns (I actually don't hate Baali/Infernalism plots, they have their place and use and can be done very interesting, have a place in horror/corruption tales, and hey, sometimes as a break it's good to just fight something explicitly the worst. But holy eff making the entire city an infernalist plotline is kind of a lot. A looooooooooooot.).<br /> <br /> So I would say revised was certainly capable of taking the Sabbat and exploring interesting ideas with them, at least in some ways. Perhaps not all ways of course. There were for instance some npcs in the pre revised Sabbat that you didn't really have the caliber of in the post revised one, as an example. But I think saying that revised was 100% bereft of interesting handles on the Sabbat, or even a couple of improvements, is a bit much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-02-2021, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T21:04:05-07:00","id":1466394,"title":"","content":"Infernalism played a WAY bigger role in second edition sabbat then it did revised. Hell, the regent was infernal. While I think infernalism should actually be one of the main antagonists for the genre, it was definitely a bit much.<br /> <br /> My favorite sabbat book is Mexico City by Night. Which showcases the depths and politics of the sabbat. The fact is for all their talk...the reality is the sabbat is no different from any other vampire or sect in regards to the jyhad.<br /> <br /> Like...cool your message is right..the antedluvians are real. To bad you became what you hated in 500 years of a sect. Your aren't special or immune to the nature of being a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T21:10:37-07:00","id":1466395,"title":"","content":"As much as I think infernalism is inherently interesting and having it as a part of the Sabbat is a great thing*, I generally prefer Revised as my favorite version of the Sabbat. V5's take on the Sabbat is useless to me as a Sabbat Storyteller and player. It seems like the END of the Sabbat as an organization and while that isn't automatically a bad plotline and has room for ex-Sabbat stories or building a new Sabbat, it definitely requires a lot of that to be done. This seems like a coda for the Sabbat as a sect: The Sabbat have degenerated and are on the verge of losing everything that made them great.<br /> <br /> The Revised verison of the Sabbat struck a good balance with the fact the Sabbat were overtly monstrous and despicable villains but also people who had a decent number of people actually seeking higher posthuman enlightenment. There was a tension between the two sides of the sect that made for an interesting twist. You had the PATHS OF ENLIGHTENMENT vampires who were inhuman, alien, and spiritual versus the Low Humanity...assholes for lack of a better description. Part of what I think is a problem is they seemed to have combined these mutually exclusive ideas for V5's Sabbat.<br /> <br /> A Path of Enlightenment follower shouldn't be a mindless ravening beast. That isn't what Paths are about. A Path follower is weird and alien in their morality. The Low Humanity vampires are the ones who act like soccer hooligans.<br /> <br /> At least how I always played them.<br /> <br /> * I think they tried to get rid of all the infernalism in the Sabbat to make them more playable and I feel this eliminated an interesting setting element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T21:20:16-07:00","id":1466398,"title":"","content":"The problem with the infernalism as a player facing thing in the Sabbat is that the writers never seemed to have a handle on using it without it basically dominating the plot where it came up. The idea of the Sabbat was to have a lot going on with them ideologically, politically, and otherwise, as much as any other playable group, that was an outright almost verbatim mission statement with the group once it became playable. The problem of infernalism, or certainly the way it was written, was that it basically took up a lot of space in which other things could fit in a playable Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Maybe if it had been written differently? But as it stood it was a thing that when invoked took up a lot of conceptual real estate that other very playable notions of the sabbat had to fight for space with. In the case of a full out city book this verged on the literal. <br /> <br /> I mean it was still there to a degree in revised. Certainly something like Archons and Templars devoted space to talking about how Inquisitors did their thing and if you wanted the players to be them and etc. etc. and I thought that had some interesting handling. <br /> <br /> I did kind of like the idea as far as the Inquisition that the sect who best understood what a terrible thing the infernal was and that it had to be combatted was, of all people, the Sabbat. It was both funny and interesting as an ironic thing as one of the dark little commentaries Vampire could make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T21:30:43-07:00","id":1466400,"title":"","content":"I think the thing about running a Sabbat game is exploring what good and evil means to a society that considers vampire life sacred, and homo sapien life to be irrelevant beyond purely practical concerns. How do you build such a society? Infernalism certainly makes for an easy adversary in such a society, since it involves giving power over to creatures who want to enslave vampires.<br /> <br /> However, it's rather unsubtle. More complex issues come up when considering the balance of freedom and the survival of the vampire species. Do you want to become purely military? That helps the Sabbat defeat their enemies, but destroys the freedom that makes unlife worth unliving.<br /> <br /> Should you devote yourself purely to advancing on a Path of Enlightenment? That helps tremendously with your personal peace of mind and freedom from the beast, but takes away time from you working to preserve the survival of all Sabbat.<br /> <br /> How much recklessness should be tolerated with regards to treatment of homo sapiens. While there is no evil that can be done to them, since they are not vampires, they are dangerous in rather the way that uranium is dangerous. That is to say, they are a valuable source of power that can destroy everyone if treated recklessly. How much recklessness do you tolerate before considering the balance between freedom and security to have overbalanced in the direction of freedom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T21:40:34-07:00","id":1466405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466398#post1466398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did kind of like the idea as far as the Inquisition that the sect who best understood what a terrible thing the infernal was and that it had to be combatted was, of all people, the Sabbat. It was both funny and interesting as an ironic thing as one of the dark little commentaries Vampire could make.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the reason the Sabbat were both pitted against, and infiltrated by, infernalism was because they are metaphorical Crusaders and Monks. In the real world, Crusaders and Monks were accused of infernalism any time the aristocracy felt threatened by them. In the real world, the accusation was just a silly attempt at avoiding paying off debts, or a power-grab. This being the WOD, the Crusader/Monks are, in fact, infiltrated by infernalists.<br /> <br /> So it's not really ironic, but rather thematic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T21:41:38-07:00","id":1466406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466389#post1466389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they could have really expanded on it and made it a viable path for the Sabbat. After all, fight fire with fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also a huge DtF fan, but I think that the Sabbat is just as much defined by the theme of being a Catholic Heresy at the core (even if not exactly forcing Christianity on their followers). So the idea of demons being a big NO for them is a fitting irony.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I'm with the notion that it can't be overplayed. It is an interesting option at <i>any</i> time, not <i>every</i> time. Otherwise it just takes from other plots while by itself becomes overplayed.<br /> <br /> A thing I recently finished deciding as my headcanon is that the demons that offer Investments by usual Vampire rules, especially those that operate by the rules in <i>Devil's Due</i>, are actually Wyrm spirits. I know some people find the rules for demons in <i>Devil's Due</i> superior to DtF, but this is just not true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T21:57:33-07:00","id":1466412,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on the Infernal is the idea the Sabbat are the best sect to do themes of occultism and dark mysteries. As much as I love the Tremere, I feel like they come across as a bit mechanalistic in terms of exploring dark secrets and supernatural power. If you want to do things like robed torch-lit ceremonies in the middle of graveyards, Cthulhu-esque idols, and &quot;things man was not meant to knoiw&quot; then the Sabbat are the best people to explore.<br /> <br /> The infernal was, admittedly, shown to be the &quot;designated bad guys&quot; of the Sabbat but Montreal by Night always struck me as something that really did a great job establishing the Sabbat as thoroughly infiltrated by demonic forces but having people willing to fight and die to purify the Sabbat of their influence. Yet it had the interesting extra layer that these people were STILL damned and evil so what were they fighting for?<br /> <br /> BLOOD CULTS did a good job of moving what I loved best of the Sabbat into mainstream vampire society but I still felt very few people ever did the &quot;Anti-Catholicism&quot; nearly as well. Maybe my infernalist ridden verison of the Sabbat was a little too CHILLING ADVENTURES OF SABRINA but it was always a lot of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T22:10:35-07:00","id":1466413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466412#post1466412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The infernal was, admittedly, shown to be the &quot;designated bad guys&quot; of the Sabbat but Montreal by Night always struck me as something that really did a great job establishing the Sabbat as thoroughly infiltrated by demonic forces but having people willing to fight and die to purify the Sabbat of their influence. Yet it had the interesting extra layer that these people were STILL damned and evil so what were they fighting for?<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>The survival and freedom of the vampire species, of course, and therefore for goodness as their species defines it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T22:15:46-07:00","id":1466416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\">