Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T06:16:24-07:00","id":1466452,"title":"","content":"I imagine that in the Sabbat, there are elders who are loosely aligned by Vauldrie (they may be cheating it) but are mostly spread out and keep to themselves rather like Camarilla vampires, and neonates who, if they aren't sharing havens, are likely in the same neighbourhood (in peace and with age, they spread out more). The Elders are actually quite wary of the packs of hungry neonates they have beneath them, so they like to play packs off one another, and they often feel threatened by Ancillae. A pack of neonates is a risk. A pack of Ancillae is a sword of Damocles. Elders will very carefully review anyone who makes it to 100. There are three possitibilities. Ideally, they'll try to form a great relationship with them in eager anticipation for them to enter the elder circle, Failing that; they'll reasign them to a nonthreatening or distant role. Third; They'll scheme to have the Ancillae killed. <br /> <br /> Infernalists? Bringing them to your side isn't possible, their loyalty to a demon is paramount. Nonthreatening role? That's just delaying the rise of someone who'll become more powerful than you. Getting the infernalist killed is by far the best option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T08:01:02-07:00","id":1466463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466445#post1466445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to not lump all demons with Nephandi who want to end all life. Some simply wish to rule the pathetic humans. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are loosely speaking g 4-6 types of entity who could be consider demons in wod. 3 are committed to the annihilation of all life, 1 plans to turn it into hell on earth outstripping anything we can imagine the other 2 will just ensure you continue suffering after you die.....which the others often do as well. They're all worse than the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-03-2021, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T14:34:16-07:00","id":1466513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466359#post1466359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never been a fan of the word &quot;antitribu&quot; myself, for anyone. I tend to think that citizens of each sect would consider themselves to be the real Gangrel/Nosferatu/Ventrue/etc, and members of the other sect to be the antitribu. In other words, both sides would use it as an insult for the other side. I've never bought that someone would call themselves something as cringey and self-demeaning as antitribu.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I understand why <i>antitribu</i> would be a self-deprecating term (or even a cringy one, although that sounds more like a matter of personal taste).<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are ideologically committed to the destruction of the Antediluvians <i>and all their non-Sabbat progeny.</i> That is what being a member of an 'anti-clan' means. Saying you are Toreador <i>antitribu</i> is akin to saying &quot;We are going to destroy Arikel and all of main Clan Toreador.&quot;<br /> <br /> At least, that is how I always understood the <i>antitribu</i> moniker in its original context (2nd Edition, Revised, and whatnot). There were always exceptions to the rule, of course, such as clan loyalty generally trumping sect loyalty in the case of the Nosferatu and Nosferatu <i>antitribu.</i> On the whole, though, claiming you were a part of an 'anti-clan' always came across to me like a proud declaration, not a sign of self-deprecation.<br /> <br /> I imagine this is why it was always emphasized from the start that &quot;Lasombra <i>antitribu</i>&quot; don't actually call themselves that. Non-Sabbat Lasombra are not ideologically committed to the destruction of the Lasombra Antediluvian (who was originally reputed to be already dead), nor to the destruction of all Lasombra in the Sabbat. The label <i>&quot;antitribu&quot;</i> simply does not apply to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","user":"Elphilm","date":". 11-03-2021, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T14:50:08-07:00","id":1466519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466355#post1466355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. <b>The Gehenna War is absolutely nothing different</b>: Justin Achill basically says that it was misinterpred as some great mass migration of the Sabbat to fight Ancients. However, it's actually them fighting the exact same war they were always fighting. They just added the Ashirra to the list of people they want to murder.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Cynical Gehenna</b>: This isn't detailed here but in LA by Night, Jason Carl had Beckett explain it as &quot;The Antediluvians awaken, eat their progeny, Embrace new ones, and go back to sleep.&quot;<br /> <br /> 3. <b>How does their violation of the Masquerade work</b>? According to the book? Shitily. SABBAT: THE BLACK HAND says the Sabbat have suffered the vast majority of casualties to the Second Inquisition and take it as a badge of pride they're fighting them head on. It has also influenced the SI's assumptions about vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for the response!<br /> <br /> 1. So...then the Sabbat <i>haven't </i>left their strongholds in North America and Europe? They are still at war with the Camarilla in those places? <br /> <br /> 2. I see. As you say, it's not detailed here, so I suppose there's no info given on when the last Gehenna was. The Fourth Generation must have known about it, logically. <br /> <br /> 3. Well, at least that makes sense. I know I ignited another argument here with this question, but for me the books' explanation of 'the Sabbat are hypocrites' never felt like enough. It just seemed unsustainable, from the perspective of the average vampire on the ground anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/480-blind-dragon","name":"Blind Dragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T14:57:32-07:00","id":1466521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466513#post1466513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine this is why it was always emphasized from the start that &quot;Lasombra <i>antitribu</i>&quot; don't actually call themselves that. Non-Sabbat Lasombra are not ideologically committed to the destruction of the Lasombra Antediluvian (who was originally reputed to be already dead), nor to the destruction of all Lasombra in the Sabbat. The label <i>&quot;antitribu&quot;</i> simply does not apply to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree to this. But the most likely reason the Camarilla Lasombra were called the anti-tribu were for OOC understanding and &quot;branding&quot; that the label antitribu meant vampires who belonged to the opposite sect they were supposed to be. It was more a term for the readers/fans, not something best used IC by the vampires themselves.<br /> <br /> On a certain level, I think the Sabbat Lasombra and Tzimisce did not have the antitribu label because they had destroyed their antedeluvian and massacred most of the pre-Anarch Revolt clan members leaving the anarch Lasombra/Tzimisce triumphant. They were now the &quot;new&quot; &quot;free&quot; clan as the old had been destroyed. The other clans had not been successful at that so they were &quot;just&quot; antitribu. (I don't necessarily think it is needed to destroy a clan's antedeluvian to do so as some antedeluvians are popularly believed to be destroyed, but it would still be needed to destroy the existing structures and elders of the main clan so that the antitribu can be said to have triumphed).<br /> <br /> It's one reason I like the phrase Old Clan Tzimisce. It gets across the same point, but not using Sabbat terminology. As such, something like the Old Clan Lasombra in the Camarilla would sound better to my ears, but I'd prefer it to be something else that can get the same point across but not duplicate the term from the Old Clan Tzimisce. Maybe something like the Old Tradition, the Legitimate, Paragon, or the Venerable. Not quite as catchy as the Old Clan though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T16:20:52-07:00","id":1466528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466444#post1466444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to consider I infernalism worse than Sabbat ideology, whatever the horrors of the sect they don't genrally represent an existential threat to life itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons aren't necessarily an existential threat, and most importantly the infernalist character may not think they are.<br /> <br /> You are right that there are demons and demonologists that just want to end the world. Those are objectively worse than the Sabbat, even if you may argue that they're not more <i>evil</i>, since it depends on how you define evil.<br /> <br /> But a demonologist that simply doesn't believe to be endangering life on this world, or even believe to be protecting it, isn't that kind of evil. And the demons are also a varied bunch, so they're not necessarily that kind of evil (or any kind, actually) either.<br /> <br /> I already had a game where a character got pissed when he found out that he sold his soul to a demon that actually had high standards and didn't want to do evil for evil's sake, much less screw the world. The demon was just as disgusted with their relation when she found out her thrall was that kind of jerk, but they would have to work together anyway (we were both PCs, he was a Mage).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466463#post1466463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are loosely speaking g 4-6 types of entity who could be consider demons in wod. 3 are committed to the annihilation of all life, 1 plans to turn it into hell on earth outstripping anything we can imagine the other 2 will just ensure you continue suffering after you die.....which the others often do as well. They're all worse than the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly that.<br /> <br /> First of all, there is one type that is for PCs, and as every PC splat they can have a lot of other goals and considerations. You can't simply ignore them, and they're not doomed to evil.<br /> <br /> Second, some of the other entities that can be considered demons don't have an actual agenda. As geared to cause suffering as they are, they don't always have it as a greater goal, as they don't have greater goals or have other, less comprehensive goals. Not all Wyrm spirits, as an example, serve directly the notion of bringing corruption to the entire world.<br /> <br /> Third, in the end this is not about the reality of demons in the setting, but the beliefs of the infernalist character. Even the Sabbat is blind to whatever is the actual goal of those entities, so their beliefs on the matter are just that, beliefs. And for all purposes, unless the demon itself plays a larger role in a story, as happened with Kupala and entity in Hunedoara, the actual demon is largely irrelevant to all that.<br /> <br /> By the way, for all its power the entity in Hunedoara was too big a loser to be a threat to the world. A demonologist that enters a pact in the firm and correct belief that they can gear their Investments towards the greater good, because the demon in question is an idiot, is worse than the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466513#post1466513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat are ideologically committed to the destruction of the Antediluvians <i>and all their non-Sabbat progeny.</i> That is what being a member of an 'anti-clan' means. Saying you are Toreador <i>antitribu</i> is akin to saying &quot;We are going to destroy Arikel and all of main Clan Toreador.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If the term were consistently used as that it would make sense. An it does seem to be V5's take on the matter.<br /> <br /> But the use of the term isn't actually that consistent. Some <i>Antitribu</i> didn't work like that at all, as was the case with Salubri and Nosferatu, and the Lasombra stand out if you claim this explanation, as they're in the sect's leadership and they <b>definitely do hunt their non-Sabbat counterparts</b>, so how can you say they're not <i>Antitribu</i> and the Camarilla ones are, instead?<br /> <br /> The theory is good, but it doesn't match well with how it was actually used in the game. And I find that addressing this history matters even if I personally think the change is for the better (slightly).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blind Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466519#post1466519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the response!<br /> <br /> 1. So...then the Sabbat <i>haven't </i>left their strongholds in North America and Europe? They are still at war with the Camarilla in those places?<br /> <br /> 2. I see. As you say, it's not detailed here, so I suppose there's no info given on when the last Gehenna was. The Fourth Generation must have known about it, logically.<br /> <br /> 3. Well, at least that makes sense. I know I ignited another argument here with this question, but for me the books' explanation of 'the Sabbat are hypocrites' never felt like enough. It just seemed unsustainable, from the perspective of the average vampire on the ground anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>1- The Sabbat left their strongholds and moved a lot, they lost almost all their cities, but essentially because they decided to become a mobile army instead of a static nation. They are also fighting the Antes or what they believe to be the Antes, it isn't clear yet. They're basically all over the place but with few home bases, now;<br /> <br /> 2- The entire <i>Cyclic Gehenna</i> thing is still Becket's theory and nothing more. It makes a lot of sense and is kind of an &quot;unofficial canon&quot;, but it probably wont ever be more than that and hardly have any actual bearing in the metaplot anyway;<br /> <br /> 3- It depends on how you personally see a lot of things. How frequently the Sabbat actually does overt stuff? How overt it really is in context? How can it be explained? How much attention authorities or media pay to the places and times it happens?<br /> <br /> None of those things have actual correct answers for your game. Your own personal expectations play a huge role in defining how you see them, but if you step back it can actually cover a very large spectrum of possibilities. So it is whatever you think makes sense for your game.<br /> <br /> Well, it was. Now it is officially worse and mostly failing anyway, and the Second Inquisition is getting ever better at hunting Sabbat. The sect is dumber and the enemy is smarter, so for V5 purposes the Sabbat is dying and is decided to die with a Bang.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466521#post1466521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's one reason I like the phrase Old Clan Tzimisce. It gets across the same point, but not using Sabbat terminology. As such, something like the Old Clan Lasombra in the Camarilla would sound better to my ears, but I'd prefer it to be something else that can get the same point across but not duplicate the term from the Old Clan Tzimisce. Maybe something like the Old Tradition, the Legitimate, Paragon, or the Venerable. Not quite as catchy as the Old Clan though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noble Lasombra? Then they may refer to the Sabbat ones as &quot;Peasants&quot; only. I also thought of Eternal or Purple, as references to Rome (being the Eternal City and purple being the color of the Senate, and for a long time a reference to aristocracy on both Roman Empires).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T16:22:12-07:00","id":1466529,"title":"","content":"I went with &quot;True Lasombra&quot; as if the Sabbat ones are failures for siding with the rabble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T16:33:31-07:00","id":1466531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466529#post1466529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I went with &quot;True Lasombra&quot; as if the Sabbat ones are failures for siding with the rabble.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely see that as a strong contender. It has the advantage of being shorter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:41:47-07:00","id":1466571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466531#post1466531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely see that as a strong contender. It has the advantage of being shorter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I agree, we have already the True Brujah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T19:13:02-07:00","id":1466580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466571#post1466571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I agree, we have already the True Brujah.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always liked the V20 note that Troile was Brujah's only childe so the True Brujah, even if they're not lying, are completely full of shit.<br /> <br /> Other possible Lasombra names:<br /> <br /> * Royal Lasombra<br /> <br /> * Magisterium Lasombra (Catholicism reference)<br /> <br /> * Patrician Lasombra (implying the others are Plebs - but that may be too Roman)<br /> <br /> * Elysian Lasombra","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/