sombra</div> </div> </div> </div>People shorten True Brujah to Trujah, so I think whatever we go with for Lasombra needs to roll off the tongue that well too. <br /> Royal Lasombra = Rasombra<br /> Magisterium Lasombra = Masombra<br /> Patrician Lasombra = Pasombra<br /> Elysian Lasombra = Easombra - that definitely doesn't work and I guess you could go Elasombra but that just seems super silly because it's just Lasombra with an E in front of it.<br /> <br /> Of those choices I prefer Rasombra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T21:03:03-07:00","id":1466603,"title":"","content":"Hellene Brujah are presumably Hujah.<br /> <br /> Fun fact: Since the only really important Greek Lasombra (And Carthage is definitely not Hellenistic), the Hellene Brujah are probably literally just referring to Critias.<br /> <br /> His new egotistic asshole self named an entire faction after himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T05:36:31-07:00","id":1466637,"title":"","content":"Could they be simply magisters? That was their Dark Ages nickname and I don\u2019t think that the Sabbat Lasombra kept it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466603#post1466603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hellene Brujah are presumably Hujah.<br /> <br /> Fun fact: Since the only really important Greek Lasombra (And Carthage is definitely not Hellenistic), the Hellene Brujah are probably literally just referring to Critias.<br /> <br /> His new egotistic asshole self named an entire faction after himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keepers of the Word played up their Greek heritage. They even had their own Olympic Games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T08:11:42-07:00","id":1466650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466580#post1466580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always liked the V20 note that Troile was Brujah's only childe so the True Brujah, even if they're not lying, are completely full of shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. The True Brujah started out in 1992's <i>Clanbook: Brujah</i> as the Brujah equivalent of the Nictuku: an uncomfortable rumor of something from the ancient past coming back to haunt one of the major clans. Taking that away from the Trujah basically removes the only interesting thing about them. What is compelling about the concept of a shadowy remnant known only in whispered rumors that turns out to be a bunch of dupes and cheats instead? It would be like taking the Nictuku and going &quot;Nope, turns out these jackasses are just off-brand Nosferatu that far post-date the main clan and don't actually contribute anything of importance to the setting.&quot; What a twist!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T08:15:19-07:00","id":1466651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466650#post1466650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. The True Brujah started out in 1992's <i>Clanbook: Brujah</i> as the Brujah equivalent of the Nictuku: an uncomfortable rumor of something from the ancient past coming back to haunt one of the major clans. Taking that away from the Trujah basically removes the only interesting thing about them. What is compelling about the concept of a shadowy remnant known only in whispered rumors that turns out to be a bunch of dupes and cheats instead? It would be like taking the Nictuku and going &quot;Nope, turns out these jackasses are just off-brand Nosferatu that far post-date the main clan and don't actually contribute anything of importance to the setting.&quot; What a twist!</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'd probably prefer that with the Nicktuju because the idea of a bunch of 4th generation running around killing &quot;real&quot; Nosferatu makes no damned sense as a setting element. I mean, what are the players going to do about it and they should always be the focus.<br /> <br /> Instead, the issue with the True Brujah is that I like the fact that they've somehow severed themselves from the emotions of Troile and made themselves believe themselves to be an &quot;elite&quot; caste of the Brujah but like all racism--it's just a near arbitrary distinction that they are clinging to. I don't want to make the Black Hand SILLY but I do like implying that they aren't as smart as they think they are.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T08:36:08-07:00","id":1466652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466651#post1466651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'd probably prefer that with the Nicktuju because the idea of a bunch of 4th generation running around killing &quot;real&quot; Nosferatu makes no damned sense as a setting element. I mean, what are the players going to do about it and they should always be the focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>W-what? Are we talking about the same setting where one of the basic elements is the idea that one night the 3rd Generation Antediluvians are going to rise up and devour their sorry progeny? The Nictuku are just an extension of that concept, not something you should use in every chronicle to wipe out the local Nosferatu warrens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466651#post1466651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead, the issue with the True Brujah is that I like the fact that they've somehow severed themselves from the emotions of Troile and made themselves believe themselves to be an &quot;elite&quot; caste of the Brujah but like all racism--it's just a near arbitrary distinction that they are clinging to. I don't want to make the Black Hand SILLY but I do like implying that they aren't as smart as they think they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of this sounds like pure poison to me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The earliest True Brujah concept does two things: it gives Clan Brujah an &quot;original sin&quot; that can come back to haunt modern members of the clan in overt or covert ways, and it makes the Brujah the original rebels, the first <i>antitribu</i> in history. Those are both cool things in my book. I certainly prefer them to the weirdly didactic tone of your ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T08:51:03-07:00","id":1466654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466650#post1466650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. The True Brujah started out in 1992's <i>Clanbook: Brujah</i> as the Brujah equivalent of the Nictuku: an uncomfortable rumor of something from the ancient past coming back to haunt one of the major clans. Taking that away from the Trujah basically removes the only interesting thing about them. What is compelling about the concept of a shadowy remnant known only in whispered rumors that turns out to be a bunch of dupes and cheats instead? It would be like taking the Nictuku and going &quot;Nope, turns out these jackasses are just off-brand Nosferatu that far post-date the main clan and don't actually contribute anything of importance to the setting.&quot; What a twist!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a big distinction on how much both concepts need to be &quot;true&quot; to work in the game.<br /> <br /> The Nictuku are a bunch of Methuselah, but otherwise, they're just Nosferatu with a different goal. If you take out their history being true they have nothing to go for them. You can make a good story based on they being a big hoax, but that's it.<br /> <br /> But the True Brujah are an actual playable faction with proper powers, weakness and Discipline. They don't need their past to be true to still work as is within the game.<br /> <br /> So it is not that their past literally don't matter, but that this truth won't affect most uses you can make of the group. They may be right, and that does have interesting implications. But if they're wrong, so what? The faction isn't destroyed or anything.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, I don't like the idea of OoC official truths. For me the uncertainty works better 9 out of 10 times for this kind of thing. I prefer that the True Brujah have reason to believe they are what they claim to be, but also that it isn't impossible for them to be wrong and the others are just silly and ignorant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T08:51:31-07:00","id":1466655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466652#post1466652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W-what? Are we talking about the same setting where one of the basic elements is the idea that one night the 3rd Generation Antediluvians are going to rise up and devour their sorry progeny? The Nictuku are just an extension of that concept, not something you should use in every chronicle to wipe out the local Nosferatu warrens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it would be like asking what the players are supposed to do about Ur-Shulgi or Mithras... I mean I guess, not much? The Niktuku are there as a horror element and a piece of the Gehenna lore. The ancients will awaken and murder their children. The Nosferatu antedeluvian simply uses his eldest children as his pawns in this process of wiping out the rest of his wayward children. The Niktuku are the &quot;boogymen&quot; that the boogymen who haunt the tunnels and sewers talk in whispers about.<br /> <br /> The Niktuku generally shouldn't be popping up in a given game session, just like Ur-Shulgi or Lazarus or Tremere probably shouldn't either. The purpose the Niktuku serve in the game is to set the mood and to represent the sort of horror story that has driven the ultimate doomsday preppers to have spent the last several centuries prepping even as they acknowledge those preparations aren't enough and will never be enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T08:56:23-07:00","id":1466656,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I really like the prepper angle for the Nosferatu, and the idea (but not necessarily the <i>presence</i>) of the Nictuku is a key element of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T09:20:58-07:00","id":1466658,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the True Brujah: a bloodline supplanted by a more successful one. The Brujah having a dark past. The Brujah having an attagonist with similar abilities but a diametrically opposing attitude (Too emotional VS Too unemotional) provides for an interesting opponent narratively beyond the usual Brujah pro-union VS Anti-union goon squads. <br /> But I also like the idea of the TB being full of shit. Chiefly because the <i>actual </i>Brujah are so full of shit<br /> <br /> And I think, mechanically, the TB are cut up primarily because far too much emphasis is placed on Temporis, which sucks. If anything, I'd like to double down on the part where the TB are emotionless. Make them psychopathic robots, caring about <i>logic </i>and \u200befficiency who deliberately try to supress what little emotion they have left. while also being ironically driven to prove themselves right as the best predator because, y'know, consistency certainly isn't what the Brujah are about. <br /> <br /> IMO, True Brujah should seperate themselves more from Brujah by dropping Presence, because a bloodline that struggles with it's emotions shouldn't have the ultimate power of emotional manipulation. Auspex, Dominate and Obfuscate are all good picks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T10:25:52-07:00","id":1466672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466652#post1466652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of this sounds like pure poison to me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The earliest True Brujah concept does two things: it gives Clan Brujah an &quot;original sin&quot; that can come back to haunt modern members of the clan in overt or covert ways, and it makes the Brujah the original rebels, the first <i>antitribu</i> in history. Those are both cool things in my book. I certainly prefer them to the weirdly didactic tone of your ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't much care for it. The idea of an unexamined &quot;Sins of the Father&quot; being justified for genocide is something that marks the Black Hand poorly. But that's just me.<br /> <br /> I'm glad it works for you. Every Storyteller is different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466655#post1466655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Yeah, it would be like asking what the players are supposed to do about Ur-Shulgi or Mithras... I mean I guess, not much?</b> The Niktuku are there as a horror element and a piece of the Gehenna lore. The ancients will awaken and murder their children. The Nosferatu antedeluvian simply uses his eldest children as his pawns in this process of wiping out the rest of his wayward children. The Niktuku are the &quot;boogymen&quot; that the boogymen who haunt the tunnels and sewers talk in whispers about.<br /> <br /> The Niktuku generally shouldn't be popping up in a given game session, just like Ur-Shulgi or Lazarus or Tremere probably shouldn't either. The purpose the Niktuku serve in the game is to set the mood and to represent the sort of horror story that has driven the ultimate doomsday preppers to have spent the last several centuries prepping even as they acknowledge those preparations aren't enough and will never be enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is funny because I absolutely FALL OF LONDON because it's about you dealing with Mithras. Also, I've run multiple Chronicles about seeking artifacts and eldritch powers to deal with Ur-Shulgi.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yes, I have the idea that the PCs should always be front and center for any major story element. Call it the Exalted in me.<br /> <br /> Still, I suppose you're correct that the Nictuku can be the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-04-2021, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T10:26:05-07:00","id":1466673,"title":"","content":"I have to agree on the Presence angle. Really they got Temporis because the authors wanted a time-based Discipline, and then it was obvious to drop Celerity as too redundant and the obvious &quot;corruption of original Temporis&quot;. Also to reduce the number of Physical Disciplines on them.<br /> <br /> But thematically speaking, Presence is the sore point. It doesn't fit their thing at all. Dominate would be a good replacement, and then we would have a Celerity-based Dominate user. If it was bound to have a gimmick Discipline, then replacing Presence for something that drains emotions instead of giving them would be better fitting.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate I'm not so sure, but Auspex is also very good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T11:10:37-07:00","id":1466683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466672#post1466672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't much care for it. The idea of an unexamined &quot;Sins of the Father&quot; being justified for genocide is something that marks the Black Hand poorly.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's unexamined about it? I don't really follow your line of reasoning here. The concept of the sins of the father is a cornerstone of Gothic literature, and by extension the Gothic-Punk milieu of the World of Darkness. You literally have a colossal father figure as the progenitor of all vampires and the sole reason why everyone in the setting is in this mess. One of the basic mechanics of the game revolves around tracing the steps of an ancient blood curse all the way back to the First Murder.<br /> <br /> If an insane, Antediluvian-worshipping cult like the True Black Hand uses the concept of ancestral sin as an excuse for the destruction of their enemies, that in no way implies that they are <i>justified</i> in doing so, or that the game leaves the concept unexamined. On the contrary, I would argue that <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> is all about examining the idea that a curse can somehow be passed on from generation to generation.<br /> <br /> But maybe I'm just misunderstanding your point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","user":"Elphilm","date":". 11-04-2021, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T11:15:12-07:00","id":1466685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466683#post1466683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's unexamined about it? I don't really follow your line of reasoning here. The concept of the sins of the father is a cornerstone of Gothic literature, and by extension the Gothic-Punk milieu of the World of Darkness. You literally have a colossal father figure as the progenitor of all vampires and the sole reason why everyone in the setting is in this mess. One of the basic mechanics of the game revolves around tracing the steps of an ancient blood curse all the way back to the First Murder.<br /> <br /> If an insane, Antediluvian-worshipping cult like the True Black Hand uses the concept of ancestral sin as an excuse for the destruction of their enemies, that in no way implies that they are <i>justified</i> in doing so, or that the game leaves the concept unexamined. On the contrary, I would argue that <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> is all about examining the idea that a curse can somehow be passed on from generation to generation.<br /> <br /> But maybe I'm just misunderstanding your point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, I feel the hypocrisy of my take on the subject (that they're still the Children of Troile while simultaneously trying to avenge Brujah) underscores the tragedy and pointless fanaticism of it all. I feel like too much of the original book acted like the Black Hand weren't nearly as twisted and depraved as the later V20 supplement did. Part of what I like about V20 and other takes on the True Hand is that they do make it clear they're a self-deluded Gehenna cult that refuses to acknowledge they're probably worshiping the Baali's founders or that the Antediluvians HATED each other as much as Caine hated them.<br /> <br /> I guess I like vampire lore that is full of self-delusion and petty spite.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T11:29:09-07:00","id":1466687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466685#post1466685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I like vampire lore that is full of self-delusion and petty spite.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does come through loud and clear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T11:30:40-07:00","id":1466688,"title":"","content":"I've suggested before that one way to differentiate the Brujah and the True Brujah discipline spreads is to flip around the dynamics of their physical and mental disciplines. Instead of an active, aggressive physical discipline (Potence), give the Trujah a passive, reactive physical discipline (Fortitude). Instead of passive, emotional mental influence (Presence), give them active, calculating mind control (Dominate).<br /> <br /> Dominate, Fortitude, Temporis. The True Brujah start to look like the Ventrue dialed up to eleven: imperious, impervious, implacable, eternal. These are creatures that should look like classical sculptures when at rest, and as deadly as the Weeping Angels when they come after you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T11:56:53-07:00","id":1466691,"title":"","content":"those are great ideas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T12:00:59-07:00","id":1466692,"title":"","content":"The True Brujah only make sense to me as part of the original package of the True Black Hand. One does not go without the other. It's part of the super secret mystery of the Tal'Mahe'Re that there is this unknown Brujah bloodline who wants revenge on the usurper's bloodline because the entire point of the Tal'Mahe'Re is to serve the antedeluvians, and since the Brujah murdered theirs, that means the entire Brujah clan is their enemy. Only the &quot;real&quot; Brujah survivors who escaped the purge are worthy of membership and survive Gehenna. If you divorce the True Brujah as members of the True Black Hand and talk about them separately, it doesn't make any sense. They aren't an independent thing, they are part of this greater conspiracy. If you handle them as some kind of independent faction, they lose their entire purpose of existing in the narrative.<br /> <br /> Now personally I never liked the idea of the True Brujah mainly because I think Temporis is silly. And while I now like Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand as an example of huge mysteries to include in your chronicle world, I can't actually use the book itself because the act of publishing it robs it of any mysteries. I can't surprise the characters at the table because I can't surprise the players. There are elements I use in my games along with a bunch of other stuff, but the True Brujah as written aren't one of them.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of these very high level Jyhad mysteries that can be discovered by the PCs if they want to go looking for them. But from my experience, PCs don't go looking for them unless the ST is crafting and forcing such a plot on them. PCs quickly get bogged down with their own backstories (always the most fascinating things to players) and the mundane aspects of living in a domain. Still, I have them in my setting lurking off stage. Just gives me more time to refine and add to them. <br /> <br /> I've never actually seen any ST actually use the True Brujah. Though in some of my early LARPs that welcomed practically any character concept, there were some twinks who played True Brujah PCs. I can call them twinks because the first thing they did was tell everyone they were actually True Brujah so they could lecture us on lore, as if we didn't have access to the same books they did. Needless to say, if you are a True Brujah, telling other vampires you are one is not something you'd actually do.<br /> <br /> = =<br /> <br /> Nictuku are awesome, but again always offstage. I do think the Nosferatu often run across things they shouldn't, and it bites them in the ass. And having this legend around can make things seem much more sinister than what they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T14:46:02-07:00","id":1466705,"title":"","content":"I don't believe in binding any element or idea to just one interpretation.<br /> <br /> Can I come up with uses for the True Brujah outside the context of DSotBH? Yes, I can. They may be this old cult all by themselves, or a bloodline with a different origin story and a grudge, they may be conspirators behind many of the high-level moves of the Jyhad, they may be an ancient offshoot that still holds to really old artifact and lore.<br /> <br /> They may be what they claim to be and yet not all of them follow the same beliefs or goals, or they may be another thing entirely and still act upon it, or yet they may have nothing to do with the elements in DSotBH and work out entirely because of their own main characteristics, an emotionless bloodline of philosophers with a strange variation of the Brujah Disciplines, a case in which Temporis is a good twist, and sometimes that's all you need.<br /> <br /> What I definitely don't need is to interpret lore so strictly as to rob myself of the ability to apply a tool in other, interesting ways when those benefit my games or character (because yes, I already had players interested in playing True Brujah and I see no reason to say no).<br /> <br /> Other than that, even by going to their roots I see absolutely no need for the True Black Hand to be right. Legends are legends. I find this notion in many RPGs that legends, myths and religions are either 90+% truth or conspiracy crafted hoaxes as stupid. It ignores the fact that stories within stories may be themselves concepts as complex as characters.<br /> <br /> How a foundation story shapes the peoples who know of them or are shaped by those people is, for me, far more relevant than deciding if this story is real or not. Their reality is meaningless outside my own satisfaction, while their interaction with contemporary characters is what can really shape new tales for me to tell. What characters do because of those stories? What they did in the past that left objects, places and stuff that can tell new stories? How the narrative itself affects the present?<br /> <br /> And how can this narrative be used and altered, by design or accident, by its narrators in the world? This's far more relevant to me than deciding whatever truly happened at the distant past. And by letting characters reinterpret and change the narrative, <i>something that is pretty common and natural irl</i>, I can make room for even more new ways those characters can be used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T22:24:54-07:00","id":1466748,"title":"","content":"I really like the concept of fallen Bloodlines desperately trying to remain or become significant, of old bitterness that has no more target to satisfy itself with (like, &quot;the guy I hate cuz he usurped my city in Corinth died two hundred years ago, and I just learned today&quot;). And aside of the 'let's make an awesome amazing cool sect of ultra-rare unique edgy secret vampires that are 'in the know' more than any other&quot;, it makes a lot of sense for ancient vampires, or lost bloodlines to get together. So Inconnu, Hand Without a Sun and the Lost Tribe are fun to exist.<br /> <br /> Now, with the True Brujah it is a very problematic matter, because to define their true intention and purpose you have to define or affirm many of the &quot;Can's and Do's&quot; of the setting. Or risk having your entire vengeance cult of True Brujah being bitter and stupid vampires who hate an entire disparate Clan cause of some old myth that few believe, and even fewer know more about. Although it can be an ironic affect, that those who think are beyond or over the Jyhad are actually the ones most manipulated by it.<br /> <br /> I find those myths fascinating, Nictucku being one. Makes sense for the most paranoid Clan to have a boogeyman. And probably many Nosferatu who have unaffiliated themselves from the Clan, will be deemed Nictucku. Cuz what is a Nosferatu that doesn't make things according to the Clan, or at least that the Clan knows about? Nictucku! Probably not, but vampires are paranoia machines. If you want to fuck with the Sewer Rats, it is simple as make they think Nictucku are in toe.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I interpret that many Bloodlines and groups, like Nictucku, Daughters of Cacophony, Baali... are basically just labels. Not really bloodlines, with their own innate powers and banes. Some of these cases are very controversial of course. My take, in my own setting, is only that things are more organic, a bit more complex (but only that its no new slate, just bits of others with misunderstanding thrown over it) and not simply a new Clan; Banes and Disciplines can take some different shapes. The Baali, for me, are a name for infernalists generically speaking, used by old vampires and lore masters; tere are cults, sects, rituals and lores yes, like a 'true Baali', which most of the structures, the types, the differences are lost to most Cainites; but they ain't a new Clan, they are inducted from other Clan (like Setites taking members from all over).<br /> To me the original Baali were not made by a single Ante, but at least three, and the founders of the Baali are Cainites from these Clans, with some uniquely developed powers and amalgams, but most of it coming from demonic Blood Sorcery and et cetera.<br /> <br /> I still haven't decided what True Brujahs are in my setting... but if there were, they would either be hermits, or vengeance bound seekers. Probably they would want to destroy every Dream and Carthage they see, so Inconnu is more probable (numerous) than Tal'Mahe'Ra. <br /> <br /> That brings me a thought. If the Sabbat was always decentralized, with the Regent having limited power over the worldwide sect, how the Tal'Mahe'Ra truly manipulated the sect? I imagine they would have to do it locally in each case. And mostly would use the sect as a coverup and host to them. So when the Gehenna Crusade exploded, and many started running to Beckoning Zones, and invading cities, the True Black Hand would go nuts trying to either stave off the assault of the sect on the ancients, or fighting them back directly. This is, if their infighting didn't brought them down before that. <br /> As surreal and sometimes silly that these plots got, I kind miss them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T10:08:35-07:00","id":1466784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466748#post1466748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find those myths fascinating, Nictucku being one. Makes sense for the most paranoid Clan to have a boogeyman. And probably many Nosferatu who have unaffiliated themselves from the Clan, will be deemed Nictucku. Cuz what is a Nosferatu that doesn't make things according to the Clan, or at least that the Clan knows about? Nictucku! Probably not, but vampires are paranoia machines. If you want to fuck with the Sewer Rats, it is simple as make they think Nictucku are in toe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Nictuku would be a label to every Nos outside the clan because they don't use the label to explain common setbacks. They use it to explain out the entire clan presence in a city going MIA. This is kind of a big thing, so a Nictuku is by necessity a big threat capable of pulling this out in some fashion.<br /> <br /> Otherwise their legend is really that they're kind of just a group of Nos. To be exactly, the 4th gen minus Baba Yaga. Some also say that the old Hag is the sire of their entire 5th gen, as Absimiliard forbade the 4th from siring and the Nictuku obeyed, hence she being in their target list.<br /> <br /> The Tal'Mahe'Ra didn't intervening in the Gehenna Crusade. They weren't a thing in the period in the official lore. They got blew up in the 6th Maelstrom and there are signs of them reforming <i>now</i>, so at the time there was just no True Black Hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T17:21:53-07:00","id":1466837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466692#post1466692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nictuku are awesome, but again always offstage. I do think the Nosferatu often run across things they shouldn't, and it bites them in the ass. And having this legend around can make things seem much more sinister than what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe I've ever done anything with them as a storyteller, but in my headcanon Nictucku are just campfire stories the Nosferatu tell each other to explain members of their warrens (or occasionally, entire warrens) going missing without explanation. Sometimes it might be to fellow Nosferatu fallen to the Beast, sometimes to hunters, sometimes to werewolves, sometimes to stranger things skulking underground.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T19:45:41-07:00","id":1466855,"title":"","content":"This book was the final nail in the coffin, that convinced me to abandon any hope of ever being interested in 5th edition World of Darkness. I was really, really hoping that a book about the Sabbat would give us the opportunity to play vampires who have turned their backs on Humanity, but no. They're relegated to being exclusively antagonists, and there aren't even any mechanics for how a Path of Enlightenment functions.<br /> <br /> Meaning there are no rules for explaining how / why these vampires haven't succumbed permanently to the Beast. They just haven't; and no, the players can not do the same thing, because that would ruin the Humanity focused aesthetic that 5th edition is trying to go for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T20:18:21-07:00","id":1466865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466855#post1466855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This book was the final nail in the coffin, that convinced me to abandon any hope of ever being interested in 5th edition World of Darkness. I was really, really hoping that a book about the Sabbat would give us the opportunity to play vampires who have turned their backs on Humanity, but no. They're relegated to being exclusively antagonists, and there aren't even any mechanics for how a Path of Enlightenment functions.<br /> <br /> Meaning there are no rules for explaining how / why these vampires haven't succumbed permanently to the Beast. They just haven't; and no, the players can not do the same thing, because that would ruin the Humanity focused aesthetic that 5th edition is trying to go for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean they explained how it worked just fine. They have a different set of values and a Path of Caine member mourning a mortal is a mortal sin. There's just no rules for it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T20:21:01-07:00","id":1466869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466865#post1466865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean they explained how it worked just fine. They have a different set of values and a Path of Caine member mourning a mortal is a mortal sin. There's just no rules for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right, they explained how it works for an NPC. We were hoping for an explanation on how they work for a PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T01:37:11-07:00","id":1466915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466865#post1466865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean they explained how it worked just fine. They have a different set of values and a Path of Caine member mourning a mortal is a mortal sin. There's just no rules for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which isn't explaining it, any more than suck, squeeze, bang, blow actually explains the internal combustion engine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T04:47:33-07:00","id":1466926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466855#post1466855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This book was the final nail in the coffin</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is the final nail in the Coffin, I wonder what W5 and M5 will be. Nuclear weapons? Astroids the size of jupiter? The sun expanding? A black hole? The so-called inevitable heat death of the universe? Vampire is the <i>safe </i>game in the series. <br /> <br /> Back to the topic that's wildly off topic. <br /> I really just imagined Niktuku as Nosferatu on steroids. Mindbendingly ugly. But also... more myth than not. Sometimes a Nosferatu will become a wight and destroy the warren. Some Nosferatu just disappear because drains and sewers and other underground localities have some pretty gnarly hazards that can crush or trap a vampire. Honestly speaking, Nosferatu are probably the second worst vampire clan to piss off (next to Malkavians) but they're quite close knit and are not great investigators like malks are. If you need to kill the Nosferatu, you should do it all in a single sweeping movement, and hope they blame the Niktuku. The Ratkin are the next biggest cause of &quot;niktuku&quot; happenings. <br /> <br /> The Ventrue have their secret masters, which is also kinda interesting but not needing as much explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T04:52:42-07:00","id":1466928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466926#post1466926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this is the final nail in the Coffin, I wonder what W5 and M5 will be. Nuclear weapons? Astroids the size of jupiter? The sun expanding? A black hole? The so-called inevitable heat death of the universe? Vampire is the <i>safe </i>game in the series.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">No Edition warring, please.</span></b><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T08:04:19-07:00","id":1466946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1466926#post1466926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this is the final nail in the Coffin, I wonder what W5 and M5 will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about the rational answer\u2026 they will just not be relevant to me.<br /> <br /> People have different interests and that\u2019s okay. I don\u2019t think it\u2019s edition warring to say that V20 and V5 deliver different experiences with different points of focus and that\u2019s okay.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m just glad that M5 was far enough down the pipeline that I got a complete set of mechanics out of M20 that I can apply whatever set of fluff I wish to it. I went more than a decade using Mage Revised after that line was replaced with Awakening. People have gone decades using just 1e AD&amp;D and their imaginations. A game edition ending isn\u2019t a cataclysm unless it\u2019s incomplete.<br /> <br /> And honestly, between the books they did put out, V20 has covered virtually every mechanical bit I can think of (admittedly they squeezed the dhampir update into BJD\u2026 literally the last possible V20 book and literally the ONLY reason I got a book filled mostly with fluff I\u2019ll never use\u2026 but still, all the mechanics are there and updated).<br /> <br /> Everything else I could think to add is mostly fluff text describing more locations and for that you can use V5\u2019s fluff (though I\u2019d personally set the Beckoning at 7th Gen or less since the normal PC range tops out at 8th Gen\u2026 thinblood alchemy if it ever needs to be a thing for your game is just an Inceptor who turned the HH2 path of alchemy into a discipline that uses blood points instead of willpower) -or- make your own.<br /> <br /> Personally, I could see some potential Sabbat fluff here to be useful if I wanted to go a certain direction with my sandbox. The nearby pack was one of the stationary ones and was mostly on Honorable Accord with one on Feral Heart and a few at low Humanity. So, if I used the V5 Sabbat book, they pretty much got overlooked when the Crusade got called and spent years holding down the fort as the bulk of Sabbat left and transformed.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re basically the post-WW2 Japanese soldiers left behind on an island unaware the war is over and waiting for orders that will never come. And when they DO figure out what happened and that they\u2019re basically no longer welcome in the \u201cNew Sabbat\u201d they\u2019ll have to figure out what they\u2019re going to do next, because they\u2019re all still loyal to each other, but otherwise are without a Sect.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> As for the Niktuku, I\u2019ve never used them, but if I do I\u2019ve got the idea in my head running with the idea that Absimilard forbade his childer from siring and only Baba Yaga disobeyed\u2026 basically, the idea is that, in a twisted sort of morality, the Niktuku only go after Nosferatu who have sired (i.e. many Nosferatu don\u2019t choose to be Embraced and so the Niktuku do not find guilt in that\u2026 but siring breaks the founder\u2019s command and so your life is forfeit). Deploy one in that fashion with a PC Nos neonate and you can inflict all manner of horrors with everyone questioning afterwards how a few neonates survived when elders were slaughtered. All sorts of potential complications there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}